{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen","id":805704,"title":"Meet The Huntsmen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T19:22:35-08:00","id":805704,"title":"Meet The Huntsmen","content":"This isn't the whole section. There's some material on what happens when you steal a Huntsman's weapon (they're fucked up). There's some material on how they actually hunt. There's also some samples. Those aren't included. But this should give you an idea of what the Huntsmen are. <br /> <br /> I'm going to put up a blog post, but we do a Monday embargo on new blog posts because of Monday Meeting Notes. I'll try to remember tomorrow. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoXzJKNkVaSzlvMFU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoXzJKNkVaSzlvMFU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoXzJKNkVaSzlvMFU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoXzJKNkVaSzlvMFU/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:28:18-08:00","id":805710,"title":"","content":"Finally, I can say something I've been wanting to say for ages.<br /> <br /> The reason I love Huntsmen?<br /> <br /> <i>They're anti-changelings</i>. They are fae shoved out of Arcadia in grossly transformed forms by the will of the True Fae, unable to come home until they succeed at their task-bring the changeling they're born to find back to Faerie.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's a little more complicated than that, but the basics stand.<br /> <br /> What would you do-who would you torment and kill-to get home?<br /> <br /> That's the Huntsmen-terrifyingly familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:30:11-08:00","id":805711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805710#post805710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, I can say something I've been wanting to say for ages.<br /> <br /> The reason I love Huntsmen?<br /> <br /> <i>They're anti-changelings</i>. They are fae shoved out of Arcadia in grossly transformed forms by the will of the True Fae, unable to come home until they succeed at their task-bring the changeling they're born to find back to Faerie.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's a little more complicated than that, but the basics stand.<br /> <br /> What would you do-who would you torment and kill-to get home?<br /> <br /> That's the Huntsmen-terrifyingly familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. They're complete dramatic foils to the Changeling condition. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:57:33-08:00","id":805722,"title":"","content":"I don't know what I expected, but it was nothing as visceral and powerful as this. And I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:02:03-08:00","id":805724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805710#post805710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, I can say something I've been wanting to say for ages.<br /> <br /> The reason I love Huntsmen?<br /> <br /> <i>They're anti-changelings</i>. They are fae shoved out of Arcadia in grossly transformed forms by the will of the True Fae, unable to come home until they succeed at their task-bring the changeling they're born to find back to Faerie.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's a little more complicated than that, but the basics stand.<br /> <br /> What would you do-who would you torment and kill-to get home?<br /> <br /> That's the Huntsmen-terrifyingly familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't have said it better myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:08:25-08:00","id":805728,"title":"","content":"I was mostly right with my guesses, though I expected the Huntsmen to be made of a part that the changelings left behind in Arcadia. The Seeming descriptions kept referencing over and over to body parts left behind.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I'll be using the Huntsmen frequently, actually. I was expecting them to be less specific and more suitable to different chronicles. But the fact that they all have the same origin, the same task and behave in the same way (save for the personality quirks of the Spirit of the Hunt that animates them) make them feel like they could get old fast. I'll probably relegate them to occasional antagonists instead of the default ones.<br /> <br /> I think there was a missed opportunity here with mortals who make a bargain with the True Fae instead, drawing inspiration from the original Huntsman. The mortal may feel sorry for the changeling, but he has to deliver her back to Arcadia or his wife's cancer is going to come back. It would make for sympathetic, tragic antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:10:40-08:00","id":805730,"title":"","content":"I've made a Huntsman for every theoretical player I've had and haven't been bored yet. But that's me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:12:49-08:00","id":805731,"title":"","content":"I guess it's just hard for me to care about antagonists whose universal, overriding motivation is always &quot;I want to stop existing because existence sucks.&quot; It just feels like there's only so much of that I can bring to the table before it gets old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:20:15-08:00","id":805734,"title":"","content":"I am simultaneously terrified of and in love with Tokens and everything they bring to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:20:52-08:00","id":805735,"title":"","content":"As opposed to a bunch of protagonists whose universal motivation is always &quot;Find your way home&quot;?<br /> <br /> Each Huntsmen has a personality beyond that, a story to tell. Yes, they all want to go home, but they also want seduce their prey or run them down or play stop-and-go with their hearts. These are stories, ancient and new, about hunting, and while they want to return home, they also want to hunt in ways that are true and meaningful to them. We have an infinite number of stories about how to get what we want, and the Huntsmen tell them more intimately, viciously, than most.<br /> <br /> Journeys, not destinations. If we focused on the reduced answer, we'd never bother telling stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-10-2016, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:23:02-08:00","id":805737,"title":"","content":"I like it so far, I expected the Huntsmen to be a more obvious threat rather than subtle, but I don't dislike it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:39:44-08:00","id":805747,"title":"","content":"Yes XD<br /> Finally, some material on the Huntsmen we can work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:41:55-08:00","id":805749,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel like the Huntsmen muddle the metaphor at the heart of Changeling, but I'm also starting to view 1e and 2e as very different games.<br /> <br /> Not to say I don't like them; they're a fascinating piece of the fluff and make very compelling villains. I really enjoy this little glimpse of what Arcadia is beyond just the Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:43:20-08:00","id":805750,"title":"","content":"Which metaphor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:06:59-08:00","id":805767,"title":"","content":"The thing is, changelings have different motivations. Not all of them want to go back home. Some of them want to create a home of their own, or just travel from place to place, or delve deep into the secret of their fae existence, or numb their memories with nightclubs and lovers, and so on. What motivates changelings is wildly different. Huntsmen always have the same motivation. They all want the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:13:11-08:00","id":805769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805767#post805767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, changelings have different motivations. Not all of them want to go back home. Some of them want to create a home of their own, or just travel from place to place, or delve deep into the secret of their fae existence, or numb their memories with nightclubs and lovers, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, do you think &quot;home&quot; is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:16:09-08:00","id":805770,"title":"","content":"The word &quot;spirit&quot; shows up quite a bit in this document. Is there are more tangible connection to the denizens of the Shadow, or is spirit just a convenient term to describe an intangible aspect of something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:17:10-08:00","id":805772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805769#post805769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, exactly, do you think &quot;home&quot; is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think stretching the definition of that word to cover anything a changeling could possibly want makes for a meaningful discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:21:36-08:00","id":805774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805772#post805772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think stretching the definition of that word to cover anything a changeling could possibly want makes for a meaningful discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I think acting like four different pursuits of security and/or peace of mind are equivalent to vastly divergent core motivations is a poor argument in general for why shapeshifting nemeses would've been better served being mortals conscripted by the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-11-2016, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:36:06-08:00","id":805780,"title":"","content":"I like it! The Token Of Reprieve is an especially fascinating idea. I can imagine some really evil Darklings who hoard these Tokens and sell them in shady goblin markets.<br /> <br /> I think it would be cool if the Hounds Of The Hunt could manifest as other types of animals, with features based on the Huntsman who summoned them. Crows that only have eyes inside their beaks, big rats with crimson flashlights replacing their snouts and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:41:32-08:00","id":805783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805750#post805750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which metaphor?</div> </div> </div> </div>CtL has gone from &quot;the abuse game&quot; to &quot;the trauma game.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805770#post805770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word &amp;quot;spirit&amp;quot; shows up quite a bit in this document. Is there are more tangible connection to the denizens of the Shadow, or is spirit just a convenient term to describe an intangible aspect of something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcadia has always had strange denizens other than the Gentry and hobs. Think of them as incarnate elements of the Wyrd, living little story pieces and sentient bits of fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:44:18-08:00","id":805784,"title":"","content":"Trauma is a much better source-it's broader, relates to more people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:46:38-08:00","id":805786,"title":"","content":"I down with the idea of wyrd-born base materials, but there was that &quot;some theorize that that spirits being forcibly transformed into hobgoblins is how the hedge gets populated&quot; bit in equinox road, and I'm just wondering how much of a connection to Shadow Realm Denizens was actually intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:01:56-08:00","id":805795,"title":"","content":"Personally I rather like these Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805767#post805767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, changelings have different motivations. Not all of them want to go back home. Some of them want to create a home of their own, or just travel from place to place, or delve deep into the secret of their fae existence, or numb their memories with nightclubs and lovers, and so on. What motivates changelings is wildly different. Huntsmen always have the same motivation. They all want the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Huntsmen and Changelings both &quot;all want the same thing&quot;, home. If you reduce it to it's most basic, then your complaint applies to both equally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:02:13-08:00","id":805797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805786#post805786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I down with the idea of wyrd-born base materials, but there was that &quot;some theorize that that spirits being forcibly transformed into hobgoblins is how the hedge gets populated&quot; bit in equinox road, and I'm just wondering how much of a connection to Shadow Realm Denizens was actually intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not drawing any definite references; some stuff is up for interpretation. If you want them to be related, sure. The Shadow doesn't get referenced at all in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:03:59-08:00","id":805798,"title":"","content":"I love it! Very different than what I expected. Thank you guys for sharing this! I wonder, even though Contracts have yet to have been spoilered, do Huntsmen get Contracts? I would assume so (since theyre made of Arcadian materials). Without Contracts, there wouldnt be much to distinguish them. Another question, is there a time limit for how long a Hunt can last? In my CofDCcomics universe, I was hoping to have Martian Manhunter as an extremely ..unique Huntsman. Perhaps a unique situation where his ability to return was cut off, and he went native? Or might he simply be on a very, very long hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:06:48-08:00","id":805801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805798#post805798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love it! Very different than what I expected. Thank you guys for sharing this! I wonder, even though Contracts have yet to have been spoilered, do Huntsmen get Contracts? I would assume so (since theyre made of Arcadian materials). Without Contracts, there wouldnt be much to distinguish them. Another question, is there a time limit for how long a Hunt can last? In my CofDCcomics universe, I was hoping to have Martian Manhunter as an extremely ..unique Huntsman. Perhaps a unique situation where his ability to return was cut off, and he went native? Or might he simply be on a very, very long hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a limit; it's detailed in one of the not-spoiled bits. Not 100% settled on it yet though. <br /> <br /> They don't get Contracts. At least, I don't believe they do yet. I might change that. Conceptually, they're a little simpler than that. Their abilities are few and potent. But, if you know about them, you more or less know what they can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:10:52-08:00","id":805802,"title":"","content":"Are there more powers to look forward to of theirs that weren't spoilered? I assume yes. I don't mind a lack of contracts--they have Merits, right? Could that include supernatural merits (say, an ifrit changeling's Huntsman from the brass and fire city has pyrokinesis)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:12:08-08:00","id":805803,"title":"","content":"Is there any significance to the circle within the shadow of a burning tree? I have a strong feeling it's one of those obscure Arcadian laws whose origin may have been forgotten even by the Gentry. It reminded me of the burning bush from the Book Of Exodus, but it might be just a coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:40:13-08:00","id":805811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805784#post805784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trauma is a much better source-it's broader, relates to more people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and there are mental illnesses beyond depression, but Wraith is great because it largely stuck to one. <br /> <br /> I don't want to get into it in this thread. Not again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:46:02-08:00","id":805814,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit lukewarm on the part where they have to kill a human to remember how the mortal world works. I don't really see how it fits into their story. I'm also having a very difficult time imagining how they manage to kill someone without understanding the basics of physical reality, unless completely by accident, and I <i>certainly</i> can't grok how they would know not to &quot;immediately grab someone off the street and gut her in plain view of everyone.&quot; The rest of the writeup was great, and I love the anti-changeling angle, but that particular bit left me scratching my head.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, all the talk of spirits of the hunt has got me in the mood to work on my werewolf crossover Freehold again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:53:42-08:00","id":805822,"title":"","content":"I think it is a progression of prey. They're Huntsmen, so.. have them hunt. First, mortal(s). Then, move on to the real dangerous game. I think it fits. OTOH, I agree with you that even with an instinct to kill, they will take time before they can pull it off, having to try out different tactics, observe, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:07:21-08:00","id":805833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805822#post805822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is a progression of prey. They're Huntsmen, so.. have them hunt. First, mortal(s). Then, move on to the real dangerous game. I think it fits. OTOH, I agree with you that even with an instinct to kill, they will take time before they can pull it off, having to try out different tactics, observe, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm just experiencing some cognitive dissonance between the fact that don't understand the laws of physical reality until after they've killed, and the fact that they take their time, observe and try out different tactics on their first victim. How do they do that when they don't know how the world works yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:14:46-08:00","id":805835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805814#post805814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated note, all the talk of spirits of the hunt has got me in the mood to work on my werewolf crossover Freehold again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to share? I am very curious, now, about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:20:20-08:00","id":805839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805833#post805833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm just experiencing some cognitive dissonance between the fact that don't understand the laws of physical reality until after they've killed, and <b>the fact that they take their time, observe and try out different tactics on their first victim</b>. How do they do that when they don't know how the world works yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded statement is supposition on Things's part and is not present in the writeup.<br /> <br /> Being individual spirits of the hunt drawn from a place that runs on emotional resonance goes a long way toward having a basic understanding of hunting and tactics. You don't need to know what a building is made of to know that it is, conceptually, shelter, nor do you need to know what an accountant does to recognize that it's imprudent to shank one in full view of a score or three of mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:49:30-08:00","id":805848,"title":"","content":"So, here's what I don't understand: why would a Huntsman ever spend their last point of Yearning? Every usage of Yearning seems to be about getting one step closer to their quarry, which makes sense, but spending the last point is an action they can't follow up on for two weeks. Plus, spending that last point seems to basically be a bit of self-inflicted trauma.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Changelings have the ability to <i>force</i> Huntsmen to spend Yearning somehow? Or the reflexive healing isn't as optional as it sounds; as in, losing all their Health kills them such that they won't re-form, so it's preferable to burn all their Yearnings when they're losing a fight so that at least they'll come back?<br /> <br /> I like'em. I'll have to re-read when I'm not exhausted to feel like I get it, but I like'em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T00:06:07-08:00","id":805854,"title":"","content":"As extension to <b>Errol</b> question, I repost my answer from other topic to the <b>DavidH</b> reply on motivation and Approaches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=805689#post805689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a default state of more-or-less dormancy, nonexistent. This is what they want. This is their comfort zone.<br /> <br /> When the Gentry pull them out of this state and send them on a task, they hate it. Existence is filthy, painful, and way too organised. It's <i>wrong</i>. Successful completion of the job lets them dissolve back into nothingness. Failure captures them in an agonising cycle where they can't regain their natural forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if Huntsmen so much hate being and Hunt - <b>WHY they collect Yearing?</b> Your description sounds like Huntsmen <b>do not</b> want to use Approaches - they want to get back to Arcadia non-existence as quick as possible. Playing in all the Hunt is only making it much longer.<br /> <br /> Myself, I would rephrase all the &quot;motivation&quot; section and mark that Huntsmen, yes, they hate being fleshy, but on the other hand - they love being in body and Hunt. They are pulled in to two conflicting directions and there are many Huntsmen that do not play in the game of Approaches, just simply go for the changeling Prey.<br /> <br /> Or if you want to highlight the idea that Huntsmen want to return time after time on Hunt and <b>all of them</b> use Approaches - they do <b>not hate</b> being corporal. That they look for the True Fae to animate them and remake in to Huntsmen. They just do not want displease Gentry masters in Hunt.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell - do not make their motivations so contradictory, as instead Hunting, our Huntsmen would spend too much time thinking if they should come back to Arcadia as quickly as they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T00:07:45-08:00","id":805855,"title":"","content":"I like it, though I am not really thrilled about how absolute &quot;Few things cause as much grief to the Fae as the loss of one of their changeling playthings&quot; is phrased.<br /> I know giving Changeling more inbuild storyhooks is one of the goals the new edition, but a small qualifier that not all True Fae react that way would be appreciated.<br /> I have seen some good stories where the relation between changeling and Fae was very different, and as is It feels like it undercuts the diversity of the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T00:14:01-08:00","id":805857,"title":"","content":"If a Huntsmen is &quot;killed&quot; by inflicting sufficient lethal or aggravated damage, are they utterly destroyed, reform after a fortnight as if they used-up their Yerning without successfully completing their hunt, or something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:00:51-08:00","id":805909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805857#post805857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Huntsmen is &quot;killed&quot; by inflicting sufficient lethal or aggravated damage, are they utterly destroyed, reform after a fortnight as if they used-up their Yerning without successfully completing their hunt, or something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>They reform as if they used up their Yearning. At least, that's my current approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:45:42-08:00","id":805958,"title":"","content":"I would assume a Huntsman at the end of his Yearning knows hes going down--and thats good. Even a two week vacation from the Iron World is better than stuck here forever. So if spending their last yearning gets them closer to ending the Hunt, they get a brief break and are one step closer to a much longer period of dormancy. Win, win. And also, Joker, I'd be inclined to think that the grief true fae feel is sort of meta, a la equinox road. IN character, they feel one thing. Bbut &quot;ooc&quot; the fae is sad to lose an opponent, a slaver, a lover, a duelist, whatever. In Arcadia, its largely just True Fae. And they get bored of each other, otherwise they'd leave humans alone. Even if your keeper utterly despises, or even is entirely apathetic, towards you.. he still relishes and loves the opportunity to feel those things, and misses them when they are gone. Like many RL abusers, I'd assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:34:15-08:00","id":806001,"title":"","content":"Thank youso much for showing this to us dave <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />,i was curious about the huntsmen for such a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:37:05-08:00","id":806004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805854#post805854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if Huntsmen so much hate being and Hunt - <b>WHY they collect Yearing?</b> Your description sounds like Huntsmen <b>do not</b> want to use Approaches - they want to get back to Arcadia non-existence as quick as possible. Playing in all the Hunt is only making it much longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have to, I assume. If they're bound by the rules of story, then they're bound by what those rules say about what hunting <i>is</i> - and in stories, hunting usually equates to stalking and escalation, not an efficient chase down. It would also make sense to say their way of working is bound by the narrative associations of what they're made from, and perhaps by the nature of what they're crafted to hunt.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my question: does every changeling have their own huntsman?<br /> <br /> They're interesting, though I personally find the fetch more so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:40:13-08:00","id":806005,"title":"","content":"It seems like the Others changed a bit too. if i rememer correctly,they didnt really have emotions in the first edition,they could pretendo to love or hate but they dont really feel those things,thats what made then inhuman,thats what made them evil.<br /> Now,they are inhuman and evil because they feel too much,their emotions are too strong,good change,they are scarier now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:06:27-08:00","id":806017,"title":"","content":"if i were a really sadistic storyteller,i'd put a character with some deformity int he chronicle,imply that it is a huntsman. and one of the character murders it,it'd be reveled they were just a person with a deformity<br /> then'd i'd lolve my ass off as the changeling clarity drop like its hot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:22:31-08:00","id":806024,"title":"","content":"So... I've read over this, and let it digest a bit, but... what is really the point of using a Huntsman? So far, they seem like... a loyalist that doesn't want to be here, that can become a display case if they want to. They don't seem like creatures with particularly any depth to them so far, besides just being a... being from a different world that just doesn't like this one, that will just keep coming. Narratively they're different, but effectively they serve a very similar role, just with different powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:32:32-08:00","id":806027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806024#post806024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I've read over this, and let it digest a bit, but... what is really the point of using a Huntsman? So far, they seem like... a loyalist that doesn't want to be here, that can become a display case if they want to. They don't seem like creatures with particularly any depth to them so far, besides just being a... being from a different world that just doesn't like this one, that will just keep coming. Narratively they're different, but effectively they serve a very similar role, just with different powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>well,i'd say,the main difference between a huntsman and a loyalist/privateer is that the huntsmen are part of a story in way deeper than a loyalist is. the huntsmen are more pure than changelings,more inhuman. and in the end,they're better at hunting than changelings should be,they are made of spirtits of hunting,hunting is 50% of that they are,they live for the hunt 50% of their time,and the other 50% is the desire to go home and end the hunt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:36:07-08:00","id":806030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805854#post805854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if Huntsmen so much hate being and Hunt - <b>WHY they collect Yearing?</b> Your description sounds like Huntsmen <b>do not</b> want to use Approaches - they want to get back to Arcadia non-existence as quick as possible. Playing in all the Hunt is only making it much longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I gather, Huntsmen hate being incarnated, but hate an unsucessful hunt <i>more</i>. They need to balance getting enough resources to make sure their hunt is successful (and thus, no torment at the end) vs extending their stay in this mudball world. And remember, it doesn't matter how much Yearning they have in stock if they successfully haul their prey back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805728#post805728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there was a missed opportunity here with mortals who make a bargain with the True Fae instead, drawing inspiration from the original Huntsman. The mortal may feel sorry for the changeling, but he has to deliver her back to Arcadia or his wife's cancer is going to come back. It would make for sympathetic, tragic antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if one of the abilities Huntsman have is a general Boon/Wish power they can use for others/mortals, that would enable this too. The Huntsman sub-contracts their hunt out to a mortal in exchange for what the mortal wants. Same as here, but with a Huntsman instead of a True Fae.<br /> <br /> Any chance of that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806027#post806027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well,i'd say,the main difference between a huntsman and a loyalist/privateer is that the huntsmen are part of a story in way deeper than a loyalist is. the huntsmen are more pure than changelings,more inhuman. and in the end,they're better at hunting than changelings should be,they are made of spirtits of hunting,hunting is 50% of that they are,they live for the hunt 50% of their time,and the other 50% is the desire to go home and end the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>And nothing says the Huntsman can't sub-contract out parts of the hunt to Loyalists (especially for a lazy/slothful or cautious Huntsman).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-11-2016, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:56:44-08:00","id":806041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806024#post806024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I've read over this, and let it digest a bit, but... what is really the point of using a Huntsman? So far, they seem like... a loyalist that doesn't want to be here, that can become a display case if they want to. They don't seem like creatures with particularly any depth to them so far, besides just being a... being from a different world that just doesn't like this one, that will just keep coming. Narratively they're different, but effectively they serve a very similar role, just with different powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a major thing about Huntsmen is that unless you use a token you Cannot escape. You cannot stop them. If you kill them or strip them of their yearning, they just come back. The changelings are tied to the narrative of the escape, and the Huntsmen are the reoccurring villains that are the manifestation of those tropes.<br /> <br /> You can reason with, escape or kill a loyalist. You can reason with, escape, or kill a privateer. You cannot escape a Huntsman, not without helping to send someone to the fate your trying to escape or you dying yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-11-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:00:06-08:00","id":806043,"title":"","content":"Beside mine narrative points, I have a mechanics question - about Disguise power. <b>If Huntsman use it, do it <i>replicate</i> or <i>become</i> the item they mimicking?</b><br /> <br /> Let's say, we have a Huntsman that cornered his Lost prey into the old manor. He want's to make a trap on them. In manor are old paintings - one of them is especially nice looking and about the size of Huntsmen, so he want to Disguise as it. Does he:<br /> <br /> A. Huntsmen <i>copy</i> the painting - and so we have TWO paintings - one original, and another that is Huntsmen in Disguise. Changelings will surely suspect that something is fishy when the see two identical paintings...<br /> B. Huntsmen <i>embodied </i>the painting - there is only one of them because Huntsmen joined the original painting.<br /> <br /> If the idea is rather answer B - <b>Maybe rename power to Embodiment or something? </b>Maybe then let Huntsmen to &quot;posses&quot; mortals they copy, rather than duplicate?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:13:13-08:00","id":806049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806024#post806024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I've read over this, and let it digest a bit, but... what is really the point of using a Huntsman? So far, they seem like... a loyalist that doesn't want to be here, that can become a display case if they want to. They don't seem like creatures with particularly any depth to them so far, besides just being a... being from a different world that just doesn't like this one, that will just keep coming. Narratively they're different, but effectively they serve a very similar role, just with different powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsmen are better at finding Icons. With an Icon, a Huntsman always knows what direction the changeling lies, unless they're on a different side (IE: Hedge vs. mundane world). That makes them utterly fearsome hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:16:09-08:00","id":806053,"title":"","content":"can you explain more deeply what are the spirits of hunting the huntsman are born of,i'm wondering what are their natural state in arcadia,oh,before i forget,do you think you can show us the new true fae soon? sorry if i'm being greedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 01-11-2016, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:21:25-08:00","id":806057,"title":"","content":"Er, forgive me if I'm saying something stupid here, but can a Huntsman's motivation change? Like, could one become so obsessed with chasing a particular Changeling they might not want to not exist, because that would stop them from targeting their new arch-nemesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:25:24-08:00","id":806061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806057#post806057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, forgive me if I'm saying something stupid here, but can a Huntsman's motivation change? Like, could one become so obsessed with chasing a particular Changeling they might not want to not exist, because that would stop them from targeting their new arch-nemesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>i can think of one example of that,in the fairest write up,there this one example fairest. there this rumor that an huntsman feel in love with her and she changed his heart. i really hope the rumor is true,i'm one a hell of a hopless romantic fr those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:32:12-08:00","id":806067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806041#post806041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a major thing about Huntsmen is that unless you use a token you Cannot escape. You cannot stop them. If you kill them or strip them of their yearning, they just come back. The changelings are tied to the narrative of the escape, and the Huntsmen are the reoccurring villains that are the manifestation of those tropes.<br /> <br /> You can reason with, escape or kill a loyalist. You can reason with, escape, or kill a privateer. You cannot escape a Huntsman, not without helping to send someone to the fate your trying to escape or you dying yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of role of a Huntsman can just be played by a particularly determined loyalist, or group of loyalists. It's just a loyalist that can't be reasoned with, that's good at finding things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806049#post806049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huntsmen are better at finding Icons. With an Icon, a Huntsman always knows what direction the changeling lies, unless they're on a different side (IE: Hedge vs. mundane world). That makes them utterly fearsome hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics wise, they're slightly different. But role wise, they occupy a space that's very similar to a loyalist... albeit, a loyalist that's better at finding people, and are a bit more sturdy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":287,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","user":"Wildfire","date":". 01-11-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:01:49-08:00","id":806087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806053#post806053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you explain more deeply what are the spirits of hunting the huntsman are born of,i'm wondering what are their natural state in arcadia,oh,before i forget,do you think you can show us the new true fae soon? sorry if i'm being greedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only work as fast as I can work. Time I spend sharing drafts is time I'm not spending doing actual development and getting the book out the door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:05:38-08:00","id":806090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806087#post806087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can only work as fast as I can work. Time I spend sharing drafts is time I'm not spending doing actual development and getting the book out the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm so sorry,i honestly forgot about that,i won't do it again,really sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:39:57-08:00","id":806111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of role of a Huntsman can just be played by a particularly determined loyalist, or group of loyalists. It's just a loyalist that can't be reasoned with, that's good at finding things.<br /> <br /> Mechanics wise, they're slightly different. But role wise, they occupy a space that's very similar to a loyalist... albeit, a loyalist that's better at finding people, and are a bit more sturdy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would strongly disagree based on my previous gaming experience. Player characters are extremely good at tracking down opponents/potential threats/antagonists and killing them. It is what protagonists do in many stories that involve life and death struggle, but is especially true in role playing games. Even with the use of the Death Clause from the <i>Book of the Dead </i>(a one time trick, as an aside this is a great way to reveal to the PCs that such a thing exists is by having an antagonistic loyalist to use it as part of its great trap against them) the Huntsman is by definition of their ability to be reformed make infinitely better reoccurring villain than any loyalist, could against any sufficiently paranoid and competent changelings Player characters. Also loyalists have breaking points because they have human frailties and I have a feeling from write up huntsmen won't be subject to breaking points, making them much more terminator-like in comparison.<br /> <br /> Also talking about instilling paranoia, an inhuman unvanquishable shapeshifting supernaturally aware of your location hunter with a means to restrain you perfectly and that has the ability to give your friends a genuine guaranteed get-out-of-Arcadia free card if they betray you is vastly different than a cruel competent fellow changeling, who lacks the ability to make any 100% guarantee of the very thing your changeling friends longs for, is dead for sure after the second time you kill him, can be mentally broken, and while he could have shape shifting powers and maybe even the ability to know where you are with the right tricks is not anywhere as scary.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-11-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:55:37-08:00","id":806130,"title":"","content":"These guys remind me of Mr. Meeseeks from Rick &amp; Morty (which is good, it is a brilliant episode).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:56:29-08:00","id":806131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806111#post806111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would strongly disagree based on my previous gaming experience. Player characters are extremely good at tracking down opponents/potential threats/antagonists and killing them. It is what protagonists do in many stories that involve life and death struggle, but is especially true in role playing games. Even with the use of the Death Clause from the <i>Book of the Dead </i>(a one time trick, as an aside this is a great way to reveal to the PCs that such a thing exists is by having an antagonistic loyalist to use it as part of its great trap against them) the Huntsman is by definition of their ability to be reformed make infinitely better reoccurring villain than any loyalist, could against any sufficiently paranoid and competent changelings Player characters. Also loyalists have breaking points because they have human frailties and I have a feeling from write up huntsmen won't be subject to breaking points, making them much more terminator-like in comparison.<br /> <br /> Also talking about instilling paranoia, an inhuman unvanquishable shapeshifting supernaturally aware of your location hunter with a means to restrain you perfectly and that has the ability to give your friends a genuine guaranteed get-out-of-Arcadia free card if they betray you is vastly different than a cruel competent fellow changeling, who lacks the ability to make any 100% guarantee of the very thing your changeling friends longs for, is dead for sure after the second time you kill him, can be mentally broken, and while he could have shape shifting powers and maybe even the ability to know where you are with the right tricks is not anywhere as scary.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively, they're not that much different form Loyalists. Except, this is just Agent Smith from The Matrix where he doesn't want to live in this world any more. A Loyalist is always going to track the player down if the ST wants it. A Huntsman is always going to track down the player if the ST wants it. Kill the Loyalist, or Kill the Huntsman? They just keep coming back if the ST wants it. It's just not terribly different than what already exists. They have slightly different abilities, but it's not that much different that what already exists. Yes, Icons exists now, and now you have to go into the hedge and grab them... over and over again, because a Huntsman might grab it. But, there's the thing. It so far exists as something just so Huntsmen can grab it and use their powers, but their powers are pretty much do-able in the current set of rules.<br /> <br /> I totally dig True Fae being put up a peg, and making them a lot harder to defeat. They just have to be replaced with something special, and I'm not sure this build of Huntsmen does a good job of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:26:09-08:00","id":806153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Huntsman is always going to track down the player if the ST wants it. Kill the Loyalist, or Kill the Huntsman? They just keep coming back if the ST wants it. It's just not terribly different than what already exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wildfire, you have my deepest sympathies. I, too have had really bad storytellers that ran every villain they threw at us as an unstoppable juggernauts devoid of any humanizing weaknesses. I know what that feels like and I want to let you know that isn't actually how the game should be run. See game mechanics and defining how things work in a setting builds a consistent frame work for a story that is more than just the pre- magna carta serfdom under a tyrannical Storyteller. See role playing isn't just a game of imaginative pretend and storytelling we play with our friends, but it has rules and mechanics which define which characters should be able to do. Just because storytellers you've been exposed to feel free to play changeling antagonists like a preternatural terminator doesn't mean that's what loyalists actually are. Loyalists are fundamentally human characters, with human weaknesses and should if they are portrayed correctly as the fully fleshed out characters they deserve to be, will have these weaknesses put on display, for a variety of reason ranging from making them sympathetic to make them even more contemptible for their pettiness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-11-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:26:33-08:00","id":806209,"title":"","content":"a important difference between huntsmen and loyalist,is that huntsmen are <b><i><u>Inevitable. </u></i></b> They <i><b>will</b></i> find you,there's no maybe with the huntsman,all changelings will face a huntsmen sooner or later,the huntsman nature ensures they never ever give up,they're not human after all,they're not even alive.<br /> A Loyalist is different,you can bargain with a loyalist,you can kill them,they can change theuir ways. theyre redeemable,changeling can reach out to them.<br /> thats is a big narrative difference for em at least.<br /> Loyalists are people<br /> Huntsmen are monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:29:36-08:00","id":806212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805835#post805835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to share? I am very curious, now, about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't finished yet, but when it is I will definitely post it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805839#post805839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bolded statement is supposition on Things's part and is not present in the writeup.<br /> <br /> Being individual spirits of the hunt drawn from a place that runs on emotional resonance goes a long way toward having a basic understanding of hunting and tactics. You don't need to know what a building is made of to know that it is, conceptually, shelter, nor do you need to know what an accountant does to recognize that it's imprudent to shank one in full view of a score or three of mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess? Maybe I'm just not grasping exactly what they <i>do</i> know before their first kill and, what they need to know so badly that they learn from the kill. If they know enough to be capable of successfully hunting a human, why do they need to do so before they can hunt their actual quarry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:32:12-08:00","id":806215,"title":"","content":"As someone who, for better or worse, never played or ST'd CtL, but has read the Core and parts of the supplements, I like these guys. The problem I saw, from my admittedly inexperienced perspective, with using True-Fae-Outside-Of-Arcadia was that to keep them legendary threats you had to make them serious monsters and <i>if </i>a Changeling actually managed to kill her Keeper in &quot;meat space&quot; then... that was it! <i><b>You are free now!</b></i> Huntsmen give the possibility of an eternal chase while allowing even the average Changeling a serious chance at fighting back. At the same time, the Gentry are kept as ominous threats of immense power behind the curtain. After all, you only kill the Evil Queen at the very end of the tale, right?<br /> <br /> As for the Loyalist vs. Huntsmen discussion, I am with Pale_Crusader. Even the most deranged Loyalist is still partly human and does things out of human motivations, even if they are not admirable. That flows into how you (can) interact and deal with them, as well as the moral weight of killing one in cold blood. A Huntsmen is entirely a creature of tales and has the abilities to match their moniker.<br /> <br /> To be entirely honest, Huntsmen is one of the first things (except Talecrafting back in 1e) that really makes me want to play CtL.<br /> <br /> The only thing that turned me off slightly is the need to kill. It just seems a bit overly contrived and unnecessarily limiting. Sure, it fits a &quot;horror story monster&quot;, but I think I would prefer if the actions they have to do earn that essential epiphany were broadened a bit to include other &quot;enlightening&quot; acts that still attract attention (and therefore can warn an astute Changeling that a Huntsman is around).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:32:22-08:00","id":806216,"title":"","content":"The difference between loyalists and Huntsmen is where the alien factor comes in-these aren't humans turned fae after you, these are fae turned human after you, and that makes a subtle but telling difference.<br /> <br /> While both loyalists and Huntsmen play a sort of spy game, the Huntsmen plays from the outside, always, while a loyalist can get inside. Loyalists can be persuaded and changed, but Huntsman can't. A Huntsman can't pretend to be a courtier the way a loyalist can. On the other hand, the loyalist can't offer miracles the way a Huntsman does. And so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> But the biggest difference is <i>intimacy</i>, deranged closeness to you. Thanks to the summoning ritual of the Huntsmen(which you'll see later), Huntsmen are bound to one changeling-they can grab multiple, but rather like fetches, their have particular power over one changeling-but more importantly, they have <i>connection</i> to one changeling over others. Switching over to a more IC presentation, they are made <i>for you</i>. If a Huntsman prefers winning by seduction, then that Huntsman is sure to be alluring to <i>you</i>, carrying the touches of everyone you've ever found attractive.<br /> <br /> They've got you on their mind, and if they understand anyone in particular, it is <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> If a fetch is a You Minus, the Huntsmen is a Anti-You, or a You Plus*.<br /> <br /> And that's something no loyalist can pull off so neatly. Keep in mind, this is a game of psychological horror.<br /> <br /> *Though I tend to reserve You Pluses for the True Fae.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A few things that I like about &quot;kill for mortal form&quot;:<br /> <br /> 1) It adds stakes. If you only temporarily banish the Huntsmen, that's another corpse because of you. If it keeps up, how many people will die because of your failures? Maybe you should turn yourself to them, to stop the killing. Maybe that matters to you. Maybe it doesn't, since that means staying here, safe. Maybe you should worry about that.<br /> <br /> 2)Call me a sucker for &quot;face of the victims&quot; type antagonists, you'd be right. Gives variety and flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-11-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:46:16-08:00","id":806230,"title":"","content":"I think the True Fae are by far the entirety of the &quot;inhuman antagonist that can't be truly killed&quot; material I need for my Chronicles. Too much of that and it slides straight into failure-induced apathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:55:11-08:00","id":806236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806230#post806230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the True Fae are by far the entirety of the &quot;inhuman antagonist that can't be truly killed&quot; material I need for my Chronicles. Too much of that and it slides straight into failure-induced apathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>tthink of it that way,if a true fae almost never leave his realm and he only have been using the huntsmen to gather changelings for as long as anyone remembers. well,that means that in the rare occasion where the True Fae decides to show up in the flesh,it is a <i>big </i>event.<br /> It means that either the Other wants to make absolutely sure you'll be brough back and pay for you mistakes,or it means that they hate youe nough to want to look at your face as they drag you to slavery. it makes them scarier.<br /> they arent really the same kind of antagonist thematically or narratively,the huntsmen are fae soldiers,the gentry are fae gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 01-11-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:56:52-08:00","id":806239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806212#post806212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess? Maybe I'm just not grasping exactly what they <i>do</i> know before their first kill and, what they need to know so badly that they learn from the kill. If they know enough to be capable of successfully hunting a human, why do they need to do so before they can hunt their actual quarry?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Huntsmen understand the basic story pattern of pursue objective - circumvent obstacle - achieve goal, but the Lost wrap themselves in stories that for the most part rely on grounding in a material understanding of reality \u2014 the baseline is a fairly animalistic packet of skills, and going after something that hides in mortal society requires the common knowledge of mortal society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:58:31-08:00","id":806241,"title":"","content":"I don't consider that &quot;it makes this omnipotent being that can't be truly killed scarier&quot; is a valid argument. At some point you push it too far into that direction and end up with the &quot;million is a statistic&quot; syndrome, where you can't establish an emotional connection or elicit an emotional response to something because you literally can't comprehend its magnitude. Making the True Fae scarier and scarier at some point <i>stops being scary</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, the True Fae show up in the material realm all the time, <i>that's how they take people in the first place</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:58:33-08:00","id":806242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806216#post806216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) It adds stakes. If you only temporarily banish the Huntsmen, that's another corpse because of you. If it keeps up, how many people will die because of your failures? Maybe you should turn yourself to them, to stop the killing. Maybe that matters to you. Maybe it doesn't, since that means staying here, safe. Maybe you should worry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hnnnnngggg... you tempt me, sir. You tempt me.<br /> <br /> Still, the downside I imagine is all these Changelings running through law enforcement or having their Ensorceled there. It gives this weird motivation for every Changeling to either have feelers in law enforcement or knowing someone who does. Every murder could be by a Huntsman! On the other hand, making it more general means a Changeling has to watch for <i>any </i>suspicious crimes or events, which leads to awesome weird paranoia. Perhaps the weird action needed to acclimatise could even be tailored to the Huntsman in question, which really fires on the guessing game, but also gives an initial data point to start research from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:59:38-08:00","id":806243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806230#post806230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the True Fae are by far the entirety of the &quot;inhuman antagonist that can't be truly killed&quot; material I need for my Chronicles. Too much of that and it slides straight into failure-induced apathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The comparison rings false.<br /> <br /> That's like comparing a rock pillar to an ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:02:40-08:00","id":806249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that turned me off slightly is the need to kill. It just seems a bit overly contrived and unnecessarily limiting. Sure, it fits a &quot;horror story monster&quot;, but I think I would prefer if the actions they have to do earn that essential epiphany were broadened a bit to include other &quot;enlightening&quot; acts that still attract attention (and therefore can warn an astute Changeling that a Huntsman is around).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you are coming from because that bit does seem a little tacked on as an after thought, like a homage towards the actual Terminator movie.<br /> <br /> It does help alienates the Huntsmen, reduces the sympathy of their position of being a play thing created for a task against their own will by making them callously kill an innocent without exception. That removes moral grayness and makes them clearly monsters. I can see why that would be desirable for some types of stories, but detrimental to other types. Alien and monstrous go well together and that is obviously what the designers are going for. Also the murder of a bystander plays a role in alerting the quarry that the hunt has started like birds flushed from a bush in the woods the local changelings would start reading obituaries and police reports with paranoid fervor. By forcing the eyes of the Changelings upon the mortal world it draws them into all types of investigative stories that are not necessarily Huntsmen or even fae related.<br /> <br /> Also by having a bunch of Lost investigating deaths in their area it reinforces the need of supernatural conspiracies to keep themselves hidden or perhaps draw the attention of some self-righteous changelings with violence and emotional trauma issues in their past. (why wouldn't some changelings hunt what they deem to be monsters?) Then again I am biased because in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\">chronicles</a> no body likes monstrous characters for good reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-11-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:03:21-08:00","id":806250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806242#post806242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hnnnnngggg... you tempt me, sir. You tempt me.<br /> <br /> Still, the downside I imagine is all these Changelings running through law enforcement or having their Ensorceled there. It gives this weird motivation for every Changeling to either have feelers in law enforcement or knowing someone who does. Every murder could be by a Huntsman! On the other hand, making it more general means a Changeling has to watch for <i>any </i>suspicious crimes or events, which leads to awesome weird paranoia. Perhaps the weird action needed to acclimatise could even be tailored to the Huntsman in question, which really fires on the guessing game, but also gives an initial data point to start research from.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're getting it! Certainly freeholds are always going to have some people with ears in the police station.<br /> <br /> To be fair, most everyone does, but yeah. They already keep their feelers out for missing people and strange incidents, what's a murder or two?<br /> <br /> And, for those who like crossover, this gives changelings some reason to poke into other folks business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:16:01-08:00","id":806255,"title":"","content":"I remember somewhere that Terminator was referenced in one of the books as a good horror movie for an implacable hunter. I guess shapeshifting makes Huntsmen the T-1000.<br /> <br /> I think I missed something: What constitutes a changeling's Icon? Is it something given to the Huntsman on creation, or is it something like a personal belonging, chosen symbol, or something they need to track down or discover before they start hunting the changeling? I can certainly imagine cutaway scenes where the Huntsman barges into a changeling's apartment, finding that he's evacuated, and searches the bare rooms to find the tiniest thing that has the changeling's 'scent' on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:20:02-08:00","id":806257,"title":"","content":"Keep your eyes open for Huntsmen Part 2!<br /> <br /> That's not a joke, this is half of the section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:25:58-08:00","id":806263,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of knowing every time you send your Huntsman back to Arcadia you get a week's reprieve at the cost of another human life. But something about it isn't jiving with the rest of the Huntsman's story for me, and I can't quite put my finger on why...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-11-2016, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:27:46-08:00","id":806265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806255#post806255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I missed something: What constitutes a changeling's Icon? Is it something given to the Huntsman on creation, or is it something like a personal belonging, chosen symbol, or something they need to track down or discover before they start hunting the changeling? I can certainly imagine cutaway scenes where the Huntsman barges into a changeling's apartment, finding that he's evacuated, and searches the bare rooms to find the tiniest thing that has the changeling's 'scent' on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you notice how all of the Seeming writeups include imagery of the Changeling leaving her heart behind? That's their icon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:28:04-08:00","id":806267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806263#post806263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of knowing every time you send your Huntsman back to Arcadia you know you'll get a week's reprieve at the cost of another human life. But something about it isn't jiving with the rest of the Huntsman's story for me, and I can't quite put my finger on why...</div> </div> </div> </div>maybe y'ou like them more when we see more of the arcadian weapons and example chracters :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:29:12-08:00","id":806270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806267#post806267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe y'ou like them more when we see more of the arcadian weapons and example chracters :&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's entirely possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:40:12-08:00","id":806282,"title":"","content":"Two questions<br /> <br /> 1) What happens when the freehold monarchs institute a law that every member of the freehold must swear a pledge to them to not accept, take, or touch a Token of Reprieve?<br /> 2) What happens if someone with time magic teleports a Huntsmen into the far future - or traps them in a bubble where time travels extreemly slowly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:48:26-08:00","id":806289,"title":"","content":"Depends on the pledge. A Sealing's not that big of a deal if it's broken at the right time, and too many Oaths on a ruling party will probably crack them, but someone breaking a oath will be an oathbreaker, with all the penalties that come with it. Bargains aren't a thing a ruler could do.<br /> <br /> I don't see the former happening.<br /> <br /> As for the latter, depends on why it's being done. If the purpose is put them past when a changeling is alive, they pick up evidence of the corpse and take it back, I suppose. Otherwise, they just keep going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:52:43-08:00","id":806292,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining a freehold monarchy desperately trying to come up with plausible excuses why they won't institute such an anti-Reprieve pledge for <i>all</i> members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:52:58-08:00","id":806294,"title":"","content":"I read the title, and immediately started hearing TF2 music in my head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, this looks good. Can't wait to see more!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:16:55-08:00","id":806314,"title":"","content":"Now Charlaquin's got me wondering if a particularly clever (and likely unscrupulous) changeling could bargain for their Icon.<br /> <br /> I'm feeling excited and creative, now.<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking about alternative origins for the Huntsmen that could still follow similar mechanics in actual play:<br /> <br /> The Hunter: &quot;Ha, ha! Your favorite toy escaped!&quot;<br /> The Keeper: &quot;I'm rather proud of that actually. He's quite a clever boy. Or girl. I forget which is which.&quot;<br /> The Hunter: &quot;Oh? I bet you a jar of Fly's Honey I could catch him!&quot;<br /> The Keeper: &quot;I accept your wager, but only if you abide by The Wild Hunt Article IX, page vermilion, paragraph banana.&quot;<br /> The Hunter: &quot;In Huntsman form and restrictions? It'll only take me a week! You're on!&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile:<br /> <br /> Bob (marked): &quot;Suddenly, I have a bad feeling about this.&quot;<br /> <br /> One week later:<br /> <br /> The Hunter: &quot;Oh, my hooves and whiskers, I forgot how dull and miserable this mortal world is! I can't take it anymore! But I can't go back empty-handed! They'll laugh at me! And take my precious Fly Honey!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:19:00-08:00","id":806317,"title":"","content":"Another couple of questions.<br /> <br /> Are gaining additional approaches purely a disadvantage because they give the Huntsman more opportunities to regain Yearning or is there something I missed?<br /> <br /> Is there any reason why a purely rational Huntsman (obviously nothing fae is ever purely rational) would plan from the start to acquire more yearning before going for the Changeling rather than trying to finish the job with just it's starting 6 points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-11-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:21:47-08:00","id":806319,"title":"","content":"For a Huntsman, stuff like Personal and Entitlement Approaches need to be fulfilled first <i>before</i> they can take someone-I think, I need to reread the section.<br /> <br /> For a True Fae, every Approach becomes another Ban. Would you personally want to go after someone who's a walking landmine/labyrinth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:27:26-08:00","id":806323,"title":"","content":"I did a quick ctrl-f for Personal and Entitlement but found nothing - perhaps one of the sections that's not in the public doc.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd hack that so they always need to fulfill Personal Approach + either Entitlement or Court. I mean, I think my original question still stands, just with the caveat for a Changeling who only has Court Approaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-11-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:30:06-08:00","id":806325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806319#post806319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Huntsman, stuff like Personal and Entitlement Approaches need to be fulfilled first <i>before</i> they can take someone-I think, I need to reread the section.<br /> <br /> For a True Fae, every Approach becomes another Ban. Would you personally want to go after someone who's a walking landmine/labyrinth?</div> </div> </div> </div>thats why when a freehold bulwarks breaks,the true fae would have special interest on the freehold changelings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:31:29-08:00","id":806327,"title":"","content":"Which is why you join an Entitlement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:34:05-08:00","id":806328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806327#post806327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why you join an Entitlement.</div> </div> </div> </div>to me,all that makes the true fae scarier in a way. since now,going after you is like going through a maze made of razors naked except for a blindfold,it means that if one Them is after you despite everything,it means they <i>really </i>wants your ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:36:25-08:00","id":806330,"title":"","content":"Is joining an Entitlement something you do lightly for the benefits? I'd hope not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm hoping that Court Approaches provide actual protection and not just a source of fuel for Huntsmen. Hopfully that section comes out soon and clears things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:38:42-08:00","id":806334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806323#post806323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a quick ctrl-f for Personal and Entitlement but found nothing - perhaps one of the sections that's not in the public doc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reference <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17na4zNJlzOh0D9Qv9pLEcnzXwSnQ8EeZGSpE486BKsc/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">the Court Creation preview</a>:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Personal Approaches</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Approaches are not exclusive to courts. As a character grows and establishes her own personal Story, she gains personal Approaches that further narrow narrowing the possible Approaches a Huntsman can take against her. <u>Huntsmen must abide by her personal Approaches to gain a point of Yearning before they can take advantage of court Approaches.</u> Personal Approaches form as a character increases in mantle, takes a formal title within the freehold or court, or joins an entitlement.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:43:53-08:00","id":806341,"title":"","content":"What I suspect: If they just ran up and grabbed their quarry, brute forcing through all the obstacles in pragmatic fashion with negligible chance of failure, it would be the narrative of a milk run, not a <i>sporting hunt</i>. They may not realize they're physically capable of bypassing the challenge.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of it as kind of like the difference between a person who plays Metroid &quot;properly&quot; as the developers intended, versus the speed runners who know how to wall climb, glitch through floors, or kill bosses before they go through all their transformations and attack patterns. The Huntsmen don't &quot;get&quot; sequence breaking. The Court Approaches exist to exploit that mindset by providing a sequence they're 'supposed' to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:44:24-08:00","id":806342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806330#post806330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is joining an Entitlement something you do lightly for the benefits? I'd hope not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm hoping that Court Approaches provide actual protection and not just a source of fuel for Huntsmen. Hopfully that section comes out soon and clears things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Do you really think anyone would make the Entitlements something done lightly? Give the writers some credit.<br /> <br /> 2)I don't think you understand how traps work. There are two parts to a trap-the bait and the actual trap.<br /> <br /> Court approaches are bait. Smart courtiers know how to turn them into a trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:51:07-08:00","id":806348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806334#post806334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reference <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17na4zNJlzOh0D9Qv9pLEcnzXwSnQ8EeZGSpE486BKsc/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">the Court Creation preview</a>:</div> </div> </div> </div>But what happens if you don't have any personal approaches? That's what I'm asking. (I read &quot;increases in mantle&quot; as you get your first at 2 or 3 dots)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806342#post806342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)I don't think you understand how traps work. There are two parts to a trap-the bait and the actual trap.<br /> <br /> Court approaches are bait. Smart courtiers know how to turn them into a trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that I don't see why a rational Huntsman would be interested in this bait. It's a lot of work for little Yearning.<br /> <br /> (I know the answer is because they're Arcadian and thus not rational. But I like it when mechanics reward you for roleplaying appropriately rather than expect you to make mechanically un-optimal decisions)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-11-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:54:06-08:00","id":806354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806342#post806342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Do you really think anyone would make the Entitlements something done lightly? Give the writers some credit.<br /> <br /> 2)I don't think you understand how traps work. There are two parts to a trap-the bait and the actual trap.<br /> <br /> Court approaches are bait. Smart courtiers know how to turn them into a trap.</div> </div> </div> </div> theres the copper court in the iron hold freehold that was being used as an example of court creation,one of the approaches is being hurt by something that they created,because their court emotion is regret. If i were one of copper cortiers i'd invest on contracts that made me tougher until i could myself bulletproof,i'd then create a new kind of gun and sell it in stores and advertise the shit of it,eventually a huntsman would hear about it and they'd have to buy one to shoot me with it if he wanted yearning,but since my skin is too hard the bullets would not hurt and i'd know who the huntsman is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:55:58-08:00","id":806359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806348#post806348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what happens if you don't have any personal approaches?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you get good at the things your Court is good at, because Court Approaches apply to courtiers and interface with the Court's strong points.<br /> <br /> You get a Personal Approach at four dots of Mantle, not earlier. &quot;Takes a formal title within the freehold or court&quot; would seem to be the easiest point of acquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:05:36-08:00","id":806370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806348#post806348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more that I don't see why a rational Huntsman would be interested in this bait. It's a lot of work for little Yearning.<br /> <br /> (I know the answer is because they're Arcadian and thus not rational. But I like it when mechanics reward you for roleplaying appropriately rather than expect you to make mechanically un-optimal decisions)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Yearning powers most of their abilities, and when out of Yearning, they die horrifically, and wake up some time later, remembering that, and <i>still </i>have to run your ass down before they can go home.<br /> <br /> Also I think you're confusing the purpose of a Storyteller's roleplaying with a player's purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:09:21-08:00","id":806378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806354#post806354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">theres the copper court in the iron hold freehold that was being used as an example of court creation,one of the approaches is being hurt by something that they created,because their court emotion is regret. If i were one of copper cortiers i'd invest on contracts that made me tougher until i could myself bulletproof,i'd then create a new kind of gun and sell it in stores and advertise the shit of it,eventually a huntsman would hear about it and they'd have to buy one to shoot me with it if he wanted yearning,but since my skin is too hard the bullets would not hurt and i'd know who the huntsman is.</div> </div> </div> </div>There ya go.<br /> <br /> Unless they start conscripting others. It's not like Huntsmen are stupid, either-they can use loyalists to test theories, humans to spy, hobgoblins to hinder.<br /> <br /> No, the Huntsmen know the game they're playing too, and most aren't so stupid as to wander into it blindly.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd be worried for said Copper Courtier. Nevermind how the Wyrd would respond-it's a terrible thing, to make yourself bulletproof.<br /> <br /> A metaphor, but in the world of the fae, that means a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:14:13-08:00","id":806388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806292#post806292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm imagining a freehold monarchy desperately trying to come up with plausible excuses why they won't institute such an anti-Reprieve pledge for <i>all</i> members.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am excited about seeing the new Pledge mechanics and limitations, that'll help answer questions like this. If pledges are as freeform and hold to the limitations roughly seen in 1e then I have a hard time seeing a plausible excuse about having changelings swearing to obey the Freehold laws and having one of those laws to be not offering aid to Huntsmen for Reprieved Tokens.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a side note: The other strategy of collecting reprieve tokens fits perfectly to make an economy for groups of Privateers, such as my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=804036#post804036\">court examples</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:15:33-08:00","id":806395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806370#post806370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Yearning powers most of their abilities, and when out of Yearning, they die horrifically, and wake up some time later, remembering that, and <i>still </i>have to run your ass down before they can go home.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you spend even a single point of Yearning in order to fufil that approach then you've at most broken even.<br /> <br /> That's the crux of my issue. I think Approaches simply don't give Huntsmen enough benefit to be worthwhile. I'll probably post a quick hack soon to show what I think would work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806370#post806370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I think you're confusing the purpose of a Storyteller's roleplaying with a player's purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Huntsmen games are going to happen; plus mechanics that encourage proper roleplaying never hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:15:56-08:00","id":806397,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that the necessity of Huntsmen to kill every time they come back seems a tad restrictive, and possibly repetitive. Sure, it can make a changeling ask themselves whether the world would be safer if they went back to Arcadia, and it can serve as a sign of a Huntsman's return. But why can't these same plot points be created without resorting to murder? Who's to say they can't have other odd behaviors generated by a clashing of the elements that animate them? Isn't it more paranoia-inducing if they <i>don't </i>have this universal necessity?<br /> <br /> Also, I'd be glad if there were a few suggestions for how to permanently kill a Huntsman, no matter how dangerous and unpleasant. It sounds like something most players would eventually want to be capable of doing. I think it would be in-character for an Autumn courtier who knows about Fetch Merging and what animates Huntsmen to research a method of Huntsman Merging (probably impossible, I know). This might even lead said courtier into the presence of the Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:27:32-08:00","id":806409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806395#post806395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you spend even a single point of Yearning in order to fufil that approach then you've at most broken even.<br /> <br /> That's the crux of my issue. I think Approaches simply don't give Huntsmen enough benefit to be worthwhile. I'll probably post a quick hack soon to show what I think would work.<br /> <br /> I think Huntsmen games are going to happen; plus mechanics that encourage proper roleplaying never hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Be clever. Not much to ask from the fae. If you need to spend yearning to make an Approach happen, you're probably just not being clever enough.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm sticking to that.<br /> <br /> 2)Oh, they will-if I ever get a say, there'll be a write up in a future book for making the Huntsmen playable chracters. But right now, the concern is for the Huntsmen as NPC antagonists, so it's built for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:29:35-08:00","id":806411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806397#post806397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd be glad if there were a few suggestions for how to permanently kill a Huntsman, no matter how dangerous and unpleasant. It sounds like something most players would eventually want to be capable of doing. I think it would be in-character for an Autumn courtier who knows about Fetch Merging and what animates Huntsmen to research a method of Huntsman Merging (probably impossible, I know). This might even lead said courtier into the presence of the Gentry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll tell you this:<br /> <br /> Every Huntsmen carries their doom with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:31:16-08:00","id":806415,"title":"","content":"Arcane, its just wonderful to know that you are working on this game and are so psyched for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:31:46-08:00","id":806417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806388#post806388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am excited about seeing the new Pledge mechanics and limitations, that'll help answer questions like this. If pledges are as freeform and hold to the limitations roughly seen in 1e then I have a hard time seeing a plausible excuse about having changelings swearing to obey the Freehold laws and having one of those laws to be not offering aid to Huntsmen for Reprieved Tokens</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, nothing that easy. Rulers could implement that with Oaths, but that's creating a load-bearing boss and then begging it to break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:36:47-08:00","id":806422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806409#post806409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Be clever. Not much to ask from the fae. If you need to spend yearning to make an Approach happen, you're probably just not being clever enough.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you don't need to spend Yearning to make your plans come to fruition, why do you need to put your plans to capture the Changeling on hold until you acquire more Yearning?<br /> <br /> The hack is almost done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806417#post806417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alas, nothing that easy. Rulers could implement that with Oaths, but that's creating a load-bearing boss and then begging it to break.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a pyramid system?<br /> <br /> The ruler makes two changeling's swear to never aid a Huntsman.<br /> The ruler makes those same to changeling swear to witness oaths for two more changeling.<br /> <br /> That's four Oaths from a freehold monarch, I'm going to guess that's not too many. And it has a nice feudal feel to it. <hr /><br /> Here's my little hack.<br /> <br /> <b>Yearning Costs</b><br /> <br /> A Huntsman's powers each have a base Yearning Cost. This cost increases by 1 Wyrd 3, 6 &amp; 9. The cost also increases by 1 at Mantle 3 and 5. The changeling may combine the bonus from Mantle and Wyrd, but only up to an increase of +3.<br /> <br /> <b>Approaches</b><br /> <br /> A Huntsman must fulfil one Personal Approach before they may attempt to capture a Changeling. If the Changeling has no personal Approach they may substitute any other Approach.<br /> <br /> Every Approach the Huntsman fulfils other than the one which permits capturing the Changeling reduces the cost of all the Huntsman's powers by 1 Yearning until they next return to Arcadia. This may not reduce the cost below (base cost \u2013 1) or below zero. A huntsman may gain this benefit before they've earned the right to capture their prey.<br /> <br /> If the Freehold Bulwark is broken, or if their Changeling prey is Courtless, the Huntsman essentially fulfils a Court Approach for free the moment they arrive on Earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Regaining Yearning</b><br /> <br /> A Huntsman may regain Yearning by trading a Token of Reprieve for Glamour. A Changeling may give up half their Wyrd (round up) Glamour which turns into Yearning at a 1 for 1 ratio. This means that a Changeling requires Wyrd 3 before a Huntsman may make a profit. A Huntsman may not ask for both Yearning and material aid from the same Token, it's one or the other.<br /> <br /> Some goblin merchants can distil merchandise connected to Changeling and create Yearning. However they can only provide Huntsmen with yearning from their personal prey. If a Changeling has sold to the market a Huntsman may acquire a single point of Yearning, for a price of course. If they are truly desperate they may provide an Icon to be distilled into a point of Yearning, plus processing fees. The Lost warn each other that items sold to the Market can lead Huntsmen to their door, not all believe the rumours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-11-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:44:28-08:00","id":806432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806250#post806250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're getting it! Certainly freeholds are always going to have some people with ears in the police station.<br /> <br /> To be fair, most everyone does, but yeah. They already keep their feelers out for missing people and strange incidents, what's a murder or two?<br /> <br /> And, for those who like crossover, this gives changelings some reason to poke into other folks business.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that is fine, but I find it is a bit overdone and there would be more to gain from broadening it because that would increase the number of institutions Changelings might be interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:46:02-08:00","id":806433,"title":"","content":"Shifted the goal posts from &quot;spending Yearning to get Yearning&quot; to &quot;Spending Yearning to capture Changelings&quot;. Please pick a topic and stay there.<br /> <br /> Plus, you've forgotten that the fae prefer stacking the deck.<br /> <br /> So, as a nutshell-clever Approaches to get Yearning, Yearning to get Changeling. Stack the deck in your favor, play the smart game, and freedom is yours quick enough.<br /> <br /> As for your hack-Jesus Christ and Mohammed on a pogostick, maybe you people should <i>actually freaking wait </i>for the actual book before you go &quot;Oh no, need to change things!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:47:07-08:00","id":806435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806432#post806432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, that is fine, but I find it is a bit overdone and there would be more to gain from broadening it because that would increase the number of institutions Changelings might be interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. It'll be something I keep in mind as development chatter for other books go on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-11-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:49:19-08:00","id":806439,"title":"","content":"It's not infeasible for the Oaths to pyramid down. It can be tedious and time consuming, but that might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:52:21-08:00","id":806442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806433#post806433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifted the goal posts from &quot;spending Yearning to get Yearning&quot; to &quot;Spending Yearning to capture Changelings&quot;. Please pick a topic and stay there.</div> </div> </div> </div>No goalpost were shifted. The goal has always been for filling Approaches to be an optimal strategy for a hypothetical Huntsman's player.<br /> <br /> You said, a clever Huntsman doesn't need to spend yearning to fufill an approach.<br /> <br /> To which I replied (essentially); if Huntsmen can accomplish so much without spending yearning, why aren't the initial six points enough to complete the hunt. Because if they are, the optimal strategy is to go straight for the capture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806439#post806439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not infeasible for the Oaths to pyramid down. It can be tedious and time consuming, but that might work.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's a little tedium among Changeling's when it comes to security? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-11-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:30:11-08:00","id":806470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a little tedium among Changeling's when it comes to security? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Two variables we need to know to answer these questions. 1st. How do Pledges work in 2e? That way we can have an idea how they are applicable to this situation of court law enforcement. 2nd. What are the sample demographics if there are indeed workload requirements that need distributed? That way we can calculate optimal ratio of the fealty tree pyramid.<br /> <br /> Also I agree that (with the exception the freehold is a bunch of privateers) there should very substantial efforts taken for there to be some type of enforcement against Reprieves being legal under Freehold laws unless there is some universal exemption done by the Wyrd itself making forbidding them by oaths impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-11-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:50:01-08:00","id":806487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806442#post806442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To which I replied (essentially); if Huntsmen can accomplish so much without spending yearning, why aren't the initial six points enough to complete the hunt. Because if they are, the optimal strategy is to go straight for the capture.</div> </div> </div> </div>At minimum, a Huntsman will likely need to spend two to three of its five viably-available points of Yearning on Mark of the Hunt, Ties Which Bind, and Tokens of Reprieve to get close enough for those two to make a difference; Disguise is liable to be a practical necessity for getting near enough to use Ties, and if anything happens to necessitate Healing or an inconvenient sunrise happens en route to Arcadia then it's back to square one.<br /> <br /> Being clever enough to sabotage a changeling's life doesn't obviate those expenditures, but it sure will give the Huntsman a little more rope to hang their quarry with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:58:48-08:00","id":806491,"title":"","content":"I could see Oaths being a way to discourage members of a Freehold from soliciting Tokens of Reprieve, and I don't see the pyramid scheme as being strictly necessary to enact such Oaths. Just depends on how paranoid the leaders of the Freehold are. But either way, it would be far from foolproof - I get the sense that if a character is willing to betray another member of her Freehold in order to get a Token of Reprieve, she would probably also be willing to accept the consequences of being an Oathbreaker. Or at least, that's how most Changelings are going to see it, and that's all that really matters.<br /> <br /> The power of Tokens of Reprieve seems to me to lie in their use as a weapon of psychological warfare. It doesn't really matter if no one in the Freehold is actually willing to break their Oaths to get one, the mere possibility that someone might is enough to make each and every member have to ask themselves &quot;do I trust that an Oath is going to be enough to stop you from betraying me if it means you'll get a free pass the next time the Huntsmen come for you?&quot; about each and every other member. That level of mistrust within a group gives the Huntsmen tremendous power over them, even if none of them would actually take the Token.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-11-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:10:16-08:00","id":806503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806411#post806411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll tell you this:<br /> <br /> Every Huntsmen carries their doom with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that's why the Arcadian Weapons section is ommited. (^w^)<br /> <br /> I suspected something else was up with those from the numerous hints on the matter (in passing and the shared text) and how unendingly relentless their threat seems at a first glance. The note their own weapons cause the Huntsmen aggravated damage helped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:29:10-08:00","id":806519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806503#post806503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So that's why the Arcadian Weapons section is ommited. (^w^)<br /> <br /> I suspected something else was up with those from the numerous hints on the matter (in passing and the shared text) and how unendingly relentless their threat seems at a first glance. The note their own weapons cause the Huntsmen aggravated damage helped.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Huntsman Document Part 1 Healing Section</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcadian weapons and iron weapons cause aggravated damage to Hunstmen. At any time, a Huntsman<br /> <br /> may reflexively spend one Yearning to heal all bashing and lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, added the quoted text with <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoXzJKNkVaSzlvMFU/view\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-11-2016, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:35:00-08:00","id":806522,"title":"","content":"Oh. Well. i thought I was being sneaky.<br /> <br /> Yeah, their Arcadian weapons do a number on changelings, but those weapons can flat out unmake the Huntsmen. Like, down to the spiritual level.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, no one lets them go easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:38:25-08:00","id":806526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806487#post806487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At minimum, a Huntsman will likely need to spend two to three of its five viably-available points of Yearning on Mark of the Hunt, Ties Which Bind, and Tokens of Reprieve to get close enough for those two to make a difference; Disguise is liable to be a practical necessity for getting near enough to use Ties, and if anything happens to necessitate Healing or an inconvenient sunrise happens en route to Arcadia then it's back to square one.<br /> <br /> Being clever enough to sabotage a changeling's life doesn't obviate those expenditures, but it sure will give the Huntsman a little more rope to hang their quarry with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Even if stacking the deck in their own favor wasn't an interest, the simple fact is is that five Yearning just isn't a very large budget to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:25:08-08:00","id":806555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806130#post806130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These guys remind me of Mr. Meeseeks from Rick &amp; Morty (which is good, it is a brilliant episode).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, that was my immediate thought too. Now I'm going to have to resist doing the Mr. Meeseeks voice if I ever get to run a Changeling game.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey I'm a Huntsman, look at me!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:26:17-08:00","id":806556,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Ties Which Bind. I've read that changelings in 2ED can spend glamour to escape from bindings and imprisonment as a template power. I assume this means that the bindings conjured by Huntsmen cannot be opened by any magic that a changeling might possess. But can changelings break them with sheer strength or a cutting tool? Would a Contract or other fae magic that grants a passive boost to Strength and/or Stamina be nullified? How about the Demolisher Merit? Also, can cold iron weapons dissolve these Ties like other fae protections? Can the powers of others splats break the Ties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-11-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:36:58-08:00","id":806559,"title":"","content":"First off, cold iron cuts anything fae, so that'll do it.<br /> <br /> Since I'm not seeing anything else, the default reading is nothing else works. Of course, logic says &quot;if it makes sense for it to work, roll it and challenge it against the Huntsman's Yearning+Wyrd&quot; or some such like that.<br /> <br /> Good question, we'll poke it with a stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:47:01-08:00","id":806565,"title":"","content":"First, awesome concept. Huntsmen are not what I'd thought they'd be, they're better. They also somehow manage to make the Immortal Assassin type of antagonist somewhat sympathetic (they're also victims of the Keepers as well, when you think about it-the difference is that's all they really can be, with even their victory only meaning a longer age before their next Durance) while still keeping them utterly terrifying, and in a way that I don't think Immortal Assassins have been before (charming masterminds rather than voiceless brutes).<br /> <br /> Second: I must add my voice to the &quot;why always murder?&quot; brigade. I get why it's there (to force the quarry to confront the fact that banishing the Huntsman is becoming complicit in serial murder), but that just seems...rather droll for what the Huntsmen are.<br /> <br /> I'd modify that into killing a victim, or driving them to a mental breakdown (Integrity 0) in nightmares and real-life gaslighting. That way, it keeps the horror of becoming incidentally complicit in a terrible crime as the Huntsman regains its bearings, but it also opens up a new set of stories, as well as increasing the paranoia of searching for Huntsman manifestation (people tend to hush up mental problems to begin with, and people go insane for reasons other than a psychotic fae mercenary rummaging around their psyches). One could even tie this into the &quot;Practicing skills for the Hunt&quot; theme, since Huntsmen psychologically torment the Lost by normal tactics; either they work on their physical skills or their cunning in preparation for their real target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:53:11-08:00","id":806569,"title":"","content":"i think ther need to kill is cool in a narrative and symbolic point of view,remember that all fae beings have act like they are part of a story. in this case it's Story of Hunting,and part of the narrative of a Hunt is the first Blood,the first time the predator destroys the pray,in a way A Story about a Hunt doesnt really begins until someone die.<br /> In the end,i think huntsmen should have to kill someone at the begginng of their journey because it's part of the Story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:59:07-08:00","id":806574,"title":"","content":"I don't really know how I feel about the huntsmen. Seems like it shifts the tone from &quot;Abuse Survivor&quot; to &quot;Abuse Sufferer.&quot; Seems like a fairly large change in tone, at least to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:05:28-08:00","id":806581,"title":"","content":"The whole of the game is going from Abuse Survivor to Trauma Survivor. Part of the psychological horror comes from the fear of going through trauma again, and the Huntsmen occupy that fear. But they are beatable-you don't have to put up with their shit. You can <i>win</i>.<br /> <br /> Or are you talking from the perspective of playing them? Because, yeah playing one of them would be tough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:07:13-08:00","id":806583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806574#post806574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really know how I feel about the huntsmen. Seems like it shifts the tone from &amp;quot;Abuse Survivor&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;Abuse Sufferer.&amp;quot; Seems like a fairly large change in tone, at least to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, assuming that the tone had shifted from abuse to trauma, I can say as someone who survived PTS that it all ways comes back. Huntsmen seem perfectly on point from that perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:12:22-08:00","id":806587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806583#post806583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, assuming that the tone had shifted from abuse to trauma, I can say as someone who survived PTS that it all ways comes back. Huntsmen seem perfectly on point from that perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>That gets a like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:19:55-08:00","id":806590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806397#post806397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I'd be glad if there were a few suggestions for how to permanently kill a Huntsman, no matter how dangerous and unpleasant. It sounds like something most players would eventually want to be capable of doing. I think it would be in-character for an Autumn courtier who knows about Fetch Merging and what animates Huntsmen to research a method of Huntsman Merging (probably impossible, I know). This might even lead said courtier into the presence of the Gentry.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Huntsman can die by a Huntsman's weapon. This is in some of the material not-yet-posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:35:40-08:00","id":806603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806581#post806581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole of the game is going from Abuse Survivor to Trauma Survivor. Part of the psychological horror comes from the fear of going through trauma again, and the Huntsmen occupy that fear. But they are beatable-you don't have to put up with their shit. You can <i>win</i>.<br /> <br /> Or are you talking from the perspective of playing them? Because, yeah playing one of them would be tough.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that they come back after two weeks like clockwork seems to diminish the whole paranoia aspect because then it's less about paranoia and more about the bi-monthly visit from your abusive Ex.<br /> <br /> As for being a Huntsmen, I don't know if you ever played Talos Principle before, but <a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=598831324\" target=\"_blank\">some of your peers have killed themselves because they keep finding themselves being torn apart by machines forever</a>. Which seems kind of like what the Huntsmen would go through, they're summoned up knowing that they're probably going to be (quite painfully) torn apart, repeatedly. Part of me wonders why they don't resent the True Fae more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:40:15-08:00","id":806610,"title":"","content":"I think the simplest way of dealing with the issues of yearning, time limits for a hunt, and approaches is for huntsmen to lose yearning over time.<br /> <br /> So say a huntsmen loses a point of yearning per week.<br /> <br /> For a huntsmen running low on yearning, using a Changeling's approaches might be very tempting, even the huntsmen's attempt fails to capture the Changeling, it might get them closer to success and at the very least they get a point of yearning to keep themselves from falling apart. <br /> <br /> As for huntsmen motivations, the key appears to be the tension between the huntsmen' s spirit/body which wants to be free and the True Fae's breath which is imbibed with the True Fae's passions and its the True Fae's breath that provides the huntsmen with its personality and other motivations.<br /> <br /> Example A True Fae is so romantically obsessed with an escaped Changeling that her breath infuses the Huntsmen with a personality inclined towards romantic obsession.<br /> <br /> The huntsmen still has the desire to be free of its humaniod form, but it has other drives and desires. Maybe this huntsmen falls in love with the Changeling, a love stronger then its desire to hunt, stronger then its desire to be free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:40:52-08:00","id":806611,"title":"","content":"Until you kill the bastard once and for all. Which can happen with Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> There's paranoia still, but once again, <i>you can win</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:51:54-08:00","id":806616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806611#post806611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until you kill the bastard once and for all. Which can happen with Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> There's paranoia still, but once again, <i>you can win</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until the True Fae just make another one to send at you. Speaking of which, what prevents a True Fae from sending a dozen at you other than being rude to the spirits?<br /> <br /> <br /> I think, though, that a fixed 2 week period is too long. Maybe something less clearly defined? If you put in two weeks then it becomes predictable and that destroys the paranoia element. Also I think two-weeks is too short for the king of threat huntsmen are supposed to be. If the dude is someone you slay on a monthly basis, then it kind of loses it's luster I'd think? After all, it's the same huntsmen, so they're going to fall into a routine and become predictable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I wonder, what happens if a Changeling captures and restrains one rather than kill it and let it poof away to fairy land again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:52:02-08:00","id":806617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806153#post806153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wildfire, you have my deepest sympathies. I, too have had really bad storytellers that ran every villain they threw at us as an unstoppable juggernauts devoid of any humanizing weaknesses. I know what that feels like and I want to let you know that isn't actually how the game should be run. See game mechanics and defining how things work in a setting builds a consistent frame work for a story that is more than just the pre- magna carta serfdom under a tyrannical Storyteller. See role playing isn't just a game of imaginative pretend and storytelling we play with our friends, but it has rules and mechanics which define which characters should be able to do. Just because storytellers you've been exposed to feel free to play changeling antagonists like a preternatural terminator doesn't mean that's what loyalists actually are. Loyalists are fundamentally human characters, with human weaknesses and should if they are portrayed correctly as the fully fleshed out characters they deserve to be, will have these weaknesses put on display, for a variety of reason ranging from making them sympathetic to make them even more contemptible for their pettiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to be shady Pale_Crusader.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen are creatures that will hunt down Changelings. There's already stuff in the game that can do that. If the storyteller already needs an unstoppable force to do it, there's already ways to accomplish that. The huntsman are just Agent Smith versions of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":287,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","user":"Wildfire","date":". 01-11-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:58:00-08:00","id":806621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806616#post806616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also I wonder, what happens if a Changeling captures and restrains one rather than kill it and let it poof away to fairy land again?</div> </div> </div> </div>The huntsman body is kept steady with yearning,and since they need to fulfill a changeling approach to gain yearning they'd dissapear if kept locked somewhere,and they'd be <i>so pissed. </i>the only way i can think of keeping an huntsmen out of arcadia indefinetly would be a major contract or spell to stop time around the huntsman and thus stop their bodies decaying,only a serious powerful being can do that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:59:40-08:00","id":806624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806616#post806616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until the True Fae just make another one to send at you. Speaking of which, what prevents a True Fae from sending a dozen at you other than being rude to the spirits?<br /> <br /> <br /> I think, though, that a fixed 2 week period is too long. Maybe something less clearly defined? If you put in two weeks then it becomes predictable and that destroys the paranoia element. Also I think two-weeks is too short for the king of threat huntsmen are supposed to be. If the dude is someone you slay on a monthly basis, then it kind of loses it's luster I'd think? After all, it's the same huntsmen, so they're going to fall into a routine and become predictable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I wonder, what happens if a Changeling captures and restrains one rather than kill it and let it poof away to fairy land again?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The summoning ritual requires an essential piece tied to you. Most True Fae have one, but damn if they lose it. No, killing a Huntsmen is a pretty good deterrent for the Huntsmen ever coming back again.<br /> <br /> 2) You assume a Huntsmen just comes right back and splats themselves against the same problems. Huntsmen are more likely to take their time and come up with clever ideas with each failure than charge on in-they may want to go back home, but they're viciously scheming creatures out to figure out a win rather than raging bulls trying to knock down a gate. The time gaps increase as more provisions are put into play, and each time a Huntsman turns up, the stakes are raised.<br /> <br /> Unless you have a shit storyteller, but again, you shouldn't play with shit people.<br /> <br /> 3) Good question. One to be answered at the table, I think.<br /> <br /> I mean, they don't just magically wiff away(unless I'm forgetting something, but I don't think I am), so you and your group has some options on what to do with a captured Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> They're about as slippery as changelings, though, so I wouldn't try holding them for too long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:08:10-08:00","id":806629,"title":"","content":"I kept thinking about the T-1000 while reading this.<br /> <br /> I like that they have to kill right away, but I'd like some indication of how often these guys come after Changelings. If these guys are a regular/frequent threat, this could lead to a massive bump to the unsolved (and unsolvable) homicide rate in any city with a large Freehold, which strains suspension of disbelief a bit. If they're less common, then it's not quite so unbelievable.<br /> <br /> When killed/discorporated outside of Arcadia, is the whole 2 weeks excruciating or just the initial explosion? If discorporated on the mortal plane, does the Arcadian material stay there, or does it return to Arcadia? If it stays in the mortal plane, what's to stop a Changeling from gathering it up and separating it so it can't reform?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:23:36-08:00","id":806643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806629#post806629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kept thinking about the T-1000 while reading this.<br /> <br /> I like that they have to kill right away, but I'd like some indication of how often these guys come after Changelings. If these guys are a regular/frequent threat, this could lead to a massive bump to the unsolved (and unsolvable) homicide rate in any city with a large Freehold, which strains suspension of disbelief a bit. If they're less common, then it's not quite so unbelievable.<br /> <br /> When killed/discorporated outside of Arcadia, is the whole 2 weeks excruciating or just the initial explosion? If discorporated on the mortal plane, does the Arcadian material stay there, or does it return to Arcadia? If it stays in the mortal plane, what's to stop a Changeling from gathering it up and separating it so it can't reform?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't make Huntsmen lightly, particularly since you have Loyaists and Fetches* in place for initial retreival. Even if those fail, if the changeling proves to be boring, there might not be a point in sending a Huntsman after them, at least immediately. If one of your favorite toys happens to be in town and you have the resources, you might make a hunting party, but that's incidental.<br /> <br /> The material discorporates, and reforms in the Hedge near Arcadia. The Huntsman suffers the entire time, far as I know.<br /> <br /> *Which, by the way, spells out a basic story outline for you, should you wish to use it. Fetches as an initial enemy(Wyrd 1-3), Huntsmen for when they prove to be desirable(Wyrd 4-7), and finally, the True Fae themselves needs to step in(Wyrd 8-10). That's nothing from the book, just a fun view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:45:40-08:00","id":806656,"title":"","content":"I think that they should only have to kill the first time they get sent after the changeling, if they die from yearning or non-permanent death they retain their knowledge of what's what until they finish their mission and return to their state of nothingness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:59:45-08:00","id":806665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806624#post806624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The summoning ritual requires an essential piece tied to you. Most True Fae have one, but damn if they lose it. No, killing a Huntsmen is a pretty good deterrent for the Huntsmen ever coming back again.<br /> <br /> 2) You assume a Huntsmen just comes right back and splats themselves against the same problems. Huntsmen are more likely to take their time and come up with clever ideas with each failure than charge on in-they may want to go back home, but they're viciously scheming creatures out to figure out a win rather than raging bulls trying to knock down a gate. The time gaps increase as more provisions are put into play, and each time a Huntsman turns up, the stakes are raised.<br /> <br /> Unless you have a shit storyteller, but again, you shouldn't play with shit people.<br /> <br /> 3) Good question. One to be answered at the table, I think.<br /> <br /> I mean, they don't just magically wiff away(unless I'm forgetting something, but I don't think I am), so you and your group has some options on what to do with a captured Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> They're about as slippery as changelings, though, so I wouldn't try holding them for too long.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So basically it's a title that they tie to an elemental that puts the Fae at less risk of themselves? Still I wonder though, for the particularly powerful of the True Fae, is it possible for them to send several at a single Changeling that they really really want?<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, the reason I assume this is because physical existence is <b>painful</b> for them, and they seemingly forget things in between deaths. So the quicker they go for it, the quicker the pain stops. That's the problem is that I don't think Huntsmen <b>can</b> be patient. At least, based on how they're described. I just don't think that having a static &quot;Two week like clock work&quot; really puts it into the right frame of reference. If they're supposed to exist to create an environment of paranoia then there needs to be juxtaposition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I assume Iron will hold them. So that begs a question, what can you do with a captive huntsmen? Can you repurpose them? Can you steal the essence of the True Fae that they imbibed into the Huntsmen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:44:24-08:00","id":806688,"title":"","content":"A captive Huntsman could easily just spend all of their Yearning and poof back to Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:50:42-08:00","id":806691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806665#post806665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically it's a title that they tie to an elemental that puts the Fae at less risk of themselves? Still I wonder though, for the particularly powerful of the True Fae, is it possible for them to send several at a single Changeling that they really really want?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to guess from the fact that Huntsmen have a primary target that being more powerful is not going to give one of the Fae any more or less of an escaped changeling than its marginally weaker brethren.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:53:48-08:00","id":806694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806616#post806616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also I wonder, what happens if a Changeling captures and restrains one rather than kill it and let it poof away to fairy land again?</div> </div> </div> </div>They poof. They have a limited time to accomplish their goal. At the end of that time, they fail. Doesn't matter where they are. They return from whence they came. The details are in other content I've not posted yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:54:48-08:00","id":806696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806665#post806665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I assume Iron will hold them. So that begs a question, what can you do with a captive huntsmen? Can you repurpose them? Can you steal the essence of the True Fae that they imbibed into the Huntsmen?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like supplement material if there ever was supplement material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:56:22-08:00","id":806697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806665#post806665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So basically it's a title that they tie to an elemental that puts the Fae at less risk of themselves? Still I wonder though, for the particularly powerful of the True Fae, is it possible for them to send several at a single Changeling that they really really want?<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, the reason I assume this is because physical existence is <b>painful</b> for them, and they seemingly forget things in between deaths. So the quicker they go for it, the quicker the pain stops. That's the problem is that I don't think Huntsmen <b>can</b> be patient. At least, based on how they're described. I just don't think that having a static &quot;Two week like clock work&quot; really puts it into the right frame of reference. If they're supposed to exist to create an environment of paranoia then there needs to be juxtaposition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I assume Iron will hold them. So that begs a question, what can you do with a captive huntsmen? Can you repurpose them? Can you steal the essence of the True Fae that they imbibed into the Huntsmen?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No, it's not a Title thing, it's a changeling thing. Give me a second....<br /> <br /> Here we are. Basically, the summoning ritual requires something, an item, that represents the changeling from their time in Arcadia. The Huntsman carries this item with it, it serves a major function for them, and when they are finally killed, that item is left for the changeling to reclaim.<br /> <br /> Unless it's worked into the background, most changelings don't <i>get</i> a lot of emblems(I'm calling them that until a proper name is introduced)-it's a safe assumption that there's only one or two as a convergence of sensibility and narrative.<br /> <br /> 2) Physical existence is <i>irritating</i>. In some ways, it's <i>frightening</i>. But it's <i>manageable</i>.<br /> <br /> Underneath mortal refuse and Arcadian sinew, though, there is a living story of the hunt, and Huntsmen, for all their dislike of the human world and flesh, are creatures who revel in the Hunt. These aren't Uratha, where the hunt is a primal, adrenaline filled action. It's lyricism, an artistry, a thrill of intellect and personality and precision. Even the brutal Wolf, who does kick down doors and ravage his targets before dragging them in a bleeding stupor back to Arcadia, prefers a certain slyness to his approach, a little convincing of pig and ingenue to let him and his big teeth in. This is not just a rush, this is not just ritual-this is <i>art, </i>this is the invisible being found by feeling it out. Even the most brutally done paintings have some measure of thought or feeling to it, if it's worth anything. For a Huntsmen, there is a satisfaction in doing the hunt <i>right</i>, and that often weighs as heavily on them as the desire to go home.<br /> <br /> 3) Like I said, I don't know. It's a question I would love to tackle in supplements, if the opportunity comes. But for now, it's best to say that's a question for the table. Cooler and stranger answers will come from there than us answering.<br /> <br /> But yeah, iron, cold iron, is master of all. The Huntsmen are reasonably chained under them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, there's a time limit? Well, that changes things.<br /> <br /> Anything I've said that can reasonably be assumed to be based on the Huntsmen having unlimited time? Scratch that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:09:02-08:00","id":806704,"title":"","content":"Oh, people were asking about iron I think? <br /> <br /> I made it a little more generous a definition. Because &quot;cold iron&quot; is a really subjective term, and would largely reflect things that aren't by any means practical tools or weapons. So, if it's iron enough that people think of it as iron, it's iron, and it counts. Cast iron, wrought iron, cold iron, dramatic irony, if it's iron, it's iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:15:57-08:00","id":806707,"title":"","content":"I think the section says something like 50% pure or what not if you want a hard line.<br /> <br /> But as Dave says, if it looks like iron, sounds like iron, and quacks like iron, it can beat a fairy to death. Or chain it. That's the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:26:40-08:00","id":806711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806704#post806704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, people were asking about iron I think?<br /> <br /> I made it a little more generous a definition. Because &quot;cold iron&quot; is a really subjective term, and would largely reflect things that aren't by any means practical tools or weapons. So, if it's iron enough that people think of it as iron, it's iron, and it counts. Cast iron, wrought iron, cold iron, dramatic irony, if it's iron, it's iron.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That should simply matters and end a few needless arguments.<br /> <br /> However, I'm now curious if Siderite, the &quot;perfected iron&quot; from Mage, will have any additional effects against Changelings or Fae. I doubt we'll find out until Signs of Sorcery, and maybe not even then,<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:30:21-08:00","id":806713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806711#post806711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That should simply matters and end a few needless arguments.<br /> <br /> However, I'm now curious if Siderite, the &quot;perfected iron&quot; from Mage, will have any additional effects against Changelings or Fae. I doubt we'll find out until Signs of Sorcery, and maybe not even then,<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's all on Mage and its' writers. Even David Brookshaw doesn't know what'll happen with that.<br /> <br /> As for this house, I'm fairly sure the policy is to just not worry about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:38:07-08:00","id":806719,"title":"","content":"Will the new Changeling corebook include a system for creating totally new Contracts and Pledges, or is that something we will not see until later?<br /> <br /> Edit: Is steel considered iron?<br /> <br /> In some settings like the Dresden Files, it has identical effects on the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:42:43-08:00","id":806721,"title":"","content":"Pledges, yes. Contracts, don't think so. In Game, how changelings do it. Equinox Road still serves you well. Out of game, actual mechanical advice, that'll be another thing to slip into a supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:43:29-08:00","id":806722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806719#post806719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Is steel considered iron?<br /> <br /> In some settings like the Dresden Files, it has identical effects on the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>%50 pure, is the hard line.<br /> <br /> With the better line being &quot;If it looks like iron, sounds like iron, and quacks like iron, it's iron&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-11-2016, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:52:56-08:00","id":806729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806722#post806722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">%50 pure, is the hard line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the purity thing is probably not a great metric, since purity is what separates iron from steel (with steel being <i>more</i> pure), and no matter how much the book stresses that it's about purity of concept, not purity of minerals, people will always get stuck on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:55:23-08:00","id":806732,"title":"","content":"True. Let me go edit that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:59:05-08:00","id":806734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806722#post806722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">%50 pure, is the hard line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would definitely include all types of steel and a lot of other alloys. Steels are just iron with varying and very small amounts of carbon and other elements such as chromium and nickel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.explainthatstuff.com/ironsteel.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn4.explainthatstuff.com/og-large-iron-bridge.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.explainthatstuff.com/ironsteel.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Iron and steel - Introduction to their science, properties, uses </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.explainthatstuff.com/ironsteel.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.explainthatstuff.com/ironsteel.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> An easy introduction to iron and steel and how we use them. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:01:37-08:00","id":806736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806719#post806719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the new Changeling corebook include a system for creating totally new Contracts and Pledges, or is that something we will not see until later?<br /> <br /> Edit: Is steel considered iron?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pledges will be freeform, so yeah. Contracts, not so much. I have supplements for that. <br /> <br /> And re: Iron, no. People think of steel as steel, by and large. Even if it's mostly iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:02:37-08:00","id":806738,"title":"","content":"I'm ambivalent on the necessary first kill part.<br /> <br /> Pros:<ul><li>It's fitting if you're going for a horror movie monster feel, since you always have some poor schmo or unlikable jerk fall victim to it in the early scenes.</li> <li>It's a perfect setup for a grizzled detective to scratch his head at some strange method of murder, so it also works if you're doing a base CoD game with mortal characters.</li> <li>It gives some changelings moral challenges if they care about the random victims.</li> <li>It can be 'refluffed' as a more persistent variety of Huntsman getting back into practice, or the result of, say, a mugger biting off more than he could chew.</li> </ul><br /> Mixed:<ul><li>A feeling of &quot;You Can't Stop Phase One&quot;: Naturally, since this is a horror game, you've got to have something to keep you afraid, and a grisly random death that might appear supernatural is going to put changelings on edge, whether it's actually a Huntsman or &quot;just&quot; a mundane but theatrical murder. I can see some potential stories in giving changelings the tools to prevent that first kill. Example: Changeling gets a prophetic dream about his soon-to-be Huntsman's first victim. He might be able to prevent it, but it means putting himself at immediate risk.</li> </ul>Cons:<ul><li>Apathy/hopelessness from the seeming inevitability of all those people being killed by huntsmen. This should be preventable by good Storytelling technique, notably not overusing Huntsmen when other viable antagonists are available.</li> <li>Potentially oversimplifies a fae monster to Always Chaotic Evil, at least in the minds of the players. Again, probably preventable with good Storytelling.</li> </ul><br /> Some ideas for potential tweaks, depending on Storyteller's needs:<ul><li>Maybe victims can potentially be saved by genre savviness, knowing cautionary tales against their vices, or by knowing bits of folklore, but sooner or later, the Huntsman will get <i>someone</i>. Presumably, Changelings could give their otherwise oblivious human friends advice along these lines to prevent them from being that first victim. This might also protect them from being used as hostages as well.</li> <li>If Huntsmen have preferred methods that are persistent across incarnations, maybe a particularly well-informed changeling could anticipate how their new Huntsmen will pick and kill their first target and potentially prevent it.</li> <li>Maybe there could be other ways a Huntsman can learn about Earth without killing 100% of the time. Killing a human might simply be the most straightforward and common method. The thought of a Huntsman not resorting to killing might be a scary prospect or a preferred style because there's no strange murder to signal their arrival.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:07:20-08:00","id":806740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806736#post806736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pledges will be freeform, so yeah. Contracts, not so much. I have supplements for that.<br /> <br /> And re: Iron, no. People think of steel as steel, by and large. Even if it's mostly iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people certainly think of steel as iron and vice versa, largely because it's true. <br /> <br /> My frame of reference was modern urban fantasy and horror that includes significant fae, such as the Dresden Files, where steel is indistinguishable from iron in its effects of the fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:09:36-08:00","id":806743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806736#post806736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And re: Iron, no. People think of steel as steel, by and large. Even if it's mostly iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the issue with giving a definition of Iron that has anything to do with purity. The stuff people think of as steel is ultimately just Fe (iron) with less C (carbon) in it than the stuff people think of as iron. It's considerably more &quot;pure iron&quot; than iron is. In my personal opinion, the best way to avoid iron vs. steel arguments is to state in no uncertain terms that what defines something as iron has nothing to do with its composition and everything to do with the way it's perceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:22:20-08:00","id":806747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806743#post806743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the issue with giving a definition of Iron that has anything to do with purity. The stuff people think of as steel is ultimately just Fe (iron) with less C (carbon) in it than the stuff people think of as iron. It's considerably more &quot;pure iron&quot; than iron is. In my personal opinion, the best way to avoid iron vs. steel arguments is to state in no uncertain terms that what defines something as iron has nothing to do with its composition and everything to do with the way it's perceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's exactly what I'm doing. <br /> <br /> Purity's a silly metric for magic. Perception holds all the magic. <br /> <br /> Which, you know, is Changeling to a T.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":