tle":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:33:59-08:00","id":806755,"title":"","content":"Okie dokie loki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-12-2016, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:35:12-08:00","id":806756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806738#post806738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]It's a perfect setup for a grizzled detective to scratch his head at some strange method of murder, so it also works if you're doing a base CoD game with mortal characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww man, now <i>that's</i> a game I would like to run!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:36:47-08:00","id":806757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806755#post806755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*glances at the section*<br /> <br /> Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. <span style=\"color:white\">six more characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:38:35-08:00","id":806758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806754#post806754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact: Filamena and I both worked on the Mistborn RPG. I dig that series.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really is amazing,a cl\u00e1ssico , id say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T22:06:21-08:00","id":806779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806697#post806697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) No, it's not a Title thing, it's a changeling thing. Give me a second....<br /> <br /> Here we are. Basically, the summoning ritual requires something, an item, that represents the changeling from their time in Arcadia. The Huntsman carries this item with it, it serves a major function for them, and when they are finally killed, that item is left for the changeling to reclaim.<br /> <br /> Unless it's worked into the background, most changelings don't <i>get</i> a lot of emblems(I'm calling them that until a proper name is introduced)-it's a safe assumption that there's only one or two as a convergence of sensibility and narrative.<br /> <br /> 2) Physical existence is <i>irritating</i>. In some ways, it's <i>frightening</i>. But it's <i>manageable</i>.<br /> <br /> Underneath mortal refuse and Arcadian sinew, though, there is a living story of the hunt, and Huntsmen, for all their dislike of the human world and flesh, are creatures who revel in the Hunt. These aren't Uratha, where the hunt is a primal, adrenaline filled action. It's lyricism, an artistry, a thrill of intellect and personality and precision. Even the brutal Wolf, who does kick down doors and ravage his targets before dragging them in a bleeding stupor back to Arcadia, prefers a certain slyness to his approach, a little convincing of pig and ingenue to let him and his big teeth in. This is not just a rush, this is not just ritual-this is <i>art, </i>this is the invisible being found by feeling it out. Even the most brutally done paintings have some measure of thought or feeling to it, if it's worth anything. For a Huntsmen, there is a satisfaction in doing the hunt <i>right</i>, and that often weighs as heavily on them as the desire to go home.<br /> <br /> 3) Like I said, I don't know. It's a question I would love to tackle in supplements, if the opportunity comes. But for now, it's best to say that's a question for the table. Cooler and stranger answers will come from there than us answering.<br /> <br /> But yeah, iron, cold iron, is master of all. The Huntsmen are reasonably chained under them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, there's a time limit? Well, that changes things.<br /> <br /> Anything I've said that can reasonably be assumed to be based on the Huntsmen having unlimited time? Scratch that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So with only a limited time before the Huntsmen poofs, isn't the problem I mentioned with them being boiled down to a bi-weekly visit from your abusive ex still valid? It doesn't seem like they'd have much time to resolve hunts, and after the first or second time who are they going to bribe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T22:32:50-08:00","id":806786,"title":"","content":"Right now, I'm between what I've read and what I'm told. It's an interesting gap.<br /> <br /> That aside, this still presupposes short amounts of time. Going for a comparison, the Arisen are on a time limit too, but that comes out to a year or two.<br /> <br /> It depends, I suppose, on the temperaments of the True Fae and the Huntsman in question, though the attitude towards the hunt as art is still valid.<br /> <br /> Really, we're dealing with narrative forces. The time is nearly up when it become dramatically appropriate for a Huntsman to start panicking. Once I find what I've missed*, I'll clarify.<br /> <br /> But I'll take a second to say this:<br /> <br /> This is not your ex's house. It's yours. As far as changelings are concerned-as far as abuse survivors go-the attitude is fairly simple:<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, sure, keep coming back. I've got bigger guns.&quot;<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, having seen many clingy, abusive assholes, this actually isn't all that out of place for the abuse survivor thing.<br /> <br /> *which, considering how frequently I've scoured this stuff up until the recent move, is really bizarre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T23:07:56-08:00","id":806795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806786#post806786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, I'm between what I've read and what I'm told. It's an interesting gap.<br /> <br /> That aside, this still presupposes short amounts of time. Going for a comparison, the Arisen are on a time limit too, but that comes out to a year or two.<br /> <br /> It depends, I suppose, on the temperaments of the True Fae and the Huntsman in question, though the attitude towards the hunt as art is still valid.<br /> <br /> Really, we're dealing with narrative forces. The time is nearly up when it become dramatically appropriate for a Huntsman to start panicking. Once I find what I've missed*, I'll clarify.<br /> <br /> But I'll take a second to say this:<br /> <br /> This is not your ex's house. It's yours. As far as changelings are concerned-as far as abuse survivors go-the attitude is fairly simple:<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, sure, keep coming back. I've got bigger guns.&quot;<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, having seen many clingy, abusive assholes, this actually isn't all that out of place for the abuse survivor thing.<br /> <br /> *which, considering how frequently I've scoured this stuff up until the recent move, is really bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Part of me would kind of rather the Huntsmen be &quot;reassigned&quot; when slain. That way, when you defeat it it's someone else's problem. Your name gets shuffled to the bottom of the &quot;list&quot; so to speak. So the reprieve is temporary, you will never know if you'll run into the huntsmen again or if another Changeling will manage to end it permanently. You still have to deal with at least one instance of the huntsmen trying to take you back in chains and turn everyone against you. So even if they <b>never show up again</b> you still recall it and you know in the back of your mind that they're not really gone. At least then I could see a larger atmosphere of paranoia, because you can't predict when his next visit will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T00:03:15-08:00","id":806821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806704#post806704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, people were asking about iron I think?<br /> <br /> I made it a little more generous a definition. Because &quot;cold iron&quot; is a really subjective term, and would largely reflect things that aren't by any means practical tools or weapons. So, if it's iron enough that people think of it as iron, it's iron, and it counts. Cast iron, wrought iron, cold iron, dramatic irony, if it's iron, it's iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite possibly the best single piece of news about 2E I've heard since announcement.<br /> <br /> 1E's definition was so nebulous, contradictory and confusing it basically came down to &quot;make stuff up at your table&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T00:10:42-08:00","id":806829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806704#post806704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cast iron, wrought iron, cold iron, <b>dramatic irony</b>, if it's iron, it's iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that a joke? Because it would be kinda awesome if it wasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T01:07:40-08:00","id":806845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=805814#post805814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit lukewarm on the part where they have to kill a human to remember how the mortal world works. I don't really see how it fits into their story. I'm also having a very difficult time imagining how they manage to kill someone without understanding the basics of physical reality...</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same reaction reading this section. I've made a quick pass over the rest of this forum topic and didn't see any definitive response. Possibly I missed it.<br /> <br /> My two cents: Instead of physically killing the mortal, have the Huntsman possess the mortal in some way, or enter their dreams and devour them. Something other mortals witnesses would not recognize as 'killing' and immediately associate with the Huntsman. Or perhaps have the condition of a Huntsman's arrival into the mortal world require a situation where a lone mortal victim is hanging out near some hedge gate, for example -- a situation Changelings would like to try and prevent, since it could help keep Huntsman from ever emerging into the real world.<br /> <br /> On a separate note, no mention of how Huntsman operate in the Hedge? I would assume they're much more at home there, and likely much more dangerous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:34:35-08:00","id":806900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806621#post806621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way i can think of keeping an huntsmen out of arcadia indefinetly would be a major contract or spell to stop time around the huntsman and thus stop their bodies decaying,only a serious powerful being can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet there's a bunch of methods, and a much bigger bunch of &quot;methods&quot; available at the local goblin market.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806738#post806738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fitting if you're going for a horror movie monster feel, since you always have some poor schmo or unlikable jerk fall victim to it in the early scenes.<br /> It's a perfect setup for a grizzled detective to scratch his head at some strange method of murder, so it also works if you're doing a base CoD game with mortal characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gives changelings a reason to worry whenever humans turn up mysteriously dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806829#post806829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that a joke? Because it would be kinda awesome if it wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would. I'm also picturing a changeling with the right domestic appliance and an analogue of that Demon play on words power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:38:07-08:00","id":806905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806829#post806829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that a joke? Because it would be kinda awesome if it wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the Goblin Merchants will insist it's not when they're trying to sell you three bottles of the stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:52:59-08:00","id":806915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806905#post806905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, the Goblin Merchants will insist it's not when they're trying to sell you three bottles of the stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Is this a joke? I'll have you know that my prices are quite sensible! See if you can get quality irony for a better price elsewhere if you don't believe me!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T06:13:16-08:00","id":806948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806915#post806915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Is this a joke? I'll have you know that my prices are quite sensible! See if you can get quality irony for a better price elsewhere if you don't believe me!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, this may be a self-fulfilling pitch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:27:35-08:00","id":807000,"title":"","content":"Speaking of dealing in non-physical items, I hope that gets support in the new edition. My favorite part about my Wizened toymaker was doing things like crafting a doll out of the sorrow a mother felt for her lost child and pure unadulterated whimsy. The only rules for this eventually came out in Goblin Markets (we hand-waved it prior) and I always felt that was a shame because stuff like that always seemed like a core part of the setting for me. How can you have a Goblin Market where there isn't a trade in dreams and memories? In our game, the Goblin Market bar sold distilled raw emotions as drinks, for Oberon's sake!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:02:44-08:00","id":807190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806905#post806905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, the Goblin Merchants will insist it's not when they're trying to sell you three bottles of the stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Be very careful, there's a lot of really bad irony out there. Some merchants even try to pass off cheap coincidence as true irony to the unwary buyer. <br /> <br /> Only buy organic, free-range dramatic irony from a reputable dealer. It might cost a little more, but it's worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:58:01-08:00","id":807231,"title":"","content":"I'm liking the Huntsmen so far, and I'm looking forward to seeing the rest of the information on them. I do have some questions and concerns, though.<br /> <br /> 1. I'm sure this will be answered in the section we haven't gotten yet, but how long do the Huntsmen have to complete their hunt? I worry that if it is too short, patience may not be a valid strategy. Are there ways for them to prolong the time they have, enabling them to play the long game? With limited time, why would any of them ease off the hunt at the last minute to prolong it?<br /> 2. Can a Huntsman bring in a different changeling, or is it a failed hunt unless they bring in the one they were created to hunt or the Token?<br /> 3. The text seems to swing back and forth between the tell being obvious or subtle. For instance, it mentions that a horned Huntsman taking on the form of a dog will still have horns that are now very hard to conceal, but then it goes on to mention that it could be sensory or thematic instead. Does the Huntsman decide how its tell will be displayed? Is it random, with the Huntsman taking on the dog form uncertain whether its horns will appear or if the dog will just smell especially musky or have a goat horn spiked collar?<br /> 4. Do they have ways to prolong their transformations? Can they take on the same transformation a second time? Is there any potential for long-term infiltration into their prey's life?<br /> 5. Are Huntsmen obvious for what they are to changelings in their natural form? Would the example of the Horned Man be able to walk into a changeling court and claim to be a newly escaped changeling in order to infiltrate their society?<br /> 6. How much of their memories are lost between making attempts to capture their prey? For instance, if a changeling traps a Huntsman until their time limit expires, will the same trap work the next time as well, or will the Huntsman remember the events of the previous hunt and learn from their mistakes? Is it just specific details that are lost, like remembering that they had been run down by some sort of carriage, but needing to kill to remember that said carriage would be called a truck?<br /> 7. Do they have ways to gain more specific information from the people that they kill, or from others that they may kill later? How much information do they gain when they kill their initial victim? I know that it seems to be common knowledge, such as the example of recognizing bricks as the material that makes up a house, but what would that cover? Do they gain an understanding of pop culture, for instance? At this point in U.S. society, most people would recognize Bart Simpson on a poster, but would a Huntsman? For that matter, do they only gain knowledge that the individuals in question were in possession of, or is it more of a symbolic sacrifice to gain a basic understanding? If the mortal it targeted happened to be someone who had lived a very sheltered life, would this cause problems for the Huntsman when confronted with things that the sheltered mortal was unaware of, or would it still recognize bricks even if the person killed had never even heard of them before? Does an abundance of people with knowledge of a subject make it more likely that a Huntsman would gain that knowledge (ie: 30 years ago, computers might have been strange things to a Huntsman, as they were the domain mostly of the people who worked with them, but today, computer basics would be common among Huntsmen because of the abundance of computer users in society)?<br /> 8. Do they need to kill a fresh person every time they emerge from the Hedge, or only each time that they gain a new quarry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:39:47-08:00","id":807453,"title":"","content":"I love it. great idea, good write up.<br /> <br /> I'm curious though, if there are other reasons for true fae to make huntsmen outside of collecting wayward changelings. Such as a gentry on its last title, remembering it left one in the form of a prob somewhere on the other side of the hedge, and sends a huntsmen to collect it, knowing its in the hands of a court?<br /> <br /> could be a means of having huntsmen tokens be not 100% evil to possess, if a changeling were to lend a hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:39:00-08:00","id":807528,"title":"","content":"After having a little time to mull it over, I think I'm a fan of the Huntsmen, over all. I can see where some folks are coming from with regard to the the Huntsmen being redundant with the True Fey themselves, since both could be viewed as unstoppable, inhuman monsters trying to drag Changelings back to Arcadia. From a narrative perspective, however, I do feel like the Huntsmen fill an important niche.<br /> <br /> The True Fey are alien, implacable, and terrifyingly powerful. However, you can't really have them show up very often without either removing your PCs from play or making the Others a lot less scary, since they keep getting beaten. As such, the True Fey are villains that are most effective when used sparingly - <i>very</i> sparingly, in my opinion. At the same time, however, just talking about how nasty and scary the True Fey are can only get you so far. Changelings, and their players, need more tangible reminders that their Keepers are still out there and haven't forgotten about them.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen are those reminders; strange and inhuman enough to be undeniably products of Arcadia, but not quite the same dread creatures of myth and nightmare that the True Fey. Furthermore, they're living(-ish) embodiments of the cruelty of the Fey, as simply being forced to exist is intensely unpleasant for them. As dangerous and cruel as they may be, this same fact makes them a little pathetic as well, and gives a tinge of tragedy to their story. This is important, I think, because the Huntsmen will show up a lot more often than their masters, and as such they will most likely be defeated much more often as well. You can't really pass them off as unstoppable, no matter how relentless they may be, but you can certainly present them as imperfect tools cobbled together by the Fey to serve a particular purpose, in much the same manner as a Fetch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-13-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:52:02-08:00","id":807600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806643#post806643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't make Huntsmen lightly, particularly since you have Loyaists and Fetches* in place for initial retreival. Even if those fail, if the changeling proves to be boring, there might not be a point in sending a Huntsman after them, at least immediately. If one of your favorite toys happens to be in town and you have the resources, you might make a hunting party, but that's incidental.<br /> <br /> The material discorporates, and reforms in the Hedge near Arcadia. The Huntsman suffers the entire time, far as I know.<br /> <br /> *Which, by the way, spells out a basic story outline for you, should you wish to use it. Fetches as an initial enemy(Wyrd 1-3), Huntsmen for when they prove to be desirable(Wyrd 4-7), and finally, the True Fae themselves needs to step in(Wyrd 8-10). That's nothing from the book, just a fun view.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad to hear that they are more of an elite-tier enemy that isn't deployed carelessly. Hopefully this will be indicated in the core book. This makes the killing upon each reentry into the mortal realm seem reasonable to me. <br /> <br /> Reforming in the Hedge near Arcadia makes sense. Again, I hope the final version of the text will describe this and make it clear that the entire fortnight is unpleasant, not just the initial messy unmaking. I'm wondering why two weeks though. Does it have some fairy tale/mystical significance that I'm unaware of? I think it might be nice to have the reformation last longer and longer each time the Huntsman is killed, giving them more motivation to hunt carefully on subsequent attempts.<br /> <br /> The progression of antagonists is nice, especially when you add in other Changelings (including Loyalists, Bridge Burners, etc.) other hobgoblins and the myriad other horrors of the CoD. Looking forward to seeing what 2e Fetches are like. I'm hoping that Charlatans are still a thing, too; they were my favorite enemies after Fetches.<br /> <br /> The new stance on iron seems like pretty much exactly what I was talking about in another thread a bit ago; identity/conceptual purity as opposed to metallurgical or chemical. I'm crossing my fingers that no errant mentions of percentages make it into the final book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T22:01:47-08:00","id":807605,"title":"","content":"If the percentages thing appears in the second draft, I'll toss Dave an e-mail about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T22:23:25-08:00","id":807619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=807600#post807600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Glad to hear that they are more of an elite-tier enemy that isn't deployed carelessly. Hopefully this will be indicated in the core book. This makes the killing upon each reentry into the mortal realm seem reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> Reforming in the Hedge near Arcadia makes sense. Again, I hope the final version of the text will describe this and make it clear that the entire fortnight is unpleasant, not just the initial messy unmaking. I'm wondering why two weeks though. Does it have some fairy tale/mystical significance that I'm unaware of? I think it might be nice to have the reformation last longer and longer each time the Huntsman is killed, giving them more motivation to hunt carefully on subsequent attempts.<br /> <br /> The progression of antagonists is nice, especially when you add in other Changelings (including Loyalists, Bridge Burners, etc.) other hobgoblins and the myriad other horrors of the CoD. Looking forward to seeing what 2e Fetches are like. I'm hoping that Charlatans are still a thing, too; they were my favorite enemies after Fetches.<br /> <br /> The new stance on iron seems like pretty much exactly what I was talking about in another thread a bit ago; identity/conceptual purity as opposed to metallurgical or chemical. I'm crossing my fingers that no errant mentions of percentages make it into the final book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally speaking I think the vagueness will cause issues, but only time will tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T22:30:35-08:00","id":807621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806643#post806643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Which, by the way, spells out a basic story outline for you, should you wish to use it. Fetches as an initial enemy(Wyrd 1-3), Huntsmen for when they prove to be desirable(Wyrd 4-7), and finally, the True Fae themselves needs to step in(Wyrd 8-10). That's nothing from the book, just a fun view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact, the last time I ran Changeling this was exactly how the Chronicle panned out. Just with a motley of Loyalists and Privateers in the place of the Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> For bonus points the campaign's themes went through a seasonal cycle. They spent Winter hiding from their enemies, Spring exploring the local Freehold and connected mortals, Summer fighting off an incursion from the Hedge, and Autumn seizing a troubling amount of power for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T22:38:57-08:00","id":807624,"title":"","content":"I may have overlooked something \u2014 in fact, I probably did, and this is probably a dumb question. That said: shouldn't Huntsmen be treated as a variation of CofD's Horrors (with Yearning replacing Potency) rather than being created as mortals are?<br /> <br /> EDIT: this question is expandable. The Horror (and Nightmare) creation rules in CofD strike me as a decent baseline for creating supernatural antagonists of all sorts, from hobgoblins to fetches to huntsmen to charlatans (assuming the latter is still a thing in CtL2e); only ephemeral entities (such as those encountered in dreamscapes) don't fit the premise of Horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-13-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T23:26:43-08:00","id":807649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=807624#post807624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have overlooked something \u2014 in fact, I probably did, and this is probably a dumb question. That said: shouldn't Huntsmen be treated as a variation of CofD's Horrors (with Yearning replacing Potency) rather than being created as mortals are?<br /> <br /> EDIT: this question is expandable. The Horror (and Nightmare) creation rules in CofD strike me as a decent baseline for creating supernatural antagonists of all sorts, from hobgoblins to fetches to huntsmen to charlatans (assuming the latter is still a thing in CtL2e); only ephemeral entities (such as those encountered in dreamscapes) don't fit the premise of Horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree all the way on this - all of embodied fae cretures should use <b>CoD</b> Horror-like rules, in place of Ephemeral Beings rules - most important elements both have - Bane and Bane, Rank\\Potency and Numina\\Dread powers. But embodied fae should not have rules like possesing mortals ( not in the ephemeral beings ways have ) or Manifestations.<br /> <br /> So Horror-like mechanics should be used for most of fae ( Huntsmen, hobgoblins, maybe Fetches also ).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T23:49:52-08:00","id":807657,"title":"","content":"I do hope that it will be easier to make hobgoblins in 2e, the work of having to stat tonnes of them up was a rather big reason for why I wasn't sure I wanted to storytell Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:18:36-08:00","id":807676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=807624#post807624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have overlooked something \u2014 in fact, I probably did, and this is probably a dumb question. That said: shouldn't Huntsmen be treated as a variation of CofD's Horrors (with Yearning replacing Potency) rather than being created as mortals are?<br /> <br /> EDIT: this question is expandable. The Horror (and Nightmare) creation rules in CofD strike me as a decent baseline for creating supernatural antagonists of all sorts, from hobgoblins to fetches to huntsmen to charlatans (assuming the latter is still a thing in CtL2e); only ephemeral entities (such as those encountered in dreamscapes) don't fit the premise of Horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was all written way before those rules. And I don't have space to include the horror creation material. I had to be super, super shorthand in this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:54:09-08:00","id":807695,"title":"","content":"Seriously, this book is packed to the gills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T01:16:54-08:00","id":807704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=807695#post807695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, this book is packed to the gills.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Best news ever *super excited*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:21:53-08:00","id":807905,"title":"","content":"I can see 3 ways to beat a huntsmen.<br /> <br /> 1. stab it with an Arcadian weapon till it dies.<br /> 2. A token of reprieve, I could see a clever changeling tricking a huntsmen into giving them one. Like the target Changeling pretends to be a particular treachrous Changeling with information on the location of the target Changeling, only to reveal that they were the one to give the huntsmen their own location, forcing the huntsmen to give up a token of reprieve which the changeling gives back to the huntsmen.<br /> 3. Run the huntsmen out of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:00:20-08:00","id":807977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=807905#post807905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see 3 ways to beat a huntsmen.<br /> <br /> 1. stab it with an Arcadian weapon till it dies.<br /> 2. A token of reprieve, I could see a clever changeling tricking a huntsmen into giving them one. Like the target Changeling pretends to be a particular treachrous Changeling with information on the location of the target Changeling, only to reveal that they were the one to give the huntsmen their own location, forcing the huntsmen to give up a token of reprieve which the changeling gives back to the huntsmen.<br /> 3. Run the huntsmen out of time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Number 1 and 3 have already been mentioned, but number 2 sounds like a perfectly in-character trickery for changelings. I did not infer anything from the preview that said Huntsmen always know whether a changeling is legitimately betraying someone or not.<br /> <br /> I assume an Arcadian law prevents the Huntsmen from just giving their Arcadian weapons to perform an assisted suicide, in addition to their conflicted enjoyment of the Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:34:17-08:00","id":808012,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think Darklings in particular are very suited to double crossing a huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:37:45-08:00","id":808016,"title":"","content":"Ooh, that'd I'd like to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:37:55-08:00","id":808017,"title":"","content":"What if you help a huntsman find yourself, thus obligating them to give you a token of reprieve, which you promptly give back to them to take to Arcadia?<br /> <br /> Or, to be less silly, help a huntsman find someone, but give them the token before he gets there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:44:27-08:00","id":808029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808017#post808017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you help a huntsman find yourself, thus obligating them to give you a token of reprieve, which you promptly give back to them to take to Arcadia?<br /> <br /> Or, to be less silly, help a huntsman find someone, but give them the token before he gets there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's assume the Huntsman isn't stupid and will make plans in accordance to his role as story upsetter.<br /> <br /> He a) makes a plan to avoid that, b) makes a plan to ensure he can sweeten the pot if he does have to take the token.<br /> <br /> These guys are <i>smart</i>. They are the oldest stories in Arcadia, given life, purpose, and everything they need to catch the most uncatchable major splat in the ChroD canon to date.<br /> <br /> Come up with a clever plan the Lost'll never see coming, and then <i>do it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:48:02-08:00","id":808035,"title":"","content":"They don't really have a <i>reason</i> to avoid that though. Huntsmen don't really give a shit if the True Fae gets the changeling or not. They just want to go back to arcadia and get some downtime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:00:34-08:00","id":808046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808035#post808035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't really have a <i>reason</i> to avoid that though. Huntsmen don't really give a shit if the True Fae gets the changeling or not. They just want to go back to arcadia and get some downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, I think, their pride or adherence to doing a story <i>right</i> would prevent them from &quot;cheating&quot;. At least, I think that's how they're presented here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:02:02-08:00","id":808047,"title":"","content":"If it was purely human logic they were running on, sure.<br /> <br /> They aren't. Their motives are a weird dance between &quot;Get home&quot; and &quot;Make the hunt a satisfying story.&quot; These guys are <i>faeries</i>. Competing and contradictory goals doesn't stop them much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-13-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:02:04-08:00","id":808048,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the Court/Personal/Entitlement Approaches. I love the concept on a fundamental level, it's just an extremely well-designed mechanic.<br /> <br /> Since I wasn't planning on using Huntsmen in my games, I was thinking about how to turn the reward from Yearning into something a Fetch, mortal, or Loyalist/Privateer Changeling can benefit from. What is the equivalent of one Yearning? One Willpower/Glamour? It feels too weak. Full Willpower/Glamour, on the other hand, feels too strong.<br /> <br /> What rewards would Approaches grant to non-Huntsmen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:04:48-08:00","id":808051,"title":"","content":"A token is still a useful bargaining chip for those with no need of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:07:02-08:00","id":808053,"title":"","content":"The Yearning approach is...not something I would do without Huntsmen. The beauty of the system is that you have a synergy between the common antagonists-True Fae are uber powerful, but have to obey every approach, Huntsmen are fairly powerful but need to rely on the Approaches sometimes to keep up their power/life, and the Loyalists aren't bound to the Approaches at all but aren't anything more or less than changelings. It's various levels of siege tactics and spy work that encourages interplay between the three main forces.<br /> <br /> It's still useful against the True Fae, but applying a mandate to use Approaches for Loyalists kill the best part about them-that they are the same as <i>you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:15:56-08:00","id":808066,"title":"","content":"I think Approaches are excellent without Huntsman, as they not only evoke the &quot;tale&quot; feel of Changeling (and one might see Approaches as a subtle way of Talecrafting), but they also have an element of occult and mysticism, as they are the &quot;escape clauses&quot; that make their enchantments of protection stronger. Just like every Contract has a Catch, so do the Approaches are ways for the magic of the Bulwark to grow stronger, story-wise, because it has specific weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not saying Loyalists et al. <i>have</i> to use Approaches. I'm trying to come up with a reward to <i>encourage</i> them to use them. As a way to try and face changelings on their own turf and beat them at their own game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:20:04-08:00","id":808068,"title":"","content":"Meh.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, I would treat using an approach as a Glamour harvesting move. Pick the most appropriate Attribute+Skill, successes become Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:28:47-08:00","id":808081,"title":"","content":"For the Loyalists/Privateers, I assume. That might be doable, as it avoids the &quot;One Point or All Points&quot; dilemma. The problem is that it's not terribly crossover-friendly. It doesn't make much sense for some supernaturals to refuel when they abide by an Approach (vampires getting Vitae out of beating someone at their own game feels... strange), and while it can work as Willpower for mortals and Hunters, it doesn't do much for Horrors and the like.<br /> <br /> Maybe instead of a Yearning, an Approach grants a Twist of Fate? Whoever abides by it and beats the changeling at their own game, gains some sort of token, evocative of the Approach itself, that they can later use to bring misfortune to either the changeling themselves (assume they're not dead or captured already), or to the rest of the Freehold. Mechanically, they could use it to downgrade a roll one step (from ES to S, from S to F, or from F to DF), or they could use it &quot;organically&quot; in a diceless scene to take control of the narrative and implement a dramatic twist.<br /> <br /> I think I like that idea. It's very Changeling in nature, and it encourages long-term antagonists of the entire Freehold to prey on the weak and accumulate Twists of Fate so that they can take out the big fish later on, and personal antagonists of the PCs to do some &quot;prep work&quot; before confronting them, which also gives time for the PCs to prepare countermeasures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:48:33-08:00","id":808312,"title":"","content":"When you think about it,Huntsmen are one of those antagonist is never a good idea to kill directly. if you kill them they's just be back angrier and you probably won't see they coming the second time they come for you,you have to find a way to trick them,and even them they may discover and come back for you,and if you can't even trick them,well,it's either going back <i>there </i>or sending someonese else to a fate to save your own skin&gt;<br /> FUCKING awesome villain i swear to god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T23:11:52-08:00","id":808481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808035#post808035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen don't really give a shit if the True Fae gets the changeling or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not clear to me that this is a true statement. Sure, everyone respects the rules and the rules say that Tokens of Reprieve are magic get-out-of-Huntsman-free cards, but I don't think Huntsmen are terribly happy about bringing back a Token. In principle, a hunt is less about the destination than the journey, yeah, so a Token is satisfactory because it's a successful hunt in the sense that you've harried and cornered your prey until they burned a last resort, but it's also kinda like a very long seduction that culminates in... watching porn together, without touching, and then sleeping in separate beds. Because ...rules? Half of their Yearning is &quot;freedom from this mortal clay,&quot; sure, but the other half is &quot;I want my Changeling back&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:30:29-08:00","id":808820,"title":"","content":"Something I hope is addressed in the Arcadian Weapon section: When a Huntsman is killed in the mortal realm, does it leave their Arcadian Weapon behind? This would provide an incredible incentive for the Huntsman to hunt carefully, since being dispatched during the hunt would likely give its prey the means to kill it, but probably makes it to easy to acquire the Huntsman's weakness. Conversely, if the Arcadian Weapon returns to the realms of the Fae when the Huntsman is dispersed (either through damaging its physical form or by it spending its last yearning), what is to keep a Huntsman from voluntarily spending its last yearning anytime its weapon is captured? I mean, a couple weeks of torment beats being permanently destroyed, amiright? Or does the weapon return to Arcadia/the Hedge if it's still in possession of the Huntsman when it's sent back, but stay in the mortal realm if someone else has gotten a hold of it? That last one seems most likely to me. I'm just hoping the book is clear on it, one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:43:06-08:00","id":808832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808820#post808820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I hope is addressed in the Arcadian Weapon section: When a Huntsman is killed in the mortal realm, does it leave their Arcadian Weapon behind? This would provide an incredible incentive for the Huntsman to hunt carefully, since being dispatched during the hunt would likely give its prey the means to kill it, but probably makes it to easy to acquire the Huntsman's weakness. Conversely, if the Arcadian Weapon returns to the realms of the Fae when the Huntsman is dispersed (either through damaging its physical form or by it spending its last yearning), what is to keep a Huntsman from voluntarily spending its last yearning anytime its weapon is captured? I mean, a couple weeks of torment beats being permanently destroyed, amiright? Or does the weapon return to Arcadia/the Hedge if it's still in possession of the Huntsman when it's sent back, but stay in the mortal realm if someone else has gotten a hold of it? That last one seems most likely to me. I'm just hoping the book is clear on it, one way or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind goes in different directions, so I've forgotten what happens to the weapon if they are killed.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'd argue it would be a matter of if they thought they could win or not, if their weapon was taken. Circumstances are such that they might still be able to claim their weapon back in short order, but if it looks like final death might hit them, they might take the misery and spend their last Yearning.<br /> <br /> Now I gotta go check.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a general rule, they get their weapons back after time, certainly if they're destroyed. Rumors exist of a way to make an Arcadian weapon permanently yours though.<br /> <br /> We'll keep it vague like that for the benefit of tease and anticipation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-14-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:48:40-08:00","id":808836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808832#post808832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, I'd argue it would be a matter of if they thought they could win or not, if their weapon was taken. Circumstances are such that they might still be able to claim their weapon back in short order, but if it looks like final death might hit them, they might take the misery and spend their last Yearning.</div> </div> </div> </div>My concern with that would be that if they take their weapon with them, regardless of who's in possession of it, it makes them nearly impossible to kill. As long as they've got a single health level left, they could just burn yearning and bamf away back to fairie land, taking the only weapon that can kill them along with. I can see that leading to some extremely frustrated players. I'm hoping that the Arcadian Weapon stays behind, at least if it's in someone else's possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:49:48-08:00","id":808837,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah.<br /> <br /> What, did you think beating a Huntsman <i>should be easy?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:57:01-08:00","id":808847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808837#post808837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah.<br /> <br /> What, did you think beating a Huntsman <i>should be easy?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>No, it shouldn't be easy. But it also shouldn't be repetitive, tedious, and punitively frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:01:00-08:00","id":808854,"title":"","content":"I mean, getting the weapon should be hard. Keeping the weapons should be hard, too. But it should be hard because the Hunstman is enacting cunning plans to retrieve it, pulling out all the stops and using all his dirty tricks, not because the Huntsman can cheat and blow through its power pool to respawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:03:05-08:00","id":808856,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that showing up every fortnight like clockwork is unlikely to be effective.<br /> <br /> &quot;In knew you were coming, so I got this suit of iron plate mail. What now, bitch?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:04:54-08:00","id":808860,"title":"","content":"I've already work the Huntsmen into <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\">my homebrew rules!</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Homebrew of Pale_Crusader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Arcadian Hunters</b><br /> For every two Permanent Atrocity that a changeling gains, they also gain an Entrapment Clause of their Keeper.<br /> <br /> An Entrapment Clause is an action done by or a circumstance changeling may find themselves within which incites their Keeper to send forth a Huntsman to recapture the changeling. The changeling gains the Hunted condition. Should the changeling trigger the entrapment clause again while they have the condition of being Hunted (by a Huntsmen), and all their approaches have been filled by that Huntsman or the changeling has no approaches that they are protected by, that changeling's Keeper will appear and snatch the changeling through a newly formed hedgegate straight back into Arcadia. This is immediately successful and may not be contested by the target in anyway. This assures capture unless an outside party intervenes. The True Fae is only exposed for those anticipating its appearance for the an instant action of the highest initiative count of the turn it appear and any other reflexive actions that could be taken on that initiative count before it vanished with its prize. Should the changeling trigger an Entrapment Clause while they have the Hunted Condition (by a Huntsman) but the Huntsman hasn't met all their Approaches then one of the changelings Supports are abducted by the true fae in the manner it would take the changeling if the Huntsman had completed the approach applicable for that changeling. The Fetch the True Fae leaves in the Support's place shares the Conspirator condition with the Huntsman pursuing the changeling, and changeling deals loss of the Support only after the Betrayed condition resulting the Conspirator condition being resolved. Should an individual or group deliberately attempt to use this phenomenon as a trap for the True Fae, the True Fae instead snatches and replaces a Support of one of those involved in the plot at some point in the present, past, or future where the Support is/was/will be vulnerable to being taken in secrecy. Time and fate have bargains with the True Fae that allow this horrific twist, and this fact is whispered of by sage changelings wishing to share the variations of cautionary examples to keep their associates from such folly.<br /> <br /> Each Keeper has five Entrapment Clauses and all changelings of that Keeper know all five Entrapment Clauses that could apply to them with preternatural lucidity which makes it impossible for them to forget. These clauses are unique to each Keeper, and the player may choose an already existing Keeper in the setting, or at storyteller discretion the storyteller may design a new Keeper with new Entrapment Clauses based on player input when a new changeling is introduced into the setting.<br /> <br /> Besides being hunted by Entrapment Clauses, each month when a changeling lacks either Freehold or Court membership, or the freehold they belong to has a lapsed Bulwark ritual, they must roll their Permanent Atrocity (0 counting as a chance die) or alert and incite their Keeper as if they had triggered an Entrapment Clause.<br /> <br /> This bane may be temporarily suspended for a changeling that uses the Privateer Whisper, and the changeling may instead offer up a token of reprieve to avoid capture even at the hands of their keeper. See the Privateer Whisper for more information.<br /> <br /> <b>Examples</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Perun</span>, Only-Lord-of-All, The Thunder King<br /> <b>Entrapment Clauses:</b><ul><li>Be shocked by electricity</li> <li>Fail to submit a yearly blood sacrifice of prize winning bull</li> <li>Submit a blood sacrifice to anyone other than Perun</li> <li>Walk under a lone tree during a rain shower</li> <li>Eat any golden colored fruit</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Black Annis</span>, Eater-of-Children, Hag under the Hill<br /> <b>Entrapment Clauses:</b><ul><li>Disobey an elder with authority if their command is followed by with &quot;Or Black Annis will get you!&quot;</li> <li>Fail to offer a human child sacrifice dedicated to Black Annis each spring.</li> <li>Speak Black Annis's name or any of her titles aloud.</li> <li>Walk under a gnarled oak tree at night.</li> <li>Touch a dead cat corpse.</li> </ul><br /> Tezcatlipoca, Enemy-of-both-sides, Lord of the Near and Nigh<b>,</b> The Night Wind<br /> <b>Entrapment Clauses:</b><ul><li>Receive a wound on the foot</li> <li>Fail to submit a cannibalistic sacrifice of young man after his honeymoon dedicated to Tezcatlipoca once a year.</li> <li>Speak any oath of office without loudly and publicly insulting self three times.</li> <li>See own reflection within an obsidian surface.</li> <li>Being covered by soot while under the night sky</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I based the concept on the final encounter of the <i>Changeling: the Lost Quick Start Demo Rules, </i>where the Duchess of the Frozen Heart betrays your characters and you have the option to respond by saying the duchess's True Name three times and her Keeper reaches through a mirror which is the nearest thing that could be a hedgegate and snatches her back to Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:14:11-08:00","id":808871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808856#post808856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that showing up every fortnight like clockwork is unlikely to be effective.<br /> <br /> &quot;In knew you were coming, so I got this suit of iron plate mail. What now, bitch?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, I totally agree. If you're talking to me, I'm specifically referring to acquiring their weapon to use against them. It becomes tedious and frustrating if the players go through all the effort of acquiring it only to have it snatched away by the Huntsman just opting to explode and respawn. It makes it nearly impossible to capitalize on what should be a major coup (capturing the weapon) because the Huntsman can always just poof off to his home turf (albeit painfully) whenever he's in real danger of dying and take his magic weapon with him. Then they just have to capture the weapon again, because it's the only thing short of betraying another Changeling that'll stop the damn thing. But as soon as it's in danger, it poofs again. This pattern not only gets tedious and frustrating, but isn't a particularly interesting story. Which is why I'm hoping that the weapon stays behind if someone else is in possession of it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:34:35-08:00","id":808890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808856#post808856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that showing up every fortnight like clockwork is unlikely to be effective.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;In knew you were coming, so I got this suit of iron plate mail. What now, bitch?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The huntsmen can't really wait too long though. Kind of why I think two weeks is too specific a time as well as being super short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:46:21-08:00","id":808900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808856#post808856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that showing up every fortnight like clockwork is unlikely to be effective.<br /> <br /> &quot;In knew you were coming, so I got this suit of iron plate mail. What now, bitch?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So you wait till they aren't wearing it. People need to pee, you know.<br /> <br /> I think the tactics section of the next part is what y'all need to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:25:22-08:00","id":808940,"title":"","content":"You know what Huntsmen sound like? Fetches. I don't mean that in a critical way. I mean that in a &quot;are these two things related?&quot; sort of way. Cousins born from the same magic, if you will. Differentiated mostly by their purpose. A fetch's purpose is to be hidden in plain sight, to be a placeholder for a missing mortal. A huntsman's purpose is to hunt. This begs the question....what else is there? What other things made manifest by will and glamour (and a soul?) do the Others have in their toychests, each brought about to accomplish some desire of the Gentry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:33:05-08:00","id":808951,"title":"","content":"Mirrors and shadows, mirrors and shadows a-plenty. Be cool to build the toybox some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:50:55-08:00","id":808974,"title":"","content":"Crossover question,Beasts killing huntsmen and haording their weapons,Yay or Nay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:09:35-08:00","id":809001,"title":"","content":"Beasts don't know the trick to keeping their weapons, so no. Even if they did, they'd need a changeling to do it.<br /> <br /> Now I want to play a Beast Collector with Arcadian Weaponry as their focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:13:01-08:00","id":809006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809001#post809001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts don't know the trick to keeping their weapons, so no. Even if they did, they'd need a changeling to do it.<br /> <br /> Now I want to play a Beast Collector with Arcadian Weaponry as their focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanna built a character together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:41:55-08:00","id":809044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808900#post808900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you wait till they aren't wearing it. People need to pee, you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Haha, joke's on you, Huntsman, for I have a catheter!&quot;<br /> - A very well-prepared Changeling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:46:08-08:00","id":809047,"title":"","content":"Ogres probably would have a harder them dealing with huntsman,ogres are experts in burtality and straightforward methods,and you can't beat a huntsman with those","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:56:58-08:00","id":809058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809047#post809047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ogres probably would have a harder them dealing with huntsman,ogres are experts in burtality and straightforward methods,and you can't beat a huntsman with those</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. In some ways, they are very effective for that reason, in the same way that the Knights of Saint Adrian are surprisingly effective against the Unchained.<br /> <br /> More on point though, Ogres might deal with brutality, but they aren't stupid by any stretch. A lot of ogres and giants from folklore and mythology are actually rather cunning, to say nothing about trolls. Changeling Ogres in particular don't have a curse that says &quot;you must be straightforward&quot;. An Ogre can emerge from beating the shit out of a Keeper as he goes to bed or even goes under anasthesia on the suggestion of the Ogre themselves. What defines them is brutality and violence, but that definition does not include simple-minded, slow, or dumb. In fact, Ogres might be the best at dealing with the Huntsmen because they understand the balance of approaches better, and know when to be clever, sneaky, and under-handed, and when to charge in and just break some skulls. They can play <i>and</i> break the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Haha, joke's on you, Huntsman, for I have a catheter!&quot;<br /> - A very well-prepared Changeling</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ha, jokes on you, changeling. You're wearing a catheter!&quot;<br /> -A much bemused Huntsman.<br /> <br /> Alternatively:<br /> <br /> &quot;Ha, jokes on you, changeling. You're wearing a catheter!&quot;<br /> -A very clever Huntsman.<br /> &quot;The things I do for this job.&quot;<br /> -Beleaguered shapechanged Huntsman,<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:04:13-08:00","id":809069,"title":"","content":"The last one is my favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:20:57-08:00","id":809081,"title":"","content":"i forgot some of th ogre characterizations. i think te seeming that would really have a bad time with the huntsmen would be the fairest .part of the fairest's nature is that they have a tendency to end up in the spotlight, in everyone attention,even if they dont want to,must be hard to hide. And if the fairest worries about her clarity, she'd have to fight the huntsmen alone. because if she asks others to help and they got hurt their clarity drops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:23:27-08:00","id":809144,"title":"","content":"Here is a bit more of my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\">Homebrew</a> about the Huntsmen,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Homebrew of Pale_Crusader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Huntsmen, Atrocity, and Attention</b><br /> Huntsmen enter the physical world and murder. These murders are an Atrocity, but are also extremely necessary for the Huntsman to even exist in the mortal world, not unlike how an accident over feeding during a vampire gaining its vitae even when it was very careful is still an Atrocity. The Huntsman as a corporeal being without a Stability Advantage it automatically gains a Permanent Atrocity from this act, and also has a capped Cover-Up of 1. They suffer an increase in severity their Cold Wrought Iron bane, gain a Personal Bane based on the nature of the murder, and this places the Huntsman immediately on a tightrope of having the maximum Attention it can have for its Cover-Up. The common knowledge of mundane world norms it gains from the murder lets it be aware of the in-world consequences of gaining the attention of authorities or monster hunters. Each time the huntsman is reformed in Arcadia without understanding of the mortal world, due to bargains struck time immemorial by the True Fae, it is considered a new creature by the forces that govern cosmic justice and it sheds its Permanent Atrocity from its past visits and its reforming isn't prevented by banes. Part of this bargain for this fae chicanery requires the Huntsmen loses all understanding of the mortal world, so it <i><u>must</u></i> murder again and put itself right back onto that tightrope to accomplish its mission. It likely that the Huntsman's Personal Banes will be different each time it reforms and hunts anew. The balance of Attention and Cover-Up does drastically limit the huntsmen\u2019s pursuit of the changeling, making them eschew tactics they would net them greater than one Temporarily Atrocity if at all possible, and if they do something that would gain them another Permanent Atrocity it is almost always in the scene immediately prior to or during their end-game. This still leaves a lot of treachery, stealth and guile available to these heartless hunters, and they should not be underestimated.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-14-2016, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:02:03-08:00","id":809176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809081#post809081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i forgot some of th ogre characterizations. i think te seeming that would really have a bad time with the huntsmen would be the fairest .part of the fairest's nature is that they have a tendency to end up in the spotlight, in everyone attention,even if they dont want to,must be hard to hide. And if the fairest worries about her clarity, she'd have to fight the huntsmen alone. because if she asks others to help and they got hurt their clarity drops.</div> </div> </div> </div>But on the other hand, Huntsmen thrive on the isolation of their targets. Fairest live in the castle, with people willing to fight for and stand for her, all on their own. She doesn't have to lead all of them, she doesn't have to guide them. They'll do it because they think she's important. If she does take the lead, she has the great advantage of a lot of resources, and can rely on cleverness beyond her own. In correlation to my usual philosophy*, sometimes a changeling just irrevocably win, and a Fairest is in the position to arrange such a clever offensive that they can just win, far more readily than others. The fairest can be one of the most secure of targets, and the sort that forces a Huntsman to start considering the Tokens of Repreive as an answer(Seriously, you guys have no idea how much they actually avoid this answer).<br /> <br /> *The usual thing I try to emphasize to people is &quot;Sometimes, you just <i>lose</i>. Sometimes, all you can do is <i>run</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:07:24-08:00","id":809227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809176#post809176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the other hand, Huntsmen thrive on the isolation of their targets. Fairest live in the castle, with people willing to fight for and stand for her, all on their own. She doesn't have to lead all of them, she doesn't have to guide them. They'll do it because they think she's important. If she does take the lead, she has the great advantage of a lot of resources, and can rely on cleverness beyond her own. In correlation to my usual philosophy*, sometimes a changeling just irrevocably win, and a Fairest is in the position to arrange such a clever offensive that they can just win, far more readily than others. The fairest can be one of the most secure of targets, and the sort that forces a Huntsman to start considering the Tokens of Repreive as an answer(Seriously, you guys have no idea how much they actually avoid this answer).<br /> <br /> *The usual thing I try to emphasize to people is &amp;quot;Sometimes, you just <i>lose</i>. Sometimes, all you can do is <i>run</i>.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they avoid it because cathing their targets is more pleasureable and more akin to their natur?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:35:37-08:00","id":809249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809227#post809227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they avoid it because cathing their targets is more pleasureable and more akin to their natur?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah. That and it also means the True Fae summon the lot of them less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:00:44-08:00","id":809626,"title":"","content":"I feel like Huntsman are great, ever all. They evoke the themes of the game very well and the presentation is great.<br /> <br /> I worry that cold iron being the One True Way(tm) to permanently end a Huntsman will result in most Changelings going for &quot;stab it with iron&quot; over &quot;run away in a giant game of cat and mouse.&quot; I am unsure if that is an actual problem, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:26:07-08:00","id":809694,"title":"","content":"Can the Huntsmen kill the True Fae who summon them, or conspire against the True Fae so that another will take that risk? Sure, they persist as immaterial entities in a sort of slumber when not on the Hunt, so another True Fae can still summon them. Unless an Arcadian law forbids them from doing that, whether subtly or forcibly, it sounds like something a deeply frustrated Huntsman might one day consider.<br /> <br /> Are the True Fae the only ones who can summon Huntsmen? One of the required ingredients is a True Fae's breath, which a clever changeling might steal or persuade into being given. Stealing or binding immaterial/abstract things is only fae, after all. If it is possible for other beings to summon Huntsmen, is the template of the Huntsman altered?<br /> <br /> What prevents Huntsmen from giving or &quot;losing&quot; their Arcadian weapons to perform an assisted suicide (other than their conflicted enjoyment of the Hunt)? Do the True Fae subject them to some nightmarish torture if they discover such &quot;cowardice&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:54:47-08:00","id":809761,"title":"","content":"I discussed the Huntsmen with my group, and one came up with a pretty interesting concept. What if a given Huntsman decides the only way to ever be immune to being sent on Hunts is to destroy reality/humanity? Granted, this wouldn't be a likely goal to actually achieve, but it'd sort of expand the Huntsman in question into a more dangerous antagonist. They'd delay and stall their hunts, killing more humans than necessary, blackmail Mages into widening this Abyss they think Huntsmen come from, damage Infrastructures, anything they can take down before finalizing the Hunt. Granted, they'd need to figure out HOW to damage reality, but.. that'd be even scarier. Goes from &quot;Im coming to get you&quot;, to &quot;I will do irreparable damage to your city, its people, and the things you love.. and THEN Im coming to get you&quot;:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T12:11:30-08:00","id":809773,"title":"","content":"Kind of reminds me of Dogma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T14:37:29-08:00","id":809849,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Sasquatch,Godzilla,Loch Ness,King Kong,Goblin,Ghoul,a Zombie with no conscious...&quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A true fae triyng to choose wwhich spirits of hunt he should send to eart now</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T15:53:25-08:00","id":809886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809849#post809849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&amp;quot;Sasquatch,Godzilla,Loch Ness,King Kong,Goblin,Ghoul,a Zombie with no conscious...&amp;quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A true fae triyng to choose wwhich spirits of hunt he should send to eart now</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So apparently Cabin in the Woods gets to be inspiration for yet another game line.