t-the-huntsmen?p=809886#post809886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently Cabin in the Woods gets to be inspiration for yet another game line...</div> </div> </div> </div>SPOILER ALERT.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Elder Gods are the True Fae.<br /> The scientis of the enterprise are the Loyalists<br /> The Monsters are huntsmen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:46:46-08:00","id":809921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809888#post809888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SPOILER ALERT.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Elder Gods are the True Fae.<br /> The scientis of the enterprise are the Loyalists<br /> The Monsters are huntsmen</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more than that though. Think about how much Cabin in the Woods relies on the archetypes of horror stories for each country. The Old Gods care about stories in the exact same way as the Gentry. It may not be so apocalyptic if the story fails, but the themes of storytelling, convention, and deconstruction make it Changeling spot on, even if the Cabin itself is Grade A infrastructure. <br /> <br /> And I thought I couldn't love that movie even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:19:58-08:00","id":809944,"title":"","content":"Not my cup of tea. The Huntsmen - as NPCs - are a little over powered for my taste.<br /> Maybe I'll change my mind when we got more details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/571-nin","name":"Nin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:27:42-08:00","id":809947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809944#post809944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not my cup of tea. The Huntsmen - as NPCs - are a little over powered for my taste.<br /> Maybe I'll change my mind when we got more details.</div> </div> </div> </div> I may be starting a risky discussion by asking this, but...overpowered how? They have multiple built-in weaknesses.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If the Huntsmen are overpowered, what does that make the True Fae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-15-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:56:59-08:00","id":809963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809694#post809694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Huntsmen kill the True Fae who summon them, or conspire against the True Fae so that another will take that risk? Sure, they persist as immaterial entities in a sort of slumber when not on the Hunt, so another True Fae can still summon them. Unless an Arcadian law forbids them from doing that, whether subtly or forcibly, it sounds like something a deeply frustrated Huntsman might one day consider.<br /> <br /> Are the True Fae the only ones who can summon Huntsmen? One of the required ingredients is a True Fae's breath, which a clever changeling might steal or persuade into being given. Stealing or binding immaterial/abstract things is only fae, after all. If it is possible for other beings to summon Huntsmen, is the template of the Huntsman altered?<br /> <br /> What prevents Huntsmen from giving or &quot;losing&quot; their Arcadian weapons to perform an assisted suicide (other than their conflicted enjoyment of the Hunt)? Do the True Fae subject them to some nightmarish torture if they discover such &quot;cowardice&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The nutshell answer to all of this is the ritual.<br /> <br /> What keeps a Huntsman from turning on the True Fae? Ritual.<br /> What keeps a changeling from summoning a Huntsman? Ritual.<br /> What keeps a huntsman from losing their Arcadian weapons and committing assisted suicide? Ritual.<br /> <br /> Well, actually, that last one dying is worse for them than for humans, they can't actually lose their weapons unless a changeling knows the trick to breaking the bindings of Huntsman and Weapon, the fact that the weapon is a very powerful and personal identifier for them(Think security blanket meets phylactery-not to say that they can't put it aside and come after you, it's just not preferable), <i>and</i> the ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:59:25-08:00","id":809965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809761#post809761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I discussed the Huntsmen with my group, and one came up with a pretty interesting concept. What if a given Huntsman decides the only way to ever be immune to being sent on Hunts is to destroy reality/humanity? Granted, this wouldn't be a likely goal to actually achieve, but it'd sort of expand the Huntsman in question into a more dangerous antagonist. They'd delay and stall their hunts, killing more humans than necessary, blackmail Mages into widening this Abyss they think Huntsmen come from, damage Infrastructures, anything they can take down before finalizing the Hunt. Granted, they'd need to figure out HOW to damage reality, but.. that'd be even scarier. Goes from &quot;Im coming to get you&quot;, to &quot;I will do irreparable damage to your city, its people, and the things you love.. and THEN Im coming to get you&quot;:</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be really cool for a villain at people's games. As a large point though, the Huntsmen have some memory issues to deal with, and their relationship to humanity is still that of the fae. These are living stories of the hunt given form and persona. Those stories come from somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:05:08-08:00","id":809969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809963#post809963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nutshell answer to all of this is the ritual.<br /> <br /> What keeps a Huntsman from turning on the True Fae? Ritual.<br /> What keeps a changeling from summoning a Huntsman? Ritual.<br /> What keeps a huntsman from losing their Arcadian weapons and committing assisted suicide? Ritual.<br /> <br /> Well, actually, that last one dying is worse for them than for humans, they can't actually lose their weapons unless a changeling knows the trick to breaking the bindings of Huntsman and Weapon, the fact that the weapon is a very powerful and personal identifier for them(Think security blanket meets phylactery-not to say that they can't put it aside and come after you, it's just not preferable), <i>and</i> the ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummm... I have to apologize, but this didn't clarify much for me. Can I assume that future drafts will expand on possible methods for sabotaging or otherwise steering the Ritual in certain directions? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:14:42-08:00","id":809981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809761#post809761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I discussed the Huntsmen with my group, and one came up with a pretty interesting concept. What if a given Huntsman decides the only way to ever be immune to being sent on Hunts is to destroy reality/humanity? Granted, this wouldn't be a likely goal to actually achieve, but it'd sort of expand the Huntsman in question into a more dangerous antagonist. They'd delay and stall their hunts, killing more humans than necessary, blackmail Mages into widening this Abyss they think Huntsmen come from, damage Infrastructures, anything they can take down before finalizing the Hunt. Granted, they'd need to figure out HOW to damage reality, but.. that'd be even scarier. Goes from &quot;Im coming to get you&quot;, to &quot;I will do irreparable damage to your city, its people, and the things you love.. and THEN Im coming to get you&quot;:</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it appears that said omnicidal Huntsman is correct: fae are born from stories, and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DHSwvtHFsOU\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the only way to end stories is to end humanity.</b></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:19:31-08:00","id":809984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809969#post809969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ummm... I have to apologize, but this didn't clarify much for me. Can I assume that future drafts will expand on possible methods for sabotaging or otherwise steering the Ritual in certain directions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong ritual.<br /> <br /> There's an order to these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:34:38-08:00","id":809993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809965#post809965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be really cool for a villain at people's games. As a large point though, the Huntsmen have some memory issues to deal with, and their relationship to humanity is still that of the fae. These are living stories of the hunt given form and persona. Those stories come from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, Changeling 2e really is Cabin in the Woods! Pretty much all of those monsters are shout outs to other genre films. Now I'm imagining Fae taking inspiration from the Cenobytes, Sandworms, Freddy, and Dementors when making their Huntsmen. As if the Gentry needed to be more terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:51:54-08:00","id":810000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809984#post809984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong ritual.<br /> <br /> There's an order to these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes and no. Yes, there's an order to these things, but no, there is also the summoning ritual and the laws behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:53:07-08:00","id":810001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809849#post809849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Sasquatch,Godzilla,Loch Ness,King Kong,Goblin,Ghoul,a Zombie with no conscious...&quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A true fae triyng to choose wwhich spirits of hunt he should send to eart now</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is always more Kanye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T18:40:29-08:00","id":810440,"title":"","content":"Will there be suggestions for making Huntsmen more threatening for advanced characters? I've been running a game where the PCs started with 25, and particularly in the case of the Summer bruisers it's unlikely a Huntsman without contracts would survive using their Approach, which tends to be direct combat<br /> <br /> Also, is there anything preventing a Changeling from 'betraying' an extremely powerful member of the freehold who's a seasoned Huntsmen killer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T18:49:59-08:00","id":810441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=810440#post810440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be suggestions for making Huntsmen more threatening for advanced characters? I've been running a game where the PCs started with 25, and particularly in the case of the Summer bruisers it's unlikely a Huntsman without contracts would survive using their Approach, which tends to be direct combat<br /> <br /> Also, is there anything preventing a Changeling from 'betraying' an extremely powerful member of the freehold who's a seasoned Huntsmen killer?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the first: Yes, there is.<br /> <br /> Be clever and use your opponents strengths against them. Don't tackle them on their own ground under you've got your hands on their rugs.<br /> <br /> As to the second.<br /> <br /> First off, the Huntsman would have to be after said killer. Second, they would have to think it was worth it to grant a changeling a Token of Repreive. Usually, that means that you're not in control, the scenario where you betray them will end up meaning you betray them, because it's engineered that way, never mind the power of you promising by the Wyrd to turn someone in. Thirdly, Oh yeah, the fucking Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Zeroeth off, there's no such thing as a seasoned Huntsman killer anymore than there's such a thing as a seasoned Strix or Idigam killer. The Huntsmen <i>are not fucking easy to take down</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-16-2016, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T20:22:33-08:00","id":810462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=810441#post810441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the first: Yes, there is.<br /> <br /> Be clever and use your opponents strengths against them. Don't tackle them on their own ground under you've got your hands on their rugs.<br /> <br /> As to the second.<br /> <br /> First off, the Huntsman would have to be after said killer. Second, they would have to think it was worth it to grant a changeling a Token of Repreive. Usually, that means that you're not in control, the scenario where you betray them will end up meaning you betray them, because it's engineered that way, never mind the power of you promising by the Wyrd to turn someone in. Thirdly, Oh yeah, the fucking Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Zeroeth off, there's no such thing as a season Huntsman killer anymore than there's such a thing as a seasoned Strix or Idigam killer. The Huntsmen <i>are not fucking easy to take down</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Quick question about the wyd in promises,back in the tirs editon,the core idea of Pledged is that you promise to do something to the wyrd and the wyrd gives you something to make you more able to achieve what you've promised,or the wyrd gives you something as a prize after you finish your mission.<br /> is that concept being expanded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T20:43:29-08:00","id":810468,"title":"","content":"It's getting streamlined and tied closer to the original source material.<br /> <br /> I understand the DSG breifly covers Sealing, Oaths, and Bargains. so you might want to check that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:38:22-08:00","id":810638,"title":"","content":"so, for my grumpy &quot;destrroy the world&quot; Huntsman, it might only be feasible if he tries it mummy style--perhaps there is a Cult that worships and seeks a particular Huntsman when he arrives, heaping personel, memories, and additional gear on them, even offering up one of their number for their First Kill (if they find him quickly enough). I mean, said Huntsman isnt likely to help them in return, and might kill them cuz Huntsman, but... I could see some big apocalyptic cult hoping to feed the whole world to the Wild Hunt, who works to remind huntsmen that their artistic hunt can be..expanded to someday prevent the agony of existing ever again. I mean, this wouldnt be the default, this would be a weird one-off twist to change things up if a group ever gets too... used to dealing with a Hunstman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:51:41-08:00","id":810644,"title":"","content":"Loyalists can and probably will maintain cults not only for their own gain but for the benefit of a Huntsman showing up. So, yeah, very Arisen like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:47:04-08:00","id":811746,"title":"","content":"In 1st ed, killing one's Fetch provided a sense of closure (reflected with mechanics) while befriending one's Fetch gave a different kind of acceptance (though without mechanics). Will there be something similar for permanently killing one's Huntsman? Befriending doesn't seem to be a possibility in this case. Huntsmen apparently have a piece of the Changeling they're made for within them; if a Huntsman is destroyed, what happens to that piece? (Probably it'll be left up to the ST, but will there be suggestions/IC rumors about what happens?) I'm not expecting answers, but I'm hoping ideas like this are in the un-spoilered half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:13:49-08:00","id":812004,"title":"","content":"Not a piece of the changeling so much as an emblem of the changeling. The Changeling can pick up the emblem and keep it from the True Fae once the Huntsman is destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:20:43-08:00","id":812010,"title":"","content":"Here's something of a scary thought: The good news is someone destroyed the huntsman that was after you. The bad news is that the person who did it took your Icon and wants you to do him just one little favor in exchange for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:03:33-08:00","id":812043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812004#post812004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a piece of the changeling so much as an emblem of the changeling. The Changeling can pick up the emblem and keep it from the True Fae once the Huntsman is destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Emblem&quot; being &quot;magically significant representation of a Changeling&quot; and not &quot;part of a Changeling's soul.&quot; &quot;Part of a Changeling's soul&quot; would be an Icon, which can be found in the Hedge, and is useful to Huntsmen to track said Changeling, but is not part of making a Huntsman, and when held by a Changeling, eventually poofs back to the Hedge. (I think.)<br /> <br /> Now I'm really curious about the differences between emblems and Icons, and which ones are used in making Fetches (presumably Icons?), and if one's emblem may become useless/untied if one goes through a dramatic enough change, or if an emblem mutates as a Changeling changes, and if one can have more than one emblem (it was mentioned that the Gentry <i>usually</i> only have enough material for one Huntsman per Changeling, implying sometimes there's more), and if emblem should be capitalized or not, and so on. But these are a) outside the scope of this topic, and b) probably in an un-spoilered part of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:04:41-08:00","id":812044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812010#post812010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something of a scary thought: The good news is someone destroyed the huntsman that was after you. The bad news is that the person who did it took your Icon and wants you to do him just one little favor in exchange for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not an icon, but that is seriously scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:07:07-08:00","id":812046,"title":"","content":"For the record, emblem is not the word for it, it's just the word I use because there isn't a proper word for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:29:23-08:00","id":812061,"title":"","content":"There's something intriguing about the specificity of the Huntsman summoning ritual. It brings Nobilis to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:32:56-08:00","id":812064,"title":"","content":"Can the true fae or other changelings use the emblem for other kinds of process besides the Huntsmen Creation Ritual (tm)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:46:09-08:00","id":812074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812061#post812061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something intriguing about the specificity of the Huntsman summoning ritual. It brings Nobilis to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea if the person who wrote it has read Nobilis, but I do love me some Nobilis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milloni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the true fae or other changelings use the emblem for other kinds of process besides the Huntsmen Creation Ritual (tm)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet.<br /> <br /> No, you're not giving me ideas for supplement material, what are you talking about?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:51:56-08:00","id":812083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812074#post812074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you're not giving me ideas for supplement material, what are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume some kind of sympathetic magic due to the possession of an item close to them. Like a forced oath or something to that effect? Maybe the ability to scry on the changeling in question? I assume it's something to those effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:55:49-08:00","id":812088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812083#post812083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I assume some kind of sympathetic magic due to the possession of an item close to them. Like a forced oath or something to that effect? Maybe the ability to scry on the changeling in question? I assume it's something to those effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can come up with more interesting options.<br /> <br /> But like I said, nothing yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:01:27-08:00","id":812096,"title":"","content":"Do you guys think there may be other spirits besides Hunting in arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:09:10-08:00","id":812101,"title":"","content":"THere might be other fae spirits. It's not something I think I'd want to explore too much at the risk of starting a thing with Werewolf, but I wouldn't close the door per se.<br /> <br /> What sort of fae spirits were you thinking of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:16:20-08:00","id":812108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812101#post812101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THere might be other fae spirits. It's not something I think I'd want to explore too much at the risk of starting a thing with Werewolf, but I wouldn't close the door per se.<br /> <br /> What sort of fae spirits were you thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm think all stories that are really really old and really really powerful have spirits in arcadia.<br /> <br /> the story of two people falling in love and getting together despite adversity,Story of a insignifanct person going in a quest for glory and becoming someone important,Stories of war between two factions<br /> those archetypes and some more are just as fixed in the human psyche,or other living things, as the story of hunting, and so in Aradia,they are represented by Spirits of Love, Spirits Of Adveture,Spirits of War","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:19:26-08:00","id":812113,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> *shifts through some files*<br /> <br /> Some stories are older than others. Still, there's an idea to explore here.<br /> <br /> (God I wish I could have contributed, like, just one line to the Neolithic Crossover section)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:03:00-08:00","id":812153,"title":"","content":"I'll just leave this here as a Neolithic Crossover idea: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sorcerer_(cave_art\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sorcerer_(cave_art</a>)<br /> <br /> The Wolf Must Hunt, but the Wolf doesn't make it into a sport.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:33:03-08:00","id":812205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812108#post812108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'm think all stories that are really really old and really really powerful have spirits in arcadia.<br /> <br /> the story of two people falling in love and getting together despite adversity,Story of a insignifanct person going in a quest for glory and becoming someone important,Stories of war between two factions<br /> those archetypes and some more are just as fixed in the human psyche,or other living things, as the story of hunting, and so in Aradia,they are represented by Spirits of Love, Spirits Of Adveture,Spirits of War</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the use of the word &quot;spirit&quot; when discussing Huntsmen and other hypothetical animated constructs made by the Gentry is vague enough to permit other ideas. Who knows, the spirits could actually be entities from the Temenos or Anima Mundi instead of the denizens of the Shadow. Both are on similar levels of primal significance, from cave paintings to creepypastas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:46:35-08:00","id":812212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806721#post806721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pledges, yes. Contracts, don't think so. In Game, how changelings do it. Equinox Road still serves you well. Out of game, actual mechanical advice, that'll be another thing to slip into a supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div> In Equinox,To Create a contract the changeling had to great feat to solidify the contract in reality,if you wanted a contract with reflections you'd have to build hundreds of mirror and put them in different locations,or put a single gigantic mirror in a highly populated are. if you wanted a contract with some kid of animal youd have to built a wildlife reserve for that animal,for a contract with darkness you'd have to blackout new york city of 24 hours etc...<br /> And if you wanted to built a Changeling Court you'd have to something even more important,something downright epic,and after you created a court,the court founders could never leave. are thos things being changed? i really hope not,cause those are some of my favorite things about the game,the possiblity of creating new things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T21:37:50-08:00","id":812385,"title":"","content":"In Equinox Road, Spirits can't really exist in the hedge, as they get converted to Hobs (swapping out their essence for glamour). Are Spirits now allowed to be in the Hedge as... spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":287,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","user":"Wildfire","date":". 01-20-2016, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T22:27:26-08:00","id":812393,"title":"","content":"Fae spirits are not Shadow Spirits. The distinction at this point isn't clarified, as one rarely deals with an Arcadian Spirit of the Hunt except when they are manifested as Huntsmen, but they aren't the same thing as, say, a Spirit of the Hunt that the Uratha would have to deal with. The distinction is one of those things I'm itching to go at in a supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T22:31:15-08:00","id":812394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812212#post812212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Equinox,To Create a contract the changeling had to great feat to solidify the contract in reality,if you wanted a contract with reflections you'd have to build hundreds of mirror and put them in different locations,or put a single gigantic mirror in a highly populated are. if you wanted a contract with some kid of animal youd have to built a wildlife reserve for that animal,for a contract with darkness you'd have to blackout new york city of 24 hours etc...<br /> And if you wanted to built a Changeling Court you'd have to something even more important,something downright epic,and after you created a court,the court founders could never leave. are thos things being changed? i really hope not,cause those are some of my favorite things about the game,the possiblity of creating new things</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're asking if we cover it in the core, we don't-we're stuffed to the gills, and in-game contract and court creation consequences were not something we could address.<br /> <br /> If you're asking if that's been removed, the answer is no. If it's not in the new core, first edition rules are assumed to be in place unless contradicted in the core or later supplemental material. All those things apply until we say otherwise. Currently, there's no plan to talk about that in the supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:02:14-08:00","id":812500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812394#post812394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're asking if we cover it in the core, we don't-we're stuffed to the gills, and in-game contract and court creation consequences were not something we could address.<br /> <br /> If you're asking if that's been removed, the answer is no. If it's not in the new core, first edition rules are assumed to be in place unless contradicted in the core or later supplemental material. All those things apply until we say otherwise. Currently, there's no plan to talk about that in the supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice,it would be a bummer if that'd be removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:34:06-08:00","id":812513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812500#post812500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice,it would be a bummer if that'd be removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how every court is supposed to have a Contract it has affinity to, having it be so annoyingly hard makes it seem like it'd be better if it was removed IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:44:09-08:00","id":812522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812513#post812513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how every court is supposed to have a Contract it has affinity to, having it be so annoyingly hard makes it seem like it'd be better if it was removed IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>there's always room for common ground,maybe to create a contract and a court,a group of changelings wouldn't need to be something gigantic and historical,but still some great feat,would be necessary.<br /> I like the sense of Irony here. Because the Main reasons the Courts are there is to defend ourselves agains the huntsmen and sometimes Even the Fae themselves. But to create a Court we would need to do something that might as well bring them right up to our doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:34:40-08:00","id":812633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812108#post812108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'm think all stories that are really really old and really really powerful have spirits in arcadia.<br /> <br /> the story of two people falling in love and getting together despite adversity,Story of a insignifanct person going in a quest for glory and becoming someone important,Stories of war between two factions<br /> those archetypes and some more are just as fixed in the human psyche,or other living things, as the story of hunting, and so in Aradia,they are represented by Spirits of Love, Spirits Of Adveture,Spirits of War</div> </div> </div> </div> I like the idea of the Fae spirits being stories, it makes them very different from shadow spirits.<br /> <br /> Like a Shadow Spirit might be a spirit of a wolf, or the conceptual spirit of research done on wolves.<br /> <br /> But there might be a type of Fae Spirit called the Big Bad Wolf Spirits, and each individual Big Bad Wolf Spirit is a variation of the big bad wolf stories, like one might be a variation of the Big Bad Wolf in little red riding hood sland another might be a variation of the three little pigs.<br /> <br /> And they don't have a heirarchy, don't feed on other spirits, ect... They're just basically a sentient story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:13:50-08:00","id":812659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812633#post812633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea of the Fae spirits being stories, it makes them very different from shadow spirits.<br /> <br /> Like a Shadow Spirit might be a spirit of a wolf, or the conceptual spirit of research done on wolves.<br /> <br /> But there might be a type of Fae Spirit called the Big Bad Wolf Spirits, and each individual Big Bad Wolf Spirit is a variation of the big bad wolf stories, like one might be a variation of the Big Bad Wolf in little red riding hood sland another might be a variation of the three little pigs.<br /> <br /> And they don't have a heirarchy, don't feed on other spirits, ect... They're just basically a sentient story.</div> </div> </div> </div> HECK YES! that'd be soooooooooo great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:14:30-08:00","id":812660,"title":"","content":"Yeah, although you need to be careful to make them distinct from Astral spirits. The Big Bad Wolf himself is almost certainly a Walker, and likely a powerful one at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:21:05-08:00","id":812666,"title":"","content":"Astral Spirits are Goeticia now and are spirits of the soul. Fae Spirits would simply be stories imprinted in the Glamour of Arcadia and possibly the hedge.<br /> <br /> I don't think they'd have things like numen.<br /> <br /> An interesting question would be could they're be an infernal version,a Fae Spirit possessed/corrupted by a demonic whisperer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:31:15-08:00","id":812708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812666#post812666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astral Spirits are Goeticia now and are spirits of the soul. Fae Spirits would simply be stories imprinted in the Glamour of Arcadia and possibly the hedge.<br /> <br /> I don't think they'd have things like numen.<br /> <br /> An interesting question would be could they're be an infernal version,a Fae Spirit possessed/corrupted by a demonic whisperer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well if I recall some Mages think that the Hedge and Arcadia are tied to the abyss somehow. So it might be possible that the Fae are Goetia that have been warped by the unreality of the Abyss, in an area of the Astral that has been also warped by the unreality of the Abyss. Might explain why the whole realm is a mess of madness and alien geometries. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:00:37-08:00","id":812725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812708#post812708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well if I recall some Mages think that the Hedge and Arcadia are tied to the abyss somehow. So it might be possible that the Fae are Goetia that have been warped by the unreality of the Abyss, in an area of the Astral that has been also warped by the unreality of the Abyss. Might explain why the whole realm is a mess of madness and alien geometries. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dave shot that right in the ass with Second Edition Mage. The default now is that mages assume it isn't, with a few cases it is.<br /> <br /> Thank god for that. The Arcadia argument is one of the most annoying theories out there.<br /> <br /> Anyways, random tangent as it relates to spirits and stuff: In my mind, in the Neolithic setting, the fae are facing a contest in the same way the mages and werewolves are. Previously, there was only the Wild Hunt, with changelings coming from people who got involved as predator and prey and escaping that. As humanity has started moving away from that, a new set of stories rise up from Arcadia, and now there's a shift of power between the Huntsmen and the Gentry. An Epic Legend, rather than a war.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if that's what they're going to do. I feel like they're just going to stick to the Gentry having always been. But man, part of me really likes the idea of the Huntsmen as the Dawn Rulers of Arcadia being usurped by the Lords of the Estates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:00:51-08:00","id":812726,"title":"","content":"That was Mage 1e, I hear the cosmology in Mage 2e is different, so I don't know if that will make sense or not, we won't know until Mage 2e is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:20:54-08:00","id":812747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812725#post812725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave shot that right in the ass with Second Edition Mage. The default now is that mages assume it isn't, with a few cases it is.<br /> <br /> Thank god for that. The Arcadia argument is one of the most annoying theories out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait, what do mages think Arcadia and the Hedge are then? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:21:09-08:00","id":812748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812725#post812725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave shot that right in the ass with Second Edition Mage. The default now is that mages assume it isn't, with a few cases it is.<br /> <br /> Thank god for that. The Arcadia argument is one of the most annoying theories out there.<br /> <br /> Anyways, random tangent as it relates to spirits and stuff: In my mind, in the Neolithic setting, the fae are facing a contest in the same way the mages and werewolves are. Previously, there was only the Wild Hunt, with changelings coming from people who got involved as predator and prey and escaping that. As humanity has started moving away from that, a new set of stories rise up from Arcadia, and now there's a shift of power between the Huntsmen and the Gentry. An Epic Legend, rather than a war.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if that's what they're going to do. I feel like they're just going to stick to the Gentry having always been. But man, part of me really likes the idea of the Huntsmen as the Dawn Rulers of Arcadia being usurped by the Lords of the Estates.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you think the spirits of the hunt chased people as spirits or they also used a ritual to have a physical body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:32:22-08:00","id":812754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812747#post812747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, what do mages think Arcadia and the Hedge are then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something else. Mage Arcadia is the Supernal overlay the Acanthus observe through Mage Sight; it's a conceptual space rather than a place you can physically go to like Faerie.<br /> <br /> Depending on how much of Imperial Mysteries carries over and trickles down to the Travelers, the Hedge could be viewed as a massive shared dream-pathway between Faerie and Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:33:33-08:00","id":812756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812747#post812747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait, what do mages think Arcadia and the Hedge are then? <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mysteries to explore. Per mage's modus operandi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812748#post812748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the spirits of the hunt chased people as spirits or they also used a ritual to have a physical body?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this theory of mine(NOTE: THIS NOT CANON!), they still had physical bodies. Whether they were reduced to spirits by the Gentry or if it's just that really old stories turn into spirits isn't something totally clear, though I favor the latter over the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:19:27-08:00","id":812777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812756#post812756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mysteries to explore. Per mage's modus operandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, typically though there's some thought among mages that &quot;fits&quot; certain aspects of other splats into their own understanding of the cosmology. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:25:10-08:00","id":812780,"title":"","content":"So, point of clarification: how fast does the Yearning economy typically flow for a huntsman? At first I thought they'd be spending it kind of slow and careful, but the more I read and chewed (especially them using instead of glamour in oneiro-fuckery) it seems like it might be faster - more like 2E WP or like glamour than something more deliberate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:25:44-08:00","id":812781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812777#post812777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that, typically though there's some thought among mages that &quot;fits&quot; certain aspects of other splats into their own understanding of the cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more a problem with the fandom than an actual facet of Awakened thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:27:09-08:00","id":812782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812777#post812777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that, typically though there's some thought among mages that &quot;fits&quot; certain aspects of other splats into their own understanding of the cosmology. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. No. That's more a Mage <i>fan</i> thing to do.<br /> <br /> Mages recognize that not only is it impossible for <i>everything</i> to fit into their understanding, they actually recognize <i>most everything</i> doesn't fit into explanations of the Supernal-or even Abyssal. The Arcana are tools of examination, the Realms are best used as models for comparison. Mages don't think they have the answer to everything, they know they don't. What they <i>do</i> think is that they can understand how everything works in its' own context.<br /> <br /> For more information, I invite you to trawl through David Brookshaw's posts. This has been a long standing point for him in regards to Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:29:16-08:00","id":812784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812781#post812781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more a problem with the fandom than an actual facet of Awakened thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>So awakened don't try to fit new information into a frame based on what they already know (Like a puzzle piece)? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:36:06-08:00","id":812791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812784#post812784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So awakened don't try to fit new information into a frame based on what they already know (Like a puzzle piece)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as that makes a shitty starting point for when you barely know anything? Yeah.<br /> <br /> Lay-werewolves have an excuse to try and crowbar any given incursion into having something to do with the Shadow because they're by nature inclined to kind of be busybodies about the places they claim responsibility for and demons know full well that the God-Machine might've done any kind of weirdass shenanigans that might mean messing with a strange supernatural being results in their being melted down for spare processes, but when your starting point is &quot;I saw the conceptual building blocks of the universe in heavily metaphorical terms, and most of that stuff is clearly not present in any of the world as I normally experience it, even the especially magical parts&quot; it's kind of a colossal failure of process to try to jam the Underworld into having some immediate relation to Stygia just because both have something to do with death.<br /> <br /> You learn the separate pieces first. Threading them into a functional map comes after you have half an idea what you're talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:40:24-08:00","id":812795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812747#post812747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, what do mages think Arcadia and the Hedge are then?</div> </div> </div> </div>My own game theories - that most Acanthus adhere to - is that Changeling Arcadia is some kind Lower Depths reflection of Supernal Arcadia - just like Underworld have wierd relation with Stygia and Shadow Realm with Primal Wild. It works enough good in story terms, even if mages see that this theory has holes. Like <i>a lots</i> of them. And they <i>are </i>other interpretation of idea on Changeling Arcadia in mage society, also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:43:32-08:00","id":812800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812791#post812791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as that makes a shitty starting point for when you barely know anything? Yeah.<br /> <br /> Lay-werewolves have an excuse to try and crowbar any given incursion into having something to do with the Shadow because they're by nature inclined to kind of be busybodies about the places they claim responsibility for and demons know full well that the God-Machine might've done any kind of weirdass shenanigans that might mean messing with a strange supernatural being results in their being melted down for spare processes, but when your starting point is &quot;I saw the conceptual building blocks of the universe in heavily metaphorical terms, and most of that stuff is clearly not present in any of the world as I normally experience it, even the especially magical parts&quot; it's kind of a colossal failure of process to try to jam the Underworld into having some immediate relation to Stygia just because both have something to do with death.<br /> <br /> You learn the separate pieces first. Threading them into a functional map comes after you have half an idea what you're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, because one doesn't have all the pieces there's no point in trying to build a framework of understanding? I don't know how I feel about that. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:50:36-08:00","id":812810,"title":"","content":"They build frameworks of understanding, it's just they have desire to drop it into terms of the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Let's use fae for a second. Mages first encountering them will note them as creatures largely identified by Fate, with strong strains of Time, Life, Forces, Matter, some decent twistings of Space and Mind, strange relationships to Death and Prime, none to Spirit. They'll explore the Fate and discover the Wyrd and it's peculiar traits that marks it as different from their concept of Fate(and from Mummy's Fate as an aside), they'll explore how the Life, Forces, and Matter all pull to zeitgeists and future dreams in relation to Time and Mind, and try and find out just what makes Arcadia tick.<br /> <br /> What they won't do is say &quot;Oh, these are Anachronisms and Moirae from Arcadia&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:53:45-08:00","id":812812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812800#post812800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, because one doesn't have all the pieces there's no point in trying to build a framework of understanding? I don't know how I feel about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're doing an astounding job of either not listening or being deliberately obtuse.<br /> <br /> The Awakened <i>do</i> build a framework of understanding. To the extent that that framework is not personalized, it is chiefly concerned with whether a given element of the cosmology is from the Supernal or the Abyss (which is not a lot of things), the various parts of the Fallen World (which is most of the things they are likely to encounter), or the Lower Depths (which is not a lot of things for a different reason than the Supernal and the Abyss).<br /> <br /> They can use their knowledge of the Arcana to discern relevant information about a given phenomenon, but the breadth of that middle category relative to the other two (and especially the first one) is reason enough for them not to claim that the Divine Fire has any direct relation to the Aether just because it registers to Mage Sight that detects the energies Prime and/or Forces deals with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:54:55-08:00","id":812814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812810#post812810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They build frameworks of understanding, it's just they have desire to drop it into terms of the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Let's use fae for a second. Mages first encountering them will note them as creatures largely identified by Fate, with strong strains of Time, Life, Forces, Matter, some decent twistings of Space and Mind, strange relationships to Death and Prime, none to Spirit. They'll explore the Fate and discover the Wyrd and it's peculiar traits that marks it as different from their concept of Fate(and from Mummy's Fate as an aside), they'll explore how the Life, Forces, and Matter all pull to zeitgeists and future dreams in relation to Time and Mind, and try and find out just what makes Arcadia tick.<br /> <br /> What they won't do is say &quot;Oh, these are Anachronisms and Moirae from Arcadia&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't really talking about the Supernal Arcadia and the Faerie Arcadia being the same thing. They're similar, but what I more meant was like, where would you place it in the cosmology in the great scheme of things? From what I've seen of the Faerie Arcadia, it looks like an area of the Shadow/Astral that has been tainted by the Abyss. Hence all the alien geometries and utter strangeness therein. It's a place you can travel to, it's not quite the Abyss, not quite the Shadow, and not Quite the Astral, but shares aspects of all three. It's a physical place you can travel, it runs on &quot;nonsense&quot; and alien geometries that don't make sense, and it's shaped like our fables not unlike what you'd see in the Astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:58:27-08:00","id":812818,"title":"","content":"y'know,Trying to fit all supernatural beings,supernatural objects and places in one single banner is somethings Beast do more than other splats,they believe everything started with the Dark Mother,and no matter how different Beast are from all the others beings in the Chroniles of Darkness they still have a underlying connection that is like family bond because they all are descedend from the Mother.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:00:56-08:00","id":812820,"title":"","content":"It depends on the individual Mage. Some would reach that conclusion, more would reach the conclusion that it is something markedly different based on the actual metaphysics of the Shadow and the Abyss in relation to Fae Arcadia and the Hedge. The world of the Fae is something mages have several theories about, and they'll be working on it for centuries to come.<br /> <br /> But your theory is something that might be done by a mage, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:21:17-08:00","id":812849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812812#post812812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're doing an astounding job of either not listening or being deliberately obtuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just a break-down in communication between us, but neither of us seem to be able to get our point across to one another effectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812820#post812820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the individual Mage. Some would reach that conclusion, more would reach the conclusion that it is something markedly different based on the actual metaphysics of the Shadow and the Abyss in relation to Fae Arcadia and the Hedge. The world of the Fae is something mages have several theories about, and they'll be working on it for centuries to come.<br /> <br /> But your theory is something that might be done by a mage, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that there is speculation, many different ideas about why this is here, why it exists, what it's purpose is. I guess more the ruling out is what I have problems with?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:57:33-08:00","id":812975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812814#post812814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't really talking about the Supernal Arcadia and the Faerie Arcadia being the same thing. They're similar, but what I more meant was like, where would you place it in the cosmology in the great scheme of things?...</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9WFJTQlZfcDA1aE0/edit\" target=\"_blank\">2ed preview for Acathus</a> seems to be strongly arguing for a united Arcadia:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AcanthusPreview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Then again, the Oracles may have only borrowed part of a fairy road for their own use, clearing the thickest thorns to let mortal souls rise. In any event, <b>Fae gods send hunters and other servants, and natives descended from mortal and fairy beings cut lairs from the undergrowth</b>--otherwise, they\u2019d have no place to dwell in the cluttered Watchtower. Ancient mages wrote of a Watchtower dominated by twisted, vine-corrupted woods....<br /> <br /> ...When a soul enters their domain, it joins the story. <b>If the Fae lures her in, a potential Witch loses her soul to it, becoming a god\u2019s hollowed out puppet. </b>Don\u2019t drink or eat what they offer. Don\u2019t fall in love, or lash out from hate, because you\u2019ll trade your destiny for theirs. The Fae build attractive, passionate stories, however. <b>His lover was once the god\u2019s slave. What will he give up to win his memory back?</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>The text doesn't out-and-out <i>say</i> that Changelings are those that got lured to Supernal!Arcadia by the Fae and that pre-awakened Mages that wander in via the Hedge risk losing pieces of their soul and getting Lost instead, but it does waggle its eyebrows in strong implication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:03:14-08:00","id":812979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812975#post812975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9WFJTQlZfcDA1aE0/edit\" target=\"_blank\">2ed preview for Acathus</a> seems to be strongly arguing for a united Arcadia:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The text doesn't out-and-out <i>say</i> that Changelings are those that got lured to Supernal!Arcadia by the Fae and that pre-awakened Mages that wander in via the Hedge risk losing pieces of their soul and getting Lost instead, but it does waggle its eyebrows in strong implication.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/303875-the-hedge-true-fae-and-mage?p=304302#post304302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1E, Arcadia and Arcadia were heavily implied to be the same place, with enough wiggle room for you to say that they weren't.<br /> In 2E, Arcadia and Arcadia are pretty clearly <i>not</i> the same place, with enough wiggle room for you to say that they are.<br /> <br /> You can count the Changeling crossover hints in Awakening - both editions - on the fingers of one hand. The &quot;controversy&quot; is almost all from the Changeling line's side, and it's too early to say if it'll continue. Who knows? Changeling 2E might not mention mages <i>ever</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly intend to not mention mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:14:23-08:00","id":812985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812979#post812979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I certainly intend to not mention mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd much prefer them to be separate and un-related. Thanks for linking the Mage dev's perspective; I missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:38:48-08:00","id":813008,"title":"","content":"Still not super keen on the whole &quot;each splat has it's own unique cosmology and never bump into one another&quot; angle, but I'm not the developer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:57:10-08:00","id":813014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813008#post813008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not super keen on the whole &quot;each splat has it's own unique cosmology and never bump into one another&quot; angle, but I'm not the developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they do bump into each other. I mean, look at vampire's core book and all the stray mentions at the god-machine. Or demon having changelings running around being bunyips, or how it talks about the Principle from Promethean in it's Core Book. Or with Beast literally tying everything except Demon together under the Dark Mother. Or hunter with .... everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:59:19-08:00","id":813017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813008#post813008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not super keen on the whole &quot;each splat has it's own unique cosmology and never bump into one another&quot; angle, but I'm not the developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then mesh them together yourself.<br /> <br /> The games are developed individually, because that's the best way to focus on the things they want to achieve. If you were developing Mummy and you had to constantly worry about how Fate relates to the Wyrd or whatever, you'd be there forever, and ultimately it'd be a poorer game for it.<br /> <br /> Looking for a coherent overall picture is a waste of time becuase there isn't one; there's just the default setting. It's not great, but it's not meant to be; just useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:03:55-08:00","id":813021,"title":"","content":"I'm actually sort of with you on that. Well, okay, the bumping into each other part, not the unique cosmology-one of my favorite things is how discordant the world of ChroD is, how no one has a damn clue what the soul actually is and how there's viable cases for both the God-Machine and Kepheria+Atum making the world and such. But I like it when the mythologies collide and clash. One of the highlights of a Demon game I got to run was roleplaying as Anpu spitting disdain for the God-Machine and demons alike while still laying out a few secrets and a choice for the PC's.<br /> <br /> I actually <i>would</i> write a section on what mages think of the fairy world, and I'd even like to blur lines and suggest connections-but I wouldn't want to do it in such a way that suggest greater unity, but rather greater mystery, with neither side being validated.<br /> <br /> Because, really, that's the core of a unified cosmology in Chronicles-Everything eventually becomes unknowable. The more they come together, the more incomprehensible it all is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:07:25-08:00","id":813024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813008#post813008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not super keen on the whole &quot;each splat has it's own unique cosmology and never bump into one another&quot; angle</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what that means and I'll tell you for free that the references to Mage in Changeling 1e didn't bring much to the table \u2014 I know I didn't enjoy the attitude behind making the Unmade a thing, and that's a phenomenon that's almost entirely based in the terrible confluence of &quot;people think mages know everything&quot; and &quot;changelings come from a part of the setting that shares a common name with one of the Supernal Realms.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gameline-level supernatural beings are rare and clustered enough that it's entirely reasonable for a given city to only host one or two types of them without extensive travel or particular interest. Werewolves attempt to manage the Shadow as the only ground-level natives with a sense for Earthly human interests and Sin-Eaters deal with the attendant issues of representing one of the most mysterious processes of one of the most mysterious otherworlds, but the Shadow and the Underworld as Dangerous Places Where Spirits And Ghosts Come From are bluebook mortal material.<br /> <br /> Mage readily offers its characters the chance to investigate the Shadow and the Underworld as particularly approachable mysterious realms alongside the types of weird shit you can get up to in the Astral, but that's not the same thing as having the answers to what the timeless chaotic story-world that fairies come from is when that place is also the home of countless gods and monsters beyond mortal ken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:26:29-08:00","id":813029,"title":"","content":"Having some things be connected is fine, but with the Arcadias, there's something of a power imbalance. Changelings flee the Fae (for the most part), because the Gentry are so very powerful and unknowable; taking one on is, quite accurately, an epic endeavor. <br /> <br /> But Mages can summon beings of Supernal!Arcadia. Making those beings <i>also</i> the Gentry means that the PCs of one splat are trivially commanding the biggest bads of another. Which is not conductive to Mages and Changelings being of a power level. (I am sure there are ways to make it work, but I still don't like it.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:34:30-08:00","id":813036,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that, assuming both Arcadias are the same, that mages are summoning hobgoblins, not the True Fae.<br /> <br /> Of course, the True Fae might answer a summon if it amuses them, with disastrous results for the mage. But then again, you can do that for non-Acanthi as well. Send a Qashmallim to an Obrimos, a Kerberos to a Moros, a Rank 8+ Spirit to a Thyrsus, a demon-like Horror to a Mastigos (or even a God-Machine Angel, if you like being foreshadow-y).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:37:48-08:00","id":813041,"title":"","content":"I'm more inclined to let a Lucifuge summon a True Fae than a mage.<br /> <br /> But yeah, no. The Arcadia Question is more or less answered with a resounding No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:04:53-08:00","id":813056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813014#post813014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they do bump into each other. I mean, look at vampire's core book and all the stray mentions at the god-machine. Or demon having changelings running around being bunyips, or how it talks about the Principle from Promethean in it's Core Book. Or with Beast literally tying everything except Demon together under the Dark Mother. Or hunter with .... everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more cosmology, not them physically bumping into one another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813021#post813021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually sort of with you on that. Well, okay, the bumping into each other part, not the unique cosmology-one of my favorite things is how discordant the world of ChroD is, how no one has a damn clue what the soul actually is and how there's viable cases for both the God-Machine and Kepheria+Atum making the world and such. But I like it when the mythologies collide and clash. One of the highlights of a Demon game I got to run was roleplaying as Anpu spitting disdain for the God-Machine and demons alike while still laying out a few secrets and a choice for the PC's.<br /> <br /> I actually <i>would</i> write a section on what mages think of the fairy world, and I'd even like to blur lines and suggest connections-but I wouldn't want to do it in such a way that suggest greater unity, but rather greater mystery, with neither side being validated.<br /> <br /> Because, really, that's the core of a unified cosmology in Chronicles-Everything eventually becomes unknowable. The more they come together, the more incomprehensible it all is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing I don't like about a unique cosmology for every flavor is that it starts to look cluttered and often times seems like the wheel is being reinvented each time. I'm just wondering though, ArcaneArts, why the two Arcadias being the same would be bad? Not saying that's my chosen interpretation, but what makes it bad? Personally speaking I like the idea of &quot;Arcadia&quot; being a place that is abyss tainted somehow as a more favored interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:10:35-08:00","id":813057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813056#post813056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant more cosmology, not them physically bumping into one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of what I said was cosmology... Especially beast... Tying cosmology together is like one of it's themes.... I mean god, everything all links up to the Dark Mother except for Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-20-2016, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:12:38-08:00","id":813058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813057#post813057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of what I said was cosmology... Especially beast... Tying cosmology together is like one of it's themes....</div> </div> </div> </div>In so far as the Begotten fit everything else in familiar terms because their perspective gives them reasons to believe the associations. Reasons which... aren't necessarily more concrete than a number of other lines' proof that their cosmology is the singular truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-20-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:13:17-08:00","id":813059,"title":"","content":"1) Just Arc or Arcane.<br /> <br /> 2) Objectively, it's bad because of presentation and reader/player setting empowerment and crossover writing and a whole bunch of other things. It creates too many snarls on too many fronts to make it worth it. Again, David Brookshaw has talked a good deal about the problems of it, and David Hill has also said some really good pieces.<br /> <br /> Subjectively, it's just an irritating theory and idea that I've had to deal with since the day Lost came out. It has not helped that most people who trumpet it have been very obnoxious, particularly since a great many of them were bad Mage fans trying to invalidate Changeling on the whole in favor of their pet splat. Considering Lost is my personal favorite game, you might imagine how that would sour me to the subject.<br /> <br /> On that note, I'm actually sort of surprised I haven't been blocked yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:33:00-08:00","id":813069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813058#post813058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In so far as the Begotten fit everything else in familiar terms because their perspective gives them reasons to believe the associations. Reasons which... aren't necessarily more concrete than a number of other lines' proof that their cosmology is the singular truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not saying their view on things is the one true state of reality. It's just that beasts specifically think everything is linked up to their heritage and goes out of their way of doing what some mage fans do. Though, they have to be right to Some degree, since their powers work on all supernaturals except God-Machine stuff so there has to be a link between the supernaturals on some level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:43:18-08:00","id":813078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813059#post813059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Just Arc or Arcane.<br /> <br /> 2) Objectively, it's bad because of presentation and reader/player setting empowerment and crossover writing and a whole bunch of other things. It creates too many snarls on too many fronts to make it worth it. Again, David Brookshaw has talked a good deal about the problems of it, and David Hill has also said some really good pieces.<br /> <br /> Subjectively, it's just an irritating theory and idea that I've had to deal with since the day Lost came out. It has not helped that most people who trumpet it have been very obnoxious, particularly since a great many of them were bad Mage fans trying to invalidate Changeling on the whole in favor of their pet splat. Considering Lost is my personal favorite game, you might imagine how that would sour me to the subject.<br /> <br /> On that note, I'm actually sort of surprised I haven't been blocked yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still fairly new here, so I don't know all the nicknames.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Mage/Changeling thing, I'm fine with them being separate. I think the problem is (as with most things) is the second you use the same name for two totally separate things people will immediately start drawing connections between the two of them. This also happened with the Awakened society of Atlantis being compared to the Disney movie Atlantis and the general mythology of Atlantis.<br /> <br /> Also, Changeling is the reason I got into CofD in the first place. Just seems fascinating and interesting. Shame that I cannot ever find a game for it though.<br /> <br /> And blocked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:44:05-08:00","id":813079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813069#post813069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I'm not saying their view on things is the one true state of reality. It's just that beasts specifically think everything is linked up to their heritage and goes out of their way of doing what some mage fans do. Though, they have to be right to Some degree, since their powers work on all supernaturals except God-Machine stuff so there has to be a link between the supernaturals on some level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts understand themselves and their abilities as an extension of powerful spiritual symbolism. They don't have to be right at all for their powers to work, they just have to be archetypally primordial enough to pull it off. Which, hey, they do.<br /> <br /> Even in practice, Beasts sort of know the limits of their theory, though the human-to-ripper-slasher phenomenon gives them reason to go &quot;Eh, you see&quot;. In the end, it doesn't matter to a Beast if the other monsters are actually siblings or only archetypally related, because they are essentially spiritual crosspieces for the human experience. Even if it's only a matter of Astral symbolism, Astral spirituality is reality for Beasts, and that means monsters are siblings. Even if they're wrong, that doesn't stop everyone else being family.<br /> <br /> Which is kind of comforting-being family isn't about being right, it's about being there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"