 for the time being, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I mean, I agree that the Hedge is not worth covering in Mage, but you're giving the impression that you're altering development of the line to win an argument on the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:19:50-08:00","id":813322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813206#post813206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Changeling's Arcadia is not Mage Arcadia; the Fae Acanthus mages summon and deal with are not the Gentry, just like the Beasts Thyrsus summon aren't Begotten, and the Demons Mastigos summon aren't Unchained. Changeling was the only game that teased such a connection (absent throwaway bits of Geist, which are also being chucked) and I'm cutting it off.<br /> <br /> For now, Mage is written from the hard angle that Changeling The Lost doesn't exist - the Hedge is absent in our grand tour of the otherworlds, while the Underworld, Shadow, Astral, and Lower Depths are all in. Once people (including several writers) get it into their heads that the cosmologies are seperate, we might talk about the Hedge for a bit in a future book.<br /> <br /> But for the time being, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several thousand thanks for this. The Acanthus write-up mislead me; I'm very, very glad that the canon* explanation says those places are separate. (I'm guessing this discussion already happened two years ago on the Mage sub-board when this came out, but thanks for re-clarifying.) <br /> <br /> I worry a little that not mentioning the Hedge or Lost!Arcadia at all might be read as tacit assumption that the Arcadias are the same, but including a short sidebar of &quot;hey guys these aren't the same thing&quot; would break your &quot;doesn't exist&quot; rule above. Not sure which would be the better way to go.<br /> <br /> *As much as the World of Darkness has a canon, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:37:12-08:00","id":813332,"title":"","content":"Yeah - the Acanthus preview was of its first draft, and my redlines consisted of &quot;you have gotten Changeling: The Lost all over this&quot;. The finished one is much less Changelingish.<br /> <br /> Mage Arcadia is the <i>Lunargent</i> Thorn - when Mage talks about The Thorns in Acanthus' Mage Sight, it's describing mirror-reflective cracks in reality that are how Acanthus process branching timelines into their supernal senses. It looks like the timelines in Donnie Darko, the cracks in Doctor Who, the Shrike in Hyperion. It's not the Hedge.<br /> <br /> They're called the Thorns because they're spikey, not because they look like the briar-maze from Sleeping Beauty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:52:26-08:00","id":813372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813206#post813206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Changeling's Arcadia is not Mage Arcadia; the Fae Acanthus mages summon and deal with are not the Gentry, just like the Beasts Thyrsus summon aren't Begotten, and the Demons Mastigos summon aren't Unchained. Changeling was the only game that teased such a connection (absent throwaway bits of Geist, which are also being chucked) and I'm cutting it off.<br /> <br /> For now, Mage is written from the hard angle that Changeling The Lost doesn't exist - the Hedge is absent in our grand tour of the otherworlds, while the Underworld, Shadow, Astral, and Lower Depths are all in. Once people (including several writers) get it into their heads that the cosmologies are seperate, we might talk about the Hedge for a bit in a future book.<br /> <br /> But for the time being, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with there being different beings with the same name. We have the Demons of the Abyss, we have the Magtigos Demons, and then we have the Fallen Angels of the godmachine which are also called Demons. However, the lack of exploration of the Hedge seems like a very obvious omission. I still think that it should be included, because there needs to be a postulate of some sort regarding it or you cannot really build off of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813332#post813332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - the Acanthus preview was of its first draft, and my redlines consisted of &quot;you have gotten Changeling: The Lost all over this&quot;. The finished one is much less Changelingish.<br /> <br /> Mage Arcadia is the <i>Lunargent</i> Thorn - when Mage talks about The Thorns in Acanthus' Mage Sight, it's describing mirror-reflective cracks in reality that are how Acanthus process branching timelines into their supernal senses. It looks like the timelines in Donnie Darko, the cracks in Doctor Who, the Shrike in Hyperion. It's not the Hedge.<br /> <br /> They're called the Thorns because they're spikey, not because they look like the briar-maze from Sleeping Beauty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed that the preview for the Acanthus definitely sounded like a Mage describing Fae Arcadia, rather than the Entities of Time and Fate that exist within the Supernal Arcadia. Personally speaking here, I'd rather that just become the description of the Fae Arcadia rather than Arcadia just being striked from the record books entirely and leaving no foundation for crossovers between Changeling and Mage. Might it be an idea to have Mages call the Fae Arcadia something else? That way one can tell if they're talking about the Lunargent Thorn or the Plane that the Gentry exist on without having to head it with a qualifying term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:19:47-08:00","id":813469,"title":"","content":"Reshy, your post boils down to, &quot;I'm fine with <i>beings</i> having the same name, but I'm not fine with <i>places</i> having the same name.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T11:06:00-08:00","id":813495,"title":"","content":"I a way, yes. Demon is a term and Arcadia is a name. That's what I believe causes the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T11:39:40-08:00","id":813518,"title":"","content":"Remember the &quot;Call The Wild Hunt&quot; and &quot;Lost And Found&quot; Goblin Contracts from the 1ED Core? Does the former summon actual Huntsmen in 2ED, and can the latter help you escape Huntsmen for a time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:26:02-08:00","id":813652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813518#post813518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the &quot;Call The Wild Hunt&quot; and &quot;Lost And Found&quot; Goblin Contracts from the 1ED Core? Does the former summon actual Huntsmen in 2ED, and can the latter help you escape Huntsmen for a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it can let you negotiate with a Huntsman chasing you, or send one out against another. The former might involve you &quot;Owing&quot; the Huntsman in exchange for sparing you, something that you're obligated by the Wyrd to fulfill. A sort of open-ended promise in exchange for not being dragged back to the Faerie by that particular Huntsman.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813332#post813332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - the Acanthus preview was of its first draft, and my redlines consisted of &quot;you have gotten Changeling: The Lost all over this&quot;. The finished one is much less Changelingish.<br /> <br /> Mage Arcadia is the <i>Lunargent</i> Thorn - when Mage talks about The Thorns in Acanthus' Mage Sight, it's describing mirror-reflective cracks in reality that are how Acanthus process branching timelines into their supernal senses. It looks like the timelines in Donnie Darko, the cracks in Doctor Who, the Shrike in Hyperion. It's not the Hedge.<br /> <br /> They're called the Thorns because they're spikey, not because they look like the briar-maze from Sleeping Beauty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back on this, I wanted to ask Dave but is there any idea how the Astral and the Faerie interact with one-another? Both places can, theoretically, reflect Faerie mythology. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T15:31:30-08:00","id":813696,"title":"","content":"Faerie as in Changeling's Arcadia? It doesn't - Changelings can't enter the Astral, as it's the interior of the human soul, and the (Hedge) thorns have done a number on them such that they're insufficiently human. From a mage's point of view, changelings splash around in the shallow end (dreams,) but mages tend to see lucid dreaming as a thing they try a few times with Mind spells and then ignore in favor of their astral-meditation ability unless they're Obsessed with it. They don't put the importance on it changelings do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T15:58:20-08:00","id":813718,"title":"","content":"There'll probably just be some random Gentry wandering around <br /> <br /> Mage: &quot;How the hell did you...?&quot;<br /> <br /> True Fae: *Shrugs*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:09:39-08:00","id":813725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813696#post813696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faerie as in Changeling's Arcadia? It doesn't - Changelings can't enter the Astral, as it's the interior of the human soul, and the (Hedge) thorns have done a number on them such that they're insufficiently human. From a mage's point of view, changelings splash around in the shallow end (dreams,) but mages tend to see lucid dreaming as a thing they try a few times with Mind spells and then ignore in favor of their astral-meditation ability unless they're Obsessed with it. They don't put the importance on it changelings do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to call it the Faerie now so that there's no confusion. That's what 3.5e did, they have Arcadia (Minor Law/Good Plane) and the Plane of the Faerie, which is kind of like one in Changeling.<br /> <br /> Also, if they cannot enter or influence the astral how do they get into the dreams of mortals? Has that ability been deprecated? Who else cannot enter the astral? I know in 1e that the Anima Mundi contained a line about Werewolves within it. If it's entirely a human construction, is the Anima Mundi no more, as it's the thought-space of the plants and animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:28:10-08:00","id":813740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813725#post813725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if they cannot enter or influence the astral how do they get into the dreams of mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entering someone's dreams has never been reliant on the ability to enter their soul. I don't know if the limitation has expanded in 2e, but in 1e fully-fledged supernatural beings that weren't mages or Prometheans with a particular Athanor were unable to enter the Temenos, i.e. the collective soul of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T23:55:42-08:00","id":813951,"title":"","content":"I figure that a Changeling encountering a Mage in a dream would be sort of like a three-dimensional being encountering a four-dimensional one. The Changeling could explore and manipulate what seems to him to be the entire world, and could interact with the Mage as long as she &quot;intersects&quot; with the dream world the Changeling is experiencing. The Mage, however, might seem to inexplicably vanish and reappear, moving along a spatial axis that the Changeling can't perceive, and possibly can't even imagine, save perhaps in an abstract sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-22-2016, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T02:29:04-08:00","id":814004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813696#post813696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faerie as in Changeling's Arcadia? It doesn't - Changelings can't enter the Astral, as it's the interior of the human soul, and the (Hedge) thorns have done a number on them such that they're insufficiently human. From a mage's point of view, changelings splash around in the shallow end (dreams,) but mages tend to see lucid dreaming as a thing they try a few times with Mind spells and then ignore in favor of their astral-meditation ability unless they're Obsessed with it. They don't put the importance on it changelings do.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there's Mordred, laughing at people's attempts to categorize the world into a neat cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:18:52-08:00","id":814056,"title":"","content":"I look forward to seeing the new rules for oniemancy in 2e, it appears Changelings can physically enter dreams via the hedge now.<br /> <br /> But even in 1e they had the Skien, which means that while for Mages personal dreams are the shallow end, for Changelings they're a much deeper pool with resources and dimesions that Mages can't access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:32:48-08:00","id":814062,"title":"","content":"Yeah, changeling and mage dreamscapes are fairly similar in size, but almost perpendicular to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:40:10-08:00","id":814120,"title":"","content":"Yeah in a sense for Mages its vertical and Changelings it horizontal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:05:12-08:00","id":815385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813696#post813696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings can't enter the Astral, as it's the interior of the human soul, and the (Hedge) thorns have done a number on them such that they're insufficiently human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind clarifying this a bit, Dave? Demons can enter the Astral (e.g., Rip the Gates), and they aren't now and have never been human, so this seems like an odd thing to say about Changelings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:18:15-08:00","id":815395,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm pretty sure the Astral includes the Anima Mundi, which is where non-human creatures dream (such as Werewolves). You'd think Changelings would get access to the Anima Mundi at the very least. And since they get access to the Oneiros via dreamwalking, I think it's just the Temenos they have no access to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:22:36-08:00","id":815396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815385#post815385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you mind clarifying this a bit, Dave? Demons can enter the Astral (e.g., Rip the Gates), and they aren't now and have never been human, so this seems like an odd thing to say about Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two issues here. First, Rip the Gates is a cheat code, a way of brute forcing something to happen even when it shouldn't. Second, it is not an innate ability of the template, but a separate power, and thus cannot be assumed to be inherently characteristic of all Unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:41:54-08:00","id":815406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815396#post815396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First, Rip the Gates is a cheat code, a way of brute forcing something to happen even when it shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing how this helps to answer my question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815396#post815396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Second, it is not an innate ability of the template, but a separate power, and thus cannot be assumed to be inherently characteristic of all Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>I neither wrote nor implied that Rip the Gates was an inherent characteristic of all Demons. Also, not seeing how its innateness or lack thereof helps to answer my question.<br /> <br /> Dave didn't say &quot;entering the Astral isn't an innate ability of the Changeling template.&quot; He said they can't enter the Astral. It could be that he merely meant that it's not innate to Changelings, but it's unclear (to me, at least) from his post. That's why I asked.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T07:38:51-08:00","id":815435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815406#post815406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing how this helps to answer my question.<br /> I neither wrote nor implied that Rip the Gates was an inherent characteristic of all Demons. Also, not seeing how its innateness or lack thereof helps to answer my question.<br /> Dave didn't say &amp;quot;entering the Astral isn't an innate ability of the Changeling template.&amp;quot; He said they can't enter the Astral. It could be that he merely meant that it's not innate to Changelings, but it's unclear (to me, at least) from his post. That's why I asked.</div> </div> </div> </div> Right, sorry; I'll try to elaborate. The thing is, Rip the Gates isn't &quot;correctly&quot; entering the Astral the way a Mage might; they are literally ripping through the things that would prevent them from entering, forcing a loophole in reality to make themselves enter even when they shouldn't be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T08:54:53-08:00","id":815492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815395#post815395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm pretty sure the Astral includes the Anima Mundi, which is where non-human creatures dream (such as Werewolves). You'd think Changelings would get access to the Anima Mundi at the very least. And since they get access to the Oneiros via dreamwalking, I think it's just the Temenos they have no access to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. Werewolves are sort of a non-human species, whereas Changelings are more like humans with pieces missing (and magical bits grafted on). Normal human beings can't enter the Anima Mundi, and we have no reason to believe that the Durance grants Changelings that ability. We <i>do</i> know that the Durance screws with a Changeling's soul, however, which is consistent with the idea that their connection with the Temenos has been severed, or at least weakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-24-2016, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:00:56-08:00","id":815497,"title":"","content":"The thing is, changelings dream. That is canon. That is, in fact, why high Wyrd was deleterious to a Changeling's Clarity, because the dreams felt so real that they were almost like being back in Arcadia. Not to mention that changelings <i>can</i> indeed enter the Astral, as they can enter a dreamer's Oneiros. They can also use the Skein.<br /> <br /> So yeah, my take is that Dave said &quot;interior of the human soul,&quot; which sounds like the Temenos to me, rather than the Astral as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:08:46-08:00","id":815501,"title":"","content":"True, but Mages can only reach the Anima Mundi by first passing <i>through </i>the Temenos and ordinary people, as I pointed out, can't really enter either. Just being able to dream doesn't mean that Changelings can &quot;go&quot; anywhere in the Astral that ordinary humans can't, except in that they can enter other people's dreams directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:31:45-08:00","id":815517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815497#post815497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ot to mention that changelings <i>can</i> indeed enter the Astral, as they can enter a dreamer's Oneiros.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually, they can't. The Oneiros is inside the human soul just as much as the Temenos is.<br /> <br /> Dancers in the Dusk has one dream combatant that's the result of an Oneiros creature being accidentally pulled &quot;up&quot; out of the Astral into the dream-layer Changelings operate in. A few pages later, there's a monster from the Temenos and a description of how Changelings bounce right off the portal to its home <i>because they can't go there.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:35:58-08:00","id":815521,"title":"","content":"Here's the 1st ed Mage meditation chart:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Target Number Destination Plane<br /> 4 successes Waking meditation<br /> 8 successes Dream meditation (waking dream)<br /> 12 successes Oneiros*<br /> 16 successes Temenos<br /> 20 successes Dreamtime<br /> * One Mana must be spent for the mage to cross over the Astral Threshold </div> </div> </div>See that? The Oneiros is not dreams, despite changeling later calling dream combat &quot;oneiromachy&quot;. Oneiros is <i>after</i> dreams, across the Astral barrier.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:37:33-08:00","id":815522,"title":"","content":"So what IS the Oneiros, then? And where is the dream-layer changelings operate in, if it's not in the Astral? Does it &quot;break&quot; the cosmology if I just make them the same thing? Because it honestly seems a lot simpler to just have changelings operate on the Oneiros and use the Skein as a sort of road that connects different Oneiros, rather than add yet another layer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:41:17-08:00","id":815524,"title":"","content":"Presumably Beast lairs make this rule not entirely absolute though, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:52:52-08:00","id":815532,"title":"","content":"Wasn't this thread about Huntsmen or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:59:59-08:00","id":815536,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah. <br /> <br /> They presumably can't enter the astral either, so cheating your way in there somehow is potentially a good way of avoiding one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:23:35-08:00","id":815583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815522#post815522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what IS the Oneiros, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the inside of your soul, man. This hasn't changed with the edition switch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And where is the dream-layer changelings operate in, if it's not in the Astral? </div> </div> </div>It's in dreams.<br /> <br /> If that seems tautological and unhelpful, good \u2014 changeling-facing cosmology is pretty much universally disorganized, as you might expect from a bunch of people who call themselves the Lost. Bits occasionally reflect into or off of the deeper parts of the cosmology, but it's not in the nature of the dreamscape to offer changelings a clear view of how their actions there affect the world at large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it honestly seems a lot simpler </div> </div> </div>The supernatural does not give two fucks about Occam's Razor outside the confines of cause-and-effect.<br /> <br /> Making the dreams changelings interact with be consistently interchangeable with the Oneiros means you give the Fae and any other prying oneiromancer the ability to mess around with people's souls as well, and the effects of messing with the Oneiros are a lot more consistently acute than messing with their dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:29:55-08:00","id":815584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815583#post815583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that seems tautological and unhelpful, good \u2014 changeling-facing cosmology is pretty much universally disorganized, as you might expect from a bunch of people who call themselves the Lost. Bits occasionally reflect into or off of the deeper parts of the cosmology, but it's not in the nature of the dreamscape to offer changelings a clear view of how their actions there affect the world at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit unsatisfying that there isn't an actual answer for &quot;where are dreams located?&quot; beyond &quot;somewhere that isn't any of the currently known planes.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess I'll just create an ad interim Plane of Dreams or somesuch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815583#post815583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The supernatural does not give two fucks about Occam's Razor outside the confines of cause-and-effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. I wasn't talking about the in-universe rationale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815583#post815583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the dreams changelings interact with be consistently interchangeable with the Oneiros means you give the Fae and any other prying oneiromancer the ability to mess around with people's souls as well, and the effects of messing with the Oneiros are a lot more consistently acute than messing with their dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the True Fae could already do that, which was the entire point of oneiromachy in the first place, and why changelings <i>really</i> want to keep the True Fae out of people's dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:32:44-08:00","id":815588,"title":"","content":"The oneiros is in your soul, so I guess you could say that the dreamscape is sort of <i>on</i> your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:43:26-08:00","id":815595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815584#post815584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the True Fae could already do that, which was the entire point of oneiromachy in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>Messing with dreams having consequences is not mutually exclusive with messing with dreams being distinct from messing with the soul, and the Fae's ability to wreak havoc through dreams if they've put in the proper appearances doesn't justify making any two-bit incubus a personality-threatening issue from its arrival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:47:25-08:00","id":815597,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I guess dreams not being the Oneiros does mesh better with things like the Dreamlands from Princess: The Hopeful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T12:24:39-08:00","id":815619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815595#post815595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messing with dreams having consequences is not mutually exclusive with messing with dreams being distinct from messing with the soul, and the Fae's ability to wreak havoc through dreams if they've put in the proper appearances doesn't justify making any two-bit incubus a personality-threatening issue from its arrival.</div> </div> </div> </div> Didn't the Astral book in 1e actually feature an Other messing around with someone's Oneiros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T12:54:12-08:00","id":815639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815619#post815619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Didn't the Astral book in 1e actually feature an Other messing around with someone's Oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. There's a Gentry that's gotten stuck in a Banisher's Oneiros, in a section which includes notes on how changelings manipulating dreams can alter the parts of an Oneiros that reflect the dreamscape (dreams play out in a subsection of the Oneiros from the point of view of someone inside, the same way the Temenos will shift about with large-scale changes in attitudes in the material world).<br /> <br /> They still can't go there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T12:59:29-08:00","id":815643,"title":"","content":"Forgive my ignorance, but why is it so important that they can't access the Oneiros/Temenos? Like, technically speaking, a Mage's soul has been altered by the Supernal, so it's not like &quot;only those with pure souls can access this&quot;, because otherwise that would essentially disqualify anything that isn't a mortal or has a minor template (and even then, it may disqualify several of those as well). So if you don't mind me asking, what's the cosmological/metaphysical explanation for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:25:37-08:00","id":815655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=815643#post815643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive my ignorance, but why is it so important that they can't access the Oneiros/Temenos? Like, technically speaking, a Mage's soul has been altered by the Supernal, so it's not like &quot;only those with pure souls can access this&quot;, because otherwise that would essentially disqualify anything that isn't a mortal or has a minor template (and even then, it may disqualify several of those as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you take a look at the relevant sidebar in Astral Realms and compare it with the Kinship categories in Beast, you'll notice that all the things in the &quot;fundamentally human&quot; category can access the collective soul of humanity just fine, ghosts notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you don't mind me asking, what's the cosmological/metaphysical explanation for that? </div> </div> </div>Connections to humanity don't come naturally to monsters, and even a mage can lose access to the Temenos if they go Mad. Changelings aren't human anymore, ergo they're barred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:28:30-08:00","id":815657,"title":"","content":"I think I'll pass on reading Beast, thanks. I'll see if I can dig up that chart somewhere else. But it's good to know there's a rationale behind it; it does make sense when put that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T12:57:49-08:00","id":817076,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Changeling visit dreams directly, at least in 2e. I think that maybe they actually visit the story your dreams are telling and the skein is the place in the hedge were these story/dreams dwell.<br /> <br /> I hypothetize this because according to the Fae Touched Spoiler Changelings can now physically travel into dreams via the hedge, so my guess is that Changelings don't interact directly with dreams, but rather through the medium of the hedge and/or skein, even when they only visit indirectly.<br /> <br /> This would explain why Changelings can't normally, if ever access the Astral Planes, but they can indirectly effect them by indirectly effecting the dreams that directly effect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:05:18-08:00","id":817085,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oneiromancy: Fae-touched characters cannot engage in oneiromancy on their own. They do not share the changeling\u2019s innate ability to walk into dreams in the Hedge, nor can they enter a sleepers dreams through touch&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When the fae-touched enters the dream, she does not go in physical form. If she is in the Hedge, her physical form remains on the outside of the Bastion in the Hedge and she gains a dream form during the dream.\u201d<br /> <br /> Evidence for my point, although the dream region in the hedge appears to the Bastion, so maybe the Skein is the road between Bastions, and Bastions contain individual Dreams?<br /> <br /> In another part its mentions Bastions as well.<br /> <br /> PS it appears that Changeling Onieromancy in 2e is more power, they couldn't enter dreams physically before, nor could they enter someones dreams without pledge, unless it was via the Skein, now it sounds like they just have to touch someone sleeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-26-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:51:28-08:00","id":817127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=806704#post806704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, people were asking about iron I think?<br /> <br /> I made it a little more generous a definition. Because &quot;cold iron&quot; is a really subjective term, and would largely reflect things that aren't by any means practical tools or weapons. So, if it's iron enough that people think of it as iron, it's iron, and it counts. Cast iron, wrought iron, cold iron, dramatic irony, if it's iron, it's iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if we got a Huntsmen (As in the Fae creature) shot by a Huntsman would that count as &quot;Irony&quot; and thus iron? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T16:45:04-08:00","id":817243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813206#post813206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Changeling's Arcadia is not Mage Arcadia; the Fae Acanthus mages summon and deal with are not the Gentry, just like the Beasts Thyrsus summon aren't Begotten, and the Demons Mastigos summon aren't Unchained. Changeling was the only game that teased such a connection (absent throwaway bits of Geist, which are also being chucked) and I'm cutting it off.<br /> <br /> For now, Mage is written from the hard angle that Changeling The Lost doesn't exist - the Hedge is absent in our grand tour of the otherworlds, while the Underworld, Shadow, Astral, and Lower Depths are all in. Once people (including several writers) get it into their heads that the cosmologies are seperate, we might talk about the Hedge for a bit in a future book.<br /> <br /> But for the time being, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh,speaking of summoning,would you mind explain how much of the rules of the book Summonings its still valid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:49:55-08:00","id":817709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=817127#post817127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if we got a Huntsmen (As in the Fae creature) shot by a Huntsman would that count as &amp;quot;Irony&amp;quot; and thus iron?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, but it is pretty ironic that a Huntsman's own weapon is one of the best ways to kill one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:52:54-08:00","id":817714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=817709#post817709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, but it is pretty ironic that a Huntsman's own weapon is one of the best ways to kill one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be amusing for Changelings to create a record place of types of situations that provoke enough Irony to hurt huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:00:44-08:00","id":817719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=817714#post817714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be amusing for Changelings to create a record place of types of situations that provoke enough Irony to hurt huntsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just play Alanis Morissette's Ironic. The fact that it doesn't contain a single example of actual irony should be ironic enough to kill any Fae creature that listens to it. But make sure to have earplugs handy, cause it could be harmful to Changelings too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:12:02-08:00","id":817724,"title":"","content":"Ok, changelings don't go into the Astral, they just interact with dreams. I get that. But for the sake of alternate takes, what do most assume would be a powerful or unusual enough circumstance to allow entry into the Astral for changelings? An obscure Goblin Contract with an especially risky drawback? A 5 dot Token or a dotless legendary Token? Could a changeling who once studied the Astral with the help of a mage one day create an Entitlement that allows changelings to go beyond the dream layer?<br /> <br /> EDIT: you know what, I should take this to another thread. Sorry if I contributed to derailing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-27-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:19:45-08:00","id":817730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=817724#post817724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, changelings don't go into the Astral, they just interact with dreams. I get that. But for the sake of alternate takes, what do most assume would be a powerful or unusual enough circumstance to allow entry into the Astral for changelings? An obscure Goblin Contract with an especially risky drawback? A 5 dot Token or a dotless legendary Token? Could a changeling who once studied the Astral with the help of a mage one day create an Entitlement that allows changelings to go beyond the dream layer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say that I don't like that we're not separating &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rMHus-0wFSo\" target=\"_blank\">Dreams</a>&quot; from &quot;Subconsciousness&quot; because it seems like the two would be part of one another. Dreams are often a reflective of the subconscious, and yet the Astral is part of the subconscious, which makes the whole thing break down and not make a whole lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:22:56-08:00","id":817733,"title":"","content":"EDIT: never mind, gonna start a different thread for this.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/817751-2ed-mages-and-the-astral-changelings-and-the-hedge-how-could-they-interact\"><b>Here is said thread.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-27-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:28:15-08:00","id":817739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=817733#post817733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey DaveB, I see no problem with the Mage 2ED core not mentioning the Hedge, but could you please tell us how <i>you</i> would have Mages interact with the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem I see with not having it mentioned, the book really should set some kind of baseline for interaction with the Hedge. Because in a game about investigating phenomena there should be at least some material to build a framework for interaction. Because otherwise you just create this kind of blank space where mages will avoid it because they can't really interact with it. It'd be like Mages being unable to perceive or interact with the shadow, because then you just threw out werewolves from potential storylines or hooks. I mean they could see werewolves, and maybe interact with them, but there's no real angle for exploring the shadow if there's no rules for interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:51:26-08:00","id":818017,"title":"","content":"I assume that if a changeling manages to permanently kill a Huntsman with its own Arcadian weapons, they cease to be along with Huntsmen. That sounds disappointing to me. If I beat the freaking Predator of Faerie, I deserve to have one of its weapons as a prize. Whether or not the Freehold and its Courts agree is another story, and the notoriety could quickly become a drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:41:59-08:00","id":818046,"title":"","content":"Even if it's not the Arcadian Weapon, I'd certainly think it'd be thematically appropriate to have some kind of spoils or earned boon from defeating the Huntsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:47:52-08:00","id":818049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818046#post818046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if it's not the Arcadian Weapon, I'd certainly think it'd be thematically appropriate to have some kind of spoils or earned boon from defeating the Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>The piece of you that let the Fae send it after you is plenty of reward, I'd think.<br /> <br /> Better to tie up a loose end than set another thread dangling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:50:11-08:00","id":818050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818049#post818049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The piece of you that let the Fae send it after you is plenty of reward, I'd think.<br /> <br /> Better to tie up a loose end than set another thread dangling.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does the piece of you even do, anyway? Is it when you can start to experience Post-traumaticGrowth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T20:01:55-08:00","id":818166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818046#post818046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if it's not the Arcadian Weapon, I'd certainly think it'd be thematically appropriate to have some kind of spoils or earned boon from defeating the Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcadian weapons are really, really, really scary. <br /> <br /> And if you make them permanent, they're even scarier. <br /> <br /> So like, if you want a reward, it's there. But it's a bittersweet truth at best. If anyone finds out what you did to make it permanent, you're not exactly going to be heralded as a hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T20:11:23-08:00","id":818170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818166#post818166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arcadian weapons are really, really, really scary.<br /> <br /> And if you make them permanent, they're even scarier.<br /> <br /> So like, if you want a reward, it's there. But it's a bittersweet truth at best. If anyone finds out what you did to make it permanent, you're not exactly going to be heralded as a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me imagine that &quot;These weapons are the weapons of a huntsman&quot;, so the only way to keep it permanently is to become a Huntsman of sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T20:59:15-08:00","id":818183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818170#post818170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me imagine that &amp;quot;These weapons are the weapons of a huntsman&amp;quot;, so the only way to keep it permanently is to become a Huntsman of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>coul b\u00ea that the weapon was made t\u00f4 help a huntsman bring someone t\u00f4 Faerie,and the only way t\u00f4 keep the weapon is shoving someone through the hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T22:43:40-08:00","id":818221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818166#post818166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arcadian weapons are really, really, really scary.<br /> <br /> And if you make them permanent, they're even scarier.<br /> <br /> So like, if you want a reward, it's there. But it's a bittersweet truth at best. If anyone finds out what you did to make it permanent, you're not exactly going to be heralded as a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but think of the legend of Lightbringer, from <i>A Clash of Kings</i>:<br /> <br /> Darkness lay across the land, and a hero, Azor Ahai, was chosen to fight against it. To fight the darkness, Azor Ahai needed to forge a hero's sword. He labored for thirty days and thirty nights until it was done, but when he quenched the steel in water the blade broke. Not one to give up easily, Azor Ahai started again, and this time labored for fifty days and fifty nights, before quenching the blade in the heart's blood of a lion he had captured. Once more, however, the steel shattered. Azor Ahai began once more, this time with a heavy heart, for he knew what he must do to finish the blade. He labored for a hundred days and a hundred nights, before calling for his beloved wife, Nissa Nissa. He asked his wife to bear her breast, and drove the red-hot blade into her heart. As she died, Nissa Nissa's soul joined with the steel of the blade, and Lightbringer was born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:32:15-08:00","id":818411,"title":"","content":"Okay, so..... I'm working on a new city as a kind of basis for all my games, crossover, singular, and not. I'm focusing primarily on using Mortal/GMC, Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Changeling. Looking forwards to getting my hands on Hurt Locker for some of those yummy minor templates to finish ironing out my mortal game. Got enough spoilers from Mage to be able to chart out their society and central Mysteries for Metro-Townsville. So, I started working on my Fae in the city. I figured out a Court system.<br /> <br /> So, I'm now looking to chart out the Gentry and the Huntsmen and the Loyalists. I'm figuring that 10% of the changelings in the Court of Courts are Loyalists. But, assuming around 100 changelings total, that suddenly seems like a lot of Huntsmen that are going to be running around the city. About how many changelings would have defeated their Huntsmen? A quarter? Half? 40 Huntsmen that show up, each killing someone (or something else to &quot;blow the hunting horn&quot; and alert their prey the hunt is on) still feels like a significant threat to the freehold at large.<br /> <br /> That feels off to me. I'm getting an &quot;enemy invasion&quot; vibe here. Does that sound about right to anyone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:48:54-08:00","id":818419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818183#post818183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> coul b\u00ea that the weapon was made t\u00f4 help a huntsman bring someone t\u00f4 Faerie,and the only way t\u00f4 keep the weapon is shoving someone through the hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder, do Changelings ostracize Darklings? Since to escape they had to betray someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:35:53-08:00","id":818457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818419#post818419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder, do Changelings ostracize Darklings? Since to escape they had to betray someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmmm,maybe not ostracizing,but they'd always be suspicious,if a darkling wanted someone else's help or being part of a motley,they'd probably have to prove themselves somehow,many changelings would be prejudiced,expect the darkling to betray someone again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:38:54-08:00","id":818458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818419#post818419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, do Changelings ostracize Darklings? Since to escape they had to betray someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not easy to tell a Changeling's Seeming by appearance alone, and Lost society doesn't attribute a great deal of significance to Seeming - you'll notice none of the Seeming writeups include the &quot;Stereotypes&quot; section that is common to X-Splat writeups. That's because it's hard to know what Seeming someone is unless they tell you, and because the Lost don't tend to make assumptions about other Lost's personalities based on their Seeming.<br /> <br /> Now, if a Darkling told you about how he escaped, you might hesitate to trust him. Certainly you'd have to wonder if he'd be willing to turn you in for a Token of Reprieve. Then again, in the back of your mind you probably know that you would have done anything it took to get out, so a part of you probably doesn't blame him. You probably don't fully trust <i>anyone</i> not to turn you into the Huntsman if there's a Token in it for them, regardless of their Seeming. You also probably don't like to think about what you would do if a Huntsman ever offered you a Token, because you're afraid you might not like your own answer.<br /> <br /> You've all done things you may regret to get free, and you'd all go to great lengths to stay free. So it's not really anyone's place to judge anyone else for what they've done or what they would do for that freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-28-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:49:14-08:00","id":818468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818458#post818458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not easy to tell a Changeling's Seeming by appearance alone, and Lost society doesn't attribute a great deal of significance to Seeming - you'll notice none of the Seeming writeups include the &quot;Stereotypes&quot; section that is common to X-Splat writeups. That's because it's hard to know what Seeming someone is unless they tell you, and because the Lost don't tend to make assumptions about other Lost's personalities based on their Seeming.<br /> <br /> Now, if a Darkling told you about how he escaped, you might hesitate to trust him. Certainly you'd have to wonder if he'd be willing to turn you in for a Token of Reprieve. Then again, in the back of your mind you probably know that you would have done anything it took to get out, so a part of you probably doesn't blame him. You probably don't fully trust <i>anyone</i> not to turn you into the Huntsman if there's a Token in it for them, regardless of their Seeming. You also probably don't like to think about what you would do if a Huntsman ever offered you a Token, because you're afraid you might not like your own answer.<br /> <br /> You've all done things you may regret to get free, and you'd all go to great lengths to stay free. So it's not really anyone's place to judge anyone else for what they've done or what they would do for that freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't Darkling traits manifest on your Mein filtered through your Kith? That's what I thought I had read from the Kiths Preview.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Darkling:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Angler fish-things with translucent skin, bioluminescent patches, and lidless, glowing eyes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elemental:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Phosphorescent figures seemingly carved from polished amber, warm ivory, and glistening ice.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fairest:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Perfectly sculpted physiques with glowing, oiled skin, halos of tiny, glimmering stars, and incandescent brands.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd think that looking like an Angler fish would be uh... blantant?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:14:41-08:00","id":818493,"title":"","content":"Sure, but is that bioluminescent fish-person a Darkling Bright One, a Beast Waterborn, an Elemental Coldscale? Throw Dual-Kith into the mix and there are a lot of ways to get someone that looks like an angler fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:32:51-08:00","id":818503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818411#post818411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so..... I'm working on a new city as a kind of basis for all my games, crossover, singular, and not. I'm focusing primarily on using Mortal/GMC, Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Changeling. Looking forwards to getting my hands on Hurt Locker for some of those yummy minor templates to finish ironing out my mortal game. Got enough spoilers from Mage to be able to chart out their society and central Mysteries for Metro-Townsville. So, I started working on my Fae in the city. I figured out a Court system.<br /> <br /> So, I'm now looking to chart out the Gentry and the Huntsmen and the Loyalists. I'm figuring that 10% of the changelings in the Court of Courts are Loyalists. But, assuming around 100 changelings total, that suddenly seems like a lot of Huntsmen that are going to be running around the city. About how many changelings would have defeated their Huntsmen? A quarter? Half? 40 Huntsmen that show up, each killing someone (or something else to &quot;blow the hunting horn&quot; and alert their prey the hunt is on) still feels like a significant threat to the freehold at large.<br /> <br /> That feels off to me. I'm getting an &quot;enemy invasion&quot; vibe here. Does that sound about right to anyone else?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think the True Fae unleash the Huntsmen right away.<br /> <br /> For some Changeling the huntsmen are summoned within say a year of returning to earth, some perhaps within a decade, others later, and some not at all.<br /> <br /> So I think the huntsmen would be hunting say 5% to 20% of a Freeholds Changelings at any given time, unless something weird happens. I think only say 1 to 3 changelings disappear per year in a stable Freehold thanks to huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-28-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:49:14-08:00","id":818522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818493#post818493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but is that bioluminescent fish-person a Darkling Bright One, a Beast Waterborn, an Elemental Coldscale? Throw Dual-Kith into the mix and there are a lot of ways to get someone that looks like an angler fish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just noting that darklings have tells for their betrayal. So it's not a complete shot in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:00:00-08:00","id":818535,"title":"","content":"So,Huntsmen are Spiritual beings,and the weapons are part of them. does that mean that when huntsmen strikes a victim with their weapons,the victim's spirit or soul,or wyrd is affected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:09:27-08:00","id":818547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818522#post818522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just noting that darklings have tells for their betrayal. So it's not a complete shot in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but again, Lost society doesn't have Seeming-based stereotypes. If you figure out someone is a Darkling, either by being told or buy guessing based on their appearance, the only thing that really tells you about them is that they did what needed to be done to get themselves out, and there's a good chance that them making it out meant someone else didn't. Depending on how cynical you are as an individual, you might think badly of them because of that knowledge, but Lost society as a whole recognizes that most Changeling's would probably have done the same in the Darkling's position, and doesn't begrudge them for taking the opportunity to escape when it was presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:16:16-08:00","id":818553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818547#post818547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but again, Lost society doesn't have Seeming-based stereotypes. If you figure out someone is a Darkling, either by being told or buy guessing based on their appearance, the only thing that really tells you about them is that they did what needed to be done to get themselves out, and there's a good chance that them making it out meant someone else didn't. Depending on how cynical you are as an individual, you might think badly of them because of that knowledge, but Lost society as a whole recognizes that most Changeling's would probably have done the same in the Darkling's position, and doesn't begrudge them for taking the opportunity to escape when it was presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Selling out to the Gentry is fairly high of a crime I'd think. Of course this means that most likely no one will trust you either because you did it before, what's one more to a Darkling? Even if it was an act of desperation and they would never do it again it shows that when it comes down to it they'll compromise their allies to save themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:24:12-08:00","id":818558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818553#post818553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Selling out to the Gentry is fairly high of a crime I'd think. Of course this means that most likely no one will trust you either because you did it before, what's one more to a Darkling? Even if it was an act of desperation and they would never do it again it shows that when it comes down to it they'll compromise their allies to save themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the same can probably be said of most Changelings, Darkling or no. Lost culture is not big on trust. There's a reason one of the main focuses of their supernatural powers is binding people to keep their promises. Lost society probably wouldn't function at all if it wasn't for Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:06:48-08:00","id":818584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818558#post818558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, the same can probably be said of most Changelings, Darkling or no. Lost culture is not big on trust. There's a reason one of the main focuses of their supernatural powers is binding people to keep their promises. Lost society probably wouldn't function at all if it wasn't for Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is that darklings regain clarity whenever they sell others out. If there's any more predisposed to evil changeling then that's them. At least with the fairest they have incentives not to be awful to their peers, whilst the darklings thrive on it. So of the lot they're probably the most unliked of the lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:09:43-08:00","id":818586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818584#post818584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is that darklings regain clarity whenever they sell others out. If there's any more predisposed to evil changeling then that's them. At least with the fairest they have incentives not to be awful to their peers, whilst the darklings thrive on it. So of the lot they're probably the most unliked of the lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>They regain Clarity when they make pragmatic decisions that others might find distasteful. I don't know where you're getting that they have to betray people for that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That's also likely a big part of the reason Freeholds like having them. They're willing to get their hands dirty and to the more... unsavory jobs - the ones that everyone knows need to done, but no one wants to be the one to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-28-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:25:58-08:00","id":818600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818586#post818586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They regain Clarity when they make pragmatic decisions that others might find distasteful. I don't know where you're getting that they have to betray people for that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That's also likely a big part of the reason Freeholds like having them. They're willing to get their hands dirty and to the more... unsavory jobs - the ones that everyone knows need to done, but no one wants to be the one to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. An excellent example of a frequently pragmatic decision that other changelings might find distasteful is selling people back to the Gentry, especially if there is one &quot;greater good&quot; or another involved. This being said the fact they are darklings in the first place is a <u>HUGE</u> &quot;Beware of Betrayal&quot; disclaimer right in their seeming. I'd imagine being a darkling is a lot like being the freehold hatchetman that no one really likes or allows too close but always respects at a safe distance. Where pragmatism trumps loyalty, there be a den of serpents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:33:06-08:00","id":818602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818586#post818586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They regain Clarity when they make pragmatic decisions that others might find distasteful. I don't know where you're getting that they have to betray people for that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That's also likely a big part of the reason Freeholds like having them. They're willing to get their hands dirty and to the more... unsavory jobs - the ones that everyone knows need to done, but no one wants to be the one to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, they could be useful. But they only regain clarity when their pragmatism impacts others. So, at best, they're as pale_crusader said, a hatchet man. However, aside from that they're probably viewed with suspicion and loathing. If anyone would get tied down in oaths it'd be them. <br /> <br /> Lest we forget that they also go insane if they come to trust anyone. More over, while they might act pragmatically they are more likely to do so to benefit themselves and not others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:33:35-08:00","id":818603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818600#post818600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true. An excellent example of a frequently pragmatic decision that other changelings might find distasteful is selling people back to the Gentry, especially if there is one &quot;greater good&quot; or another involved. This being said the fact they are darklings in the first place is a <u>HUGE</u> &quot;Beware of Betrayal&quot; disclaimer right in their seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to get at is, if a Changeling doesn't have that same disclaimer for every single other Changeling, regardless of Seeming, she's going to get herself turned in for a Token <i>real quick</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818600#post818600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine being a darkling is a lot like being the freehold hatchetman that no one really likes or allows too close but always respects at a safe distance. Where pragmatism trumps loyalty, there be a den of serpents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point of Darklings is that they're not any more pragmatic than other Lost, they're just more transparent about it. They follow the words of good ol' captain Jack - a dishonest man you can always trust to be dishonest. It's the &quot;honest&quot; ones you've got to watch out for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:38:14-08:00","id":818607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818602#post818602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, they could be useful. But they only regain clarity when their pragmatism impacts others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does the writeup say that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818602#post818602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, at best, they're as pale_crusader said, a hatchet man. However, aside from that they're probably viewed with suspicion and loathing. If anyone would get tied down in oaths it'd be them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As should all Lost be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818602#post818602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lest we forget that they also go insane if they come to trust anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not terribly remarkable in a society as untrusting as the Lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818602#post818602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More over, while they might act pragmatically they are more likely to do so to benefit themselves and not others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does the writeup say that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:11:30-08:00","id":818670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does the writeup say that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exact sentence from Clarity of Abandon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any time a Darkling is forced to step in and make a bad choice for other characters, make the choice no one else could, she gains a a sense of herself. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:17:30-08:00","id":818673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818670#post818670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here:</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the exact opposite of &quot;benefit themselves and not others.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:28:45-08:00","id":818684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818673#post818673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the exact opposite of &quot;benefit themselves and not others.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Gaining a sense of oneself sounds pretty beneficial to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:38:05-08:00","id":818692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818684#post818684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Gaining a sense of oneself sounds pretty beneficial to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;For other characters&quot; is directly counter to &quot;and not others&quot; regardless of motivation. A Darkling doesn't regain Clarity for selling out their motley to save their own skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:39:59-08:00","id":818694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818607#post818607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does the writeup say that?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blessing: Clarity of Abandon. There are just times when the <b>best choice is the worst choice</b>. Any time a Darkling is forced to step in and <b>make a bad choice for other characters</b>, make the choice no one else could, <b>she gains a a sense of herself</b>. She regain a point of Clarity for free. It is, of course, important for a Storyteller to machinate these sorts of situations about once a story, as much as it is a <b>Darkling\u2019s tendency to seek out these situations for herself.</b> </div> </div> </div>To regain clarity they must make a choice that negatively impacts someone else, and it seems to imply (more than anything else) that these choices must be made for allies. Eg. Choosing to fight someone wouldn't regain clarity, even if you're making a bad choice for your opponent because you're fighting them. On the other hand, refusing to fight along-side allies in a heated battle would regain you clarity. Darklings run on backstabbing and betrayal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818607#post818607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As should all Lost be.<br /> <br /> That's not terribly remarkable in a society as untrusting as the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Curse: A Shade\u2019s Distrust. A Darkling has been injured in the past, and believes she\u2019s injured others to survive. A Darkling trusted once, a long time ago, and anyone asking her to trust may be pushing her too hard. <b>Trusting anyone</b>, even a Darklings\u2019 closest allies, following them blindly, causes the Darkling to suffer a Clarity break. </div> </div> </div>Thing is that it's literally the act of <b>trusting anyone</b> that makes them go insane. Changelings, Mortals, Vampires, Demons, etc. If you can name it, they can't trust it. It's not a consequence of Changeling society, it's a consequence of being a Darkling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818692#post818692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;For other characters&quot; is directly counter to &quot;and not others&quot; regardless of motivation. A Darkling doesn't regain Clarity for selling out their motley to save their own skin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are wrong about this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:51:33-08:00","id":818705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818694#post818694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is that it's literally the act of <b>trusting anyone</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Blindly.</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498215#post498215\">There was already discussion on this in the appropriate thread</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses\">that's carried forward</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:54:29-08:00","id":818710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818705#post818705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blindly.</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498215#post498215\">There was already discussion on this in the appropriate thread</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses\">that's carried forward</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, well I didn't see that. The formatting spoke to me of &quot;Trusting anyone&quot; and/or &quot;Following Blindly.&quot; Still, this lack of trust seems like it'd make them basically impossible to work with in more than the most superficial manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-28-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:57:53-08:00","id":818715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818694#post818694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To regain clarity they must make a choice that negatively impacts someone else, and it seems to imply (more than anything else) that these choices must be made for allies. Eg. Choosing to fight someone wouldn't regain clarity, even if you're making a bad choice for your opponent because you're fighting them. On the other hand, refusing to fight along-side allies in a heated battle would regain you clarity. Darklings run on backstabbing and betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrase &quot;negatively impacts someone else&quot; is not anywhere in the text you just quoted. She's stepping in to make the bad choice <i>for someone else</i>. As in, <i>so they don't have to make it themselves.</i> It's a &quot;the hero we need, but not the one we deserve&quot; kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818694#post818694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is that it's literally the act of <b>trusting anyone</b> that makes them go insane. Changelings, Mortals, Vampires, Demons, etc. If you can name it, they can't trust it. It's not a consequence of Changeling society, it's a consequence of being a Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trusting Blindly is a Clarity Breaking Point because it was blind trust that landed them in Arcadia in the first place. That doesn't mean they can't trust with good reason. And it also doesn't mean the rest of Changeling society are automatically trusting. Changelings don't trust other Changelings, so they're not surprised when Darklings (who are Changelings) don't trust other Changelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818694#post818694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are wrong about this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's definitely right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:58:48-08:00","id":818716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818694#post818694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darklings run on backstabbing and betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily true. Is that the easiest option, the path of least resistance? Sure. But here's a few examples of how Darklings can regain clarity without harming others:<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;Someone has to investigate that Hollow. There might be a clue there, but if we go, we might trigger a trap left by Jack's Keeper.&quot;<br /> Darkling: &quot;I'll do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;We have to negotiate with the werewolves, but one wrong word and whoever does it is going to end up in shreds.&quot;<br /> Darkling: &quot;I'll do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;We have to stop that Huntsman! It's going after our loved ones one by one until we give him Jill!&quot;<br /> Darkling: &quot;I'll take him out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Darklings can regain Clarity by choosing to be brave, to do what everyone else is too afraid to do, those risky things that are <i>bad ideas</i> and <i>bad decisions</i>, but someone has to do it in order for things to go well. Not all Darklings are hatchet men. Some are daredevils, lone wolves, thrill seekers, antiheroes, madmen or all of the above. Darklings, to regain Clarity, must do something others balk at doing. And that can be bravery instead of treachery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:02:57-08:00","id":818718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818716#post818716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not necessarily true. Is that the easiest option, the path of least resistance? Sure. But here's a few examples of how Darklings can regain clarity without harming others:<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;Someone has to investigate that Hollow. There might be a clue there, but if we go, we might trigger a trap left by Jack's Keeper.&quot;<br /> Darkling: &quot;I'll do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;We have to negotiate with the werewolves, but one wrong word and whoever does it is going to end up in shreds.&quot;<br /> Darkling: &quot;I'll do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;We have to stop that Huntsman! It's going after our loved ones one by one until we give him Jill!&quot;<br /> Darkling: &quot;I'll take him out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Darklings can regain Clarity by choosing to be brave, to do what everyone else is too afraid to do, those risky things that are <i>bad ideas</i> and <i>bad decisions</i>, but someone has to do it in order for things to go well. Not all Darklings are hatchet men. Some are daredevils, lone wolves, thrill seekers, antiheroes, madmen or all of the above. Darklings, to regain Clarity, must do something others balk at doing. And that can be bravery instead of treachery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I see &quot;Bad&quot; in a different context, because when I see &quot;Bad&quot; I see &quot;Negative&quot; not &quot;Bad&quot; as in &quot;Risky.&quot; The whole throwing yourself in danger seems to run counter to their Curse, because you're putting trust into others to throw yourself into danger. It doesn't seem to follow, the two appear to conflict. This is hwy I see &quot;Bad&quot; as in &quot;Negative&quot; as doing what you're saying involves investing trust, which would be a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:14:08-08:00","id":818726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818718#post818718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole throwing yourself in danger seems to run counter to their Curse, because you're putting trust into others to throw yourself into danger. It doesn't seem to follow, the two appear to conflict. This is hwy I see &quot;Bad&quot; as in &quot;Negative&quot; as doing what you're saying involves investing trust, which would be a breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you ever assume that being in danger means trusting someone? Hell, why would you assume that <i>caring</i> about someone means that you trust them? Let's break both things down right quick:<br /> <br /> I can go and take on a danger and not trust anybody to help me or see me through. This is extremely common IRL and I don't think it merits any further explanation. Darklings don't need to trust people in order to run risks. Hell, you could say that merely <i>existing </i>as a changeling is a risk.<br /> <br /> Now, for the caring part. It is entirely possible that you can develop affections and relationships without trust. Now, <i>they</i> might trust <i>you</i>, but it doesn't have to go both ways. Will this relationship be healthy? Probably not, unless the Darkling takes careful steps to maintain an appearance of trust that pacifies his partner. But there is a difference, if subtle, between <i>not trusting</i> and <i>distrusting</i>. A changeling can care about someone they don't trust by accepting &quot;not trusting&quot; as their baseline state (which is what the text suggests), and saving their overt <i>distrust</i> for people they suspect of harmful intent.<br /> <br /> Is it risky to care about someone you don't trust? Absolutely. However, it builds up on the idea of darklings being daredevils instead of backstabbers, so it does fit thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:15:20-08:00","id":818728,"title":"","content":"I read it as Darklings regain clarity when they <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ShootTheDog\" target=\"_blank\">Shoot the Dog</a>. The Darkling makes those hard choices because no one else will. They escaped because they made such a decision in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be an intentional, conscious act of betrayal that gets them out of Arcadia, but it can easily feel like one because they made a decision, and benefited from it while someone else suffered. It might have been a painful split second decision, or a cold calculation that the needs of the many outweighed the needs of the few. Part of what makes a Darkling is that there was no ideal course of action that would have benefited everyone involved. They made a hard decision because they didn't see an easier answer coming up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JQJA5YjvHDU\" target=\"_blank\">Darklings excel at Missile Command</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:22:43-08:00","id":818731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818692#post818692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;For other characters&quot; is directly counter to &quot;and not others&quot; regardless of motivation. A Darkling doesn't regain Clarity for selling out their motley to save their own skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly true. However he could either sell out his motley to save the freehold, or sell out his freehold to save his motley to regain clarity. Those in particular probably violates oath... Speaking of Oaths I am excited to see the new pledge mechanics. If you are not protected by a pledge the Darkling is under then you are on <u>VERY</u> thin ice, and find yourself near the top of sacrifice-when-needed list.<br /> <br /> <i>Shane the Darkling hands his motley mate, Richard the Wizened, a clay token of Reprieve right before leaving him at his workshop door, the night after it was revealed the investigation into the strangled raver-girl downtown mean that a Huntsman was after Richard. Shocked, Richard's stared into Shane's pitch black eyes unable to voice his many questions. Shane just shakes his head and says, &quot;We knew your huntsmen would be coming soon when that Huntsman came for Cassy last month.&quot; Silently Richard glances down at the token, a knot in his gut. Cassy was a Beast barely out of the hedge a week when her Huntsman came for her and hadn't accepted Fealty under the Freehold charter, so she wasn't protected by that oath. Guilt filling his chest at the thought of what his mate did on his behalf and anxious about how he was going to explain his luck to the freehold, Richard turned from Shane to enter his workshop.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-28-2016, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:25:57-08:00","id":818734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818726#post818726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you ever assume that being in danger means trusting someone? Hell, why would you assume that <i>caring</i> about someone means that you trust them? Let's break both things down right quick:<br /> <br /> I can go and take on a danger and not trust anybody to help me or see me through. This is extremely common IRL and I don't think it merits any further explanation. Darklings don't need to trust people in order to run risks. Hell, you could say that merely <i>existing </i>as a changeling is a risk.<br /> <br /> Now, for the caring part. It is entirely possible that you can develop affections and relationships without trust. Now, <i>they</i> might trust <i>you</i>, but it doesn't have to go both ways. Will this relationship be healthy? Probably not, unless the Darkling takes careful steps to maintain an appearance of trust that pacifies his partner. But there is a difference, if subtle, between <i>not trusting</i> and <i>distrusting</i>. A changeling can care about someone they don't trust by accepting &quot;not trusting&quot; as their baseline state (which is what the text suggests), and saving their overt <i>distrust</i> for people they suspect of harmful intent.<br /> <br /> Is it risky to care about someone you don't trust? Absolutely. However, it builds up on the idea of darklings being daredevils instead of backstabbers, so it does fit thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if you look at the subtext to Darklings and Fairest they have opposing themes. Darklings focus on sacrificing others, and Fairest focus on sacrificing themselves. I don't know how this keeps getting missed by the readers here (Or perhaps I'm just the daft one) but it seems like people keep forgetting that the theme of the Darklings is betrayal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aren't the Beasts the more daredevil type?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In her mind, or in reality, that meant screwing someone else over. It meant leaving someone behind. It meant taking advantage of the situation and making the hard choice not the right choice. And in that decision, she let shadows in, she accepted it in and abandoned the light and righteous path. She decided, in that key moment, that the righteous are fools or liars, and she would be neither. </div> </div> </div>That, to me, speaks of them betraying another to save their own hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-28-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:35:09-08:00","id":818743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818734#post818734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you look at the subtext to Darklings and Fairest they have opposing themes. Darklings focus on sacrificing others, and Fairest focus on sacrificing themselves. I don't know how this keeps getting missed by the readers here (Or perhaps I'm just the daft one) but it seems like people keep forgetting that the theme of the Darklings is betrayal.<br /> <br /> That, to me, speaks of them betraying another to save their own hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme of Darklings is not betrayal, it's hard choices. Sometimes that includes betrayal, but not always.<br /> <br /> You seem to assume that people are machines that do the same thing over and over again. There is such a thing as <i>context</i> and <i>nuance</i> that affects what people do. There is also <i>character growth</i> and <i>change over time</i>. This is the exact same problem you had with the Beast Seeming. You are hyperfocusing on a single aspect, excluding everything else, and then assuming that that aspect is the entirety of the Seeming.<br /> <br /> You will find things a lot more palatable if, instead of being reductionist and trying to boil things down to a single, easily digestible concept, you do the exact opposite. Expand concepts you don't quite agree with or like. Push the envelope, stretch definitions.<br /> <br /> I didn't like the idea of a sixth of a Freehold being people who have to betray others to stay sane, so I pushed. I expanded boundaries, sought out alternative, creative definitions. It's way better to say &quot;my darklings are less about betrayal and more about being daredevils and lone wolves&quot; than to say &quot;I don't like darklings and I'm going to complain about it repeatedly.&quot; The former is practical and productive, the latter is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:06:03-08:00","id":818768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818728#post818728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read it as Darklings regain clarity when they <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ShootTheDog\" target=\"_blank\">Shoot the Dog</a>. The Darkling makes those hard choices because no one else will. They escaped because they made such a decision in Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to bump this since it seems you missed it Reshy, I think you misunderstood this quote from the preview:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Any time a Darkling is forced to step in and make a bad choice for other characters, make the choice no one else could</i></span></span><br /> <br /> It doesn't mean the result of the choice is bad for the other character, it means the choice is bad and the Darkling makes it so that the other character doesn't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Fixing a typo 01-28-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:37:33-08:00","id":818786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818743#post818743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theme of Darklings is not betrayal, it's hard choices. Sometimes that includes betrayal, but not always.</div> </div> </div> </div>You hit the nail on the head there. Darklings are pragmatists. They do what needs to be done, even when no one else can (or will) bring themselves to do it. Sometimes that means betraying or sacrificing other people. Sometimes it means being the one who kills the suspected Loyalist to keep the Freehold safe. Sometimes it means being the one who beats up the bad guy to get the location of the bombs before they both go off, while everyone else looks the other way and pretends they aren't complicit in torture. Sometimes it means taking the bad rap so the Fairest who fucked up can save face. Darklings don't have to hurt others for personal benefit to regain Clarity, they just have to put what's best over what's right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:45:27-08:00","id":818795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You will find things a lot more palatable if, instead of being reductionist and trying to boil things down to a single, easily digestible concept, you do the exact opposite. Expand concepts you don't quite agree with or like. Push the envelope, stretch definitions. </div> </div> </div>You act like I do it intentionally to provoke a reaction, I don't. It just the way my brain processes information. &quot;Change the way you think about things&quot; is not exactly something that's easy to do intentionally. The fact I'm even talking about it, and asking about it is me trying to gain some perspective. However, all information is still filtered through my biases and preconceptions, and I don't know if I can really help that or not. Sorry if it bugs you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818743#post818743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The theme of Darklings is not betrayal, it's hard choices. Sometimes that includes betrayal, but not always.<br /> <br /> You seem to assume that people are machines that do the same thing over and over again. There is such a thing as <i>context</i> and <i>nuance</i> that affects what people do. There is also <i>character growth</i> and <i>change over time</i>. This is the exact same problem you had with the Beast Seeming. You are hyperfocusing on a single aspect, excluding everything else, and then assuming that that aspect is the entirety of the Seeming.<br /> <br /> I didn't like the idea of a sixth of a Freehold being people who have to betray others to stay sane, so I pushed. I expanded boundaries, sought out alternative, creative definitions. It's way better to say &quot;my darklings are less about betrayal and more about being daredevils and lone wolves&quot; than to say &quot;I don't like darklings and I'm going to complain about it repeatedly.&quot; The former is practical and productive, the latter is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The three themes I get from Darklings are &quot;Abandonment&quot; &quot;Betrayal&quot; and &quot;Pragmatism&quot; in about that order. The thing is, if it's about being pragmatic I think the text should be more obvious about it. <b>This has probably already been fixed or addressed, in all fairness</b>. However, the fact that their pragmatism is tinged with their feelings of abandonment and betrayal speaks to me that together a lot of their pragmatism would be shaped around these. &quot;I don't need anyone else&quot; and &quot;I can't trust anyone else.&quot; Your examples about sacrificing ones self to help your friends, as far as I can tell by the text as I understand it, would inflict a breaking point. Why? Because you're risking your own neck for people you don't trust, you're being loyal to these people. This comes across as exactly what the &quot;blindly following&quot; would involve. It doesn't mean that you're a lemming, but it does mean that you are more focused on yourself.<br /> <br /> I mean, an example of a non-betrayal example would be like executing an antagonist rather than keeping them in prison, because we all know that if you lock them up they'll eventually escape (Also, because it's Changelings and they run on stuff like that). If he saw Batman bringing in the Joker for the second time in a month to put him in the locker, he'd probably ask Batman to look the other way and execute him himself. Brutal, pragmatic, and thematically appropriate. However, Darklings going out of their way to be the willing sacrifice? That's the Fairest's themes, not the Darklings. Willing to throw your life on the line like that I would consider &quot;Blind Faith.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the last thing regarding 1/6th being backstabbing scumbags, that might actually be within the theme of the game. For instance, if no one trusts the Darklings then they'll be on the fringe of society, playing into their themes of abandonment. It would also be pragmatic, in a way. If the freehold is attacked, they can easily distance themselves from it. They aren't as tied down by the courts as well (Not counting mystic oaths). <br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly on the concept of character growth, the problem is that their curse inhibits their opportunities at growth. Maybe this has been addressed, but I think that the curse would be better if they lost clarity whenever someone betrays them that they trust (or think that they've been betrayed), rather than it being a breaking point for the mere act of trusting. As far as I know, from what has been released so far, there does not seem to be any way to circumnavigate your Curse. This means, to a greater or lesser degree, that the Darkling can never truly trust anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:47:25-08:00","id":818797,"title":"","content":"So, as examples of scenarios when Darklings would get Clarity:<br /> <br /> Motley: &quot;We've found this Token of Reprieve, but who holds on to it? Who do we trust to keep it? Argue, squabble, possible violence.&quot;<br /> Darkling: *takes token, breaks it* &quot;There. Now no one needs to be saddled with that kind of temptation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;We know there's more Huntsmen coming. We need to keep this weapon. But it will only stay if we throw Enpy here back to their Keeper.&quot;<br /> Darkling: *grabs weapon, breaks it* &quot;It's not worth that price.&quot;<br /> alt!Darkling: *throws Enpy through a Hedge Door* &quot;It's worth it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Huntsman: &quot;Mwahaha, choose, puny Changeling! The freedom of your friend, or yours!&quot;<br /> Changeling: &quot;I, I, I choose--&quot;<br /> Darkling: *shoots friend* &quot;They choose themself. Now get out of here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, things that are hard choices, rather than bad ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:50:51-08:00","id":818801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818797#post818797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as examples of scenarios when Darklings would get Clarity:<br /> <br /> Motley: &quot;We've found this Token of Reprieve, but who holds on to it? Who do we trust to keep it? Argue, squabble, possible violence.&quot;<br /> Darkling: *takes token, breaks it* &quot;There. Now no one needs to be saddled with that kind of temptation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;We know there's more Huntsmen coming. We need to keep this weapon. But it will only stay if we throw Enpy here back to their Keeper.&quot;<br /> Darkling: *grabs weapon, breaks it* &quot;It's not worth that price.&quot;<br /> alt!Darkling: *throws Enpy through a Hedge Door* &quot;It's worth it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Huntsman: &quot;Mwahaha, choose, puny Changeling! The freedom of your friend, or yours!&quot;<br /> Changeling: &quot;I, I, I choose--&quot;<br /> Darkling: *shoots friend* &quot;They choose themself. Now get out of here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, things that are hard choices, rather than bad ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly self-serving, seems appropriate. The examples of a Darkling throwing themselves into danger though, I don't think that really follows their theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:56:02-08:00","id":818805,"title":"","content":"Here are the things that are universally true of Darklings:<ul><li>They all made the choice that escaping Arcadia was more important to them than taking the moral high ground.</li> <li> They all have their sense of agency reinforced when they make those kinds of morally grey choices that would make others balk.</li> <li> They are all reminded of the trauma they experienced in Arcadia when they are forced to put blind faith in someone else.</li> </ul><br /> That's it. Any themes of betrayal and abandonment are non-essential. If those three things are true of a character, the character can be a Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:57:47-08:00","id":818807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818805#post818805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are the things that are universally true of Darklings:[list][*]They all made the choice that escaping Arcadia was more important to them than taking the moral high ground.[*] They all have their sense of agency reinforced when they make those kinds of morally grey choices that would make others balk.[*] They are all reminded of the trauma they experienced in Arcadia when they are forced to put blind faith in someone else.That's it. Any themes of betrayal and abandonment are non-essential. If those three things are true of a character, the character can be a Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's completely fine then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:02:34-08:00","id":818811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818801#post818801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fairly self-serving, seems appropriate. The examples of a Darkling throwing themselves into danger though, I don't think that really follows their theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't break their theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:03:57-08:00","id":818812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818795#post818795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I think that the curse would be better if they lost clarity</div> </div> </div> </div><i>None</i> of the curses are &quot;you lose Clarity when.&quot; You <i>risk</i> Clarity in the circumstances established by your Seeming's curse, but a gamble is not a loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:04:33-08:00","id":818813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818811#post818811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't break their theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sure? Shadowknight's example of a Darkling going out to fight and probably die to give the rest of the group some time would seemingly to me be in the realm of &quot;blind faith.&quot; Not that they <b>couldn't</b> but it'd remind them of their time in Arcadia and most certainly not count for clarity regeneration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818812#post818812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>None</i> of the curses are &quot;you lose Clarity when.&quot; You <i>risk</i> Clarity in the circumstances established by your Seeming's curse, but a gamble is not a loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, risk clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:10:16-08:00","id":818817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818801#post818801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The examples of a Darkling throwing themselves into danger though, I don't think that really follows their theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <b>exactly</b> the sort of thing a good-hearted Darkling would do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Someone has to sacrifice themselves. Everyone else is just going to waste time trying to work out some impossible and dangerous gamble to save everyone, but will instead end up getting us all killed. So I'm going to do the pragmatic thing and sacrifice myself. Someone has to do it, so it might as well be me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:11:49-08:00","id":818818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818817#post818817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <b>exactly</b> the sort of thing a good-hearted Darkling would do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Someone has to sacrifice themselves. Everyone else is just going to waste time trying to work out some impossible and dangerous gamble to save everyone, but will instead end up getting us all killed. So I'm going to do the pragmatic thing and sacrifice myself. Someone has to do it, so it might as well be me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a stretch for me. I mean you <b>could</b> do it, but I don't think it'd regain you any clarity. In fact, offering up to be the sacrificial lamb I'd think gets you a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:29:56-08:00","id":818827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818795#post818795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You act like I do it intentionally to provoke a reaction, I don't. It just the way my brain processes information. &quot;Change the way you think about things&quot; is not exactly something that's easy to do intentionally. The fact I'm even talking about it, and asking about it is me trying to gain some perspective. However, all information is still filtered through my biases and preconceptions, and I don't know if I can really help that or not. Sorry if it bugs you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I tell you that is because I used to be similarly reductionist, but I've found that my enjoyment of things has greatly improved when I choose to stretch them rather than condense them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818795#post818795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your examples about sacrificing ones self to help your friends, as far as I can tell by the text as I understand it, would inflict a breaking point. Why? Because you're risking your own neck for people you don't trust, you're being loyal to these people.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume that the changeling doesn't enjoy the act of doing something others are too afraid of doing. You assume the changeling is acting like a Fairest, nobly sacrificing themselves for others. It doesn't have to be that way. It can be that the darkling <i>enjoys</i> being in danger, facing what nobody else does, taking on the monster everyone fears. And if it helps his friends, then hey, bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818795#post818795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willing to throw your life on the line like that I would consider &quot;Blind Faith.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't have to be that way. It can actually be a symptom of pride and superiority. I can easily imagine a darkling that looks down on people, considering them blind, trusting sheep, easily frightened and manipulated. That way, taking on a dangerous mission would be less about blind faith and more about disdain towards the capabilities of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818795#post818795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the last thing regarding 1/6th being backstabbing scumbags, that might actually be within the theme of the game. For instance, if no one trusts the Darklings then they'll be on the fringe of society, playing into their themes of abandonment. It would also be pragmatic, in a way. If the freehold is attacked, they can easily distance themselves from it. They aren't as tied down by the courts as well (Not counting mystic oaths).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Loyalists cover the &quot;outcast&quot; and &quot;backstabbing scumbag&quot; Seeming a lot better than Darklings. Darklings, to me, are the rogues of the freehold. Some may be backstabby, but others can play on the &quot;lovable rogue&quot; archetype and be cast in a more positive light. Hell, from the Darkling themes, you'd think there would be an equal amount of darklings who accept betrayal as a part of who they are and darklings who loathe betrayal because they've suffered it themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818795#post818795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly on the concept of character growth, the problem is that their curse inhibits their opportunities at growth. Maybe this has been addressed, but I think that the curse would be better if they lost clarity whenever someone betrays them that they trust (or think that they've been betrayed), rather than it being a breaking point for the mere act of trusting. As far as I know, from what has been released so far, there does not seem to be any way to circumnavigate your Curse. This means, to a greater or lesser degree, that the Darkling can never truly trust anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is entirely possible that, if you don't mind your Clarity going up and down fairly often, to trust people as a darkling while making the hard decisions for them. In fact, both things complement each other that way. The changeling loses sanity when they trust, so they reclaim their agency by making the hard choices for those they care about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818813#post818813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You sure? Shadowknight's example of a Darkling going out to fight and probably die to give the rest of the group some time would seemingly to me be in the realm of &quot;blind faith.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to assume that a changeling is acting altruistically by facing danger. There's a reason I used the terms &quot;thrill-seeker&quot; and &quot;daredevil.&quot; It's entirely possible that a darkling <i>enjoys</i> taking risks <i>because</i> they are things others avoid, because doing that thing everyone is too afraid to do gives them a sense of agency that reminds them of their escape. Hell, take this example of a darkling that escapes Arcadia: A bunch of changelings are locked up and forced to do whatever, and the Keeper says that whoever passes the Trial of the Seven Fires can claim the Golden Key and escape. However, there is only one Key and only one changeling can escape. The changeling that chooses to go through the Trial that everyone else is too afraid to do, claims the Key (and technically &quot;betrays&quot; the others by taking their means of escape) can easily become a daredevil that thrives when they face something that others are too cowardly to face.<br /> <br /> Hell, you can even spin that darkling as being <i>regretful</i> that the Keeper forced him to betray the others, and seek to avoid betrayal at all costs because it makes him feel like he's playing by his Keeper's game. Any Durance where the Keeper forces changelings to step on each other in order to escape and/or survive spawns darklings that <i>didn't mean to betray anyone and may feel horrible about it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:35:49-08:00","id":818833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818812#post818812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>None</i> of the curses are &quot;you lose Clarity when.&quot; You <i>risk</i> Clarity in the circumstances established by your Seeming's curse, but a gamble is not a loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that. But, I run into this same bit of dissonance when talking about Humanity in Vampire. <br /> <br /> Statistically, you're not actually likely to lose Clarity when you reach a breaking point. What you're likely to do is get a Condition and net a Beat. Ultimately, if you play it up, this means two Beats. <br /> <br /> You're not being punished or losing anything most of the time; most of the time, your character grows from the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:43:35-08:00","id":818836,"title":"","content":"In short, roleplaying incentives is the new name of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:46:29-08:00","id":818837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818827#post818827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I tell you that is because I used to be similarly reductionist, but I've found that my enjoyment of things has greatly improved when I choose to stretch them rather than condense them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, but it takes time. Not to mention that we probably aren't identical in thought so our developmental patterns are different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818827#post818827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You assume that the changeling doesn't enjoy the act of doing something others are too afraid of doing. You assume the changeling is acting like a Fairest, nobly sacrificing themselves for others. It doesn't have to be that way. It can be that the darkling <i>enjoys</i> being in danger, facing what nobody else does, taking on the monster everyone fears. And if it helps his friends, then hey, bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just seems contrary to their theme. Again, it's not that they <b>couldn't</b> do it, but they don't get a special clarity boost from it. Might help though if there are examples of valid clarity boosts to better substantiate what they're supposed to aim for in that regard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818827#post818827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't have to be that way. It can actually be a symptom of pride and superiority. I can easily imagine a darkling that looks down on people, considering them blind, trusting sheep, easily frightened and manipulated. That way, taking on a dangerous mission would be less about blind faith and more about disdain towards the capabilities of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a bit different from what you were seemingly suggesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818827#post818827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Loyalists cover the &quot;outcast&quot; and &quot;backstabbing scumbag&quot; Seeming a lot better than Darklings. Darklings, to me, are the rogues of the freehold. Some may be backstabby, but others can play on the &quot;lovable rogue&quot; archetype and be cast in a more positive light. Hell, from the Darkling themes, you'd think there would be an equal amount of darklings who accept betrayal as a part of who they are and darklings who loathe betrayal because they've suffered it themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that if any Seeming was a Privateer it'd probably be the Darkling. At any rate, they are roguish, that's fine. I'm not saying it's not fine to have them, just that trusting them is far far far less likely to happen compared to other Seemings. They have their moral compromise reflected on their body. I would much rather that Darklings have the capacity to trust, rather than it being a breaking point. Then it seems less like it's limiting and more about being smart about who you trust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818827#post818827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is entirely possible that, if you don't mind your Clarity going up and down fairly often, to trust people as a darkling while making the hard decisions for them. In fact, both things complement each other that way. The changeling loses sanity when they trust, so they reclaim their agency by making the hard choices for those they care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to do it, I suppose. Though, the problem with making those choices is that people will inevitably judge you for it. I mean, to some capacity, the Changelings can understand that it's part of your behavior. On the other hand, there's always going to be that niggling doubt that when the chips are down you'll sell them out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818827#post818827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to assume that a changeling is acting altruistically by facing danger. There's a reason I used the terms &quot;thrill-seeker&quot; and &quot;daredevil.&quot; It's entirely possible that a darkling <i>enjoys</i> taking risks <i>because</i> they are things others avoid, because doing that thing everyone is too afraid to do gives them a sense of agency that reminds them of their escape. Hell, take this example of a darkling that escapes Arcadia: A bunch of changelings are locked up and forced to do whatever, and the Keeper says that whoever passes the Trial of the Seven Fires can claim the Golden Key and escape. However, there is only one Key and only one changeling can escape. The changeling that chooses to go through the Trial that everyone else is too afraid to do, claims the Key (and technically &quot;betrays&quot; the others by taking their means of escape) can easily become a daredevil that thrives when they face something that others are too cowardly to face.<br /> <br /> Hell, you can even spin that darkling as being <i>regretful</i> that the Keeper forced him to betray the others, and seek to avoid betrayal at all costs because it makes him feel like he's playing by his Keeper's game. Any Durance where the Keeper forces changelings to step on each other in order to escape and/or survive spawns darklings that <i>didn't mean to betray anyone and may feel horrible about it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem though is that the Darkling internalizes the act of betrayal/pragmatism. That's why I don't think these particular examples work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:51:16-08:00","id":818842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818813#post818813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You sure? Shadowknight's example of a Darkling going out to fight and probably die to give the rest of the group some time would seemingly to me be in the realm of &quot;blind faith.&quot; Not that they <b>couldn't</b> but it'd remind them of their time in Arcadia and most certainly not count for clarity regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? You don't need to put any faith in someone to put yourself in danger for their sake. A cynical person (which I imagine many Darklings are) could easily say &quot;you're probably going to get yourself killed anyway, but you've at least got a better chance if I make this call&quot;, that's making a difficult decision for someone else. That's a Clarity bump. Besides that, the blind part is key. If your faith is demonstrably justified, it's not blind and isn't a Clarity Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818813#post818813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, risk clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is often a desirable thing. As Dave points out, if nothing else you're at least going to get a Beat and a Condition out of the deal, which can get you another Beat. More if it's Persistent. And heck, you might succeed the Breaking Point roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-28-2016, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:58:45-08:00","id":818850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818837#post818837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds a bit different from what you were seemingly suggesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's different. It's a different example. Not every darkling works the same way, you won't find a single &quot;archetypal&quot; darkling that embodies the &quot;darkling essence&quot; and behaves in perfectly stereotypical ways. Different darklings approach their blessing and curse in different ways. I just showed you one of many ways what you were saying was false.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818837#post818837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if any Seeming was a Privateer it'd probably be the Darkling. At any rate, they are roguish, that's fine. I'm not saying it's not fine to have them, just that trusting them is far far far less likely to happen compared to other Seemings. They have their moral compromise reflected on their body. I would much rather that Darklings have the capacity to trust, rather than it being a breaking point. Then it seems less like it's limiting and more about being smart about who you trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the darkling was helping someone else by Privateering. That's an angle you're not getting. A darkling is not actually self-serving, in terms of their blessing. A darkling that makes a hard choice for himself doesn't regain Clarity. A darkling that makes a hard choice <i>for someone else</i> does.<br /> <br /> Taking from what MachineIV said, you will always gain XP for trusting people as a darkling, which makes you more powerful. Darklings <i>grow in power </i>by trusting others. You know what happens to characters that never take risks, avoid all confrontations, stay in their comfort zone and never do anything that might hurt them? They stay flat. They never grow, in power or otherwise. Darkling is the only seeming that gains literal character growth and experience from going through the learning pains of trusting others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818837#post818837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one way to do it, I suppose. Though, the problem with making those choices is that people will inevitably judge you for it. I mean, to some capacity, the Changelings can understand that it's part of your behavior. On the other hand, there's always going to be that niggling doubt that when the chips are down you'll sell them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if it benefits someone other than the darkling, or else he doesn't regain Clarity for it. The Seeming that sells other changelings out for their own benefit is the Loyalist, not the Darkling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818837#post818837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem though is that the Darkling internalizes the act of betrayal/pragmatism. That's why I don't think these particular examples work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to assume that internalising means mimicry. Internalising means &quot;to incorporate (the cultural values, mores, motives, etc., of another or of a group), as through learning, socialization, or identification.&quot; You incorporate the values, but it doesn't mean you mimic them. You simply accept that betrayal is a thing that happens to people, which is why you don't trust. It doesn't mean that you yourself are a betrayer. Or do you become a mugger when you get mugged and accept that it's just a thing that happens to people? You don't have to be a conman to be distrustful and accept that people get taken advantage of all the time.<br /> <br /> Are there darklings that become subsumed by their experiences? Of course. But it's not the norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:29:59-08:00","id":818866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818850#post818850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it's different. It's a different example. Not every darkling works the same way, you won't find a single &quot;archetypal&quot; darkling that embodies the &quot;darkling essence&quot; and behaves in perfectly stereotypical ways. Different darklings approach their blessing and curse in different ways. I just showed you one of many ways what you were saying was false.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the problem with personality powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818850#post818850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if the darkling was helping someone else by Privateering. That's an angle you're not getting. A darkling is not actually self-serving, in terms of their blessing. A darkling that makes a hard choice for himself doesn't regain Clarity. A darkling that makes a hard choice <i>for someone else</i> does.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're helping the Gentry, don't you know? After all, everything would be so much simpler if all the Changelings just let the Gentry call the shots. I mean, sure you'll kick and scream bloody murder, but ultimately it's for your own good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818850#post818850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking from what MachineIV said, you will always gain XP for trusting people as a darkling, which makes you more powerful. Darklings <i>grow in power </i>by trusting others. You know what happens to characters that never take risks, avoid all confrontations, stay in their comfort zone and never do anything that might hurt them? They stay flat. They never grow, in power or otherwise. Darkling is the only seeming that gains literal character growth and experience from going through the learning pains of trusting others.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't those exact things common in all characters, not specifically Darklings?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818850#post818850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if it benefits someone other than the darkling, or else he doesn't regain Clarity for it. The Seeming that sells other changelings out for their own benefit is the Loyalist, not the Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought that was Privateers (Who sell Changelings to the Gentry for kick-backs), not loyalists (Who have freedom in exchange for providing a steady stream of candidates).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818850#post818850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to assume that internalising means mimicry. Internalising means &quot;to incorporate (the cultural values, mores, motives, etc., of another or of a group), as through learning, socialization, or identification.&quot; You incorporate the values, but it doesn't mean you mimic them. You simply accept that betrayal is a thing that happens to people, which is why you don't trust. It doesn't mean that you yourself are a betrayer. Or do you become a mugger when you get mugged and accept that it's just a thing that happens to people? You don't have to be a conman to be distrustful and accept that people get taken advantage of all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the text (as written in the 1st draft) says that you betrayed someone else. So yes, you are, by definition, a betrayer. Whether or not you keep doing so is a different story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818850#post818850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there darklings that become subsumed by their experiences? Of course. But it's not the norm.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're not partially changed by the experience, wouldn't they have a different Seeming then? I guess that's the problem I am having. If they just ignore the Betrayal part, then why aren't they a separate seeming?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818842#post818842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? You don't need to put any faith in someone to put yourself in danger for their sake. A cynical person (which I imagine many Darklings are) could easily say &quot;you're probably going to get yourself killed anyway, but you've at least got a better chance if I make this call&quot;, that's making a difficult decision for someone else. That's a Clarity bump. Besides that, the blind part is key. If your faith is demonstrably justified, it's not blind and isn't a Clarity Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean you can <b>kind of</b> justify it. But if they're going to get themselves killed anyway, why let them pull you down with them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818842#post818842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is often a desirable thing. As Dave points out, if nothing else you're at least going to get a Beat and a Condition out of the deal, which can get you another Beat. More if it's Persistent. And heck, you might succeed the Breaking Point roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems kinda metagaming, but I'm not the designer. I do know that in my groups if you take a dramatic failure the STs usually punish you for it egregiously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:46:39-08:00","id":818874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean you can <b>kind of</b> justify it. But if they're going to get themselves killed anyway, why let them pull you down with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you know you would fare worse than them. Or, again, what if you've seen that they're worth trusting? What if they've proved time and time again that they can get the job done when given the chance? Buying them the time they need at a personal cost to yourself is a decision founded on pragmatism, not on blind faith.<br /> <br /> Besides that, sometimes making the tough call does mean trusting someone. In those situations, the Darkling gains Clarity and rolls a Breaking Point. Worst case scenario, it's a wash. Best case, you succeed (or maybe even exceptionally succeed) the Breaking Point roll and don't lose the Clarity you just gained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems kinda metagaming, but I'm not the designer. I do know that in my groups if you take a dramatic failure the STs usually punish you for it egregiously.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case, your groups don't sound like an environment I would enjoy playing in. But you do you. More importantly, this kind of &quot;metagaming&quot; is central to the design of CofD 2e. The system is meant to give the player out-of-character incentives to take actions that are not strictly beneficial to the character for the sake of drama. That's literally how characters grow and progress in this system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:48:38-08:00","id":818876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're helping the Gentry, don't you know? After all, everything would be so much simpler if all the Changelings just let the Gentry call the shots. I mean, sure you'll kick and scream bloody murder, but ultimately it's for your own good.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gentry don't need anybody to make hard decisions for them, so it doesn't count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't those exact things common in all characters, not specifically Darklings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, so a darkling's journey to character growth will happen through trusting others and making hard decisions for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought that was Privateers (Who sell Changelings to the Gentry for kick-backs), not loyalists (Who have freedom in exchange for providing a steady stream of candidates).</div> </div> </div> </div>Both types sell changelings back to Arcadia for their own benefit, they're just different benefits. The Darkling does not regain Clarity for doing so unless selling someone out helps someone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the text (as written in the 1st draft) says that you betrayed someone else. So yes, you are, by definition, a betrayer. Whether or not you keep doing so is a different story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't subscribe to the definition that a single act of betrayal makes you a betrayer, but that a <i>habit</i> of betraying makes you one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're not partially changed by the experience, wouldn't they have a different Seeming then? I guess that's the problem I am having. If they just ignore the Betrayal part, then why aren't they a separate seeming?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seemings are how you gain agency and escaped Arcadia. If you betray someone to escape, whether you liked it or not, you become a Darkling. You are changed by the experience but you don't have to continue doing it. One example given to the Fairest is that people will look up to them as leaders <i>whether the Fairest wants or enjoys it or not</i>. You can play a Fairest that did one good thing for someone and now everyone looks up to them and he hates it, and you can play a Darkling that did one bad thing to someone and now he can't trust people and he hates it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:49:14-08:00","id":818878,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I think that a Darkling and a Mage in the Guardians of the Veil could actually click really well, if their similarities didn't make them think the other is a threat. Both cling hard to the whole &quot;Hard Man making Hard Choices&quot; ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:50:13-08:00","id":818880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't those exact things common in all characters, not specifically Darklings?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, since blindly trusting someone isn't a breaking point for all characters, just darklings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they're not partially changed by the experience, wouldn't they have a different Seeming then? I guess that's the problem I am having. If they just ignore the Betrayal part, then why aren't they a separate seeming? </div> </div> </div>Changed yes. But it doesn't completely dominate who you are. It's more subtle than just &quot;Okay you have this seeming so your mind is now warped to think in this way&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems kinda metagaming, but I'm not the designer. I do know that in my groups if you take a dramatic failure the STs usually punish you for it egregiously. </div> </div> </div>Metagaming is the point to beats. That's why being able to turn a normal failure into a dramatic failure exists. Suffering in CofD leads to character development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:55:07-08:00","id":818882,"title":"","content":"I read a book the obter day called Servant of the Undedworld,the main car\u00e1cter was a warriors serving a God Of Death,and he had a pair of knives that could paralyse his enemies, but the interestimg about the knives is that they comfort him,when he touched the knives he was Reminded of emptiness of Undedworld and it made him calmer,more focused in his mission,in the chanfeling world,could he be a huntaman with a weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:12:04-08:00","id":818894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818866#post818866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems kinda metagaming, but I'm not the designer. I do know that in my groups if you take a dramatic failure the STs usually punish you for it egregiously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Games should not be exercises in punishment. At very least Chronicles of Darkness games should not be exercises in punishment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:34:40-08:00","id":818904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818876#post818876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't subscribe to the definition that a single act of betrayal makes you a betrayer, but that a <i>habit</i> of betraying makes you one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither people nor history view Traitors and Betrayal very well, heck there's <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/RewardedAsATraitorDeserves/RealLife\" target=\"_blank\">a reason why many traitors get executed</a>.<br /> <br /> Merely doing the act once is enough to ensure no one trusts you anymore the second they learn of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818876#post818876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seemings are how you gain agency and escaped Arcadia. If you betray someone to escape, whether you liked it or not, you become a Darkling. You are changed by the experience but you don't have to continue doing it. One example given to the Fairest is that people will look up to them as leaders <i>whether the Fairest wants or enjoys it or not</i>. You can play a Fairest that did one good thing for someone and now everyone looks up to them and he hates it, and you can play a Darkling that did one bad thing to someone and now he can't trust people and he hates it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, why is being looked down upon for this a bad thing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818874#post818874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you know you would fare worse than them. Or, again, what if you've seen that they're worth trusting? What if they've proved time and time again that they can get the job done when given the chance? Buying them the time they need at a personal cost to yourself is a decision founded on pragmatism, not on blind faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you justify pretty much every trusting action as pragmatic?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818874#post818874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides that, sometimes making the tough call does mean trusting someone. In those situations, the Darkling gains Clarity and rolls a Breaking Point. Worst case scenario, it's a wash. Best case, you succeed (or maybe even exceptionally succeed) the Breaking Point roll and don't lose the Clarity you just gained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows, I haven't seen it in play so I can't really say.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818874#post818874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, your groups don't sound like an environment I would enjoy playing in. But you do you. More importantly, this kind of &quot;metagaming&quot; is central to the design of CofD 2e. The system is meant to give the player out-of-character incentives to take actions that are not strictly beneficial to the character for the sake of drama. That's literally how characters grow and progress in this system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I can try to pass it by the ST and see what they think. The ST also uses shared beats as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818880#post818880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, since blindly trusting someone isn't a breaking point for all characters, just darklings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more referring to this: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know what happens to characters that never take risks, avoid all confrontations, stay in their comfort zone and never do anything that might hurt them? They stay flat. They never grow, in power or otherwise. </div> </div> </div>Anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818880#post818880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changed yes. But it doesn't completely dominate who you are. It's more subtle than just &quot;Okay you have this seeming so your mind is now warped to think in this way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's the defining character trait or flaw you pulled away from it, I'd imagine it'd be pretty significant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818880#post818880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metagaming is the point to beats. That's why being able to turn a normal failure into a dramatic failure exists. Suffering in CofD leads to character development</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818894#post818894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Games should not be exercises in punishment. At very least Chronicles of Darkness games should not be exercises in punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just saying how my group does it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:34:51-08:00","id":818905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818894#post818894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Games should not be exercises in punishment. At very least Chronicles of Darkness games should not be exercises in punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, looks like i bought such a nice whip for nothing,it nas some nice metal spikes in the end too ,#(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:43:47-08:00","id":818909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818904#post818904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merely doing the act once is enough to ensure no one trusts you anymore the second they learn of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. As I mentioned before, it's entirely possible any number of Darklings in your games (including most, if you so desire) come from Durances where the Keepers <i>forced</i> them into twisted games of betrayal/survival of the fittest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818904#post818904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, why is being looked down upon for this a bad thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's needlessly fracturing an already paranoid society? Like, in your games, run it however you want, but don't assume that's how everyone is going to run it that way, or that others don't run things in drastically different ways to yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:58:29-08:00","id":818916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818904#post818904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't you justify pretty much every trusting action as pragmatic?</div> </div> </div> </div>N... no? Not unless trusting is actually the pragmatic thing to do in that situation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you only get the Clarity gain once per story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818904#post818904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who knows, I haven't seen it in play so I can't really say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wha...? What is there to see in play? If you make the hard choice for someone that they can't make for themselves, you regain a point of Clarity. If making that choice also requires you to blindly trust someone, you get a Clarity Breaking Point. If you fail that Breaking Point, your Clarity is at the exact same level it was at before you made this particular tough choice. If you succeed that Breaking Point, your Clarity is higher than it was before you made the choice. Ergo, it's always a good bet for the Darkling to make that call, even if it requires them to trust someone, because they've literally got nothing to lose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818904#post818904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I can try to pass it by the ST and see what they think. The ST also uses shared beats as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pass what by your ST? It's not like I'm proposing some outlandish houserule, I'm literally just explaining how CofD works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T19:10:17-08:00","id":818924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818909#post818909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. As I mentioned before, it's entirely possible any number of Darklings in your games (including most, if you so desire) come from Durances where the Keepers <i>forced</i> them into twisted games of betrayal/survival of the fittest.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make any sense. The whole point of darklings is you gained <b>agency</b> though betrayal/pragmatism. If it's forced upon you then it's just a role like any other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818909#post818909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's needlessly fracturing an already paranoid society? Like, in your games, run it however you want, but don't assume that's how everyone is going to run it that way, or that others don't run things in drastically different ways to yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Seeming who's notable feature is betrayal and pragmatism could be useful, but it does not setup a good foundation for future relationships.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818916#post818916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">N... no? Not unless trusting is actually the pragmatic thing to do in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm unique in that I have an excuse or a rationale for basically anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818916#post818916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, you only get the Clarity gain once per story.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818916#post818916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wha...? What is there to see in play? If you make the hard choice for someone that they can't make for themselves, you regain a point of Clarity. If making that choice also requires you to blindly trust someone, you get a Clarity Breaking Point. If you fail that Breaking Point, your Clarity is at the exact same level it was at before you made this particular tough choice. If you succeed that Breaking Point, your Clarity is higher than it was before you made the choice. Ergo, it's always a good bet for the Darkling to make that call, even if it requires them to trust someone, because they've literally got nothing to lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, once per session. I guess it really depends on how your ST is running the game. Albeit, hopefully not in the &quot;drive everyone crazy&quot; way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818916#post818916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pass what by your ST? It's not like I'm proposing some outlandish houserule, I'm literally just explaining how CofD works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, just they have their own view of how the game should be played and found the &quot;failure beats&quot; weird and metagamey. I understand it's part of the rules, but I'm saying that it's one of the rules that my ST never quite liked or understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T19:26:21-08:00","id":818931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818924#post818924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't make any sense. The whole point of darklings is you gained <b>agency</b> though betrayal/pragmatism. If it's forced upon you then it's just a role like any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always choose to not to play, which may be a valid Fairest or Beast outcome to those. Overcoming the Keeper's challenge and claiming freedom IS agency, because you chose to do whatever it took to escape, even if it meant playing the Keeper's twisted games. Choosing to succumb would be the implicit alternative here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818924#post818924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Seeming who's notable feature is betrayal and pragmatism could be useful, but it does not setup a good foundation for future relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're useful, they can't be that reviled by society, logically speaking. Every Seeming has its personality flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T19:48:18-08:00","id":818941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818924#post818924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, just they have their own view of how the game should be played and found the &quot;failure beats&quot; weird and metagamey. I understand it's part of the rules, but I'm saying that it's one of the rules that my ST never quite liked or understood.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very strange though to levy criticisms against rules and design when they're intentionally being misused. Like, nobody's obligated to play straight out of the book. I know we encourage house ruling and stuff. But if you choose to not use the rules, it's hard to take it seriously when you talk about how things don't work. <br /> <br /> It's like if you decide to replace your car's spark plugs with carrots, then tell people that the car isn't working. Of course it isn't.<br /> <br /> If you think players don't constantly make choices for out-of-character reasons, that's probably a place where agreement here is just going to break down. I've literally never, in all my years seen, ran, or played in a game where players weren't consistently making choices for out-of-character reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T20:25:00-08:00","id":818956,"title":"","content":"Also, if you want a really easy way to conceptualise Darklings: <br /> <br /> When faced with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolley_problem\" target=\"_blank\">Trolley Dilemma</a>, Darklings don't even see it as a dilemma; they pull the lever with no hesitation. Most people view that as kinda creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T20:34:04-08:00","id":818963,"title":"","content":"I totally get where ReshyShira's coming from.<br /> <br /> I regularly play with two disparate groups of various NWoD/CofD games and the difficulty to transitioning over to the metagame currency style of CofD was literally too much for one of those groups so they're basically sticking with 1E from now on. The other group took to it like a fish to water, even in spite of some of the conditions being too heinous to resolve, the aspirations/beats/conditions cycles flowed pretty naturally and it worked really well.<br /> <br /> If you're having a hard time grasping that style of meta-roleplay with incentives and it doesn't come naturally to you, the rules can read like you've been given the ability to play six different flavours of fishmalk with hard stereotypes that are likely to destroy any cohesion your group has. There can be a huge amount of dissonance between the expectations of 1E and CofD, so I'm not surprised that this sort of issue keeps coming up during the preview when the mechanics get into the heavily meta area (especially in some areas I have myself gone &quot;wait what, how is that ever going to work?&quot; which I will willingly own starting arguments on).<br /> <br /> If you've got a group that gets it intuitively? It works really well. People enjoy the complications and interesting things. You get interesting stories and have a lot of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:18:30-08:00","id":819210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818956#post818956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you want a really easy way to conceptualise Darklings:<br /> <br /> When faced with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolley_problem\" target=\"_blank\">Trolley Dilemma</a>, Darklings don't even see it as a dilemma; they pull the lever with no hesitation. Most people view that as kinda creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moreover they don't even feel a twinge of guilt (because they just did the opposite of what would cause them to gain the Guilty condition) and actually feel more actualized by making that choice (because they gained Clarity, which means they gained clarity -it's important to remember game terms are real words too-). So, yeah the creepy factor is pretty high.<br /> <br /> It is important to remember a central theme of Changeling:the Lost is <i>Beautiful Madness</i>. The whole game has undertones of Lewis Carroll's writings and that changeling seemings all represent that character willingly carving out chunks of their own psyche to escape the prison of Arcadia, and ensures the theme of madness is present in every player character and many of the NPCs. (Fun idea for a terrifying time: Playing a sane mortal in a Changeling: the Lost Game, it would like being a sane person in a supernatural asylum)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-29-2016, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:33:02-08:00","id":819223,"title":"","content":"Which is why I don't think Darklings would get a bad rap in changeling society. Literally everyone in a Freehold is at least a little bit crazy. Durances <i>break</i> you, and the actions you took in Arcadia were the actions of a broken person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:01:31-08:00","id":819252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819223#post819223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I don't think Darklings would get a bad rap in changeling society. Literally everyone in a Freehold is at least a little bit crazy. Durances <i>break</i> you, and the actions you took in Arcadia were the actions of a broken person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good points, and well made.<br /> <br /> That being said, lets look outside of Changeling society. Couple madness and supernatural powers and you have a very explosive mix that can easily lead to what can be classified from a mortal perspective as monsters. Introspective changelings could easily be able to empathize with the mortal view of these types of problems and pursue protective feelings to an extreme were they become secret supernatural vigilantes (aka mentally-damaged super heroes, or supernatural monster-hunters). Having both in the same society means that society will be lopsided towards one side or other depending on who is most effective and who is most numerous. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=804036#post804036\">Here</a> is an example of one extreme towards the monster side of that scale. I draw my inspiration from a notorious Portland LARP community with a reputation of bullying other LARP communities. Please note I did not name which LARP community so if you are offended then you are also acknowledging being part of the problem, and I do not owe you an apology. Also note the city of Portland has a real life issue of Human trafficking, a history of shanghaiing and Pirate LARPs. There are privateers whispered of and reviled in cannon and I can think of no place better for such a group than Portland Oregon. (Mexico city is also a fine candidate due to being the kidnap capital of the world, but since they don't have Shanghaiing history and Pirate LARPs -that I'm aware of- they would not very likely have pirate-themed privateers)<br /> <br /> Woe to those that gain the attention of a Darkling vigilante. I mean Ogres will just use violence against you, which is no where as scary of what a motivated darkling is capable of. Also this is a fine testament of why you maintain supernatural conspiracies in the chronicles of darkness because drawing the attention of emotionally damaged changelings who have issues with people being victimized is very dangerous. (The same can be said of righteous or self-righteous Mages, Vampires, or Werewolves but Lost being mentally unbalanced raises volatility in their case.)<br /> <br /> Side note for Beasts: Kidnapping for the benefit of others is an available tool that is in the Darkling's potential toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-02-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:24:12-08:00","id":819269,"title":"","content":"I think most of changeling society is going to be shaped by the Courts of a given Freehold, barring major upheavals that change the current courts for new ones. So yeah, I agree, but I also think that there's plenty of room for all sorts of Freehold attitudes and changeling psychologies.<br /> <br /> One thing I forgot to mention that I thought of last night, re: Darklings et al., is that Seemings are not something you have to embrace. When you escape Arcadia, the Wyrd grants you the Seeming based on the action you took to escape. The Wyrd is a force that empowers narrative in the world, and making a dramatic narrative statement, such as escaping, draws the attention of the Wyrd. The Wyrd then looks at you and says &quot;This is who you are,&quot; and grants you your Seeming. The mechanics for gaining and risking Clarity are about your own psychological responses to that, however you want to justify them. Maybe the Darkling regains Clarity when he makes a hard decision for another person because they're performing a penance for the people they betrayed during their Durance. They think that since they're already &quot;tainted&quot;, they can do the dirty/risky work for others, and that in so doing, they will eventually find absolution.<br /> <br /> The way I see Seemings is as a sort of nonverbal &quot;contract&quot; between the changeling and the Wyrd. The changeling escapes, proves that they're narratively important, and the Wyrd gives them a gift, one that comes with a Blessing and Curse, and goes &quot;Okay, you got my attention, now go and be someone. Don't disappoint me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:51:45-08:00","id":819293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819210#post819210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is important to remember a central theme of Changeling:the Lost is <i>Beautiful Madness</i>. The whole game has undertones of Lewis Carroll's writings and that changeling seemings all represent that character willingly carving out chunks of their own psyche to escape the prison of Arcadia, and ensures the theme of madness is present in every player character and many of the NPCs. (Fun idea for a terrifying time: Playing a sane mortal in a Changeling: the Lost Game, it would like being a sane person in a supernatural asylum)</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the theme of 1st edition Changeling. Fortunately, David Hill has expressed intentions to move Changeling away from shallow, stereotypical portrayals of mental illness, so &quot;madness&quot; will thankfully not be a theme of Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:22:44-08:00","id":819315,"title":"","content":"I weather an action risks clarity or gains depends on the perpective of the Changeling more then objective fact. If the Changeling thinks he's in control of a situation, but in reality is relying on blind faith, but doesn't realize it, it doesn't activate the curse, but if the Darkling believes he's acting in blind faith, even if she's just being paraniod and isn't acting on blind faith, then the curse activates. Just personal opinion, this makes the in character perpective the abiter of the curse/blessing, not some attempt at external objectivity for something that will usually be entirely subjective.<br /> <br /> So the question becomes does the CHARACTER believe based on their beliefs/values, that an action is blind faith, or honourable betrayal for the greater good.<br /> <br /> This stops things from deevolving into a constant debate between the Storyteller and the players on if an action counts or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:24:22-08:00","id":819317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was the theme of 1st edition Changeling. Fortunately, David Hill has expressed intentions to move Changeling away from shallow, stereotypical portrayals of mental illness, so &quot;madness&quot; will thankfully not be a theme of Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that, but cutting major portions of their psyche is how they gain Seemings and their stability advantage is named Clarity, which implies a struggle to maintain clarity. Also the fact we track stability advantages at all convey themes that facing difficult things has emotional and mental affects on characters, sometimes in extreme cases results in madness, broken and fugue conditions but also states of being. And for all those reasons I respectfully disagree with the totality you state your claim. Maybe the theme is not as highlighted, which I would also disagree with but for now I concede to move the discussion along, it is just plain inaccurate to say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;madness&quot; will thankfully not be a theme of Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a side note I totally agree with<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">David Hill has expressed intentions to move Changeling away from shallow, stereotypical portrayals of mental illness.</div> </div> </div> </div>and that is entirely true; The portrayals are less shallow and with less stereotypical common misconceptions about mental illnesses. Mechanics that affect gaining and dealing with fear and guilt, brokenness, madness, and fugue which differ than &quot;normal&quot; character is a very nuanced and interesting way to deal with mental illness and damage to the psyche caused horrors near the edge of human imagination. Your conclusion that means madness will not be a theme is just incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-29-2016, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:37:41-08:00","id":819325,"title":"","content":"I think the goals/purpose of loyalists can be nearly anything, they can be spies on the locale freehold, they be allies to the huntsmen, they can recruit humans into a True Fae's service or to become future changelings, they could be gathering/collecting objects and stories from the mortal that they're master desires, they simply be rewarded for loyal service in Arcadia, they could be under orders to undermine the huntsmen &amp; loyalists of a rival True Fae, they could be sent to fight a threat that endangers the mortal world and by extension the interest of the True Fae, they could sent to the mortal world to explore a prophecy, or they could be sent with a purpose that makes no sense at all to most people.<br /> <br /> That's what makes the Loyalists so interesting compared to huntsmen, privateers, and other lackey's of the True Fae, they're purpose can be almost anything, it can be horrible in a veriety of ways or it can be belevent, and that's before you take into account the loyalists personal adgenda, like why they agreed to serve the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T11:03:13-08:00","id":819376,"title":"","content":"The game is now a Storytelling Game of Beautiful Lies and Bittersweet Truths, as an aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T11:41:16-08:00","id":819395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819317#post819317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that, but cutting major portions of their psyche is how they gain Seemings and their stability advantage is named Clarity, which implies a struggle to maintain clarity. Also the fact we track stability advantages at all convey themes that facing difficult things has emotional and mental affects on characters, sometimes in extreme cases results in madness, broken and fugue conditions but also states of being. And for all those reasons I respectfully disagree with the totality you state your claim. Maybe the theme is not as highlighted, which I would also disagree with but for now I concede to move the discussion along, it is just plain inaccurate to say:<br /> <br /> On a side note I totally agree with<br /> <br /> and that is entirely true; The portrayals are less shallow and with less stereotypical common misconceptions about mental illnesses. Mechanics that affect gaining and dealing with fear and guilt, brokenness, madness, and fugue which differ than &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; character is a very nuanced and interesting way to deal with mental illness and damage to the psyche caused horrors near the edge of human imagination. Your conclusion that means madness will not be a theme is just incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason I put madness in quotation marks. Changeling 2e deals heavily with themes of trauma and the mental health effects it can have. Mental illness is certainly something it deals with, but there's a big difference between that and &quot;madness&quot; which is an incredibly loaded term, especially in the context of RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T11:48:02-08:00","id":819398,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna put it out there, if they wanted to treat the word &quot;madness&quot; with more caution and respect, it may have been a good idea to rename the Madness Condition to something like Frantic or Unstable instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:11:26-08:00","id":819407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819398#post819398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just gonna put it out there, if they wanted to treat the word &amp;quot;madness&amp;quot; with more caution and respect, it may have been a good idea to rename the Madness Condition to something like Frantic or Unstable instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But, at least the description of the Condition makes it clear that it does not represent mental illness, but the result of supernatural mindfuckery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:23:37-08:00","id":819412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=818692#post818692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;For other characters&amp;quot; is directly counter to &amp;quot;and not others&amp;quot; regardless of motivation. A Darkling doesn't regain Clarity for selling out their motley to save their own skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this issue isn't as clear cut as you want it to be. Philosophers have debating the substance of helping the group to help oneself for millenia. At best this argument will be a push, so I'd let it go of I were you. Your position might not be a loser but it's also not a winner. No one's going to change anyone's mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:37:47-08:00","id":819424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819412#post819412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, this issue isn't as clear cut as you want it to be. Philosophers have debating the substance of helping the group to help oneself for millenia. At best this argument will be a push, so I'd let it go of I were you. Your position might not be a loser but it's also not a winner. No one's going to change anyone's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't have to change people's minds. He's right.<br /> <br /> Like Dave pointed out, Darklings aren't traitors by virtue of their blessings, they're the decision makers when everything is bad. Trolley can hit one person or five? Darklings condemn the one. Nuke the alien ship and lose a city or hope that a small team of four idiots can save the planet and risk the planet? The Darklings launch the nuke.<br /> <br /> Safety for the freehold for a year by giving themselves up or freedom for themselves for a number of years equal to every person taken? It's not a hard choice for the Darklings-they'll give themselves up.<br /> <br /> A Darkling does not reaffirm their sense of self when they betray people. They reaffirm their sense of self when they make the choice no one else can make. Unless the Loyalists write-up says otherwise, there will never be a Seeming that restores Clarity by throwing people under the bus. It might allow for it, but it will never be predicated solely on that principle.<br /> <br /> They're Mad-Eye Moodys, not Barty Crouch Jr's, as it were.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Better Example: They're the pre-Day of the Doctor War Doctor. Given the choice of letting a war roll around all of time and space, wrecking everything in its' parth and destroying/condemning their people to a pocket of madness in order to keep the universe safe, Darklings will take on every guilt that comes with being the last of their kind. If you want a conceivable betrayal scenario, if condemning every changeling to Arcadia meant denying anymore True Fae coming to Earth ever again, the Darklings'd do that. They'll fight to find an answer they like better than that, to challenge every bad ending in hopes of finding a good one.<br /> <br /> But if it comes down to two bad endings, you can trust the Darkling to take the lesser one before it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-29-2016, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:45:47-08:00","id":819430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819395#post819395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mental illness is certainly something it deals with, but there's a big difference between that and &quot;madness&quot; which is an incredibly loaded term, especially in the context of RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>On these we completely agree.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness definitely deal with mental illness and the word &quot;madness&quot; is extremely loaded, especially in the context of role playing games.<br /> <br /> I won't eschew the word &quot;madness&quot; simply because it contains certain romantic notions about the nature of the mind/heart and captures the grandiose theatrical whimsies of many works of fiction about the subject of delusions and the insane. Also sometimes my writing waxes poetic with honey laden prose which are very suited to the use of the word &quot;madness&quot;.<br /> <br /> I respect your clinical view points and desire for modern clear understanding in language about a profound and meaningful topic. Many great people have struggled with mental illnesses and malaise of the mind has been at the root of many horrific tragedies and brilliant inspirations. I also applaud you making your meaning and intentions plain in a respectful manner.<br /> <br /> :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-29-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:51:55-08:00","id":819433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819424#post819424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Darkling does not reaffirm their sense of self when they betray people. They reaffirm their sense of self when they make the choice no one else can make. Unless the Loyalists write-up says otherwise, there will never be a Seeming that restores Clarity by throwing people under the bus. It might allow for it, but it will never be predicated solely on that principle.<br /> <br /> They're Mad-Eye Moodys, not Barty Crouch Jr's, as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like it's become limited in the other direction. And it all feels like the distinctions are very arbitrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:01:42-08:00","id":819444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819433#post819433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like it's become limited in the other direction. And it all feels like the distinctions are very arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what's arbitrary about the distinction between &quot;making hard choices&quot; and &quot;betrayal&quot;. Like... They're two objectively different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:14:23-08:00","id":819456,"title":"","content":"I don't think that it's useful, productive or practical to try and focus on a single aspect of a Seeming when there are plenty of options to do things differently. People tone up or down things in their gamelines as it better suits their tastes. I have to tone down some of the grimdarkness in the setting to prevent darkness-induced apathy, and I've read posts here saying that such a thing is <i>precisely</i> the point of the game for them, and instead emphasise that aspect to its fullest. And both things are okay.<br /> <br /> The material written in the books is not sacrosanct. It's inspiration, guidelines, ideas, suggestions. Be a scavenger. Take what you like and discard the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:43:13-08:00","id":819478,"title":"","content":"It seems like people recalling what the Darkling says when they quote it in this thread is wondering away from the actual wording in the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-darklings/\" target=\"_blank\">Darkling </a>write-up again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clarity of Abandon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are just times when the best choice is the worst choice. Any time a Darkling is forced to step in and make a bad choice for other characters, make the choice no one else could, she gains a a sense of herself. She regain a point of Clarity for free.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This includes but is not limited to:<ul><li>Kidnapping a Beast to hand over to imprisonment to a Huntsmen for a Token of Reprieve to save someone else(besides yourself). (ie The Beast's worst fear)</li> <li>Killing the serial killer instead of turning him into the police where he has a chance to escape and hurt people again.</li> <li>Bring serious harm to someone a Fairest ordered to partner with you for the greater good of the freehold. (ie a Fairest's breaking point)</li> <li>Tell the Ogre the ugly truth he never acknowledged about those he hurts so he can stop. (ie an Ogre's breaking point)</li> <li>Cause a Wizened to fail a project she is working on because it'll bring ruin to her family life. (ie a Wizened's breaking point)</li> <li>Clandestinely murder anyone's friend who is truly a burden and whom they'd be better off without. (a pretty terrifying thought)</li> <li>Require another Darkling to trust her because she needs to be trusted to help even though the Darkling knows exactly how traumatic that is for the other Darkling. (ie a Darkling's breaking point)</li> <li>Tell the Elemental the ugly truth about those hurt in its chaotic wake to get the Elemental to realize they have to be more considerate of others. (ie an Elemental's breaking point)</li> <li><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> destroying a Token of Reprieve to prevent a Motley from tearing itself apart over it.</div> </div> </div> </div></li> </ul><br /> <br /> There is a whole lot of room to hurt/upset others in the name of helping others (who may be the person you are upsetting/hurting, and sometimes it is someone else). This can be used as an antihero, an antagonist motivated by the welfare of those other than himself, or a dark protagonist. All are valid expressions of these mechanics.<br /> <br /> 'Bad' can mean a slue of things from politically inconvenient, emotionally unsettling to others, morally wrong, tactically incorrect, or many other options. It seems important that the choice must be something that would be difficult for someone else who didn't have the Darkling's seeming would resist for some reason they feel is &quot;right&quot;, &quot;good&quot;, or &quot;correct&quot; and the darkling doesn't need to hesitate because they've already accepted in their soul that they are not &quot;right&quot;, &quot;good&quot; or &quot;correct&quot; because their actions during their escape from their Durance.<br /> <br /> While other seeming can be scary withing their own context, Darklings can get away with <u>anything</u> (which respect towards Clarity) as long as it is for someone else. The worse they'll feel is a very very fleeting guilt or being &quot;broken&quot; for very brief time since gaining the clarity resolves those feelings, or even more scary they can be even more self-actualized if they didn't fail their break roll. People who don't feel bad for doing things that hurt others can be extremely frightening to those that recognize them for what they are.<br /> <br /> I will say characters that represent different sections of the moral spectrum will probably clump together because people of differing moral disposition tend to (but not always) dislike the company of those radically different than themselves either because are disgusted by those significantly worse than themselves, or feel judged by those significantly better..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":".  good points ShadowKnight. I've edited my post to reflect the corrections. 01-29-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:58:09-08:00","id":819491,"title":"","content":"You don't actually have to hurt anybody as a Darkling, though. An example of a hard decision nobody wants to make, which was posted in this thread a few pages back, is destroying a Token of Reprieve to prevent a Motley from tearing itself apart over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:27:26-08:00","id":819573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819398#post819398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just gonna put it out there, if they wanted to treat the word &quot;madness&quot; with more caution and respect, it may have been a good idea to rename the Madness Condition to something like Frantic or Unstable instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Madness is also one of the Conditions I didn't write. I did manage to turn &quot;Derangements&quot; into a function of Conditions, which changed some of those implications. <br /> <br /> FWIW. <br /> <br /> I don't believe we'll be using it in Changeling 2e, at least with that name. For that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:35:26-08:00","id":819578,"title":"","content":"Good to know! I mean, at this point, one is used to the way mental illness is handled in RPGs, but this is a breath of fresh air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:01:31-08:00","id":819821,"title":"","content":"I'm trying very hard to understand what is appealing about this, since from where I'm sitting (ie I just read the linked document, no other discussion about it) the Huntsmen seem to border on the game-ruining.<br /> <br /> This thread verges on the 500 posts, though, so I can't really go through it all. Is there some good post someone could link me to explaining why people, uh... like this at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:04:21-08:00","id":819823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819821#post819821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying very hard to understand what is appealing about this, since from where I'm sitting (ie I just read the linked document, no other discussion about it) the Huntsmen seem to border on the game-ruining.<br /> <br /> This thread verges on the 500 posts, though, so I can't really go through it all. Is there some good post someone could link me to explaining why people, uh... like this at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>why game ruining ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:09:11-08:00","id":819827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819823#post819823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> why game ruining ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I feel very comfortable going into an extended rant about why I hate something when I don't know the reasons why other people do like it. I'd prefer if I gained understanding before making a fool of myself by complaining loudly and too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:16:15-08:00","id":819830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819821#post819821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying very hard to understand what is appealing about this, since from where I'm sitting (ie I just read the linked document, no other discussion about it) the Huntsmen seem to border on the game-ruining.<br /> <br /> This thread verges on the 500 posts, though, so I can't really go through it all. Is there some good post someone could link me to explaining why people, uh... like this at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been way off topic for several pages now, so it's nice to see someone bringing this back around to the Huntsmen. Could you elaborate on how you see Huntsmen ruining a game? We might be better able to address more specific critiques.<br /> <br /> As for what I like about them, the biggest thing for me is that simply by existing they create dramatic tension. Even if I as an ST don't plan to use Huntsmen in a story, my players will always need to be prepared for the threat. Anyone or anything could be a huntsman in disguise, so the freehold has a tangible reason to constantly keep up the Bulwark. You're never truly safe as a Changeling, you have to maintain constant vigilance. And on top of that, if you find out a huntsman is after you, you can no longer fully trust other Lost, because any one of them could sell you out for a get out of jail free card.<br /> <br /> I don't think I would actually use Huntsman terribly often, because they're such a game-changer when they show up. But the same can be said of Strix and Idigam. The titular antagonists of the game lines' signature Chronicles are enormous plot catalysts, so you only use them when you want the story to be heavily focused on dealing with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:21:32-08:00","id":819833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819821#post819821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying very hard to understand what is appealing about this, since from where I'm sitting (ie I just read the linked document, no other discussion about it) the Huntsmen seem to border on the game-ruining.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not planning on using Huntsmen myself, so don't worry, you're not alone.<br /> <br /> I think people like them because of the paranoia factor they bring, and the interesting dilemmas they create with Tokens of Reprieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:22:15-08:00","id":819834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819830#post819830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've been way off topic for several pages now, so it's nice to see someone bringing this back around to the Huntsmen. Could you elaborate on how you see Huntsmen ruining a game? We might be better able to address more specific critiques.<br /> <br /> As for what I like about them, the biggest thing for me is that simply by existing they create dramatic tension. Even if I as an ST don't plan to use Huntsmen in a story, my players will always need to be prepared for the threat. Anyone or anything could be a huntsman in disguise, so the freehold has a tangible reason to constantly keep up the Bulwark. You're never truly safe as a Changeling, you have to maintain constant vigilance. And on top of that, if you find out a huntsman is after you, you can no longer fully trust other Lost, because any one of them could sell you out for a get out of jail free card.<br /> <br /> I don't think I would actually use Huntsman terribly often, because they're such a game-changer when they show up. But the same can be said of Strix and Idigam. The titular antagonists of the game lines' signature Chronicles are enormous plot catalysts, so you only use them when you want the story to be heavily focused on dealing with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right, that's interesting. Thanks.<br /> <br /> How to put my issues with them concisely... Okay, first I'd like to make sure I'm not missing something: from the write-up I've seen, Huntsmen seem to be impossible to slay indefinitely; they only fade and reform over a fortnight. The moment one is after you, it seems like you're in for a new attack every 15 days for as long as you can keep push them back, until they win. Is this correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:32:22-08:00","id":819837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819834#post819834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, that's interesting. Thanks.<br /> <br /> How to put my issues with them concisely... Okay, first I'd like to make sure I'm not missing something: from the write-up I've seen, Huntsmen seem to be impossible to slay indefinitely; they only fade and reform over a fortnight. The moment one is after you, it seems like you're in for a new attack every 15 days for as long as you can keep push them back, until they win. Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. Huntsmen can be killed, but the section that explains how was left out of this preview. It was brought up in the thread that a Huntsman's own weapon may be one ways to do it. It's also possible cold iron might work? Both are speculation, but we do know while it is difficult to kill them, it's not impossible. Also, while it takes them a fortnight to regenerate, it's unlikely that they'll keep throwing themselves at a wall every 15 days. They are cunning hunters, so they're likely to take their time, develop a new strategy, and possibly wait it out just to keep their prey on its toes.<br /> <br /> All that said, yes, when a Huntsman comes for you, you're only safe for brief windows of time until either it catches you, you give it a Token of Reprieve, or you kill it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:34:05-08:00","id":819839,"title":"","content":"You know now that I think about it, they kind of remind me of It Follows. Without the stupid part where you have to boink someone to pass it to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:59:10-08:00","id":819850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819837#post819837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not entirely. Huntsmen can be killed, but the section that explains how was left out of this preview. It was brought up in the thread that a Huntsman's own weapon may be one ways to do it. It's also possible cold iron might work? Both are speculation, but we do know while it is difficult to kill them, it's not impossible. Also, while it takes them a fortnight to regenerate, it's unlikely that they'll keep throwing themselves at a wall every 15 days. They are cunning hunters, so they're likely to take their time, develop a new strategy, and possibly wait it out just to keep their prey on its toes.<br /> <br /> All that said, yes, when a Huntsman comes for you, you're only safe for brief windows of time until either it catches you, you give it a Token of Reprieve, or you kill it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they can be killed, that's better. I imagine that will end up being the default issue in most game - a lot of players I've seen balk at doing blatantly evil stuff against other Changelings in CtL games (an amusing change from Vampire) and there's only so long you can stomach perpetual attack by cunning opponents who may be prone to casualties and torturing your loved ones to draw you out.<br /> <br /> I have... many issues with Huntsmen. They're game-warping in a way, say, the Strix aren't. A Strix is universally bad news, but it can be bad news in many different ways, and it can be bad news for different people, for your city as a whole, for you in particular, for some third party. You can be peripherally involved, you can mitigate the bad news, the bad news may happen and leave you much worse off but still alive (well, undead). The Huntsmen are bad at this: they come after you, and the only possible endings to your confrontation are 1) game over, 2) you kill it, 3) you betray your fellow Changelings. This is much more narrow and restrictive.<br /> <br /> One thing I am particularly annoyed at is that, at several points, the write-up says that a wise Changeling who managed to temporarily drive out a Huntsmen picks up and moves to a new town. This is irritating because it's a non-starter for most game. You don't leave town: you can't. CtL, like most nWoD games, thrives on the building of a single community, one city or town, and the exploration of its characters, intricacies and plots, its factions and conflicts, its secrets and opportunities. If you leave town, hours upon hours of work by the ST and emotional investment by the players are dropped down the drain; plots are left hanging to never be resolved. Beloved characters go off-screen forever. I know of more than one group in which this would effectively end the game as players lose interest.<br /> <br /> On a different topic, the Huntsmen also morally compromise the Changelings in a way that didn't exist before. A Changeling who chooses to live is a Changeling who accepts that, every so often, a human being will die to power up their nemesis. Maybe one in a lifetime. Maybe a dozen in a year. Now I don't want to appear like I am blind to what CtL has always been - there's always been danger and ambiguity to the existence of Changelings and the formation of their society, much interesting material to exploit in how their relationship to others and the world could be symbiotic, parasistic, abusive. But this is a far cry from &quot;by choosing to live outside of Arcadia, you choose to have unknown strangers die every so often.&quot; It adds a measure of tremendous selfishness to the existence of Changelings which makes them... closer to vampires thematically.<br /> <br /> The above wouldn't be a problem if it weren't connected to something which other people like and I don't: the inevitability of Huntsmen. They seem to be not merely a new antagonist, but *the* new antagonist, a strength which terrifies Changelings and brings them together to defend themselves. The Huntsmen will always come for you, sooner or later. This narrows down Changeling games; it gives their society a focus which I think is too strong, too tight. It closes off story options rather than opening them; it takes over narrative space, reducing Changeling to a story rather than a toolbox for stories. The setting of Changeling is now the setting of the Huntsmen's preys, and it defines them.<br /> <br /> Another way in which it brings Changelings closer to Vampire (which I don't think is a good thing, much as I love VtR to bits) is how it fosters distrust. One of the main antagonists of Changelings were always Loyalists and Privateers: but those were outsiders, even when infilitrated in the Courts. They were the Changelings who had made the wrong choices, the enemy with a friendly face, the ones who escaped and yet are still in chains. The Courts were, fundamentally, about how victims of the Fae draw together, share suffering and find a communality in them. Now, everyone you meet - friendly or not - is a potential traitor, someone who can use what they know about you to hurt you. It used to be that helping a Keeper catch a Changeling was the greatest crime, and those who did it pariah. Now it's something anyone can do.<br /> <br /> This fosters the wrong kind of paranoia: an inward paranoia. Rather than being frightened of the world outside your tight-knit group, rather than having to confront the complex interplay of the safe space of a Lost community and the dangerous opportunity of the 'real' world, you now have incentive to hide from everyone and everything. Courts exist as a way to defend yourself against Huntsmen, but they're also the main reason Huntsmen threaten you: you need the Court, but you also need to hide from the Court. From your friends. No one can know enough to hurt you.<br /> <br /> This is, again, thematically closer to Requiem. This sense of inward, rather than outward, paranoia, is something I have never associated with Changeling and do not want to associate. <br /> <br /> I also don't like the Huntsmen being &quot;spirits&quot; and being universal in the way they are - it jars strongly with my vision of Arcadia, gives it a consistency and predictability I do not like; but I imagine this comes with changes to what Arcadia is that depart from the old vision already. <br /> <br /> I also, frankly, find the Huntsmen boring, and find them to swallow space previously occupied by more interesting opponents. They're anti-Changelings, humen with a tell that can hide as things, and exist only to hunt you down. Despite all claims to the contrary, they cannot truly be unique. A brutal, wrathful monster that wants to tear down everything in its way to catch you, and a patient, sadistic monster that wants to exploit your attaches to slowly draw you out in the open and snatch you, are still pure-octane hunter-abducters who cannot be bargained with (except in this one specific way they all share) and want to abduct you. They have none of the variance and potential of goblins, Loyalists, Privateers, True Fae acting in person, all of whom can have many varied objectives and desires and can be interacted with in many ways - including socially or mentally. <br /> <br /> Now sure, I can always still use these antagonists, the Huntsmen don't take them away from my toolbox. But they do take primacy in the narrative, and this alone has considerable impact on the general framing of the setting and its characters.<br /> <br /> ...I think that's it. That gets most of my issues down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:03:50-08:00","id":819853,"title":"","content":"The essence of Changeling, to me, is about carving out a space for yourself in the world where you are safe. Not safe from physical harm, only, but also from stereotype and control and deceit. Can that actually be done? Open question. But the structure of Changeling society, from Pledge to Motley to Court to Freehold, is to me about wrapping yourself with protective layers of understanding. The Pledge is an understanding in the mafia sense, where you're protected by reprisal. The Motley is an understanding in the friendship sense, where you're protected by companionship. The Court is an understanding through perspective, where you're protected from tiresome argument. The Freehold is an understanding through identity, where you're protected by common feeling. They're all the same, but all different.<br /> <br /> The True Fae are, of course, the essence of what these things are protecting you from. The Strangers have to be <i>strangers</i>. People who don't understand. People who can't understand. While a mortal can be uplifted into allyship, the Fae will always, at best, be uncomprehending. This makes the protective layers effectively impenetrable: in order for the Fae to really attack you, they have to have some kind of understanding and that subverts and undermines the essence of the Stranger. What gives them their opening is that people who <i>do</i> understand, but are still willing to enable attacks upon you. That's the Loyalist.<br /> <br /> Here, though, we have a slight problem. Not insurmountable, at all, but a problem. There's a vast gulf between Stranger and Traitor: between complete lack of understanding and complete understanding. That's the hole filled by the Huntsman. The Huntsman's job, in my view, is to have <i>gradual</i> understanding. They start uncomprehending, but with time and patience, they learn. They understand the onion skins and are able to infiltrate them by subverting those layers. They're theoretically redeemable, sure, but it takes a <i>lot</i> of time and a lot of collateral damage will happen on the way. Whereas the Loyalist can be turned back, with comparatively little damage, the Huntsman can't. Not without massive damage. Choosing not to kill a Huntsman who is at your mercy is a lot like Batman choosing not to kill Joker: do you choose to break your own mind, or do you let them hurt so many more people?<br /> <br /> Which is where we get into story. (Speaking of OOC story, not Arcadian stuff.) The story-purpose of the Huntsman is the essence of the antagonist. By exactingly confronting the very things that make a Changeling who he is, the Huntsman highlights why those things are the way they are, how they work, what bends them, what breaks them. Can the Strangers and Loyalists do this? Sure. Absolutely. But the Strangers are extremely external, whereas the Loyalists are extremely internal, and this makes it hard to really give weight to both of those forces. The Huntsman straddles the boundary and spells out both sides by negotiating it. They're <i>built</i> to negotiate that boundary, and it makes them ideal for exploring both. By hitting the center, it frees up narrative room for the Strangers to have their strangeness emphasized, and Loyalists to have their loyalty emphasized.<br /> <br /> Let's change the story. Let's posit the Changelings as ghetto-dwellers. The Stranger is the Man, the impersonal, bureaucratic machine that lays down a highway through your world without ever understanding the damage that was done. The Loyalist is the drug-dealer, the pimp, who's willing to knowingly get you hurt for their own gain. But the Huntsman is the cop, who has profiles and statistics about crime and training and authority to break down your door and kick you while you're down. Who thinks he understands you, because he's been briefed a hundred times and has met a thousand criminals, but who approaches you with hostile prejudice from the beginning because you're not really a person to him: you're a target, a threat, an objective.<br /> <br /> Anyways. I'm not 100% sold on their details myself; I'm still waiting to see how everything else shakes out. But they work for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:04:45-08:00","id":819854,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Omicron completely.<br /> <br /> When I put myself in a changeling's shoes. think about the Huntsmen and their implications, and suicide starts to seem like a logical and practical option, I know something went wrong somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:17:50-08:00","id":819860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819853#post819853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>This all makes a lot of sense; I think I could warm up a lot to the concept if their inevitability and omnipresence as The Enemy of Changelings whose existence define them were toned down, and the part where they kill someone every time they manifest quietly dropped. As it stands though, these facts distort this whole picture into something that overshadows their good side (in my personal opinion) and makes them incompatible with the game I love as I knew it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:24:45-08:00","id":819867,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen anyone say they like &quot;the inevitability of Huntsmen&quot;. And I've actually read this whole thread. Occasionally with regrets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:47:23-08:00","id":819878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819867#post819867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen anyone say they like &quot;the inevitability of Huntsmen&quot;. And I've actually read this whole thread. Occasionally with regrets.</div> </div> </div> </div> i like the fact they're inevitable,they bring the feeling that you'll never be 100% safe,that there always ythe change the people you hate can get you back,i like that,i like the sense of they always can come back,you'll never be safe, thats why it's called a &quot;Game of Beautiful Lies And BitterSweet Truths&quot; the beautiful lie would be you convincing yourself that now you're safe and dont have to worry about them anymore,and the bittersweet truth is accepting that eventually something is going to coming for you and prepare yourselft for this,the huntsman are scary,they bring the horror to the game. to me,they're a good addition to the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:14:09-08:00","id":819884,"title":"","content":"Welp, the first part of today just went to this thread.<br /> <br /> Gonna dress, eat, start laundry, and then we'll see if we can provide a perspective here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:25:33-08:00","id":819890,"title":"","content":"I strenuously disagree with the idea that the Huntsmen killing innocents makes Changelings somehow &quot;selfish&quot; or that they are morally required to commit suicide or go back to Arcadia. Changelings are literally just trying to live their lives, and then these supernatural serial killer assholes come after them, and kill at least one bystander in the process. Blaming the Changeling for that is like blaming Jodie Foster for the attempted assassination of Ronald Reagan, or blaming FDR for the death of the mayor of Chicago, who was killed during an assassination attempt on Roosevelt. I mean, I don't think very many people watch <i>Terminator</i> and think that Sarah Conner is a bad person because the number of people the terminator kills trying to get to her.<br /> <br /> At the same time, however, I could see the murder of innocents being a source of drama, since the Changeling may very well <i>feel</i> responsible for the acts of a Huntsman pursuing them. Heck, even if the Huntsmen didn't <i>have</i> to kill anyone, committing a series of murders and leaving some kind of calling card for their target could be a pretty effective way of drawing out a changeling they're pursuing. This brings an element of guilt and self-recrimination to the lives of many Changelings, which I think is very much in keeping with the theme of abuse and trauma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-30-2016, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:32:11-08:00","id":819895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819890#post819890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I strenuously disagree with the idea that the Huntsmen killing innocents makes Changelings somehow &quot;selfish&quot; or that it morally requires them to commit suicide or go back to Arcadia. Changelings are literally just trying to live their lives, and then these supernatural serial killer assholes come after them, and kill at least one bystander in the process. Blaming the Changeling for that is like blaming Jodie Foster for the attempted assassination of Ronald Reagan, or blaming FDR for the death of the mayor of Chicago, who was killed during an assassination attempt on Roosevelt. I mean, I don't think very many people watch <i>Terminator</i> and think that Sarah Conner is a bad person because the number of people the terminator kills trying to get to her.<br /> <br /> At the same time, however, I could see the murder of innocents being a source of drama, since the Changeling may very well <i>feel</i> responsible for the acts of a Huntsman pursuing them. Heck, even if the Huntsmen didn't <i>have</i> to kill anyone, committing a series of murders and leaving some kind of calling card for their target could be a pretty effective way of drawing out a changeling they're pursuing. This brings an element of guilt and self-recrimination to the lives of many Changelings, which I think is very much in keeping with the theme of abuse and trauma.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you choose to live, many people will die as a result&quot; has a kind of inherency and predictability that real life rarely presents. This isn't the assassination of one president being blamed on the person who unknowingly caused the circumstances in which one person would kill them. This is &quot;Huntsmen always come for Changelings, always, and they always kill people, always, so by choosing to live you choose to have people die for you.&quot; It doesn't make you morally responsible for it, but those people<i> are still dead </i>and they still wouldn't be dead if you hadn't chosen to live free. It's that kind of amusing collapsing point of morality and emotion where you're not actually responsible for it, but if you're capable of telling yourself &quot;well it's not my fault&quot; as you see the corpses mount over the course of you're life you're probably a<i> huge asshole.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-30-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:34:58-08:00","id":819897,"title":"","content":"I never said suicide was a moral requirement. I said that once you take into account that you've been replaced, so nobody's going to miss you; there's someone that will keep coming back unless you find a way to put him down for good, killing innocents in the process, endangering your loved ones and tempting your allies to betray you, and that if they succeed, you'll be sent back to relive the worst period of your life... well, suicide begins to make sense, practically speaking. It solves pretty much everyone's problems. It's not &quot;selfish&quot; to try and stay alive and find happiness, but it would surely be quite convenient for everyone, yourself included, if you didn't exist anymore.<br /> <br /> And that's a bit too bleak for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:51:36-08:00","id":819903,"title":"","content":"I've played an in-dev game called RimWorld, where you control some people who crash land on a distant planet and have to build a colony to survive. In a few long-running games, I'd end up facing hordes of 200+ raiders with 20 colonists, and successfully killing the bulk with mines, turrets, and entrenched positions. I had to engineer a makeshift crematorium just to get rid of all the bodies. There's always a point where I start feeling a twinge of guilt, even though it's all self-defense and that there's no option to reason with them.<br /> <br /> I think the obligatory trail of death from Huntsmen is something Storytellers should put some thought into, and probably ask their players about. As people have said, the idea that a Huntsman could be out there is a powerful tool in itself, so it's probably better to use them infrequently. But once one arrives, I think there's a lot of useful drama to be had about the problem, and how a Changeling might work to prevent further murders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:02:04-08:00","id":819931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819897#post819897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said suicide was a moral requirement. I said that once you take into account that you've been replaced, so nobody's going to miss you; there's someone that will keep coming back unless you find a way to put him down for good, killing innocents in the process, endangering your loved ones and tempting your allies to betray you, and that if they succeed, you'll be sent back to relive the worst period of your life... well, suicide begins to make sense, practically speaking. It solves pretty much everyone's problems. It's not &amp;quot;selfish&amp;quot; to try and stay alive and find happiness, but it would surely be quite convenient for everyone, yourself included, if you didn't exist anymore.<br /> <br /> And that's a bit too bleak for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a realistic (if tragic) outlook for characters who are metaphors for survivors of severe trauma. To me, this is a plus side to the Huntsman, but I can definitely see how it would be too dark for some folks' taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:29:39-08:00","id":819947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819931#post819931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a realistic (if tragic) outlook for characters who are metaphors for survivors of severe trauma. To me, this is a plus side to the Huntsman, but I can definitely see how it would be too dark for some folks' taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that, from an unemotional perspective, it also removes the reason to play the game, and for changeling societies to even exist. If the most logical and practical thing a changeling can do is commit suicide, and their emotional state supports that conclusion (which is believable after the trauma experienced in Arcadia, coming back to see that they've been replaced and they have no place in the world, all of which are likely to lead to depression), then one wonders what's the point in playing the game at all, or how changeling society exists at all when it's extremely hard to present a changeling reasons for them to not kill themselves. Because no, it actually doesn't get better.<br /> <br /> See, contrast with Promethean, where the characters are allegedly in an even worse situation than changelings. The core difference between the moods of that game is that <i>the very point of Promethean is reaching the New Dawn</i>. It's hammered over and over across the book, all the mechanics revolve around it, everything circles around the idea that you can get rid of all the bad things in your life, and not only that, but it's <i>expected </i>of you to do it, to the point where the majority of Prometheans and ex-Prometheans are either on the Pilgrimage or have already reached their New Dawn, with only a minority becoming Centimanni or dying permanently before they can reach their New Dawn.<br /> <br /> One of Promethean's core themes is hope, and the really awful circumstances a Promethean has to deal with enhance that hope because at no time do you feel like suicide is legitimately a more practical option.<br /> <br /> Even in Vampire, you can argue that the justifications a vampire tells herself are quite believable and hard to contradict. Maybe she <i>can </i>only feed on animals, or feed without killing. Maybe she <i>can</i> get used to a night schedule. Maybe she <i>can </i>keep her head down and stay out of politics. Maybe it <i>isn't</i> so bad to be a vampire. And while those justifications can be proven false, they don't necessarily have to, and are completely up to the Storyteller and player.<br /> <br /> With the Huntsmen, it's assumed that they <i>will</i> come for you, that they <i>will</i> kill innocent people, and that they <i>will</i> cost you a lot to get rid of them, perhaps causing irreversible damage to you and your relationships in the process. And hell, because every changeling gets one, killing your own Huntsman doesn't mean you're free from them. You can still be targeted by one to get at someone else, or just become collateral damage. And even if you finally become powerful enough to deal with them, there's the True Fae, which we've been told are <i>even scarier than before</i>. Like, it just doesn't end. There is no New Dawn. There is no rest, no reprieve. It's almost like the game says &quot;You can't actually survive trauma, you can't move on. It will always haunt you. You can just try to run for as long as you can before it finally wears you down and catches up to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's just not the Changeling game I want to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:37:47-08:00","id":819956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819947#post819947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Huntsmen, it's assumed that they <i>will</i> come for you</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting this from, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:45:33-08:00","id":819958,"title":"","content":"Not from the book, I assure you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:50:42-08:00","id":819960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819956#post819956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting this from, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It is this last which is most terrifying. <b>Every changeling</b>, on some level, <b>knows that she might be kidnapped and sent back</b>, perhaps even that it\u2019s likely.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When it is the changeling\u2019s turn to be sought out\u2014and <b>every changeling\u2019s turn comes someday</b>\u2014&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A changeling who has exchanged a token for her freedom would do well to pull up stakes and move quickly, <b>for the Huntsmen always return</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;During this break from the Hunt, the wise changeling heads for a new town in the hopes of remaining free for another day, a week, a year. <b>The break is never long enough</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen will always come for you, and it seems that changelings know this instinctively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:52:45-08:00","id":819962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819960#post819960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;It is this last which is most terrifying. <b>Every changeling</b>, on some level, <b>knows that she might be kidnapped and sent back</b>, perhaps even that it\u2019s likely.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When it is the changeling\u2019s turn to be sought out\u2014and <b>every changeling\u2019s turn comes someday</b>\u2014&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A changeling who has exchanged a token for her freedom would do well to pull up stakes and move quickly, <b>for the Huntsmen always return</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;During this break from the Hunt, the wise changeling heads for a new town in the hopes of remaining free for another day, a week, a year. <b>The break is never long enough</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen will always come for you, and it seems that changelings know this instinctively.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those quotes indicate that a Huntsman is created for every single Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:54:51-08:00","id":819966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819962#post819962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of those quotes indicate that a Huntsman is created for every single Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Every changeling's turn comes someday&quot; seems to indicate that yes, indeed, sooner or later you will get a Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:56:58-08:00","id":819968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819947#post819947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Huntsmen, it's assumed that they <i>will</i> come for you, that they <i>will</i> kill innocent people, and that they <i>will</i> cost you a lot to get rid of them, perhaps causing irreversible damage to you and your relationships in the process. And hell, because every changeling gets one, killing your own Huntsman doesn't mean you're free from them. You can still be targeted by one to get at someone else, or just become collateral damage. And even if you finally become powerful enough to deal with them, there's the True Fae, which we've been told are <i>even scarier than before</i>. Like, it just doesn't end. There is no New Dawn. There is no rest, no reprieve. It's almost like the game says &quot;You can't actually survive trauma, you can't move on. It will always haunt you. You can just try to run for as long as you can before it finally wears you down and catches up to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's just not the Changeling game I want to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's one more reason I advocate Storytellers consider the option of <i>not</i> using them, rather than let players assume it's inevitable. Uncertainty about whether or not a Huntsman will come for you allows ambiguity of whether they're seeing a Huntsman's tell or just seeing coincidences. Additionally, the Gentry aren't necessarily going to be interested in getting you back. They might just shrug and move onto other forms of entertainment because they were getting bored with you anyway. But you don't know if you're lucky like that, and even if you are, you'll never know when your Keeper might suddenly develop nostalgia for your Durance and want you back.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, there needs to be hope to contrast the horror. I'm not sure what I'm going to do for the Gentry and Huntsmen in my chronicles, but I want it so they can be defeated, though it won't be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:58:41-08:00","id":819969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819960#post819960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;It is this last which is most terrifying. <b>Every changeling</b>, on some level, <b>knows that she might be kidnapped and sent back</b>, perhaps even that it\u2019s likely.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When it is the changeling\u2019s turn to be sought out\u2014and <b>every changeling\u2019s turn comes someday</b>\u2014&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A changeling who has exchanged a token for her freedom would do well to pull up stakes and move quickly, <b>for the Huntsmen always return</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;During this break from the Hunt, the wise changeling heads for a new town in the hopes of remaining free for another day, a week, a year. <b>The break is never long enough</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen will always come for you, and it seems that changelings know this instinctively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add to that: &quot;Every changeling knows this on some level and it eats away at the quiet corners of changeling social life. <b>The Huntsmen come for everyone sooner or later.</b>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-30-2016, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T14:05:02-08:00","id":819974,"title":"","content":"The document explicitly says &quot;The Huntsmen come for everyone, sooner or later.&quot;<br /> <br /> Side question, when it says Huntsmen are undetectable in their natural forms by magic or glamour, does that mean undetectable *as Huntsmen* or in general? I ask because it's a relevant distinction for things like Wards that attack intruders to the Hollow. Obviously if there were an easy magic solution for detecting Huntsmen it wouldn't be long before the Courts figured out a way to cast it nigh constantly, but if they're immune to magic based detection period that raises interesting new wrinkles, including detection by omission. If I used something like Contracts of SpellBound Autumn to scan a crowd and one dude comes up completely blank to Wyrd Vision, that's a dead give away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T17:48:55-08:00","id":820053,"title":"","content":"The fact that a Huntsman could come for you at any time doesn't make life any more pointless or hopeless than the fact that there are a thousand things that could kill you on any given day,or the fact that, someday, every one of us will die. Nobody knows how much time they have left on this earth, and the Huntsmen don't really change that very much.<br /> <br /> Plus, the fear of threats from Arcadia has <i>always</i> been a defining feature of Changeling society in <i>Lost</i>. One doesn't have to look any further than the Seasonal Courts: each court is literally defined by how it reacts to that threat: by preparing to fight (Summer), by turning the tools of the Fae against them (Autumn), by going into hiding (Winter), or by living it up and not worrying about tomorrow (Spring). The whole point of even having a rotating leadership is to try and keep the True Fae off balance, because <i>nobody</i> in a freehold really believes that the Others will simply forget about them or leave them alone.<br /> <br /> If anything, I see the Huntsmen and the system of Approaches as giving Changelings <i>more</i> hope. The True Fae are alien and powerful beyond mortal comprehension (and have pretty much always been depicted as such), but now we have both a good reason for them not to come after Changeling's in person and a type of Arcadian foe that can realistically defeated, if only for a while. They never really go away, sure, but that doesn't mean the courts cant keep sending them packing back to Arcadia in agony. As scary as the Huntsmen may be, Changelings have the home field advantage, not to mention the advantage of numbers and a whole court full of magical folk with more tricks up their collective sleeves than any one Huntsman could match.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I feel like, from a practical standpoint, Loyalists and Privateers are really no less inevitable and relentless than than the Huntsmen. They may not be magical robots with a single all-consuming purpose, but no matter how effective the Changelings in your Freehold are at defeating their schemes, you're never actually going to get rid of them for good. Some Changelings will always go bad, and the Fae will always be able to break humans to do their bidding. Sooner or later, these threats will reappear, and just as with the huntsmen, all a Freehold can do is stick together and take care of the threat as it arises.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it all adds up to a pretty decent metaphor for dealing with trauma. No, it never goes away, and it will always be a part of who you are. There will always be bad days when you feel those old aches and life might not even seem worth living. But you have good days too, and great days, and mediocre days, because you are so much more than the trauma you have suffered. And even when things are looking bleak, you don't have to face your demons alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-30-2016, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T17:53:36-08:00","id":820057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819969#post819969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add to that: &quot;Every changeling knows this on some level and it eats away at the quiet corners of changeling social life. <b>The Huntsmen come for everyone sooner or later.</b>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I can see that reading. I have a hard time with reading it the same way you guys are, though, because that doesn't sound like the intended meaning of that paragraph.<br /> <br /> To me, I read that and I see that Changelings <i>believe</i> that a Huntsman will come for everyone sooner or later, because that's the motivation for accepting a Token, and that whether or not that's true is irrelevant because the point is that Changelings believe it and this guides their actions. But maybe I'm reading too much into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T17:55:09-08:00","id":820058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820053#post820053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that a Huntsman could come for you at any time doesn't make life any more pointless or hopeless than the fact that there are a thousand things that could kill you on any given day,or the fact that, someday, every one of us will die. Nobody knows how much time they have left on this earth, and the Huntsmen don't really change that very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough, I thought about pointing out that the quoted sentence sounds very reminiscent, at least to me, of &quot;Do not send for whom the bell tolls; it tolls for thee.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T19:52:13-08:00","id":820102,"title":"","content":"The comparisons to the old Gentry and the inevitability of death, in my opinion, fails to hold up when you actually analyse the details. In 1e, the True Fae were used very sparingly as direct antagonists. Their threat was always present, but distant. A changeling's main threats were loyalists and privateers, and fetches for those that wanted their old lives back.<br /> <br /> With the addition of the Huntsmen, their inevitability, cunning and relentlessness, there is no reprieve. It goes beyond accepting trauma as part of you and personifies it into an almost undefeatable foe. The way the Huntsmen work needs that they are extremely hard to defeat, inevitable and very competent at what they do, or else there would be no point accepting a Token from them. The narrative value of the Token is directly linked to how effective they are as antagonists.<br /> <br /> What are the numbers? How effective are the Huntsmen? If they are highly effective at their job, it's further proof on the &quot;better consider suicide&quot; side. If they're not, what's the value of a Token? Why are the Gentry sending out something that doesn't want to do its job and isn't even that good at it? And if the Huntsmen are only moderately good at their job, how do the numbers change when you add the loyalists and privateers? How many changelings die or are taken back to Arcadia every year? What's the average life expectancy of a changeling?<br /> <br /> It's very easy for all these factors to present an overwhelmingly bleak existence for changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T19:57:10-08:00","id":820105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820102#post820102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comparisons to the old Gentry and the inevitability of death, in my opinion, fails to hold up when you actually analyse the details. In 1e, the True Fae were used very sparingly as direct antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The literal first supplement in the line devoted an entire chapter to their use as direct antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T20:05:47-08:00","id":820108,"title":"","content":"And supplements are, by definition, optional. I approve of the idea on principle; more options are always good, but it doesn't actually alter what I said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T20:12:45-08:00","id":820110,"title":"","content":"When they were first discussed, I had some concerns whether the role of Huntsmen would push the paranoia and inevitability in Changeling to a paradigm altogether approaching Demon, which I find inherently more fatalist in its outlook. But right now, from the draft, the unspoiled details that have been hinted at and the comments from the people working on it, I feel much more assured. I don't think the intended spirit of Changeling 2e is so grim as some people are getting from all this, even if I can understand why they'd say so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-30-2016, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T20:36:43-08:00","id":820117,"title":"","content":"Okay, so ostensibly, this is a response primarily to Omicron, which is something I never really thought I'd have to do in my life, but here we are. And ostensibly, this is also about the Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> But, really, no, if I'm honest, I think it's time we had a &quot;back to basics&quot; sort of chat, because I've been seeing a lot of funny ideas about Changeling that's been bothering me some-stuff like Changelings being the most moral of the splats and a strange twist of perspective on what, exactly, people think Changeling seems to be doing. It's really, really weird, and I think it's worth tackling the subject. But before all of that, I have an apology to make. It works out, because it let's me set a stage for this discussion.<br /> <br /> <b>My Right for My Crown, My Left for My Dagger-Societal Oaths and Why No One's Going to Ban Tokens of Reprieve.</b><br /> <br /> Soooo a lot earlier in the thread, it was asked why the rulers of a Freehold don't just demand everyone make a Pledge to not take Tokens of Reprieve and let the Wyrd sort it all out. I countered at the time that doing such would require a lot of individual Oaths to be laid down on the rulers, and that would inevitably break them. And, were I not forgetting some of the other functions of Oaths, I'd have been right on that. But I wasn't. So, let's quickly chat about that.<br /> <br /> As the Demon Storyteller's Guide points out, there are three kinds of Pledges in Second Edition, being Sealings, Oaths, and Bargain. Oaths break down into three other categories-they work more or less the same regardless, but the distinctions are important. My focus when I made my declaration was on Personal Oaths, namely because the majority of mechanical diversity lies in that area, but Personal Oaths aren't what you'd use to swear to the Freehold, the Court, and the rulers. No, that belongs to Societal Oaths, which binds you to the concept and the definitions laid out in the groundwork of these constructs. You can have as many people swear their allegiance to Hold and Court that you want, and so long as the Bulwark stands, you're golden.<br /> <br /> So, yes, actually, you could just include a clause in the Societal Oath that basically says &quot;I will uphold and keep the laws of the Freehold and Courts&quot; and then make sure one of the laws is to not take a Token of Reprieve, and BAM, anyone who takes it is an oathbreaker, and you can expect your happy ass to become grass if you don't make headway out of town. Hooray, problem solved, right?<br /> <br /> Well. No. Pay attention, and feel free to challenge this as you read on, because this tenet is important for what we're going to chat about. It's can be seen as a sort of crux for Changeling.<br /> <br /> Here's a simple fact-Tokens of Reprieve are powerful currency in a game like Changeling the Lost. No one wants to be the ones who earns it, of course, and no one wants to be the one caught with it-but it is something everyone wants to have in their bug-out kit. When you need to bargain for a mighty favor and you think you can do a deal under the table, a Token of Reprieve is how you you pay the champion of the Freehold to break into a Valkyrie base for your mate. When anyone asks where you got it, you of course say you nicked it at a Goblin Market, or picked it up off the corpse of a bloody Loyalist, or you made a deal with someone else for it. Of course you do. It doesn't matter if it's true or not. Changelings are mortified to find out you have one, but if they can get their hands on it, they'll at least be willing to hear the deal. And hey, so long as <i>you</i> don't have to betray anyone, you'll gladly ignore the clause of not mentioning the seller at all. Or you turn the person in, but hey, that Token should go to someone, and you gave up a traitor. You earned it legitimately. Of course, you have to persuade the ruler that it should remain with you than 'get locked up in the treasury'. You know, for the good of the Freehold. The simple fact is is that having Tokens of Reprieve in a community is going to be good for you, whether you be a Sovereign of Paris or a poor exile newly returned home-it's just a matter of getting your hands on it. You can't do that if the freehold keeps them from even being grabbed.<br /> <br /> No one wants to earn it, but everyone wants one. And that's just the way the Lost are, because, deep down, there's a conflict of interests for changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>Torn Apart-The Tug of War Of Changeling Between Hearth and Nightmare</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have... many issues with Huntsmen. They're game-warping in a way, say, the Strix aren't. A Strix is universally bad news, but it can be bad news in many different ways, and it can be bad news for different people, for your city as a whole, for you in particular, for some third party. You can be peripherally involved, you can mitigate the bad news, the bad news may happen and leave you much worse off but still alive (well, undead). The Huntsmen are bad at this: they come after you, and the only possible endings to your confrontation are 1) game over, 2) you kill it, 3) you betray your fellow Changelings. This is much more narrow and restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to address this point directly at this point. I probably will later, but at this point, I wanted to sort of frame it and look at it on the wall as a contemplation piece, something I stare at while I mutter to myself, and really to the room. Because, I feel like while I understand and can even appreciate this sales point, it highlights the problem of the image of direction with Changeling.<br /> <br /> From day one, Changeling the Lost has been about The Long Way Home. That's what was sold in the theme section of the introduction. This game is about finding your way back 'home', back into a sense of security and comfort. It's about losing the flinch, the quickness of breath, the dilated pupils, when you see the carousel, the china doll, the scarecrow. It's about knowing everything is in its' place because you put it there, it's about knowing which laws of the Wyrd you obey and why you do them, it's about knowing when the goblins in the shadows are allowed to take a step over the threshold because it's okay for them to do so. It's about becoming safe and becoming comfortable. Lost's grand ol' image for a characters final act is one where they can walk around cool and confident, not worrying, because they know the world and they know themselves and can keep themselves and their own safe without becoming recluse or a siege engine or any number of other extremes. And you can do it!<br /> <br /> ...it's all so....pretty, isn't it? So nice, so clean, so hopeful. It is. It can be done. It's a big reason this game is as popular as it is. <i>You don't have to be scared, of others or yourself. You can feel safe, once upon a time and forever after</i>. So pretty, so precious.<br /> <br /> It's kind of naive. Maybe we lost sight of where Changeling goes because we like that dream too much. Maybe when I say &quot;Bleakest game, my ass&quot;, I'm ignoring something.<br /> <br /> Second Edition isn't letting people forget. It's taking a lot of moves to drag our eyes away from the dream and back to reality, looking us square in the eye and saying, clearly, &quot;It's about the <i>long</i> way home, not just the way home.&quot; Because, at the end of the day, The Long Way Home is just a way of re-expressing an idea in a high-minded way for people higher up the hierarchy. But down at the base of a changeling's needs, The Long Way Home reads a different way, and it's between those two readings you find Lost as a whole.<br /> <br /> See, strip it of glamour and hope, The Long Way Home reads &quot;Don't Go Back to Arcadia&quot;. And really, in the mud and shade of the forest, that's all that matters. Even if a Lost has no house, no friends, no family, nothing but their name and their flight-there, dressed in the blood of maggots with the dreaming toads and the sleeping snakes coiled around the singing mycelium, there, Lost is found in the simple promise that shatters worlds and breaks fates, there in the words &quot;<i>I am never going back</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling 101, right? But it's strange where people think this takes Lost as a game. See, you can have adventures centered around The Long Way Home. Grand comedies and tragedies full of romance and horror and sorrow and humor and exquisitely strange and beautiful things you could never hope to see in life put next to quiet and simple and serene things that you yourself have in abundance. Lost always has and always will have a place for that.<br /> <br /> But deep down, in the cracks of beauty and hope, down where the seeds can no longer take root and the water freezes and yet the sludge gathers and mingles and stews, there, in the advertisement promising a psychological horror, on the shelf in deepest green and under your pillow in colorless truth, <i>I am never going back</i> sinks its' teeth in and binds the story and the players and gives it the power that makes people not only dream of better, but <i>fight</i> for better. By way of necessity, though, it must also suggest the darker, more terrible answers. It is here where changelings fall, where changelings find themselves in the darkling fright of grim choices. And truth be told, it is always stronger. The Long Way Home is never as strong as <i>I am never going back</i> by itself. <br /> <br /> In a way, Changeling as a game is always going to come back to a singular direction, because of the intrinsic strength of <i>I am never going back</i>. It will always turn it's eyes down Arcadian roads. It has an inexorable gravity to it. The lower need of <i>I will never go back</i> crumbles and devours the higher need of The Long Way Home, and the only way to truly overcome that, to give The Long Way Home it's true due, is to dive through <i>I will never go back</i> and come out the other side.<br /> <br /> So, why is this important? Why do I feel the need to emphasize this weird dichotomy of two phrases that sort of mean the same thing? Well, that's easy.<br /> <br /> Because you aren't the only one dealing with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Images They Sell-Trust and Distrust in Changeling the Lost</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way in which it brings Changelings closer to Vampire (which I don't think is a good thing, much as I love VtR to bits) is how it fosters distrust. One of the main antagonists of Changelings were always Loyalists and Privateers: but those were outsiders, even when infilitrated in the Courts. They were the Changelings who had made the wrong choices, the enemy with a friendly face, the ones who escaped and yet are still in chains. The Courts were, fundamentally, about how victims of the Fae draw together, share suffering and find a communality in them. Now, everyone you meet - friendly or not - is a potential traitor, someone who can use what they know about you to hurt you. It used to be that helping a Keeper catch a Changeling was the greatest crime, and those who did it pariah. Now it's something anyone can do.<br /> <br /> This fosters the wrong kind of paranoia: an inward paranoia. Rather than being frightened of the world outside your tight-knit group, rather than having to confront the complex interplay of the safe space of a Lost community and the dangerous opportunity of the 'real' world, you now have incentive to hide from everyone and everything. Courts exist as a way to defend yourself against Huntsmen, but they're also the main reason Huntsmen threaten you: you need the Court, but you also need to hide from the Court. From your friends. No one can know enough to hurt you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, minor deviation here-I fucking love Omicron. Easily one of my favorite people here on the forums, has been for a long time, and is a incredibly sharp dude. One of my frequent regrets is that he isn't more active here in the nWoD Threads. <i>ALL THAT SAID</i>, This paragraph here is the reason I'm responding, because I read his stuff, and I was feeling a little crestfallen until I read this, at which point I freely admit I laughed and asked my screen &quot;Dude, have you been playing the same game as me?&quot; None of that negates what I said about him, and it's going to stop being about him explicitly after this-but seriously, wut?<br /> <br /> So, back on track, it's an intrinsic part of the game, this divide between the high-minded Long Way Home and the base need of <i>I am never going back</i>, and it fights on every level of Changeling the Lost. More importantly, it fights in every <i>changeling</i>. No one wants to be that guy, no one wants to be that asshole, but every changeling has in them that <i>I am never going back</i> and the questions of how far that goes. Hell, <i>this is why loyalists are even a thing</i>.<br /> <br /> Actually, let's take a deviation and talk, bluntly, about how loyalists and private-No, let's start at an even more base level. Let's talk fairies.<br /> <br /> Fairies, quite simply, are outsiders. Their ways are not your ways. As expressions of nature, of foreigners, of the mentally and socially disabled, of dreams and of strange inner workings, of all this and more, fairies as a wide, cultural base of icons that live beyond the edge of the village are the 'dwellers of the outside'. Offer them a kindness and they curse you, never thank them and you get blessed. They act in ways that don't make sense, according to their own internal logic that you might be able to discern with empathy and observation and care, but would never be able to make sense off just by way of your own framework. You have to slant your point of view, see under the table and behind the curtain, to really get them. On the whole, fae are liars and deceivers, less by choice and more by fate or chance. You can't always trust how the fae will react, because they are subject to laws and worlds within that aren't your own. The images they sell are illusion and dream, always a measure of dishonesty, and you have to play the game well to avoid becoming addicted to goblin fruit or asleep in a fairy circles.<br /> <br /> In Changeling the Lost, <i>the majority of people you interact with are fairies</i>. Welcome to the norm. Hell, in First Edition, every changeling has the Contracts of Smoke and Mirror as an aptitude-you were expected to never be what you appeared. Many things are up for grab and trade, though the most important resource was always too expensive for you to ever just barter for.<br /> <br /> Put even more simply, at it's core, basest level, <i>there was never a reason to trust anyone around you</i>. This is why the cornerstone of any changeling society was Pledges, which forced people to behave in accordance to laws.<br /> <br /> From this emerges the Loyalist and Privateer narrative, the teeth of <i>I am never going back</i> sinking into the fairy tale schema and emerging on the other side as antagonists. Now, while it can be fun to just have roving bandits and such all around the place, really the <i>first</i> reason why changelings built complex pledge systems for societies stems from the fact that there are Loyalists and Privateers among them. It doesn't stop them, either. Loyalists and Privateers have always been assumed to infiltrate freeholds and find clever ways to work around and subvert the Wyrd frameworks in order to casually make people disappear. See, the Lost are all inside, and the Loyalists and the Privateers have the advantage of being both inside and outside. This was the default from day one.<br /> <br /> As a natural extension, then, the game by and large becomes a big game of Coup or Werewolf(the card game, not Forsaken or Apocalypse)-everyone is keeping track of who is doing what and in accordance to what's been said, and finding incongruities in the executions, trying to find out who's going to stab them in the back before anyone else does. At it's basest level, that's what goes on in a freehold. It's forcing levels of trust and seeing what emerges from the remaining distrust of world and others. It's stabbing people with something immutable and seeing if that person is a traitor or not. This game has always been about paranoia and distrust, and what trust and camaraderie can grow from it.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that the goal posts have always been shifting, because Pledges don't just save you from the obvious traitors-they keep you safe from <i>everyone else</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnarled Roots-Changelings Are Not Good Guys, Folks</b><br /> <br /> It <i>hurts</i> to write that. Actually, it hurts to write a lot of this, because it's a lot darker than I usually deal with Changeling at. Hang in there, I don't intend to end on gloom, but I sure need to walk through it.<br /> <br /> See, Changeling, as it works out, continues to be as intrinsically deceitful as its' subject matter because i<i>t's so easy</i> to find fifty shades of heroism in the Lost. Sure, the Winter Court are selfish assholes and Summer Court has bullies, and sure, everyone's a little broken, but in the end, in comparison to True Fae, Huntsmen, Loyalists and Privateers, we have us a clear divide of good guy and bad guy to root and hiss for, right?<br /> <br /> Yeah, mark that as a no.<br /> <br /> A point of interest, to spark this section off, is the Morality systems of First Edition. What to glean here? Well, consider Humanity(Both Vampire and Promethean) and Wisdom. Really, these were just the same old morality system as mortals had, even if Wisdom had some additions. And, well, yeah, sure. These are all things that mimic the human worldview and spiritual foundation. Vampires strove not to lose it, Mages balanced it, and Prometheans sought it.<br /> <br /> But Changeling is the second gameline of the First Edition lot to feature something that deviates much more strongly from the Morality standard after Werewolf's Harmony, and for good reason: <i>Changelings aren't humans</i>.<br /> <br /> This, honestly, was one of my favorite things to come up in Hunter the Vigil's Mortal Remains. The simple fact of the matter is that every changeling is a broken person with a mercurial, transforming basis-their context is always questionable. This can lead to a lot of unclean and unpredictable responses. They can grow, they can progress, sure, no doubt, but until they get 'home', every changeling is a dangerous wreck of a person who can't even claim a human mindset anymore-they must adapt and come to understand themselves and their worlds through the eyes of a fairy.<br /> <br /> Freeholds have to protect their citizens from each other because of this risk of 'sudden eruption', particularly in a world that encourages. Hell, stop and consider, for a second, the Hedge. One of it's biggest qualities is that it forces people who enter to reconsider their values. Think stealing is a sin? After weeks of starvation in the Hedge, will you still think that when you see a goblin leaves his stall unattended? That's more or less a straight up example from the book of what the Hedge <i>does</i> to people. And that's just one of several forces that tug and pull on any given changeling.<br /> <br /> The simple fact is that Changeling, as a game, can't ever really have a game about good guys and bad guys in a clean cut manner, because it's entire basis embraces a system of shifting perspective, and it has to live with the fact that a character who would never, ever do a thing one day might find the wrong set of colliding glassworks of interests and circumstances the next day and do that exact one thing. This is the truth, this is the fight. Changelings have to crawl through mud and shade to find the high ground, to see things as they are, and the entire time, illusion and dream and dishonesty will pull them this way and that way and keep them ever and ever lost.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, always and forever, <i>anyone in Changeling could turn out to be a traitor, the one who most threatens your own, personal </i>I will never go back. It has always been that way. This isn't new. It's easy to lose, under the game's hopeful lights, but it has always been there. This has always been the game.<br /> <br /> That's just how it is. You always risk going back. Not all roads require your legs.<br /> <br /> <b>Crossing Your Heart, Hoping to Never Let You Get Away-The Huntsmen in the Scheme of Things</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have... many issues with Huntsmen. They're game-warping in a way, say, the Strix aren't. A Strix is universally bad news, but it can be bad news in many different ways, and it can be bad news for different people, for your city as a whole, for you in particular, for some third party. You can be peripherally involved, you can mitigate the bad news, the bad news may happen and leave you much worse off but still alive (well, undead). The Huntsmen are bad at this: they come after you, and the only possible endings to your confrontation are 1) game over, 2) you kill it, 3) you betray your fellow Changelings. This is much more narrow and restrictive.<br /> <br /> I also, frankly, find the Huntsmen boring, and find them to swallow space previously occupied by more interesting opponents. They're anti-Changelings, humen with a tell that can hide as things, and exist only to hunt you down. Despite all claims to the contrary, they cannot truly be unique. A brutal, wrathful monster that wants to tear down everything in its way to catch you, and a patient, sadistic monster that wants to exploit your attaches to slowly draw you out in the open and snatch you, are still pure-octane hunter-abducters who cannot be bargained with (except in this one specific way they all share) and want to abduct you. They have none of the variance and potential of goblins, Loyalists, Privateers, True Fae acting in person, all of whom can have many varied objectives and desires and can be interacted with in many ways - including socially or mentally.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, here we are, in this den of uncertainty about who and what and why and when and where and how, with the world being this ever uncertain thing that you just need to find your own personal certainty in, and who do we have represent that? Really, the whole lot of Arcadian forces. Hobgoblins can fill in that niche, but their function is actually markedly different as this goes, and they hew more towards the Long Way Home side of the argument rather than the <i>I will never go back</i>. So, by Arcadian forces, previously we meant True Fae, Fetches, and Loyalists, occasionally with Privateers. But really, when you splinter the argument down, each of these makes very different cases, nevermind the power gap we're about to chat about in a bit. The Fetch is simply &quot;You can't go back&quot;. A compelling antagonists, sure, love them to death, but it's a pawn. It holds the fort while other forces come on. Loyalists and Privateers? Compelling, but not inexorable enough, too human, too fragile, too broken. They are too 'you' to properly hit the buttons of <i>I will never go back</i>. And the True Fae themselves? Eh, they could be, but the terror of them is more compelling when they are the place to come to.They are the back you will never go to, it's strange, off-rhythm for them to seek you out. There's a hole in the world, there's a hole in your heart, there's a hole where your strength and fear used to be.<br /> <br /> That aside, the gap <i>really was</i> an issue. Loyalists just didn't get the attention they needed to be something between the Fetch and the True Fae, and really, they couldn't be-as changelings, they were best on a sliding scale. Fetches don't have a long enough span given their place to really go far in the Mid-Wyrd Area, and the True Fae became cheapened when they became weaker for showing up. Again, there was a hole in the world. We needed an icon who could stand just outside the door, the one who whispered gently, with the muck and the shade and the blood of maggots, into your delicate ear &quot;Let me in.&quot; Someone on the threshold, with a hand firmly on the chain of <i>I will never go back</i>, one who could throw a city in uproar.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen. The Huntsmen can be intimately outside. The Huntsmen can break every dream and delusion you have about the Long Way Home, and they can make it all the stronger by smashing them down. The Huntsmen can be powerful but not godly, the Huntsmen can wear the thousand faces that is missing, faces to fill the hole in the world, in the narrative, in the changelings themselves.<br /> <br /> And, really, I find arguments of narrowness astoundingly wrong. The Huntsmen have a target, sure, and they have a fairly simple goal-bring that person back-but you don't move queen pieces strictly like a rook or a bishop. I think a lot of this comes down to some story misconceptions.<br /> <br /> I mean, why can't a Huntsman go after a city? What's keeping him from grabbing the Bulwark and flipping on it's head? Why does a Huntsman have to go after you? Who says a Huntsman even has to exist for you immediately? Who says that indiscriminate chaos can't happen? Who says you can't bargain with them?<br /> <br /> I mean, when you get right down to a very basic level, the True Fae, the Loyalists, the Fetch(knowingly or not), all of them want to abduct you and ship you back to Arcadia. This is a one directional game, all roads lead to Arcadia. <i>I will never go back</i> requires conflict with the many faces of <i>back</i>. It's not like this limitation hasn't always existed, cause it always has-if it's in service to Arcadia, it's there, like Hitler lingering over a forum thread, waiting to come in.<br /> <br /> If I am honest, Changeling the Lost Second Edition has been plagued more by shallow, narrow, rigid readings since day one than any other second edition came out. I sometimes worry that in a fit of irony, the fandom is now so stuck in its' own nostalgia that it can't see what's really go on. The Huntsmen thread has had some of the most superficial readings I've seen to date.<br /> <br /> Because a Huntsman has a goal, but each one can have their various ambitions, and they have the tools to do so much beyond just capturing one fae. The Huntsmen can ramp out the paranoia by hiding among the courtiers, ousting them to the world and each other with a swing of their weapons, tempt the Lost into their own death spiral, lie and deceive their way into the heart of a Bulwark and break it over their knees.<br /> <br /> In fact, Huntsmen are something of a Bulwark breaker, stirring the pot and causing chaos and disharmony until they can dance their way into the ritual and shatter them. They come with a hall of mirrors and pointed fingers and lies and viciousness. The Huntsmen may be here to grab one person, and that may be the goal, but they have other goals, other tastes, over attitudes, that weigh in just as much<br /> <br /> On the other extreme, we have people who think they plague the game, who read inevitability and constancy where, honestly, there isn't. The changelings of first edition were constantly afraid that the True Fae were going to come for them, and somehow everyone was okay with that. If I were a twee writer, I would suggest that the frantic worrying and complaining over similar sentiment over the Huntsmen is just proof that they thought the Huntsmen actually would. But that's farking useless.<br /> <br /> Still, it's worth noting that this pervasive sense of the True Fae just swooping in and taking the changelings until they were dead or given a better offer is as old as Lost itself is. People used to bitch time and again during the early day of the games.<br /> <br /> And then reality settled in. Like reality settles in with the Huntsmen. You'll notice there's not a whole lot of bitching about how the True Fae just sweeping in anymore.<br /> <br /> In game, again, it's not always immediately worth it to make a Huntsman. The Huntsman doesn't always spring immediately back into the game upon coming back, despite the time limit. The Huntsman does not just dogmatically pursue a single target, because while that target is central, it can do so much more that make it's time worth while. It has it's own balance of The Long Way Home and <i>I will never go back</i> to handle. All these reasons and more is why they are both worthy of being the cart upsetter for a chronicle <i>and</i> why they are not as pervasive as people make them out to be.<br /> <br /> Out of game, it just makes sense to use them where narratively it's appropriate-they are creatures of narrative, as are the True Fae. You can do a lot with them if you dream with their abilities, and you get the most when you don't play them like the Terminator, but rather as what they are-wickedly clever and persistent stake-raising, tone-changing knives.<br /> <br /> Flex a little, dream a little, breathe a little. Dive into the dark and pull out on the other side to find what's there. Because the Huntsmen are just one half of the equation, much the same way <i>I will never go back</i> is only one half of the game.<br /> <br /> <b>There's a Star For Me In That Night-Between the Bleak and Hopeful</b><br /> <br /> So, I've been doing an indulgence of bleakness. Congratulations TvTropes, I give you some due.<br /> <br /> Now to tell that bleakness to go choke on a bag of baby dicks like I always do.<br /> <br /> I've dug deep into the darkness of this game, but I want to make it clear that I don't fucking much care for a bleak game. I never have. I never will. I don't truck with fatalistic tragedy, as many people in this thread seem to think Changeling is becoming. And I'll tell you, here and now, this game is not a stage for fatalistic tragedy.<br /> <br /> I've been harping on and on about the due of the darkness of <i>I will never go back </i>because, yes, I feel like so many people seem to have lost sight of it, but this game was not pitched as having a theme of <i>I will never go back</i>. It's theme is the Long Way Home. <i>I will never go back</i> is what informs the Long part of that phrase, it's what makes the changelings Lost, it's what makes it psychological and terrifying and deeply, beautifully important to so many people.<br /> <br /> Because despite every bit of mud and shade and blood of maggots that is drawn from <i>I will never go back</i>, at it's heart, Changeling tells you, the character, you, the player, you,the world-<br /> <br /> Changeling tells you <i>that you can win.</i><br /> <br /> Changeling tells you <i>that you can have a happy dream, that you can have the happy story</i>.<br /> <br /> It tells you that by challenging you to take <i>I will never go back</i> head on, to dive through it and tear through it, that with cleverness and trust and hope, <i>always hope</i>, that one day-<br /> <br /> One day, you'll be okay. That you and yours will be okay. Because you fought your way through it. Because you didn't run, or hide, or just tell yourself a story about how it might be better, it'll be okay.<br /> <br /> It won't be safe. It might not be comfortable.<br /> <br /> But it'll be okay. Because you can match it. Time and time again. With each new and old shadow on the doorstep, with each new growth of towering trees, for every Huntsman you face.<br /> <br /> You'll be okay. Whoever <i>you</i> are in this case.<br /> <br /> That's Changeling the Lost. It needs the bleak. It needs the traitors. It needs the confusion and the loss and the weakness. It needs the Huntsmen and the storms and the easy lies to believe. It needs them because you can't be okay without acknowledging them, without fighting them, without winning and losing to them, until you transcend the story into living, 'til you transcend moments of time into a life.<br /> <br /> That's Changeling the Lost. That's the game I fell in love with. And that's the game David Hill and his crew are bringing you all with Second Edition.<br /> <br /> Maybe, if you read it again, with clarity, with a broadness and flexibility of reading, you can see how that's happening. It's my hope that you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T20:43:34-08:00","id":820121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819895#post819895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If you choose to live, many people will die as a result&quot; has a kind of inherency and predictability that real life rarely presents. This isn't the assassination of one president being blamed on the person who unknowingly caused the circumstances in which one person would kill them. This is &quot;Huntsmen always come for Changelings, always, and they always kill people, always, so by choosing to live you choose to have people die for you.&quot; It doesn't make you morally responsible for it, but those people<i> are still dead </i>and they still wouldn't be dead if you hadn't chosen to live free. It's that kind of amusing collapsing point of morality and emotion where you're not actually responsible for it, but if you're capable of telling yourself &quot;well it's not my fault&quot; as you see the corpses mount over the course of you're life you're probably a<i> huge asshole.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You apparently missed a pair of things earlier in the thread:<br /> <br /> 1) True Fae need something very specific and very rare to send a Huntsman after someone, and once they use it once, that thing is gone. I think Arc said that Huntsmen come for you, at most, twice in a lifetime.<br /> <br /> 2) Huntsmen can, and are, permanently killed by their own weapons. It takes a bit to get said weapons to recognize you as the new wielder, but it can be done.<br /> <br /> Also, that suicide thing? Maybe. Maybe death is a better option than outwitting a Huntsman, if you can think of no better way to stop them forever. But you are not responsible for their crimes they do-your Keeper summoned them. You are the victim here, one who happens to have the bad luck to be in a place where other people are victimized, same as you. But your &quot;crime&quot; was escaping an obsessive slaver. It's not your fault they exist, and anyone who says (in-universe, I'm not saying you're one of them OOC) so is generally ignorant, or trying to justify the real abuser, the Other.<br /> <br /> (Okay, generally the first, since the Gentry are, by definition, inhuman, not figures of the status quo to be protected. But I can see the latter as a viewpoint belonging to Gentry cultists and loyalists).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T20:47:16-08:00","id":820124,"title":"","content":"Jesus Christ on a piece of buttered toast, I have not written that much since I explained <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217778-inspiration-from-demon?p=218544#post218544\">why Demon can't answer Changeling</a>.<br /> <br /> Yes, shameless plugs, but you'll find relevant wisdom there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:15:32-08:00","id":820136,"title":"","content":"You got all of my likes, Arc. All of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:21:53-08:00","id":820139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820121#post820121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You apparently missed a pair of things earlier in the thread:<br /> <br /> 1) True Fae need something very specific and very rare to send a Huntsman after someone, and once they use it once, that thing is gone. I think Arc said that Huntsmen come for you, at most, twice in a lifetime.<br /> <br /> 2) Huntsmen can, and are, permanently killed by their own weapons. It takes a bit to get said weapons to recognize you as the new wielder, but it can be done.<br /> <br /> Also, that suicide thing? Maybe. Maybe death is a better option than outwitting a Huntsman, if you can think of no better way to stop them forever. But you are not responsible for their crimes they do-your Keeper summoned them. You are the victim here, one who happens to have the bad luck to be in a place where other people are victimized, same as you. But your &quot;crime&quot; was escaping an obsessive slaver. It's not your fault they exist, and anyone who says (in-universe, I'm not saying you're one of them OOC) so is generally ignorant, or trying to justify the real abuser, the Other.<br /> <br /> (Okay, generally the first, since the Gentry are, by definition, inhuman, not figures of the status quo to be protected. But I can see the latter as a viewpoint belonging to Gentry cultists and loyalists).</div> </div> </div> </div>They can come after you a lot more than that, but once you reclaim your emblem(It still needs a canon word), It's hard to find a replacement. Like I said, it has to be an iconic item tied to you and Arcadia. Some have more than others, but that's still not a lot. And yeah, there is a way to claim a Huntsman's weapon. Not that you need to, but it helps.<br /> <br /> Love the rest of this, as an aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:36:17-08:00","id":820144,"title":"","content":"I have very mixed emotions on that post, broad agreement with the fundamentals aside.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that what you are saying there does come through the final text (because us readers lacking the whole perspective otherwise can only read so much without the whole context).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:56:05-08:00","id":820156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820144#post820144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have very mixed emotions on that post, broad agreement with the fundamentals aside.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that what you are saying there does come through the final text (because us readers lacking the whole perspective otherwise can only read so much without the whole context).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that kind of subtle theme is the kind of thing that needs to be explicitly called out in the text (&quot;Let's be frank-Changeling is a game about the <i>Long </i>Road Home and the <i>Long</i>ness of it is due to how fundamentally alien the Lost become during their Durances and the fact the majority of the Keepers want that road to lead straight back into their domains..&quot;).<br /> <br /> But it's not something new to changeling (see the paragraph at the beginning of every book that explains things are not hopeless).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T03:56:47-08:00","id":820244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820117#post820117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling tells you <i>that you can win.</i><br /> <br /> Changeling tells you <i>that you can have a happy dream, that you can have the happy story</i>.<br /> <br /> It tells you that by challenging you to take <i>I will never go back</i> head on, to dive through it and tear through it, that with cleverness and trust and hope, <i>always hope</i>, that one day-<br /> <br /> One day, you'll be okay. That you and yours will be okay. Because you fought your way through it. Because you didn't run, or hide, or just tell yourself a story about how it might be better, it'll be okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be exceedingly useful if this was brought up to the fore and used to balance the Huntsmen. Perhaps there would've been less &quot;shallow&quot; readings if the text had been less &quot;every changeling gets their turn&quot; and more balanced in tone. Hell, my own distaste for the Huntsmen would've done a complete 180 if they had been portrayed as uncommon or even rare (as it would befit their status as Mid-Wyrd antagonists).<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside about the shallow readings, I get what you mean. You mean &quot;give us some trust that we know what we're doing, that it will a great product in the end.&quot; I totally get you. But one-way trust is a bit of a tall order, no? I think that if instead of dismissing interpretations as shallow, particularly if there are enough that you find it surprising, it might be worth looking into? Ask people what exactly doesn't click for them? Trying to gather info to refine and polish the final product instead of pitching another sale? Trust is a two-way street and all that. &quot;You're not getting it&quot; is just as useless and reciprocal as &quot;I'm not going to give the writer any good faith.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2e is not going to stop making Changeling my favourite gameline. I already know this. I <i>have</i> complete confidence that it's going to be an even better game than 1e, issues notwithstanding, and that I'll be gushing about the awesomeness of this or that later on. Maybe people get it, they really do, but certain things are deal-breakers for them. It's like you baked a cake for them, and it's really elaborate, and you're showing off some new techniques you learnt. And then, when the person tastes it, they can't stop talking about the anise you used. And you're like &quot;but what about the berries, the chocolate, the French vanilla? Why aren't you appreciating all that?&quot; Maybe they do appreciate it, but they just can't get past the anise. It happens. It's not really anybody's fault.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820121#post820121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that suicide thing? Maybe. Maybe death is a better option than outwitting a Huntsman, if you can think of no better way to stop them forever. But you are not responsible for their crimes they do-your Keeper summoned them. You are the victim here, one who happens to have the bad luck to be in a place where other people are victimized, same as you. But your &quot;crime&quot; was escaping an obsessive slaver. It's not your fault they exist, and anyone who says (in-universe, I'm not saying you're one of them OOC) so is generally ignorant, or trying to justify the real abuser, the Other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody really said anything about changelings being responsible for the people the Huntsmen kill (pretty sure we all know better than that). In fact, nobody suggested the idea that suicide is the morally responsible thing to do either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T08:42:44-08:00","id":820354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820244#post820244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be exceedingly useful if this was brought up to the fore and used to balance the Huntsmen. Perhaps there would've been less &amp;quot;shallow&amp;quot; readings if the text had been less &amp;quot;every changeling gets their turn&amp;quot; and more balanced in tone. Hell, my own distaste for the Huntsmen would've done a complete 180 if they had been portrayed as uncommon or even rare (as it would befit their status as Mid-Wyrd antagonists).</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this part made it clear that they are supposed to be quite rare:<br /> <br /> &quot;Because the introduction of the Huntsmen into a chronicle signals very strong thematic elements, Storytellers should be careful when or even if they appear. Huntsmen are extremely compelling villains, and the threat of their appearance should always be there, as trying to prepare for their inevitable Hunts is part of what keeps changeling society together. Teasing out this threat, even if it\u2019s never actually followed through on, contributes great dramatic tension to a Changeling: the Lost campaign. For all its power, however, the greatest dramatic tension is not in the act of appearing. The actual appearance of a Huntsman is a much stronger, more overt thing and your chronicle will shift accordingly. Once the Huntsmen show up, a chronicle naturally becomes about the Hunt and surviving it intact.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820244#post820244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as an aside about the shallow readings, I get what you mean. You mean &amp;quot;give us some trust that we know what we're doing, that it will a great product in the end.&amp;quot; I totally get you. But one-way trust is a bit of a tall order, no? I think that if instead of dismissing interpretations as shallow, particularly if there are enough that you find it surprising, it might be worth looking into? Ask people what exactly doesn't click for them? Trying to gather info to refine and polish the final product instead of pitching another sale? Trust is a two-way street and all that. &amp;quot;You're not getting it&amp;quot; is just as useless and reciprocal as &amp;quot;I'm not going to give the writer any good faith.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't put words in Arc's mouth, but that's not how his comments about shallow readings came off to me at all. Shallow readings are like the recent assertions that all Darklings must betray people. Or the comments about Fairest being &quot;Ventrue Changelings&quot;. Or the complaints that the new Wizened are cyborgs or batman villains. A shallow reading is latching onto one or two parts of a writeup and letting those few parts define the entire writeup for you, when if you looked at it with a more open mind you can clearly see that it's written to be interpreted more broadly than that. Shallow readings are distilling complex concepts down to an easily digestible archetype, and then complaining that the concepts are too archetypal and lacking in nuance. There has been a <i>lot</i> of that going on with the Changeling previews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820244#post820244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e is not going to stop making Changeling my favourite gameline. I already know this. I <i>have</i> complete confidence that it's going to be an even better game than 1e, issues notwithstanding, and that I'll be gushing about the awesomeness of this or that later on. Maybe people get it, they really do, but certain things are deal-breakers for them. It's like you baked a cake for them, and it's really elaborate, and you're showing off some new techniques you learnt. And then, when the person tastes it, they can't stop talking about the anise you used. And you're like &amp;quot;but what about the berries, the chocolate, the French vanilla? Why aren't you appreciating all that?&amp;quot; Maybe they do appreciate it, but they just can't get past the anise. It happens. It's not really anybody's fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't see that happening, so much as people are complaining the cake doesn't have French Vanilla when it absolutely does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820244#post820244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody really said anything about changelings being responsible for the people the Huntsmen kill (pretty sure we all know better than that). In fact, nobody suggested the idea that suicide is the morally responsible thing to do either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to step aside from the suicide argument because I can't see myself saying anything on it that would be helpful or facilitate productive discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T08:52:40-08:00","id":820358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820354#post820354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought this part made it clear that they are supposed to be quite rare:<br /> <br /> &quot;Because the introduction of the Huntsmen into a chronicle signals very strong thematic elements, Storytellers should be careful when or even if they appear. Huntsmen are extremely compelling villains, and the threat of their appearance should always be there, as trying to prepare for their inevitable Hunts is part of what keeps changeling society together. Teasing out this threat, even if it\u2019s never actually followed through on, contributes great dramatic tension to a Changeling: the Lost campaign. For all its power, however, the greatest dramatic tension is not in the act of appearing. The actual appearance of a Huntsman is a much stronger, more overt thing and your chronicle will shift accordingly. Once the Huntsmen show up, a chronicle naturally becomes about the Hunt and surviving it intact.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I interpreted the exact opposite. After all, they can't be <i>that</i> rare, or else you <i>can't</i> maintain a constant threat of their appearance. Furthermore, the players live in an organic world that, ideally, continues to exist and go on when they're not around. Give a Freehold enough members and at some point, you could easily reach a point where there's always a Huntsman going around. And even if there aren't any Huntsmen about, the text clearly wants the ST to push the idea that they might come, to keep them present even when they're not around. It may not be the same as an active Hunt, but it's also hardly a breather either.<br /> <br /> That said, if the intention was to make Huntsmen quite rare (on a Freehold level, not on an individual changeling level), I'll stand corrected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820354#post820354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't put words in Arc's mouth, but that's not how his comments about shallow readings came off to me at all. Shallow readings are like the recent assertions that all Darklings must betray people. Or the comments about Fairest being &quot;Ventrue Changelings&quot;. Or the complaints that the new Wizened are cyborgs or batman villains. A shallow reading is latching onto one or two parts of a writeup and letting those few parts define the entire writeup for you, when if you looked at it with a more open mind you can clearly see that it's written to be interpreted more broadly than that. Shallow readings are distilling complex concepts down to an easily digestible archetype, and then complaining that the concepts are too archetypal and lacking in nuance. There has been a <i>lot</i> of that going on with the Changeling previews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820354#post820354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don't see that happening, so much as people are complaining the cake doesn't have French Vanilla when it absolutely does.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's valid. It could also be that the anise is overpowering the French Vanilla, so even if it <i>is</i> there, some people can't taste it. It may be that anise is an unusual flavour while vanilla is what everyone is used to, so people are focusing on the strange new thing over the comfort flavour they've gotten used to and taken for granted. It's probably a bit of everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820354#post820354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to step aside from the suicide argument because I can't see myself saying anything on it that would be helpful or facilitate productive discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same, I find victim-blaming abhorrent and I don't want my &quot;here's something drastic to illustrate my point&quot; example to be interpreted like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:26:24-08:00","id":820379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820358#post820358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, I interpreted the exact opposite. After all, they can't be <i>that</i> rare, or else you <i>can't</i> maintain a constant threat of their appearance. Furthermore, the players live in an organic world that, ideally, continues to exist and go on when they're not around. Give a Freehold enough members and at some point, you could easily reach a point where there's always a Huntsman going around. And even if there aren't any Huntsmen about, the text clearly wants the ST to push the idea that they might come, to keep them present even when they're not around. It may not be the same as an active Hunt, but it's also hardly a breather either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok, I can see where you'd get that interpretation. What I got out of that paragraph was that the Huntsman are meant to be used more as a looming threat than as an active antagonist. That's why &quot;Storytellers should be careful when <b>or even if</b> they appear.&quot; While the fear of the Huntsman should be ever-present, rare should be the game where you're actually forced to face one.<br /> <br /> I don't know if anyone else had this experience, but for me, there was always a big dilemma in 1e. The characters were always supposed to be afraid that one day their Keeper might snatch them back to Arcadia, but it was difficult to make that threat feel real. Making the Gentry undefeatable kills the dramatic tension, because if they can just come snatch you and there's nothing you can do about it, there's no point in trying to prevent it because you'll inevitably fail. If they have game stats they can be defeated, but that cheapens their mystique as creatures of pure narrative. As Arc eloquently put it, the Gentry were in a weird place between being the &quot;where&quot; you'll never go back to and the &quot;who&quot; that would bring you back, and that just didn't quite work. The Huntsman solve that problem. They can actualize the threat that Faeries are going to come and take you back to Arcadia, while also being a monster with stats that you can fight back against. And if you beat it, if you kill it, your Keeper is still out there and still wants you back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:42:23-08:00","id":820387,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, I actually never had that problem. Mainly because I ran into a lot of people who assumed the Gentry never left Arcadia, and I was like &quot;Um, you do remember that they <i>kidnap people all the time</i>, right?&quot; So the way I saw it, it was easy to keep the Gentry a looming presence by having them actually interact with the mortal world. One of my dearest tropes is &quot;Tea With Cthulhu&quot;, and one of my favourite scenes I've ever ran was when my player's mother told her that she'd spent the afternoon having coffee with a most charming gentleman that raised some very vague red flags for the changeling. I allowed the character to waver a bit over whether she was being overly paranoid or not. And then she goes to bed and finds a black rose on her pillow.<br /> <br /> The Keeper was never &quot;fightable&quot;, he never interacted with the changeling at all, but all it took was one friendly conversation and one harmless rose and the menace of the Gentry became way less distant than it had been. To me, it always made sense that the True Fae can't just waltz into a Freehold and take whoever they want because the high-Wyrd changelings present A) have the means to detect True Fae incursions, and B) have the means to actually <i>kill</i> the True Fae, or at least that particular Actor. So the Gentry tease and threaten in order to unbalance the changeling and get them in a vulnerable position where they <i>can</i> actually drag the changeling back screaming before anybody can save them.<br /> <br /> I never played Changeling like Werewolf or Coup. On the contrary, I always emphasised just how blasphemous the Loyalists and Privateers were, and how much changelings depended on each other to survive. If you'd asked me which supernatural creature was most likely to engage in that sort of thing, I'd have said Vampire first, with Mage second and Changeling third.<br /> <br /> The role of the distant, immensely powerful but ultimately defeatable threat was already covered by the True Fae. I totally agree that they don't fit the &quot;Mid-Wyrd antagonist&quot; thing they were looking for, that's definitely something I fully understand, but that I thankfully don't really have to deal with in my games. Since I default to a crossover setting, I can easily borrow antagonists or splats from other books to fill that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:43:14-08:00","id":820389,"title":"","content":"Listen to Charly, for she speaks truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:50:23-08:00","id":820394,"title":"","content":"Never implied otherwise.<br /> <br /> There's immense value in sharing diverging experiences and opinions, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:05:32-08:00","id":820403,"title":"","content":"In lieu of time, I have to point at someone making sense rather than reply personally. I have a comment on that Changeling as Coup thing I want to get into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:08:47-08:00","id":820405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820387#post820387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strangely enough, I actually never had that problem. Mainly because I ran into a lot of people who assumed the Gentry never left Arcadia, and I was like &quot;Um, you do remember that they <i>kidnap people all the time</i>, right?&quot; So the way I saw it, it was easy to keep the Gentry a looming presence by having them actually interact with the mortal world. One of my dearest tropes is &quot;Tea With Cthulhu&quot;, and one of my favourite scenes I've ever ran was when my player's mother told her that she'd spent the afternoon having coffee with a most charming gentleman that raised some very vague red flags for the changeling. I allowed the character to waver a bit over whether she was being overly paranoid or not. And then she goes to bed and finds a black rose on her pillow.<br /> <br /> The Keeper was never &quot;fightable&quot;, he never interacted with the changeling at all, but all it took was one friendly conversation and one harmless rose and the menace of the Gentry became way less distant than it had been. To me, it always made sense that the True Fae can't just waltz into a Freehold and take whoever they want because the high-Wyrd changelings present A) have the means to detect True Fae incursions, and B) have the means to actually <i>kill</i> the True Fae, or at least that particular Actor. So the Gentry tease and threaten in order to unbalance the changeling and get them in a vulnerable position where they <i>can</i> actually drag the changeling back screaming before anybody can save them.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, what you're describing here reads to me like an excellently portrayed Huntsman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820387#post820387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never played Changeling like Werewolf or Coup. On the contrary, I always emphasised just how blasphemous the Loyalists and Privateers were, and how much changelings depended on each other to survive. If you'd asked me which supernatural creature was most likely to engage in that sort of thing, I'd have said Vampire first, with Mage second and Changeling third.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, Changelings absolutely rely on each other to survive. A lone Lost is easy pickings, you need that Bulwark to keep you safe, to force the Huntsman to have tea with you grandmother instead of just waltzing right in and taking you. It's also the reason the Huntsmen need Tokens of Reprieve. A united Freehold is too strong for a Huntsman to defeat, so the Huntsman's first job is to divide them. He tempts the weak-willed with promises of security if he ever comes back to them, and threatens the strong-willed with the promise that he will convince the weak-willed to betray them. Sure, you can call turning in another Changeling treason if you like. But ultimately, what are the weak ones going to be more afraid of? Being labeled a traitor, or being dragged back to their Keeper?<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen sow distrust among the people who have the greatest need to trust each other. That's exactly what makes them great antagonists for Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820387#post820387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The role of the distant, immensely powerful but ultimately defeatable threat was already covered by the True Fae. I totally agree that they don't fit the &quot;Mid-Wyrd antagonist&quot; thing they were looking for, that's definitely something I fully understand, but that I thankfully don't really have to deal with in my games. Since I default to a crossover setting, I can easily borrow antagonists or splats from other books to fill that niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Personally, I hate the idea of the Gentry being defeatable. As soon as you defeat them, that's it. Congradulations, you've won Changeling, you've reached the end of the long road home, and there's finally nothing left to be afraid of. That could be a fine conclusion to a chronicle, but that knowledge cheapens the threat of the Gentry at any point before the end of the campaign. The players know that as soon as their Keepers begin to tire of tea with their grandparents, it's about to be game over one way or another. You either beat the big bad, or you die trying, or he takes you back. That billboard signaling &quot;this is the finale&quot; removes a lot of dramatic tension.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen, on the other hand, they can do everything the Gentry can do for a chronicle, <i>and</i> the game can keep going after you beat them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-31-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:23:34-08:00","id":820418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820405#post820405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, what you're describing here reads to me like an excellently portrayed Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually thought I could've reframed that scene with a Huntsman instead of a Stranger, right after I posted. That's relevant for something I'll get into in a sec.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820405#post820405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, Changelings absolutely rely on each other to survive. A lone Lost is easy pickings, you need that Bulwark to keep you safe, to force the Huntsman to have tea with you grandmother instead of just waltzing right in and taking you. It's also the reason the Huntsmen need Tokens of Reprieve. A united Freehold is too strong for a Huntsman to defeat, so the Huntsman's first job is to divide them. He tempts the weak-willed with promises of security if he ever comes back to them, and threatens the strong-willed with the promise that he will convince the weak-willed to betray them. Sure, you can call turning in another Changeling treason if you like. But ultimately, what are the weak ones going to be more afraid of? Being labeled a traitor, or being dragged back to their Keeper?<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen sow distrust among the people who have the greatest need to trust each other. That's exactly what makes them great antagonists for Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I'm a bit worried that too much distrust and not enough trust will make changeling society hard to run as a ST. Sometimes I just want to run a game where the Freehold is mostly fine, at least for the time being, especially in small towns and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820405#post820405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. Personally, I hate the idea of the Gentry being defeatable. As soon as you defeat them, that's it. Congradulations, you've won Changeling, you've reached the end of the long road home, and there's finally nothing left to be afraid of. That could be a fine conclusion to a chronicle, but that knowledge cheapens the threat of the Gentry at any point before the end of the campaign. The players know that as soon as their Keepers begin to tire of tea with their grandparents, it's about to be game over one way or another. You either beat the big bad, or you die trying, or he takes you back. That billboard signaling &quot;this is the finale&quot; removes a lot of dramatic tension.</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually got me there, because none of my changeling games ever made it that far, so I never ran into that problem. Those are all good points, can't really argue with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820405#post820405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Huntsmen, on the other hand, they can do everything the Gentry can do for a chronicle, <i>and</i> the game can keep going after you beat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but agree.<br /> <br /> Welp.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm coming around. Maybe the Huntsmen aren't as bad as I thought.<br /> <br /> Thanks for taking the time to write all that, Charlaquin. I may not be terribly good at articulation, but I do very much appreciate the effort and thought you put into the explanations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:24:18-08:00","id":820419,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that individual Gentry can be defeated, but there's always more of them. Given their chaotic nature, you can never really know how many of them there are. If you kill your Keeper, you have a new problem: You're suddenly a limited edition collectible in the eyes of their favorite enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:29:13-08:00","id":820421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820419#post820419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that individual Gentry can be defeated, but there's always more of them. Given their chaotic nature, you can never really know how many of them there are. If you kill your Keeper, you have a new problem: You're suddenly a limited edition collectible in the eyes of their favorite enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's truth in this, but there's also truth in being the immortal killer. That changeling is not someone you challenge lightly-indeed, a conflict with such a changeling might be beyond the realm of mere play and instead be the setting for a new chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:56:03-08:00","id":820438,"title":"","content":"So, there are two things I want to comment on in regards to my monolith back there.<br /> <br /> 1) So, despite spending a huge time explaining why bleakness is important, I don't like it. I may have said <i>I will never go back</i> is what gives the series its' bite, but that was because I was making a point for the dark side of Changeling. I'm not doing that now, so truth be told, it's the Long Way Home that gives its' bite.<br /> <br /> Well, actually, as I alluded to, neither of those is true. It's a tug of war between the two, threatening to tear a changeling apart-but you will, or you should, spend more time on building home than risking pulling it apart. I know this pretty well, as a player. My first character, Noah Pyre, was someone I bugged my GM to let me do all sorts of side stories. I literally built my Hollow and Hedge Garden from the ground up, doing several stories of stealing stuff from the junkyard and making bargains at the Goblin Market. I researched contracts and scoured the Hedge on my own time. Noah ended up as an insanely powerful character because I spent a lot of my side time building home. Honestly, it was the most fun I ever had, and it had great unintended consequences, because I became this crazy powerful nuke of the Autumn Court that was reclusive. I wasn't far away from going True Fae in the eyes of the freehold, so when Candelabra, my keeper, attacked my Hollow, it was just me and my motley, and I was holding the door while getting everyone else out predominantly. That was such a prominent moment of Long Way Home versus <i>I will never go back home</i> for me. I was actually able to win it, too.<br /> <br /> Building a home and trust and hope-that was where a lot of the fun of the game was for me. I enjoyed tending to my garden and trying to keep it from devouring my flesh and Clarity. I enjoyed going through the Hedge to find forces to bargain with for Contracts, with nothing but an old, moldy book as a guide. But I needed the enemies at the gate to make the game effective-not because I constantly needed challenges, but because I had to <i>think</i> I constantly had challenges. I needed the paranoia to inevitably learn to not let it ruin Noah's life.<br /> <br /> 2) Speaking of enemies at the gate, man, do I get not using the Loyalists in a Coup like manner, or anyone else for that matter. That was a recent awareness thing. In the beginning, I used them like the Wild Hunt, right alongside the True Fae. Looking back, I can see had a level of dissatisfaction with that, but the idea of the hunt was so strong in my mind, I just did it this way.<br /> <br /> But as I played the game and read and learned more, it started hitting me how that was a little unrealistic. It wasn't effective. It made more sense to have traitors, after a few readings of the core, people who found the niche place to make people disappear. But I enjoyed my outsiders at the gate too. I eventually fell out of favor of using loyalists all together, actually, focusing a lot on court politics. In the middle of that, the realization of how much any given changeling worries about their safety hit me.<br /> <br /> It took me contrasting Lost with Descent for me it finally get back into using the Loyalists, and I used them a lot to play games of three card monte with the freehold while also shaking their chains and getting people to think about jumping ship. Even then, the Loyalists as a whole never really did it for me-they were more a faceless mob, with every face I made for them kind of feeling too little. The Huntsmen fixed a lot of that for me.<br /> <br /> But anyways, the big thing is that Changeling is <i>not</i> actually a big game of Coup. Loyalists can and should be used that way, take advantage of the fact they are versatile in a way Huntsmen aren't, but Changeling isn't Coup. It's not Descent.<br /> <br /> I referenced my Inspiration from Demon thread shortly after the last because I wanted to support the idea that the big thing about Changeling is that any given character really is less at risk than they think they are. Not that they're safe, mind you-their paranoia is legitimate, their fear is real. But Changeling is more of the fear in your head than the fear without. In this way, you can't play the game like Coup or Descent. You can't constantly push the <i>I will never go back</i> button. And the game as it is now keeps that in Mind. The Huntsmen might come <i>inevitably</i>, but not now, and even when they do, not <i>constantly</i>. It's not a constant pressure on a freehold. It's a car accident. Most of the time, you spend your time driving, and you avoid shit, but you worry about it happening anyways, until you become calm and confident enough to not just crash willy nilly.<br /> <br /> When you come across a car accident, or worse get in one yourself, it naturally ramps up your fear of crashes again. And that's life until you get to a point where you are capable enough that even when you fear the car crash, you're ready to handle the possibilites. That's Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:01:55-08:00","id":820442,"title":"","content":"That was actually really reassuring, Arc. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:28:44-08:00","id":820458,"title":"","content":"You're welcome. That was stuff I intend to include more of in the last part, but I had actually spent my whole day writing that, and I wanted it to be done.<br /> <br /> I think as rough guide, you want your games, in reality, to be about 20% <i>I will never go back</i>, 80% Long Way Home, but you want the presentation, what you make your characters think it is(or at least, see it as, as it's important that they use Clarity to break it down and see it as it is), to be about 50/50. That can be a hard thing to sell subtly in a game text(I could see talking bluntly about this in a supplement), so I do get why people miss it-but it is there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-31-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:29:31-08:00","id":820459,"title":"","content":"Thank you for taking the time to make such a thorough and insightful post and following it up with further explanations of your position, Arc. Particularly for those who had expressed doubts, but it addressed very important things regardless, and I found it a very substantial read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:35:55-08:00","id":820464,"title":"","content":"You're welcome!<br /> <br /> Like I said, I love me my rose petals, but it felt like people had moved too far away from the thorns-hell, even the just the mud.<br /> <br /> Changeling <i>can</i> be a really bleak game-as I said, this actually came up a lot when it first came out, and I felt it was time I gave credit to that,even though I still reject it. Go through hell to better enjoy heaven, eh Jane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:01:51-08:00","id":820478,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EarnYourHappyEnding\" target=\"_blank\">Earn your happy ending</a>. It's hard, but you can carve out a home.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Thinking about the Huntsman's tell, now, and how to get players worried that a Huntsman is after them, including false alarms. It seems like you can repeat just about anything enough to get players worried that a Huntsman might be after them. &quot;I keep seeing the number 6 everywhere!&quot; As a Storyteller, I can imagine accidentally triggering a sufficiently paranoid player's pattern recognition.<br /> <br /> Any tips on how to get a new player sufficiently paranoid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:02:17-08:00","id":820479,"title":"","content":"Re: bleakness vs. hope in Changeling, I see them as two sides of the same coin. Changeling is only able to be the hopeful game that it is because it has the potential to be extremely bleak. Borrowing from Arc's wonderful post again, the hopeful message is that in spite of everything, you can win. You can make it home. But that victory is only as inspiring as the adversity it triumphed over. That's why I'm always confused when I see statements like &quot;Changeling is the darkest line&quot; or &quot;Changeling is the brightest line.&quot; Because to me it's both. The dark is needed to give the light context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:03:11-08:00","id":820481,"title":"","content":"Hey, Arc, I was thinking about your comment on Loyalists. One of the best examples of a Privateer/Loyalist I saw was actually not a one of those at all, and wasn't even in a changeling book. I think it was in Mortal Remains? Shivers, I think was the name of the changeling? I just liked how it exemplified the way I always saw those antagonists: as sad, tragic characters who are just so broken they are willing to do anything to avoid going back. And most of them know what they're doing and hate themselves for it, but the fear is just stronger.<br /> <br /> I think that's an interesting place to take Loyalists and Privateers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:28:11-08:00","id":820500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820418#post820418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I'm a bit worried that too much distrust and not enough trust will make changeling society hard to run as a ST. Sometimes I just want to run a game where the Freehold is mostly fine, at least for the time being, especially in small towns and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a reasonable concern, and I think this is exactly why the writeup cautions ST's to think carefully about when and if to use Huntsman. In the normal course of play, they should be a back-of-the-mind sort of danger. You might have your contingency plan for if you ever have to deal with a Huntsman, but you probably don't expect to have to use it. I love Arc's comparison to a car accident. That's exactly the sort of thing we all know is inevitable, but we tend to think &quot;but it won't happen to <i>me</i>.&quot; Until someone you know gets in an accident, or you have a close call yourself.<br /> <br /> So most of the time, the Freehold is fine. Until the ST starts making a point of describing every time one of the players sees the words Bad Wolf. The players start to worry about the significance of those words, and the frequency with which they keep appearing. They start to wonder if it might be a Huntsman's Tell. Paranoia starts to build. You check and re-check the Bulwark rituals to make sure everything is still holding up. You make a trip to the Goblin Market to see if you can get your hands on a Token of Reprieve <i>just in case.</i> And maybe that's all that ever comes of it. Maybe the words stop appearing as often, and eventually, the ST stops pointing them out alltogether. Maybe you got yourself all worked up over nothing. Maybe things are finally back to normal.<br /> <br /> This gives the ST valves to control the flow of paranoia. It can be a constant slow drip, or a build up and then die down, or an occasional sudden burst that disappears as quickly and unexpectedly as it arrived. Most likely, some mix of all of the above. All of this without ever needing to actually use a Huntsman.<br /> <br /> The story where the Huntsman actually shows up can be a powerful one, but you don't want to use it every game. Just like you don't do an Idigam story every time you play Werewolf, or a Strix story every time you play Vampire. But their existance allows you to tease the possibility that <i>maybe this is the game where he's actually going to break out the Huntsmen/Idigam/Strix.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820387#post820387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for taking the time to write all that, Charlaquin. I may not be terribly good at articulation, but I do very much appreciate the effort and thought you put into the explanations.</div> </div> </div> </div>My pleasure. I enjoy these discussions, and they help me improve my own understanding of the game as well. I probably wouldn't have thought this critically about how best to use the Huntsman in my own games if it hadn't been for this conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-31-2016, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:30:14-08:00","id":820503,"title":"","content":"I definitely see the narrative value of Hunstmen as an extension of the Keeper, as something that can take you back without being the Keeper itself, and as an arm that can be cut off, metaphorically speaking. Narratively, I get why they're important.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, they feel pretty anemic to me, mostly because Yearning puts such a low cap on their otherwise potent abilities. The difficulty of permakilling them aside, I feel like I have more to fear from Loyalists with the same exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:18:22-08:00","id":820562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820481#post820481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Arc, I was thinking about your comment on Loyalists. One of the best examples of a Privateer/Loyalist I saw was actually not a one of those at all, and wasn't even in a changeling book. I think it was in Mortal Remains? Shivers, I think was the name of the changeling? I just liked how it exemplified the way I always saw those antagonists: as sad, tragic characters who are just so broken they are willing to do anything to avoid going back. And most of them know what they're doing and hate themselves for it, but the fear is just stronger.<br /> <br /> I think that's an interesting place to take Loyalists and Privateers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to do a story where a courtier just kidnaps someone out of the blue. As the players investigate, they discover a Huntsman offered a Token of reprieve for someone who's no longer to them ages ago, but the courtier didn't know the Huntsman was gone. When you get to the final confrontation, empathetic characters'll find out that the Changeling's sense of security finally broke after a series of unfortunate circumstances, and now he's waiting to make a terrible trade that'll never come. Ideally as a story, but it could be fun to do as an arc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820503#post820503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely see the narrative value of Hunstmen as an extension of the Keeper, as something that can take you back without being the Keeper itself, and as an arm that can be cut off, metaphorically speaking. Narratively, I get why they're important.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, they feel pretty anemic to me, mostly because Yearning puts such a low cap on their otherwise potent abilities. The difficulty of permakilling them aside, I feel like I have more to fear from Loyalists with the same exp.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, but furthermore, okay, we'll make them nightmares when we get the chance. Challenge accepted and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:43:47-08:00","id":820572,"title":"","content":"I sorta get why people would say changeling is the brightest or darkest line given how wrapped up it is in both. But, it's sorta like Geist, where it being both is part of the point. In geist, your a person who has been engulfed in the darkness and was lifted out into the light, but while you can't help but see the shadows walking around, you make sure your surrounded in light. In changeling, you were trapped in a world of tinted windows where good becomes bad and bad becomes good, and when you finally escaped you found the world full of darkness and go out in search for the lights that are hanging around, it might be difficult because being in the tinted world has made it hard to judge what paths will lead to darkness and which will lead to light, but you go out searching anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-31-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:52:22-08:00","id":820575,"title":"","content":"I've had this idea for a while, but I thought I'd bring it up as an alternate use for a Huntsman: My first chronicle is going to involve a book called Biblio Antiqua, and I'm wondering if there could be a variant Huntsman as one of the many people trying to get their hands on it. If the idea of sending a Huntsman specifically after an object doesn't fit, I think I could have acquiring the book be part of an NPC Changeling's personal approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:17:55-08:00","id":820597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820458#post820458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome. That was stuff I intend to include more of in the last part, but I had actually spent my whole day writing that, and I wanted it to be done.<br /> <br /> I think as rough guide, you want your games, in reality, to be about 20% <i>I will never go back</i>, 80% Long Way Home, but you want the presentation, what you make your characters think it is(or at least, see it as, as it's important that they use Clarity to break it down and see it as it is), to be about 50/50. That can be a hard thing to sell subtly in a game text(I could see talking bluntly about this in a supplement), so I do get why people miss it-but it is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't you talk about this stuff bluntly in the corebook, though? That just seems odd to me.<br /> <br /> I mean, it is an RPG core book - they're instruction manuals as much as they're world building setting, and instruction manuals need to be as unambiguous as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:29:34-08:00","id":820609,"title":"","content":"Because I don't think I can write something for a section I have no jurisdiction, but I am damn certain I'll get on a book about the Huntsmen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:32:19-08:00","id":820614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820575#post820575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had this idea for a while, but I thought I'd bring it up as an alternate use for a Huntsman: My first chronicle is going to involve a book called Biblio Antiqua, and I'm wondering if there could be a variant Huntsman as one of the many people trying to get their hands on it. If the idea of sending a Huntsman specifically after an object doesn't fit, I think I could have acquiring the book be part of an NPC Changeling's personal approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>The preview says that Fae create Huntsmen to bring back something that they desire, which is often a changeling. This means that it does not need to be a changeling, and can be an object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:40:01-08:00","id":820615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820614#post820614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The preview says that Fae create Huntsmen to bring back something that they desire, which is often a changeling. This means that it does not need to be a changeling, and can be an object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, it'd be pretty silly for a Feud to wind up stalling out because every member had cast all their Titles to Earth in a fit of desperation. Having a reliable retrieval mechanism is invaluable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:40:37-08:00","id":820617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820609#post820609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I don't think I can write something for a section I have no jurisdiction, but I am damn certain I'll get on a book about the Huntsmen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's fair. Just came off weird from that statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T16:11:53-08:00","id":820628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying very hard to understand what is appealing about this, since from where I'm sitting (ie I just read the linked document, no other discussion about it) the Huntsmen seem to border on the game-ruining.<br /> <br /> This thread verges on the 500 posts, though, so I can't really go through it all. Is there some good post someone could link me to explaining why people, uh... like this at all?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> why game ruining ?</div> </div> </div> </div>So a major theme throughout a lot of 'fluff' in 1e Changeling:the Lost was the paranoia about being dragged back to Arcadia, and the repeated motif that all of changeling society was designed to somehow prevent that. Mind you there was absolutely no mechanics support these themes and motifs so they just hung there for ad hoc storyteller implementation through plots, which had no equitable arbitrary systems to single out who was actually at risk, and how the danger manifests.<br /> <br /> 2e Changeling fixes this by defining how changeling society actually provides protection in a real and meaningful way (Courts providing Approaches and Freeholds providing Bulwark rituals). Huntsmen as antagonists are part of defining the paranoia and dangers changelings face. A shapeshifting being trying to drag a specific changeling back to Arcadia with the power to perfectly restrain them and bribe the changeling's associates and enemies with a one-time guaranteed Get-out-of-Arcadia-Free card powerfully expresses why Paranioa is justified in the setting.<br /> <br /> Before there even was mention of 2e being released I had noticed the themes didn't have mechanics to support them so I made some for my homebrew based on the ending of the Changeling the Lost Quickstart Demo. Soon as I saw the Huntsmen, Approaches, Bulwark mechanics I was overjoyed and included them.<br /> <br /> Here is a link to my previous post within this thread on this topic. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=809144#post809144\">Homebrew Huntsmen Limitations</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=808860#post808860\">&quot;Arcadian Hunters&quot; Bane</a><br /> <br /> Please note Huntsmen only have limitations in my homebrew because I apply the same limitations that apply to all supernatural beings in my homebrew to them as well.<br /> <br /> As you can see, Arcadia Hunters Bane takes the idea that changelings need Approaches and Bulwark rituals even further, making freehold and court membership even more an imperative to escape inevitable recapture.<br /> <br /> Also I'd like to point out Chronicles of Darkness is not just a Role Playing Game but is specifically and clearly in the Horror Genre. Huntsmen keeps the feel of suspense, apprehension, along with moments of panic, dread, and terror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-01-2016, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T21:35:16-08:00","id":820728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=812780#post812780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, point of clarification: how fast does the Yearning economy typically flow for a huntsman? At first I thought they'd be spending it kind of slow and careful, but the more I read and chewed (especially them using instead of glamour in oneiro-fuckery) it seems like it might be faster - more like 2E WP or like glamour than something more deliberate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bumping this question cus I think it got lost behind an argument about Mage and it's relevant to discussion of how dangerous Huntsmen are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T21:57:24-08:00","id":820741,"title":"","content":"Depends on tactics and engagement of Approaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T22:08:55-08:00","id":820743,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that would depend on two things: how aggressive and impulsive the Huntsman is, and exactly what the freehold's Approaches are. The harder an Approach is to fulfill, the harder it is to regain Yearning. The more trigger-happy the Huntsman, the faster they'll spend it. Which means that Huntsmen who've survived, who've succeeded before, who are experienced and patient and cunning... aren't going to be burning through their reserves too quick. I'd expect them to sit on it until they burn it all in a burst of power at the end of a Hunt, maybe dole out a bit here and there and take the time to regenerate it before moving onto the next step of their master plan.<br /> <br /> How easy is it to find out an Approach, anyways? If Changelings aren't being trusting, I can't imagine they'd explain it all to someone if they didn't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T22:41:34-08:00","id":820754,"title":"","content":"True Fae and Huntsmen know the rules they have to play by when they look at a changeling. It's as plain to them as the target's hair color or fashion choices for the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T22:51:12-08:00","id":820758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820743#post820743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How easy is it to find out an Approach, anyways? If Changelings aren't being trusting, I can't imagine they'd explain it all to someone if they didn't have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of Approaches is to bait the Huntsmen into coming after you on your terms instead of theirs. Keeping them secret would be pretty counter-productive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:15:35-08:00","id":820799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820758#post820758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of Approaches is to bait the Huntsmen into coming after you on your terms instead of theirs. Keeping them secret would be pretty counter-productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really; I can come up with ideas where forcing the Huntsmen to figure out the terms before actually coming in on them would make sense. Not relevant though, since it'd be off-theme a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:25:40-08:00","id":820804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820799#post820799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really; I can come up with ideas where forcing the Huntsmen to figure out the terms before actually coming in on them would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not the Fae and thus have no need to abide by an Approach.<br /> <br /> Hiding your Approaches means you need to bait the Huntsmen into looking for the bait that makes them come after you under the auspices of your strong suit, which is a bit too circuitous even for fairy plots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T09:29:21-08:00","id":821042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=819424#post819424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't have to change people's minds. He's right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry you misunderstand. I'm not saying that Satchel's not right. I'm saying the other person's not wrong. The sentence being discussed actually entails both things. But we're getting rather off-topic. This is a Changeling thread, not a thread on textual entailment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T10:40:19-08:00","id":821073,"title":"","content":"It seems like we have several discussions in this thread. One is a discussion about Huntsmen, their purpose within and affect upon Chronicles. One discussion is about preferences in themes found within Chronicles and a debate arguments listing strengths of each preference. One discussion about madness and how mental illness is handled in Chronicles of Darkness and how it fits into the themes of 2e Changeling: the Lost. I've just contributed to the discussion about tangent conversations, though I am not the first one in this thread to notice or mention it.<br /> <br /> There are repeating tethers between some conversations, or a clear branching point where it began as part of the original discussion and then became distinct without merging back.<br /> <br /> My question is this:<br /> <br /> Would it be a beneficial, and if so possible, to have these discussions segregated into different threads? If that is beneficial and possible, would it also be possible to have posts that reference the other discussions just have a link pointing there, and would all this be worth the effort?<br /> <br /> This thread is full of great stuff and I am really enjoying what everyone is saying.<br /> <br /> Back to the discussion about Huntsmen<br /> <br /> I don't believe Huntsmen necessarily mean the setting has to be bleak, or have an atmosphere of gloomy desperation. Surely Huntsmen beings the themes of paranoia that was through out the 'fluff' of 1e Changeling: the Lost, to 2e Changeling: the Lost and act as a concrete way to know why there is paranoia. Having themes of paranoia, especially if it is hopeless to fight against would be an exercise of bleakness and generate an atmosphere of gloomy desperation. If you look at both the mechanics and fluff which now more fully reflect each other, that isn't the reaction or purpose of changeling society. In 1e Changeling: the Lost the whole threat of being dragged back to Arcadia was constantly discussed in the fluff and sometimes vaguely alluded to in mechanics like the Fealty task/boon without any clarification or measurement of its effect, or really if it actually has any effect at all in a way the modern characters could have faith in enough to justify pledging loyalty and submitting to being governed in a near feudal system.<br /> <br /> The level of paranoia justified by Huntsmen is about the same always alluded in fluff in 1e Changeling: the Lost. The reaction there was not bleak hopelessness but vigilance and to create a society for protection. Even the Winter court did give into bleak hopelessness and their core emotion was sorrow; they had a reaction of hiding which is not something you'd bother to do if there was no hope. The same is true of the Dusk court even though their emotion was fatalism, they still had hope to have a meaningful struggle which they see as destined to be lost.<br /> <br /> Also 2e Changeling: the Lost compared to 1e Changeling: the Lost the reasons behind joining a court and freehold have actual benefits that help protect them besides &quot;I guess if the True Fae only attacks while we are in a group we have a better chance to fight them off&quot; and &quot;volunteering to be policed without the governing body having any real ability to strike back at the True Fae in retaliation OR protect you while you are out of line of sight&quot;. ei completely ineffective at acting as a deterrent to True Fae snatching someone and can't really protect you the vast majority of the time.<br /> <br /> So, to be more brief:<br /> Huntsmen, Court Approaches, and Freehold Bulwarks make the structure of changeling society make sense and actually protective against a less nebulous threat. Also with the ability for huntsmen to bribe people with Tokens of Reprieve there is a much better reason to require everyone to submitted to being policed by authority. These things together make Changeling society the only plausible source of security and freedom from Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-01-2016, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T11:00:41-08:00","id":821077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821073#post821073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is this:<br /> <br /> Would it be a beneficial, and if so possible, to have these discussions segregated into different threads? If that is beneficial and possible, would it also be possible to have posts that reference the other discussions just have a link pointing there, and would all this be worth the effort?</div> </div> </div> </div>People on this forum have tended to be pretty good about taking conversations to other threads when asked. The Mage stuff, for instance, already got broken out into another thread on the Mage forum.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not surprising that this is the thread that's pulling in a lot of derails. It's the first Huntsmen thread. This is the Huntsmen Chronicle. If nothing else, I'd say that's a good sign because, for better or worse, they clearly <i>matter</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T11:34:48-08:00","id":821094,"title":"","content":"I'll second what Pale Crusader said about the courts. When I was reading the 1e main book, I didn't quite get how the courts offered that much protection, or what the danger of being courtless really was. Having Huntsmen following rules about approaches made the courts much more immediately relevant and understandable to me as a newbie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:16:11-08:00","id":821205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820438#post820438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip<br /> <br /> When you come across a car accident, or worse get in one yourself, it naturally ramps up your fear of crashes again. And that's life until you get to a point where you are capable enough that even when you fear the car crash, you're ready to handle the possibilites. That's Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, I was actually in a car accident last year and this is a super good way to look at the life of the Lost. Thank you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:48:37-08:00","id":821220,"title":"","content":"How Broadly are the effects of a huntsman weapon? are they focused on only hurting targets or they can they be used for more indirect uses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:55:09-08:00","id":821223,"title":"","content":"No changeling wants to be cut by them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:58:16-08:00","id":821226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821205#post821205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, I was actually in a car accident last year and this is a super good way to look at the life of the Lost. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do wonder if the inevitability of the Huntsman turns it from &quot;fear and paranoia of future crashes&quot; to &quot;there's a psycho with a car that is looking to run you down in the street.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:09:56-08:00","id":821235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821226#post821226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do wonder if the inevitability of the Huntsman turns it from &quot;fear and paranoia of future crashes&quot; to &quot;there's a psycho with a car that is looking to run you down in the street.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if your GM has a poor sense of narrative.<br /> <br /> Even then, it's <i>a</i> Huntsman. Through your entire life of driving and fear of crashes and learning how to deal with it, a psycho trying to run you down who's dealt with in the end still only amounts to a small fraction of that life.<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, it doesn't end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:27:07-08:00","id":821246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821226#post821226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do wonder if the inevitability of the Huntsman turns it from &quot;fear and paranoia of future crashes&quot; to &quot;there's a psycho with a car that is looking to run you down in the street.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Huntsmen are the car crash in this metaphor. If there's a psycho trying to force you to have a car crash, it's the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:30:41-08:00","id":821249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821246#post821246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Huntsmen are the car crash in this metaphor. If there's a psycho trying to force you to have a car crash, it's the Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that is not an un-apt description.<br /> <br /> But a good one knows how, where, and when to do it for the narrative. It's not a constant case of pushing the <i>I will never go back</i> button.<br /> <br /> A bad one? Sure, but that's why we have storytelling sections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:36:00-08:00","id":821254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821249#post821249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, that is not an un-apt description.<br /> <br /> But a good one knows how, where, and when to do it for the narrative. It's not a constant case of pushing the <i>I will never go back</i> button.<br /> <br /> A bad one? Sure, but that's why we have storytelling sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was getting at; the Storyteller has the power to relentlessly chase players down and ram Huntsmen into them, or to make Huntsmen a natural thing that can't be completely avoided but can be reduced by safe driving practices. The fact that bad STs can use story elements badly is not the fault of the story elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:38:46-08:00","id":821260,"title":"","content":"I know, but the descriptor of a Storyteller as a psycho trying to run you off the road was too delicious to leave alone but too judgmental to merely touch without clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:44:34-08:00","id":821262,"title":"","content":"Oh, gotcha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:11:10-08:00","id":821279,"title":"","content":"Second edition definitely does a better job of making Courts relevant, but there were pretty good reasons to join one even in first edition. Specifically, Mantle and Court Contracts. Mantle's actual use varied from Court to Court, but generally speaking it gave you pretty good abilities for what it cost. The first dot, and first power, were free, and in at least a few cases at higher Mantle you got access to special powers not available through other channels. <br /> <br /> Court Contracts were typically one of the most potent tools available to characters near the start of the game. Unlike every other Contract, the Court ones usually used Attribute + Skill + Mantle, meaning that even Wyrd 1 and 2 Changelings could potentially get dice pools big enough to work on a Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:58:10-08:00","id":821302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821279#post821279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second edition definitely does a better job of making Courts relevant, but there were pretty good reasons to join one even in first edition. Specifically, Mantle and Court Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point about Mantle and Court contracts. I am very excited to see how this is handled now that Courts are no longer just a simple multiple choice question and now have as many option as there can be imagined background stories of Freeholds. I wonder how the courts contracts will look like for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=804036#post804036\">Courts</a> I designed for Portland Oregon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:03:48-08:00","id":821305,"title":"","content":"Even though the write-up said each Court only gets one contract, I decided to be old-school for mine and have a contract for the concrete expression of the court's theme and one for the emotional aspect. I just really liked that dichotomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:19:58-08:00","id":821315,"title":"","content":"There's still a scaleable Emotional Contract setup for people to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:28:40-08:00","id":821322,"title":"","content":"Oh, well that's convenient. Can't wait to see it, since I wager it's going to be quite relevant. Emotional influence was one of Changeling's big thematic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:45:38-08:00","id":821332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=821305#post821305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though the write-up said each Court only gets one contract, I decided to be old-school for mine and have a contract for the concrete expression of the court's theme and one for the emotional aspect. I just really liked that dichotomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>you're in luck,all courtss have contracts of emotion,its a defatult thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:22:20-08:00","id":822484,"title":"","content":"Will Huntsmen use Wyrd as their Powerstat? They don't have a Glamour pool, but they use Yearning for oneiromancy. If yes, what is the normal Wyrd rating for most of them, and can they increase or decrease their Wyrd? Can they have superhuman stats at Wyrd 6+? They're not combat juggernauts, so they'd probably have 6+ in Wits, Manipulation, Stamina, Investigation, Survival, Stealth, Subterfuge and the like. Are they immune to Contracts and the magic of other splats meant to temporarily suppress their desire to complete the Hunt? You can't do that to G-M Angels, so Huntsmen are probably immune too. It's either Token Of Reprieve or no reprieve.<br /> <br /> Can Huntsmen develop a fondness for certain aspects of the material world despite having a love-hate relationship with their &quot;job&quot;? I like to imagine that whatever hobbies they bother to have are quite weird and benefit from their shape-shifting somehow. That would help making each Huntsman more distinct. What they really want is retirement, but I pity anyone who interferes with their vacations, such as they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:07:57-08:00","id":824360,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Huntsmen need something like the Show Of Power Exploit of Demons to mimic the powers of those they are impersonating and avoid suspicion? Or is that included in their shape-shifting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T11:50:56-08:00","id":824501,"title":"","content":"They're mostly mimicking changelings. They have contracts and all the other stuff, why would they need more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T12:10:31-08:00","id":824512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=824501#post824501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're mostly mimicking changelings. They have contracts and all the other stuff, why would they need more?</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. If a True Fae knows the Huntsman it is creating will infiltrate a Freehold with a significant number of other supernatural types looking out for each other, the Huntsman will probably be given an Arcadian Weapon or just a Token that does the same thing as Show Of Power.<br /> <br /> And the Huntsmen have Contracts? How do they activate them? Can they use certain Approaches as Catches? For example, a Waterborn Elemental has aquatic chases as a personal Approach. The Huntsman sent after said changeling will probably be able to use 2ED equivalents of Control The Elements, Communion With The Elements and Fang And Talon, in addition to its innate powers.<br /> <br /> The more I think about the Huntsmen, the more they seem like awesome material for a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MirrorBoss\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Mirror Boss Fight</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T13:23:31-08:00","id":824551,"title":"","content":"I found time to track down the post you mentioned in the &quot;good guys thread&quot;. Hopefully this isn't just repeating stuff in the pages since.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820117#post820117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My Right for My Crown, My Left for My Dagger-Societal Oaths and Why No One's Going to Ban Tokens of Reprieve.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> On this section, it seems like your point is that the reason the Freehold doesn't just ban all Tokens of Repreve is that changelings want them very badly.<br /> <br /> There's two things I want to raise about that. The first is, a sense of security that the others in your freehold aren't going to betray you is something Changelings want badly but, really, that isn't that important because the second thing is, if nobody wants to ban Tokens of repreve why not just make it a law of the freehold that you can't make deals with the Huntsman instead? Make a second law that anyone who acquires a token of repreve must immediately make a truthful public statement saying how they got it, to stop the Huntsmen using a loyalist intermediary.<br /> <br /> Actually, this would probably run to pages upon pages of legalease, but the point is. You can have your cake and eat it. Tokens of Reprieve aren't evil because they exert a One Ring like aura of corruption. The Tokens are fine, it's betraying other Changelings to the Gentry that's the issue. So if banning Tokens isn't acceptable to the Freehold, ban betrying Changelings to Gentry or their agents.<br /> <br /> Nobody's going to object to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820117#post820117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dude, have you been playing the same game as me?&quot; None of that negates what I said about him, and it's going to stop being about him explicitly after this-but seriously, wut?</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with what you're saying in this section; but at the same time every time I played Changeling, it was the same game Omnicron was playing. What I mean is that I don't see a contradiction.<br /> <br /> You're right, there is no reason to trust anyone without a Pledge. But the thing is, Changelings are very very very good at writing pledges. In a functioning Freehold the Changelings trust each other, not because they are trustworthy people (they're not) but because they're all Pledged to obey a code of laws and Changelings trust in the pledge and in the laws. They've read it, they've checked for loopholes, and they've concluded that it's safe to be sociable with the Freehold.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I think having Freehold laws against dealing with the Huntsmen is a good thing. And the combination of Tokens of Repreve and laws to ban them are thematically perfect. In 1E changelings were untrustworthy mecurial faeries who you shouldn't trust until you've gotten a Pledge and had your lawyers review it. In 2E changelings are untrustworthy mecurial faeries who have a massive incentive to betray you and so you really shouldn't trust them until you've got a Pledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820117#post820117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loyalists and Privateers have always been assumed to infiltrate freeholds and find clever ways to work around and subvert the Wyrd frameworks in order to casually make people disappear. See, the Lost are all inside, and the Loyalists and the Privateers have the advantage of being both inside and outside. This was the default from day one.</div> </div> </div> </div> The only time loyalists came up in one of my games, they were basically an invading army rather than subtle infiltrate.<br /> <br /> The assumption was there, but I could never figure out how they actually do it. I tell you what I would like to see, and that's a write up of a game of Changeling played by an experienced where one player is a Loyalist but the other players don't know who it is.<br /> <br /> I mean, if I was a Freehold Monarch using the 1E rules and I suspected a loyalist or priviateer was in the Freehold I'd get all Changelings into a big hall and make a group pledge that means everyone has to read out a list of questions, and give an truthful answer to each with &quot;yes&quot; or &quot;no&quot;, then give them a list with about a dozen variations of &quot;are you a loyalist, a privateer or a Gentry?&quot;<br /> <br /> I haven't tried to word that without loopholes, in game I would, but basically Changelings have absolutely great tools for rooting out infultration and I just never understood how you'd get around them. Which might be why it never came up in our games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:29:57-08:00","id":824591,"title":"","content":"Oh, Huntsmen do get Contracts? I rescind my objections, I thought they were limited to their Yearning abilities.<br /> <br /> I'm with The Kings Raven on the issue of trust, a well worded Pledge is pretty ironclad. I actually gave my first storyteller headaches in the opposite direction, characters would start in on &quot;How can we trust-&quot; &quot;Because I swear on my true name to tell no lies, now shut up and listen&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:50:59-08:00","id":824606,"title":"","content":"There's some powerful stuff in this thread... I'm only just starting to learn about Changeling: The Lost, but two things cropped into mind immediately for the use of Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> 1) The Huntsman doesn't necessarily need to use violence to bring you back to Arcadia. I could very well see a patient Huntsman doing everything they can to dismantle your life. To sow distrust and betrayal amongst those you called friends and family. To try to take all your accomplishments and ruin them. To try to make having a life outside of Arcadia... pointless. And in that moment where everything you've tried to built is in shambles. When the relationships you created have had their bridges burned. When you can't see if there is anything left for you in this world anymore... That Huntsman can be there, holding their hand out to you and saying, &quot;It will be alright. You don't belong here. There is nothing left for you here anymore and you can finally leave it all behind. Your master misses you. They say it will be different. Come back with me.&quot; That sounds horrifying to me, really. And powerful.<br /> <br /> 2) The Huntsman doesn't necessarily need to be after the PCs to impact the story. The Huntsman can be after an NPC and messing with the Freehold to locate their quarry to bring back. Do the Changelings band together? Do they take the opportunity to gain some Tokens of Reprieve? How does a PC react when they have a Huntsman's attention as a source to their true quarry?<br /> <br /> ...Some very evocative thoughts with that, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T15:01:23-08:00","id":824612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=824606#post824606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some powerful stuff in this thread... I'm only just starting to learn about Changeling: The Lost, but two things cropped into mind immediately for the use of Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> 1) The Huntsman doesn't necessarily need to use violence to bring you back to Arcadia. I could very well see a patient Huntsman doing everything they can to dismantle your life. To sow distrust and betrayal amongst those you called friends and family. To try to take all your accomplishments and ruin them. To try to make having a life outside of Arcadia... pointless. And in that moment where everything you've tried to built is in shambles. When the relationships you created have had their bridges burned. When you can't see if there is anything left for you in this world anymore... That Huntsman can be there, holding their hand out to you and saying, &quot;It will be alright. You don't belong here. There is nothing left for you here anymore and you can finally leave it all behind. Your master misses you. They say it will be different. Come back with me.&quot; That sounds horrifying to me, really. And powerful.<br /> <br /> 2) The Huntsman doesn't necessarily need to be after the PCs to impact the story. The Huntsman can be after an NPC and messing with the Freehold to locate their quarry to bring back. Do the Changelings band together? Do they take the opportunity to gain some Tokens of Reprieve? How does a PC react when they have a Huntsman's attention as a source to their true quarry?<br /> <br /> ...Some very evocative thoughts with that, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T15:31:19-08:00","id":824629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=824551#post824551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if I was a Freehold Monarch using the 1E rules and I suspected a loyalist or priviateer was in the Freehold I'd get all Changelings into a big hall and make a group pledge that means everyone has to read out a list of questions, and give an truthful answer to each with &quot;yes&quot; or &quot;no&quot;, then give them a list with about a dozen variations of &quot;are you a loyalist, a privateer or a Gentry?&quot;<br /> <br /> I haven't tried to word that without loopholes, in game I would, but basically Changelings have absolutely great tools for rooting out infultration and I just never understood how you'd get around them. Which might be why it never came up in our games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think literally the only reason in the games I played where it worked was because people changed allegiances over time due to plot, or they literally did not have enough Wyrd to hold any more binding pledges.<br /> <br /> A paraphrased example of &quot;I swear to (character) that I am not a willing agent of the Gentry&quot; or whatever was really common and foolproof enough for the social contract of the players.<br /> <br /> It was much more common that working with Loyalists was more of a poisoned chalice, in that you knew it was a bad idea, but they were often the safest way out of what was an otherwise intractable situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 02-05-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:10:37-08:00","id":824648,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the consequences for breaking a Pledge are not <i>so</i> severe that no one would ever break one. They can be quite harsh, and no doubt they are a very powerful tool that gives the Lost a much-needed sense of security. But even a flawlessly worded contract is only as strong as the punishment for breaking it; a desperate enough Changeling may still be tempted, and a cautious enough changeling may still be paranoid. It's a question of what price are you willing to pay for security, and do you know what price the next guy would pay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:27:29-08:00","id":824660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=824648#post824648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the consequences for breaking a Pledge are not <i>so</i> severe that no one would ever break one. They can be quite harsh, and no doubt they are a very powerful tool that gives the Lost a much-needed sense of security. But even a flawlessly worded contract is only as strong as the punishment for breaking it; a desperate enough Changeling may still be tempted, and a cautious enough changeling may still be paranoid. It's a question of what price are you willing to pay for security, and do you know what price the next guy would pay?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was never the problem (and it has happened in our game before) - it's the very fact that Changelings could make supernaturally binding pledges in the first place. The very act of breaking one of those &quot;loyalty' pledges would usually do all of the work - either the pledge would bind and therefore you had an assurance, or they would refuse/break it and you knew that the target was untrustworthy. Beyond that point it didn't matter, it just makes the type of infiltration stories where someone infiltrates the court for months and there's a bunch of intrigue incredibly difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T22:39:55-08:00","id":824832,"title":"","content":"Whoops! Went and checked, and I did not find Contracts in the Huntsmens writeup. That might be one of those things that is supposed to be in there that's missing, like the time limit, because I seem to recall someone saying something about it. But in the meantime, I'm going to assume I was wrong and that they don't have Contracts.<br /> <br /> There's some bullshit that needs addressing here, but I don't have a tolerance for bullshit right now. Later, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T14:30:30-08:00","id":825100,"title":"","content":"I think a Freehold Law or Pledge against dealing with Huntsmen would do the opposite of actually mitigating or dealing with the conflict of interest. It would exacerbate it. In the moment of truth, it would divide changelings even more between survival and loyalty to their companions. Faced with a deal by a Huntsmen in a position of weakness, they have no options. A Huntsman would not just leave a refusal be, but accepting a Token means breaking a promise on the Wyrd and marking yourself as a traitor.<br /> <br /> So congrats, you've managed to put the entire Freehold consistently on edge about getting caught in the crossfire between Huntsmen and their quarry - which as previous discussion and examples have established is not going to be rare, because they have methods more complex than &quot;beeline for the quarry&quot;. From where I stand, the set up will see it fracture under the pressure.<br /> <br /> Changelings want Tokens. None want to be the person who accepts one, but they know that in their place they would do the same. There is no confidence to be gained from a pledge bound law to not negotiate with Huntsmen for tokens. Just the assurance that the freehold is liable to break apart because people are inevitably going to do it driven by <i>never going back</i>.<br /> <br /> That's assuming that a ruler would actually manage to implement it and it wouldn't get shut down by an at best lukewarm response of silent opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-06-2016, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:01:27-08:00","id":825109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825100#post825100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So congrats, you've managed to put the entire Freehold consistently on edge about getting caught in the crossfire between Huntsmen and their quarry - which as previous discussion and examples have established is not going to be rare, because they have methods more complex than &quot;beeline for the quarry&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsmen themselves will be rare though. Unless we're talking about the Freehold of a very large city (New York, London, Paris, etc.), Huntsmen are basically natural disasters. They don't happen often, but when they do, they just <i>change</i> things. Once a Huntsman sweeps in, nothing will ever be the same anymore.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd wager that these sorts of Pledges would be doable in small Freeholds where Huntsmen are genuinely exceedingly rare. And then, the Pledge wouldn't really break anything because the sheer <i>shock </i>of facing a Huntsman is likely to shake a changeling to the core, creating delicious drama when it comes to whether they should accept the Token and break the Pledge or risk that maybe there are more Huntsmen coming. Or hell, maybe <i>this</i> Huntsman takes you too if you refuse his offer. In a small Freehold, such a Pledge would make sense and would still be hella broken when the Huntsmen came, but since the Huntsmen are so rare, it'd still see use.<br /> <br /> In a large city where Huntsman are about as common as major building fires, there wouldn't be such a Pledge because of the sheer amount of commerce surrounding Tokens of Reprieve. However, a higher frequency of Huntsmen would mean a much more prepared Freehold. Not necessarily more paranoid or less cohesive, I'd say, but certainly more deadly. I'd wager those Freeholds would have obscure Entitlements specifically designed to counter the Huntsman's pernicious influence in Lost society, from wise Viziers to strong Victors to crafty Black Apples. In large cities, I'd wager low-Wyrd changelings would be generally very safe from the Huntsmen, whose attentions would be focused on the high-Wyrd heroes of the Freehold. In small towns and the like, a low population means that everyone is a fair target.<br /> <br /> So I'd say that in large cities, + Huntsman Frequency, - Danger for the Average Changeling, and viceversa for small towns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:02:04-08:00","id":825110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825100#post825100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Freehold Law or Pledge against dealing with Huntsmen would do the opposite of actually mitigating or dealing with the conflict of interest. It would exacerbate it. In the moment of truth, it would divide changelings even more between survival and loyalty to their companions. Faced with a deal by a Huntsmen in a position of weakness, they have no options. A Huntsman would not just leave a refusal be, but accepting a Token means breaking a promise on the Wyrd and marking yourself as a traitor.<br /> <br /> So congrats, you've managed to put the entire Freehold consistently on edge about getting caught in the crossfire between Huntsmen and their quarry - which as previous discussion and examples have established is not going to be rare, because they have methods more complex than &quot;beeline for the quarry&quot;. From where I stand, the set up will see it fracture under the pressure.<br /> <br /> Changelings want Tokens. None want to be the person who accepts one, but they know that in their place they would do the same. There is no confidence to be gained from a pledge bound law to not negotiate with Huntsmen for tokens. Just the assurance that the freehold is liable to break apart because people are inevitably going to do it driven by <i>never going back</i>.<br /> <br /> That's assuming that a ruler would actually manage to implement it and it wouldn't get shut down by an at best lukewarm response of silent opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're correct about what the result would be. But I can still see an influential leader campaigning for such a pledge to say Changelings won't accept tokens from Huntsmen. Think of it, would you want to be the one to speak up and say, &quot;Hey, this is a stupid pledge for us to make!&quot; doesn't that single you out as a Changeling that <i>would </i>deal with a Huntsman for a token? The peer pressure would be immense because no one wants to admit that! And why wouldn't someone influential and trying to be in charge try and force something like that through?<br /> <br /> And it would all end up burning in flames.<br /> <br /> ...I'm good with this. Chronicles of Darkness are stories of conflict and drama. This sounds like an excellent source for both, and people constantly make sub-optimal decisions all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:05:37-08:00","id":825111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=824606#post824606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The Huntsman doesn't necessarily need to be after the PCs to impact the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=824648#post824648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the consequences for breaking a Pledge are not <i>so</i> severe that no one would ever break one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically this is true, but thematically. These are faeries; in 90%+ of faeries stories I've read faeries are literally incapable of breaking a promise. I'm hoping that 2E ups the consiquences; or at least creates an Oathbreaker Condition that means every changeling can instantly tell who's broken a Pledge and thus shun them.<br /> <br /> At the very least, if someone breaks a Pledge with <i>you</i> a Changeling is instantly aware, so &quot;I pledge to tell the truth. I am not a loyalist&quot; will still work. Actually, come to think about it, a Courtly Emblem Oath sort of does this in 1E. If by Freehold law every Changeling may only use a Courtly Oath for a specific Pledge like &quot;don't aid the Gentry or their servents&quot; then every Changeling who notices another Changeling who broke it would know not only have they lost favour with the Court, they've sided the Gentry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825100#post825100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So congrats, you've managed to put the entire Freehold consistently on edge about getting caught in the crossfire between Huntsmen and their quarry - which as previous discussion and examples have established is not going to be rare, because they have methods more complex than &quot;beeline for the quarry&quot;. From where I stand, the set up will see it fracture under the pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, that's a feature not a bug.<br /> <br /> Firstly it means that Changelings are going to put even more effort into not getting caught between a Huntsman and their quarry. Secondly it means that if a Changeling does get caught then they can't offer much help to the Huntsmen because they're banded an oathbreaker and all the other Changelings will avoid them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember. The default state is that the entire freehold is on edge that their fellow Changelings will betray them for a shiny Token of repreve. Making Changeings on edge about the Huntsmen instead is a massive improvement over the default.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:20:52-08:00","id":825121,"title":"","content":"I would equate the Others more to natural disasters than the Huntsmen, who precisely because of everything they represent can be extremely personal (but then, so can Fetches and Gentry) and bring calamity on an individual level which has repercussions on the social groups of Changelings. Yes, maybe it's actually doable in some circumstances. It's a situation with a lot of sides to it, and a lot of potential. And it absolutely would make a fantastic source of drama; you could make some very interesting stories just out of the suggestion itself.<br /> <br /> What I really wanted to get at is that it's not a universal answer, it's not an ironclad solution, and it's <i>not</i> having your cake and eating it. Never. It's a method that might help, that might bring a degree of security, but it comes with its flaws and with its own conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T19:09:23-08:00","id":825193,"title":"","content":"Okay, so because there's always people who don't get the point(and it's often consistently the same people), we'll try going at this in a less flowery way.<br /> <br /> Simply put, changelings are both <i>paranoid</i> and <i>opportunistic</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not an uncommon pairing. Fairies often <i>aren't</i> regular features in the lives of characters we follow in stories, they often keep to themselves. But, when you get in touch with them, they like to take the window and get something out of it. Changelings, broadly speaking, play this too a tee. On the one hand, no one wants to stick their neck out too far. Even Summer preferred to not stick their neck completely out-they might go to war, but they preferred guerilla tactics. On the other hand, when encounters happen, they often try to score something out of it, if for no other reason that it gives them an edge in the future. With this in mind, let's go through and point out some problems with the &quot;We'll just keep the Huntsmen from ever being a problem!&quot; mentality.<br /> <br /> <b>1) &quot;Just Don't bargain with the Huntsmen!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, no.<br /> <br /> For a second, let's ignore the fact that Tokens of Reprieve are commodity that people want, regardless of the consequences, and hit instead on a much larger issue- the condemnation of anyone who fails to beat the Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> Again, people seem to think that the Huntsmen coming as an invading army, willing to challenge the mass. They aren't. They don't hit the crab's shell, they strike for the joints. They go after their target through cleverness, cunning, and exploitation. If they can't get their target, they go after someone weaker. The Huntsmen are not above grabbing a newly returned Changeling, dragging them back to the gates, and then giving them an ultimatum-take the bittersweet deal or die/go back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> And what are you supposed to do in those cases? You're clearly outclassed, and you have <i>I will never go back</i> pounding away at your being. Are you supposed to just give up and sacrifice yourself for the greater good? Sure, maybe, but the Lost are going to lose a lot of people to that. If you take the bargain, you stand a chance of finding a window between your betrayal and their return to make it all right, you might tell yourself if you're noble. But in all honesty, you're probably not. You're scared out of your self, you're falling into the hopelessness of the scenario, and even if the devil is offering a hand up, why would you reject it when the alternative is hell?<br /> <br /> But nooooooooooooooooooooo, some people out there want everyone to sacrifice for the greater good whether they want to or not. Any changeling in a freehold with a Societal Oath saying &quot;Don't ever make bargains with the Huntsmen&quot; are <i>fucked</i>. Any changeling who gets stuck in that scenario is gonna have to either die or go back to hell, and the Huntsmen will exploit this to shit. They'll send little public messages, hanging from nooses off the Ruler's house, little boxes in the talkative ones' houses with fingers and ears, and little messages that simply state &quot;If only they had another choice&quot;. A Huntsman'll ramp that shit up until people are clamoring for the Ruler's heads. They might not make a deal, but if a Huntsman show up and says &quot;I want your King&quot;, they might just sit by and let him do it.<br /> <br /> And in that moment, man oh man, won't a Ruler wish there were some Repreives in circulation then.<br /> <br /> Which brings me back to my original point. Everyone wants one, no one wants to earn it. A Huntsman coming is a terrible thing, but it's also an opportunity. Arcadians aren't the only ones who scheme and machinate, changelings are just as guilty as that as anyone. By not having said clause, you create an opening for, at best, saving graces for future tragedies and, at worst, you cover your own ass when the Huntsmen come for you. You don't have it for <i>anything</i> if you close the doors.<br /> <br /> But hey, let's ignore that for a second, and say that you have them coming in somehow, but you still want to control the way people get it. This brings me to....<br /> <br /> <b>2) &quot;Check In Your Token of Reprieve at the Door!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Fucking hell, the possible logistics of this in a freehold give me a headache. But before we talk about logistics, let's return to a very, <i>very </i>simple fact of changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>NO CHANGELING WANTS A TARGET ON THEIR BACK!</b><br /> <br /> LEt me emphasize a certain part so people get the idea.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>NO CHANGELING</i></u> WANTS A TARGET ON THEIR BACK!</b><br /> <br /> To illustrate the problem, let's assume a changeling bought a Token of Reprieve at a Goblin Market, about as honest as a way to get is they can. That changeling <i>now</i> has to go and inform at least one person(this ties into the logistical problem) that they have a Token of Reprieve. Which, you know, is a hot commodity people are more than willing to get their hands on. So, now, our changeling her is outed that he has a Get Out of Jail Free card, and they have to live with the attention of that fact. On the immediate side, the changeling can expect to be robbed, blackmailed, threatened, and/or generally have people to trying to spirit said Reprieve away. But, fine, let's assume that people aren't going to do that, because then they need to tell one person how they got it, and that can get them in trouble(Ignoring the thousand and one ways this can be subverted, because logistics is a bitch). You still have people trying to bargain, flatter, seduce, reason,hassle, and generally doing what they can to get you to part with it with no small amount of frequency. And that entire time, you, a paranoid creature trying to hide, are just attracting more and more attention. Guess who's getting targeted. Fuck, even if not all of that, when shit hits the fan, our changeling is still the &quot;Break Glass In Case of Emergency&quot; chick, and if she isn't willing to play ball, a bullet might be deemed excusable.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>NO CHANGELING WANTS A TARGET ON THEIR BACK!</i></u></b><br /> <br /> And that's what this basic system, however you incarnate it. Whether you tell it to a private official or the whole of the freehold, it's a target on your back, and for creatures like changelings, that sort of thing is going <i>fuck</i> with their Clarity, at the least. It makes lives miserable, and if life is miserable, why the fuck bother coming back?<br /> <br /> Oh, speaking of, let's talk logistics, because fuck man, legalese.<br /> <br /> First off, an acknowledgment-yes, Changelings are masters of legalese. they are <i>all</i> about clause after clause <i>after clause</i> of minutia and details and filling holes.<br /> <br /> Except when it cuts them off. See, <i>every changeling</i>(let me say that again, <b><u><i>EVERY CHANGELING</i></u></b>) wants rooms to wiggle out of. Everyone wants an <i>escape</i>, because they understand the dangers of restriction. Changelings are forever in a catch-22 so long as they are paranoid to such a degree as to need massive legal documents to keep themselves safe, because every wall they set up is a wal that potentially imprisons them again. They can either be naked but free or secure but chained. Most freeholds struggle <i>deeply</i> with finding the right balance of this, because changeling will react <i>violently</i> to not feeling safe enough <i>and</i> to feeling too bound up.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, changelings could just wall this up with harshness upon harshness upon harshness-but they aren't going to, because that makes them fucking uncomfortable as hell.<br /> <br /> So, logistics. The various incarnations of &quot;Announce to the public&quot; all kind of suck. For starters, let's assume you just have to tell a official of the freehold who has the jurisdiction to hear such things. Well, okay. What happens if we're out in the Hedge, I get one, and I tell the guy and shoot him afterwards to keep my secret, lying to the court about what happened? Nothing, the system is pointless. But, okay, they have provisions against that. That means you still have one person who knows your secret alone, although he might be obliged to tell the other officials about it. That takes times and creates windows for exploitation easily enough, and in the mean time, that one guy has power over you, even if pledges keep him from being horrible about it. Hell, nothing says people have to believe him when you tell him you got it at Market-he might say it with complete sincerity, and the community will still feel paranoid just because it fucking exists. And if he doesn't have to say anything, there's some many ways to take advantage of him before he takes advantage of you. So, to avoid those pitfalls, what, you have to tell a lot of people? What, do you have to get a number of people? What do you do in the meantime? What if you can't get a number together in time? can you just tell your con-conspirators that you have it? Or do you have to tell the whole damn freehold? Does this mean the freehold has to gather every night a Huntsman is in town just to hear &quot;Hey guys, I must solemnly and sincerely tell you I got my Reprieve from the Market?&quot;, all the while giving your enemies a nice shot to gather you up?<br /> <br /> The instant you make a law that says Reprieves must be made public, you open a fucking Pandora's Box of exposure and manipulation, a problem that can't happen as much if people just keep their damn mouths shut about it. It's might <i>feel</i> safer to make it public, but if freeholds already run a risk of being a den of vipers biting at each other, these sorts of rules fucking just accept it as a loss. And in the end, it's not that useful, because....<br /> <br /> <b>3) &quot;I can trust who I'm talking to!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> It's funny, to me, how what you say is what keeps society glued together as changelings, considering that who you look like is never consistent anyways.<br /> <br /> Like, is this a me thing? Am I the only one who grew up with fairy tales where the constant theme, the major motif, was &quot;Nothing is as it seems?&quot; Did I just grow up with more tricksters than anyone else here? I don't think I am. For the record, this point might be exaggerated a little, but still, it must be made.<br /> <br /> The point here is that fairies are all about illusion and dream. It's less prevalent in Second Edition, but I must reiterate again- <i>The Contracts of Smoke and Mirror were assumed to be affinity powers for all changelings</i>.<br /> <br /> Why is no one really in terror of that fact? Why does no one feel scared about it? Because just because it's easy to get doesn't ,mean everyone has, of course. But still!<br /> <br /> STILL!<br /> <br /> That's scary as fuck!<br /> <br /> Because you can walk the fuck into anywhere, say something totally untrue, and people will believe you, because you're bound by pledges to say certain things!<br /> <br /> <b>AND THAT YOU WAS NEVER YOU!!</b><br /> <br /> It gets doubly scary in the scenarios put forth by people who are wrong here, because it encourages a subversive system that invites people to make friends with people who can easily change their shape and lie for them-ie, people outside of the freehold system, who are <i>less </i>trustworthy than the freehold. But that's what happens, this scenario invites changelings to find ways to cheat their defenses for their own freedom, and the Huntsmen and the Loyalists lick their lips and love every fucking second of it, because the system is so rigid that a lie can really break everything down. A Huntsmen just has to walk in as someone else while they aren't there, say &quot;Hey, I fucking sold out someone to the Huntsmen for a token&quot; ,disappear cackling, and that person is going to be in deep shit, because, what they found a way to flaunt the pledge just to piss people off?<br /> <br /> And that's one of several nightmare scenarios! In a group of creatures who are already skittish and mercurial, trying to stamp down and keep them penned up just pushes the subterfuge card even more! And the more personally restrictive it is, the more people are going to rely on their bug-out kits being held by people in <i>not in the freehold</i>. You encourage the game of faces by being the fucking Panopticon! It's just-changelings are inherently slippery, illusory, deceptive creatures. That's how they live! That's how they survive!<br /> <br /> It doesn't fucking help, because it immediately pressures any changeling who has a bad day into a much bigger compromise than they would have been on their own. Of course, we can get all third Reich with this and-Hey, not a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <b>4) &quot;Are you a Loyalist or not?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> The following spoiler is only tangentially related. In fact, let's just say it's not, but I enjoy my excuses anyways.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m1bLXk6UVts\" data-code=\"m1bLXk6UVts\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/m1bLXk6UVts/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> HAHAHAHAHHAHAHAHA-huuuuuuuuuh, whew, that was...that was stupid. Well, okay, no the video is funny enough, but it sort of hits on the humor of the &quot;Are you a Loyalist or now?&quot;, because like every other binding, blinding, suffocating lightblub surveillance trick here, it's not sane.<br /> <br /> The simple fact is that while this might root out some loyalists, what this does fundamentally is just create a cloud of paranoia that unsettles the freeholders into a constant state of distrust, which is easily exploitable, and gives the Huntsmen and Loyalists room to just slip on through, because said pledges don't affect them anyways. This inquisition mindset will do much the same as any of the other suggestions and cause changelings to stop relying on the freehold and instead start making clever deals outside of the freehold. I don't want to waste any more time on this. I wanna make one other quick point, and then I'm going to actually <i>answer</i> this entire damn mindset.<br /> <br /> <b>$@#%!) &quot;The Loyalists are invaders from the outside, not infiltrators!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> Wut.<br /> <br /> It's abundantly clear, by now, that this idea doesn't truck with me, because the way changelings will work with these Pledge ideas, let alone Loyalists and Huntsmen, leads to a total break down. But I've harped on that enough, it's time I questioned the mentality this comes in.<br /> <br /> Asides from it <i>just not fucking making sense logically</i>, I have to wonder where people thinks this fits into the scheme of things in Changeling the Lost, or even the larger Chronicles of Darkness. This game rarely favors barbarians at the gate, and often it's just a setup for the larger problems of the infilitrators on the inside. It's never about just the brute and the brawler, it's often far more about the sneaks and the connivers.<br /> <br /> I mean, stop for a second and think about how most people handle werewolves-hell, even how the World of Darkness handles werewolves in Apocalypse. Big bruisers, death machines, loud, noisy, blunt. They're mauls.<br /> <br /> But Chronicle's werewolves? They're <i>scapels</i>. They are dangerously sneaky, clever, and exact. They still have some brute possibility, but for the most part, their hunt is a thing of guerilla tactics and precision moments. They are subtle knives.<br /> <br /> And that's <i>fucking werewolves</i>, one of the most commonly loud and noisy creatures in the supernatural genre. Fairies are gonna be <i>damnably</i> conniving.<br /> <br /> it's fun to have Loyalists at the gate. It is! I often do use them this way, I've said as much. But the point of having <i>anything</i> at the gate is to give the Loyalists on the inside some room to move and change things. Loyalists( and Huntsmen) are always going to slip their way into the cracks at the joints, they're never going to actually handle the walls. They slip in and they cause chaos and havoc.<br /> <br /> So, enough of this, it's time for...<br /> <br /> <b>5)&quot;Okay, So HOW is this supposed to work?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> &quot;But Arc,&quot; I say to myself in a different voice for entertainment value, &quot; Pledges are supposed to the be glue for changeling society! If all these ideas suck so hard, why would any changeling bother using Pledges at all to make their society secure? I argue that you're fundamentally wrong on this basis!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well,&quot; I respond to myself in my normal voice, &quot;that would be true if I was telling myself that the basis we're approaching Pledges as was correct. But the biggest problem we have right now is an understanding of just what, metaphorically, Pledges are in a changeling society.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then I drop the act, because I don't have hand puppets to make this fun. But still, there's a fundamental point here that needs to be addressed, the principle on which these ideas <i>fail</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>PLEDGES ARE NOT WALLS.</i></u></b><br /> <br /> They aren't walls or curtains or inquisitions that you can use to keep out the enemy. That's not what Pledges, as a basic function of the Wyrd, do, it's not even how they act. The Wyrd is a connective force, it bridges one thing to another thing. It's <i>not </i>a wall. Pledges are string and ribbon, or maybe in their strongest iconography, chains. They bind people together.<br /> <br /> How does that matter? Well, let's get down to it. Are the ideas presented here viable in any way? And I answer, yes! And you ask, How, Mister Pedantic?<br /> <br /> Easy, I say.<br /> <br /> Stop playing at the macro-level and apply it to the micro-level.<br /> <br /> Scoietal Oaths acting as impositions have to cover too much and just foster resentment and distrust. But at the motley level? With people you trust and care about, or at least really want to? Here, it's a lot more effective, because it's tight knit, personal, fueled by trust rather than paranoia. It's not someone infringing on anyone, it's each person keeping each other safe, it's their idea and their bindings.<br /> <br /> Freeholds don't build walls. Societal Oaths <i>can't</i> be walls. What Societal Oaths do is provide a framework, a loom, from which Personal Oaths stretch out to wrap around. Freeholds build little clusters of safety, then daisy chain them back and forth within the framework as motleys and function groups tie together inevitably, until there's this strong, but flexible net of security the unites everyone together and builds genuine camaraderie far more easily than the tyrannical methods impositions from on high.<br /> <br /> These ideas at the Motley level fill in the cracks and is harder to fool because there's a higher level of knowledge of others that backs that trust up-loyalists and Huntsmen aren't demons, and are much more likely to crack under the eyes of their 'mates' than those of the freehold. It means there's less logistics, because motleys govern those details themselves. These ideas, an expression of respecting borders, menas there's less pushing and greed and envy and general backstabbing.<br /> <br /> Now, I know what I'm thinking you're thinking. &quot;But Arc, you can't make every group try to do that shit, anymore than you can make it work on the large scale!&quot;<br /> <br /> Not wrong, and here's where the officials of a freehold have to trust their citizens-but the odds are in their favor. The odds of a motley being willing to tightly bind themselves to one another is pretty high, and from there, it's just working to get motleys to build up trust and faith in each other, which is still easier than getting them to trust a gargantuan force like the freehold system or the freehold mob. It's chainmail, not plate.<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion</b><br /> <br /> Look, I'll be honest and blunt, because apparently that works. These ideas, forced at a freehold level, are stupid. Really, <i>really</i> stupid. Changelings as a whole just won't work with it, because it's too much, it's too <i>G</i><i>entry-esque. </i>Sure, on the motley level, it's a lot more likely to happen, and from there you just have to network one motley to another until you have a solid enough wall. That has it's own risks, but it's a lot more likely to happen and stand. But as a freehold wide imposition?<br /> <br /> No. It's stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T20:15:06-08:00","id":825221,"title":"","content":"Thank you <i>so much</i> for answering that topic in such a blunt way Arc, because there was more I wanted to say but couldn't find the words to, and you said significantly more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T20:20:27-08:00","id":825226,"title":"","content":"I just got a fresh shipment of likes, and Arc has once again taken all of them. Yes, all of them.<br /> <br /> An additional aspect that comes to mind with manipulating things is that if there's one standard pledge, it's going to be easy to figure out the loopholes in it. If Motleys do different variations of their pledges to each other, you can't break the freehold by exploiting the same loophole repeatedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:51:39-08:00","id":825260,"title":"","content":"Over five years of changeling with multiple different, independent groups that have come to the same conclusions is badwrongfun, got it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:55:23-08:00","id":825262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825260#post825260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">badwrongfun</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not interested in participating in a discussion, message received.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:01:51-08:00","id":825266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825262#post825262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not interested in participating in a discussion, message received.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any more, definitely. I'll just stew in my juices or whatever and read whatever shows up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:16:45-08:00","id":825273,"title":"","content":"It's not badwrongfun. It's not like I haven't had some of these assumptions myself.<br /> <br /> BUT it's important that these assumptions are fan assumptions and not subject to what the text has said. A lot of what I've said is true for First Edition-it's all there in the text of the core and expanded on in the supplements. Second Edition has been built on that foundation. If people aren't understanding why something works because of a failure to appreciate what the long-standing design pointed out in the text was doing, someone has to point out what the 'canon' point of departure.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, Let me drop the freelance writer title for a second and just simply say &quot;No, this sort of attitude doesn't make sense to me.&quot; Despite seeing how things have built up, really, it's just that. If I was a player in these scenarios, I couldn't invest in them. It breaks my suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> If other people can see how that works, great? I guess? Until they can't see how something is supposed to work. I enjoy the Huntsmen, and as a player I would want to go against one as a player. But people probably wouldn't use them, because their vision doesn't give the Huntsmen the base assumptions they need to work, and so I, as a player, would always be left wanting at that table.<br /> <br /> You can't expect me to listen to you all say &quot;The Huntsmen don't work&quot; when it's clear that crucial facts about the game seemingly got missed by you all. This is why I have made such a clear point of going back to the core basics that Changeling works on. You can go back to having fun with the wrong way after that, but I'm going to have my say all the same.<br /> <br /> If anything, I'm trying to keep people from severing fun with bad logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T02:00:49-08:00","id":825321,"title":"","content":"I genuinely don't see why people would want to avoid the Huntsmen. Like, I get it if you don't want to use them. But if you are going to use them, it makes no sense to try and &quot;gotcha&quot; the Huntsmen. You can't &quot;gotcha&quot; a creature that is literally made of Arcadia and True Fae. You can *defeat* it, sure, and you can escape its Grasp, but you can't just pre-emptively deny it what it's meant to do. And Changelings know this! They have Fate and Narrative in their blood! They know how the story is supposed to go!<br /> <br /> Trying to deny the Huntsmen the use of their strengths before they even show up is such a... *human* thing to do. It's just not how stories go.<br /> <br /> Now, what can a smart Freehold do against the Huntsmen? Prepare. Keep an ear in the news for murders. Document all Huntsmen tells they know of and have everyone memorise them. Learn and document as much as they can about Huntsmen in general and teach it freely. Cold iron, always keep some in the Freehold somewhere. Magic, use whatever magic you have to add to your state of preparedness. Develop quirks, things that might make the Huntsmen harder to imitate you, something that might also help cement your clarity. Delve into Hedge lore and develop Entitlements to help you and the Freehold.<br /> <br /> You can't weasel your way out of a story. But you can be genre savvy and prepared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T02:42:03-08:00","id":825330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825321#post825321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, what can a smart Freehold do against the Huntsmen? Prepare. Keep an ear in the news for murders. Document all Huntsmen tells they know of and have everyone memorise them. Learn and document as much as they can about Huntsmen in general and teach it freely. Cold iron, always keep some in the Freehold somewhere. Magic, use whatever magic you have to add to your state of preparedness. Develop quirks, things that might make the Huntsmen harder to imitate you, something that might also help cement your clarity. Delve into Hedge lore and develop Entitlements to help you and the Freehold.<br /> <br /> You can't weasel your way out of a story. But you can be genre savvy and prepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>You pretty much summarized what I envisioned as Ziggy's role as Sorcerer of the Autumn Court, right there. He keeps a record of known Gentry and Huntsmen, their individual quirks, frailties and such, studies lore to recognize other Gentry, and he's always on the lookout for new contracts the freehold can use against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T03:38:09-08:00","id":825342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Huntsmen are not above grabbing a newly returned Changeling, dragging them back to the gates, and then giving them an ultimatum-take the bittersweet deal or die/go back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> And what are you supposed to do in those cases? You're clearly outclassed, and you have <i>I will never go back</i> pounding away at your being. Are you supposed to just give up and sacrifice yourself for the greater good?</div> </div> </div> </div> Arc, I think this makes it clear that you fundamentally miss the point of why laws to ban dealing with the Huntsmen would exist.<br /> <br /> Of course they screw over that guy. The entire point of the law is to explicitly screw over that guy. You know they porobably won't sacrafice themself, so the Freehold sacrafices them first. It's like cutting out a cancer, it absolutely sucks if you're the cancer, but it's great if you're the cell next to the cancer because you're not getting infected.<br /> <br /> And it does give you other options, in fact it gives you a lot more options than it takes away. Those options are every other Changeling in the Freehold. If a Huntsman is after you, or if a Huntsman is trying to use you to go after some other Changeling - you can go to any other Changeling in the Freehold and because of that law you know they won't take this oppotunity to side with the Huntsmen for a Token.<br /> <br /> <br /> A strong united freehold that works togeather to protect each other from the Huntsmen is a far better solution than some Changeling making a deal, then trying to set it right before it's too late. Laws against bargains with the Huntsmen keep the freehold strong and united, by ruthlessly cutting out any members who threaten that unity; it sucks if you're the guy who gets cut out but you're outvoted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except when it cuts them off. See, <i>every changeling</i>(let me say that again, <b><u><i>EVERY CHANGELING</i></u></b>) wants rooms to wiggle out of. Everyone wants an <i>escape</i>, because they understand the dangers of restriction.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, but every Changeling also wants the other guy's side of the deal to be iron clad, they're fundamentally unfair like that.<br /> <br /> But this isn't an argument against laws banning deals with the Huntsmen; this is an argument for Changelings to make a bad decision not to ban dealing with the Hunstmen.<br /> <br /> Which is a perfectly reasonable thing to do. Vampires could solve most of their problems (except bordom) if they stopped backstabbing and allocated resources fairly but they don't. Heck you could say the same about humans. So why not say that Changelings have the same problem?<br /> <br /> But the difference between Changelings and Vampires is that Changelings have a really simple mechanical solution to some of their biggest problems, and you're telling players they shouldn't use it. Heck, back when we were talking about Courts I proposed the Flower Courts who have a mortal Monarch who's effective precisely because they're don't have Changeling's psychological issues - what stops them from enacting the law? And if the Changelings don't like it, tough, their Bulwark is powered by obedience to the human monarch.<br /> <br /> You know that a lot of players are going to end up using it, and if the books don't acknowlege that then you're neglecting those players. You're not giving them the storytelling advice they should have to say what do you do after the Changelings enact those laws. The Huntsmen leave signs saying, &quot;wouldn't it be better if you had more options&quot;. Well that's the start of the story, not the end. The Queen isn't just going to sit there and wait for the Huntsmen to sow dissent.<br /> <br /> What happens next. Does the Queen create a full time anti-Huntsman guard? Do they have a string of victories that prevent the Huntsmen fermenting rebellion or do they fail? Does a powerful sorcerer protest loudly against the Laws, renounce his Court, and a dozen Tokens of Repreve are found in his Chambers afterwords, how does that affect the Freeholds views? <br /> <br /> What happens if Pledging to obey the sacred laws laid down by the first Freehold Monarch was part of the Bulwark ritual and those laws ban deals with the Huntsmen or require some kind of Token of Repereve registry. Assuming the Freehold doesn't collapse, how do the Changelings make it work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, is this a me thing? Am I the only one who grew up with fairy tales where the constant theme, the major motif, was &quot;Nothing is as it seems?&quot; Did I just grow up with more tricksters than anyone else here? I don't think I am. For the record, this point might be exaggerated a little, but still, it must be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know something. I honestly do think you're the only one who grew up with that, because I can think of lots of faerie tales that weren't like that.<br /> <br /> Take <a href=\"http://www.pitt.edu/~dash/grimm014.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Three Spinning Women</a> as an example. A girl makes a deal with faeries, she upholds her end of the deal and lives happily ever after. Or heck, take <a href=\"http://www.mordent.com/folktales/grimms/rumplestiltskin/\" target=\"_blank\">Rumplestiltskin </a>himself delt straightforwardly with the milinner's daughter. A necklace for a day's spinning, a ring for a day's spinning. Those are completely fair and above board trades. Now he did ask for a baby (and maybe his entire plot was to make that third trade - but the text never says so thus we can't assume it) but there was no trickery or illusions there. It was again an above board straight forward trade, and the Milliner's Daughter could have said no. In fact, when the Milliner's Daughter agrees Rumplestiltskin even goes back on his deal to give her a chance, he doesn't have to do that, and when the Milliner's Daughter wins his game (completely above board I might add) he honours his loss and dosen't take the child.<br /> <br /> In fact Lords of Summer has a lovely bit about the Rumplestiltskin story form a Changeling point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lords of Summer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What annoys the Goldspinners is how the so-called victims never, ever, take responsibility for the deals they make</div> </div> </div> </div> And you know what, they have a point. The Milliner's Daughter selling her child was a scummy thing to do, she knew she'd be Queen if this third room was spun to gold and didn't even try to negocaite a defered payment for when she had the resources of a kingdom to offer in return.<br /> <br /> So yes. I do think you've read different faerie stories to the rest of us. To me there's lots of faerie tales where the moral is &quot;honour the deal you make&quot;. Which is probably why I think that Pledges can accomplish more than you do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because the system is so rigid that a lie can really break everything down. A Huntsmen just has to walk in as someone else while they aren't there, say &quot;Hey, I fucking sold out someone to the Huntsmen for a token&quot; ,disappear cackling, and that person is going to be in deep shit, because, what they found a way to flaunt the pledge just to piss people off?</div> </div> </div> </div> Thinking about it, this really makes it clear why I disagree with you. it comes across as you saying<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen's schemes cannot be foiled.<br /> <br /> The Changeling's defences cannot work.<br /> <br /> That's not a good scheme. It's a terrible scheme, but it feels like you're saying it works automatically because it's not banned by the Pledge and you don't like those Pledges. But in practice it absolutely falls apart the instant the Changelings remember two things<br /> <br /> 1) Every Huntsman and half the people here can disguise themselves as somebody else.<br /> 2) The only reason he'd ever say that is if he wanted to sow panic.<br /> <br /> The thing about being part of a society of scheeming illusionists is that everyone expects scheemes and illusions and puts effort into not being fooled. When everyone knows that illusions are a possibility they'll realise it's far more likely that this was an illusion rather than someone finding a brilliant and extremely rare advantage, and then deciding to reveal the ace up their sleeve in the most public way possible.<br /> <br /> They'll still going to investigate both possiblities because paranoia, but they're not just going to fall apart from one little disguise when the most likely possibility is that it was someone in disguise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Illusions and trickery are scary, but they're not nearly as powerful as you say. Their existence doesn't invalidate pledges against aiding the Gentry, because those pledges put big limiations on the infultrating loyalist. You have to disguise yourself as a member of the Court, and if the Changelings who know whoever you're disguised as think something's amiss or if that Changeling turns up unexpectedly and you're face to face with, or if the King declares a spot check, everyone in the room swear you're not a loyalist, then the Loyalist is in big trouble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simple fact is that while this might root out some loyalists, what this does fundamentally is just create a cloud of paranoia that unsettles the freeholders into a constant state of distrust</div> </div> </div> </div> You're thinking like a human, not a Changeling.<br /> <br /> For humans constant reminders that there's threats and that nobody's trusted without pledges sow distrust.<br /> <br /> For Changelings constant reminders that there's threats and that nobody's trusted without pledges is just normal and can't do any (more) harm; but Pledges create trust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder where people thinks this fits into the scheme of things in Changeling the Lost, or even the larger Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> I already answered that.<br /> <br /> It doesn't fit thematically; but when Changelings have such good tools to root out infultraters the only thing Loyalists can be is outsiders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't walls or curtains or inquisitions that you can use to keep out the enemy. That's not what Pledges, as a basic function of the Wyrd, do, it's not even how they act. The Wyrd is a connective force, it bridges one thing to another thing. It's <i>not </i>a wall.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>That's</b> your counter argument?<br /> <br /> Your counter aruguement to using Pledges to determine who's not part of our group is &quot;it's a connective force&quot;?!<br /> <br /> For the purposes of determining group loyalty a connective force that links A-B-C but not L is even better than a wall between A-B-C and L.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scoietal Oaths acting as impositions have to cover too much and just foster resentment and distrust. But at the motley level? With people you trust and care about, or at least really want to?</div> </div> </div> </div> Fun fact.<br /> <br /> Plenty of Changeling's I've played didn't trust their Motley's, didn't particualarly want too, and they still worked as an effective member of the group, because the things they were scared of were forbidden by a Pledge.<br /> <br /> Also, Freeholds are on the micro level. In my experience they're about 30-50 members on average. Both Freeholds and Motley's are lower than Dunbar's number.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825193#post825193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the tyrannical methods impositions from on high.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this is another thing I disagree with.<br /> <br /> On what world does &quot;Don't aid the Gentry&quot; qualify as tyranical? That's like saying laws against rape are a tyanical imposition from on high. It makes absolutely zero sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T03:45:13-08:00","id":825346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825330#post825330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You pretty much summarized what I envisioned as Ziggy's role as Sorcerer of the Autumn Court, right there. He keeps a record of known Gentry and Huntsmen, their individual quirks, frailties and such, studies lore to recognize other Gentry, and he's always on the lookout for new contracts the freehold can use against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think every court is going to have something useful to contribute against the Huntsmen, even beyond their Approaches.<br /> <br /> In the traditional Seasonal system, Summer trains and prepares to defeat the Huntsmen permanently, Autumn gathers fey lore and crafts enchantments and contracts to hamper the Huntsmen, Spring gets to <i>know</i> the Freehold, to spot the Huntsmen and Loyalists that seek to infiltrate, and Winter studies the Huntsmen themselves, how they work and what they do, so that they can be the Will Graham to the Huntsman's Hannibal, all from the shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T04:00:38-08:00","id":825348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825321#post825321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to deny the Huntsmen the use of their strengths before they even show up is such a... *human* thing to do. It's just not how stories go.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. <a href=\"http://www.pitt.edu/~dash/grimm004.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Story of a Boy Who Went Forth to Learn Fear</a>. The antagonist's strength is fear; the protagonist's power is having no fear at all. Thus he denies all the antagonists' their strength before the story shows up.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, you say it's a human thing to do. The players are all human, so you know that plenty of groups will do so. That means there should be advice for how to tell interesting stories after the laws are laid down. And that does not mean advice for how to screw over players for playing it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T04:15:43-08:00","id":825352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825348#post825348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree. <a href=\"http://www.pitt.edu/~dash/grimm004.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Story of a Boy Who Went Forth to Learn Fear</a>. The antagonist's strength is fear; the protagonist's power is having no fear at all. Thus he denies all the antagonists' their strength before the story shows up.<br /> <br /> Besides, you say it's a human thing to do. The players are all human, so you know that plenty of groups will do so. That means there should be advice for how to tell interesting stories after the laws are laid down. And that does not mean advice for how to screw over players for playing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Huntsmen's strength is not simply fear. It's deception, paranoia, temptation, treachery, the tenacity of a force that it's hard to kill, who knows what other powers they may have.<br /> <br /> Using a Pledge to try and protect changelings from Huntsmen is actually an okay idea, but trying to &quot;gotcha&quot; the Huntsmen, being like &quot;okay, so with this, we become immune to one of the Huntsmen's weapons,&quot; just goes completely against the narrative purpose of the Huntsman. If you look at a Huntsman in the eye and refuse the Token, it shouldn't be because you're bound by a Pledge so it's not really that much of a choice. It should be because he's asking you to condemn one of your best friends to hell.<br /> <br /> I feel that what the book should advice would be how to make Pledges that help the Changelings face the Huntsmen without actually providing an immunity to the Huntsman's weapons. Instead of &quot;you can't accept a Token of Reprieve&quot; or &quot;you have to notify if you have a Token of Reprieve&quot;, it should be more like &quot;If you accept a Token of Reprieve, you are Oathbound to try and learn as much as possible about the Huntsman you're helping, so that you can later discreetly pass on your wisdom to the Freehold archives&quot; or something along those lines. Something that <i>furthers</i> a story, rather than shuts it down.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Assumption made an ass out of just me this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-07-2016, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:03:18-08:00","id":825372,"title":"","content":"I think it's the same problem with a lot of utopian &quot;there ought to be a law&quot; thoughts. The problem is that human language prevents you from coming up with the perfect pledge. Imagine all those D&amp;D players who think they're being clever with pages of text for a Wish. As I see it, the tighter you try to lock down things with pledges, the more creative people are going to get to subvert it or turn it against pledge-abiding people, and the cost of knowing that is heightened vigilance against clever loopholes and false positives, and from there it's a vicious cycle of greater and greater legalese.<br /> <br /> Instead, having simple and varied pledges among Motleys means that there are comparatively simple loopholes that they can see coming and work against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:04:14-08:00","id":825373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825352#post825352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You miss the point of the story. The protagonist <i>already felt the fear</i>. The fear <i>was already there</i>. So he conquered the fear in a narratively appropriate manner before the final confrontation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait? What?<br /> <br /> Can you point to the bit that said he felt fear, because I never see any fear from the protagonist at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825352#post825352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Huntsmen's strength is not simply fear.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well obviously. The story was an example of a faerie tale where the antagonists powers were neutralised before the story starts. Not an implication that the Huntsmen's only weapon was fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825352#post825352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a Pledge to try and protect changelings from Huntsmen is actually an okay idea, but trying to &quot;gotcha&quot; the Huntsmen, being like &quot;okay, so with this, we become immune to one of the Huntsmen's weapons,&quot; just goes completely against the narrative purpose of the Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually consider one of the main narrative purpose of the Huntsmen to be a reason why Changelings don't trust anyone without a Pledge. There's now huge incentives for every Changeling to turn trator.<br /> <br /> There's still plenty of nasty tricks Huntsmen have left to make them scary and interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825352#post825352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that <i>furthers</i> a story, rather than shuts it down.</div> </div> </div> </div> I consider this law to be something that furthers a story, because there's lots of interesting things the Freehold can do when the members have a base level of Pledge-enforced trust that they can't do without.<br /> <br /> But really, every decision furthers some story and ends others. It's really a question of what you're interested in, which probably changes on a game by game basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:24:28-08:00","id":825382,"title":"","content":"I think we might be missing something kinda obvious,changelings arent a bunch of paran\u00f3id selfish people always wanting to stick a knife on someones back,changelings are a group of survivors banding together for support,most courts are like big support groups,s\u00f3 when a huntsman comes the changelings wont just go into a crazy &quot;every man for himself&quot; mode,theyll unite,they help each obter,they are not going to leave the huntsman's target alome,they fucking help him,why would they form freeholds and courts if they dont want to tais care of each obter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:25:32-08:00","id":825383,"title":"","content":"I think we might be missing something kinda obvious,changelings arent a bunch of paran\u00f3id selfish people always wanting to stick a knife on someones back,changelings are a group of survivors banding together for support,most courts are like big support groups,s\u00f3 when a huntsman comes the changelings wont just go into a crazy &quot;every man for himself&quot; mode,theyll unite,they help each obter,they are not going to leave the huntsman's target alome,they fucking help him,why would they form freeholds and courts if they dont want to taike are of each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:38:43-08:00","id":825385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825373#post825373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wait? What?<br /> <br /> Can you point to the bit that said he felt fear, because I never see any fear from the protagonist at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, thought I knew what story you were talking about, so I didn't actually read it. Upon actually reading it, it seems clear that the monster is not actually a major narrative point in the protagonist's life, but instead the means by which he finds fortune. One could replace the spirit for some other encounter in which the boy's impassivity allows him to do what no other can, and the story would carry along all the same.<br /> <br /> That is not the role Huntsmen occupy in a Changeling's narrative, much less on a societal level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825373#post825373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well obviously. The story was an example of a faerie tale where the antagonists powers were neutralised before the story starts. Not an implication that the Huntsmen's only weapon was fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not actually neutralised, however. The protagonist is immune. That is a key difference. At no point does the protagonist craft a way to neutralise the monster's weapons, he just happens to be naturally immune to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825373#post825373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider this law to be something that furthers a story, because there's lots of interesting things the Freehold can do when the members have a base level of Pledge-enforced trust that they can't do without.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it genuinely feels like an attempt to avoid conflict instead of actually dealing with it. That's what it boils down to. And it's not even the evasiveness of outsmarting the enemy in a crucial moment, it's just terribly anticlimactic. The only thing that such a Pledge would be good for, dramatically speaking, is to explore what happens when it's broken. Because otherwise it feels like it cockblocks interesting story elements rather than enabling them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:41:42-08:00","id":825386,"title":"","content":"Sorry bout the double por by te way,um on mobile","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:53:38-08:00","id":825388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825385#post825385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My bad, thought I knew what story you were talking about, so I didn't actually read it.</div> </div> </div> </div> No worries, this stuff happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825385#post825385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not the role Huntsmen occupy in a Changeling's narrative, much less on a societal level.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference? The Huntsmen are antagonists, the Boy Without Fear's antagonists were the spirits in the castle.<br /> <br /> What about a Huntsmen who the Storyteller created just because his player had an Aspiration of aquiring some Arcadian Weaponry?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825385#post825385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not actually neutralised, however. The protagonist is immune. That is a key difference.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why's that an important distinction? Would you be ok with a Freehold that's naturally immune to buying Tokens of Repreve? Say it's built near on an ancient druid grove that for some reason means Huntsmen cannot offer Tokens within 100 miles?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825385#post825385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that it genuinely feels like an attempt to avoid conflict instead of actually dealing with it. That's what it boils down to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it sort of is. To me it's a way of avoiding uninteresting conflict so that it doesn't get in the way of interesting conflict.<br /> <br /> Obviously that's personal taste but I'm not too interested in the Freehold fighting itself, except as a problem to be fixed. I'm far more interested by the Freehold united against external threats; or the Courts united against an external foe which is the other Courts in the Freehold.<br /> <br /> <br /> But there's another part to it. I geuninely believe that under the 1E mechanics and what we've seen in 2E teasers using laws to protect against Huntsmen and infultration is a mechanically superior approach to the common Changeling goal of never being captured again. Thus there should be storyteller advice for what happens when players inevitably make that decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T07:22:56-08:00","id":825396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825342#post825342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Arc, I think this makes it clear that you fundamentally miss the point of why laws to ban dealing with the Huntsmen would exist.<br /> <br /> Of course they screw over that guy. The entire point of the law is to explicitly screw over that guy. You know they porobably won't sacrafice themself, so the Freehold sacrafices them first. It's like cutting out a cancer, it absolutely sucks if you're the cancer, but it's great if you're the cell next to the cancer because you're not getting infected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want to just address this, because the way you put it bugs the everloving hell out of me.<br /> <br /> The point is that no one wants to be the guy who gets screwed over without any chances just because a Huntsman saw them as a weak link or chose to use them as a weapon against their quarry. It's ludicrous to expect Changelings as a whole to be okay with a pledge backed law that makes them a sacrifice by default the moment they are confronted with that choice. Huntsmen may not be common, but they're inevitable, and that way of doing things is closing off more opportunities to <i>stay and continue living</i> (and help others) than the alternative.<br /> <br /> Also, are you even listening to yourself? You're comparing any Changeling who becomes a target of the Huntsmen as a means to get to their real objective to <i>cancer</i>. This smacks dangerously close to victim blaming. Granted, it's fairly common to find victims who blame themselves, but that's a horrible thing to say about Changelings as a detached party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-07-2016, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T07:45:29-08:00","id":825402,"title":"","content":"I'm used to thinking in terms of D&amp;D/Pathfinder, where less obvious issues can often be untangled by pointing the party's paladin at it and asking who's evil. Much of the time, however, you don't need to worry about the DM being insidious enough to subvert it because it's going to be a dungeon crawl with the big bad wearing Darth Vader armor. It can be fun in its own way, but having black and white morality has been straining my suspension of disbelief for a while.<br /> <br /> I realize this is entirely about taste, but I'm interested in Changeling precisely because you need to pay attention to things like courtly politics and the messy issues that come with keeping a fearful group of people together in a world with no easy &quot;detect evil&quot; ability, clearly identifiable evil races to be slaughtered without a pang of conscience, or pure shining paragons of heroism. I want to play out that internal conflict about safety versus heroism, rather than brush off danger with the confidence that the party cleric can just revive me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T07:51:59-08:00","id":825407,"title":"","content":"I love Yolf and I cannot lie.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of this-Look man, if you don't see how a bunch of paranoid, opportunistic, mercurial victims might rail against something that pins them in a corner without possible answers might object to a system that forcibly creates corners for the their abusers to slam them into with no hope of escape, I'm not sure I can help you.<br /> <br /> <i>I will never go back</i>, as a fundamental force in people's lives, means trying to always have a way out. It means always having a way to slip out. Changelings don't take kindly to captors.<br /> <br /> I'm done for now. I can't keep bleeding words on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T07:58:46-08:00","id":825410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825388#post825388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference? The Huntsmen are antagonists, the Boy Without Fear's antagonists were the spirits in the castle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spirits were not actually antagonists. They were trials. Their narrative function is more akin to an inanimate obstacle to overcome or a riddle to solve than to actual entities of their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825388#post825388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a Huntsmen who the Storyteller created just because his player had an Aspiration of aquiring some Arcadian Weaponry?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how the Storyteller ran that Huntsman. You <i>can</i> run Huntsmen as obstacles/puzzles/challenges rather than actual entities, but that's not really the way they're envisioned in the text. It's not badwrongfun, but it sorta explains the nature of the discussion, and IMO it'd be a lot better to simply say &quot;this is how I'll be homebrewing/refluffing Huntsmen in my games.&quot; It avoids an unnecessary argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825388#post825388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why's that an important distinction? Would you be ok with a Freehold that's naturally immune to buying Tokens of Repreve? Say it's built near on an ancient druid grove that for some reason means Huntsmen cannot offer Tokens within 100 miles?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have the same feelings on the actual result (that it stifles conflict and doesn't really give anything back), but I would consider it a more honest approach than trying to finagle the rules. Saying &quot;I'm homebrewing this Freehold so that it's immune to Tokens of Reprieve&quot; still gets you what you want, but it makes sure everyone is on the same page and prevents needless arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825388#post825388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it sort of is. To me it's a way of avoiding uninteresting conflict so that it doesn't get in the way of interesting conflict.<br /> <br /> Obviously that's personal taste but I'm not too interested in the Freehold fighting itself, except as a problem to be fixed. I'm far more interested by the Freehold united against external threats; or the Courts united against an external foe which is the other Courts in the Freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the exact same way as you. The thing is, I assume that, in small Freeholds, Huntsmen are extremely rare. You'd see one every few years, or even once per decade. But when the Huntsman finally comes, it should cause tremendous upheaval. Turning the Freehold against itself would be IMO one of the milder results. In larger Freeholds, you might get one or two Huntsmen a year, but changelings have already taken measures to avoid falling into infighting. Measures that involve guile and cleverness rather than exploiting a narrative force against what it stands for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825388#post825388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's another part to it. I geuninely believe that under the 1E mechanics and what we've seen in 2E teasers using laws to protect against Huntsmen and infultration is a mechanically superior approach to the common Changeling goal of never being captured again. Thus there should be storyteller advice for what happens when players inevitably make that decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the 2e text is going to support that. Just a hunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:00:30-08:00","id":825411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825396#post825396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, are you even listening to yourself? You're comparing any Changeling who becomes a target of the Huntsmen as a means to get to their real objective to <i>cancer</i>. This smacks dangerously close to victim blaming. Granted, it's fairly common to find victims who blame themselves, but that's a horrible thing to say about Changelings as a detached party.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other thing about that mentality scares me: What about false positives? It strikes me as equivalent to handing the legal system over to a hybrid computer/literal genie and assuming that it's infallible. What if someone breaks the letter of the pledge without breaking the spirit of it? The Wyrd only cares about the letter, and the more elaborate you get with technicalities, the more likely the Wyrd is going to lash out for you trying to game the system. The Wyrd is unforgiving and doesn't care about extenuating circumstances or intentions, and True Fae understand it far better than any Changeling ever could. That's why you can't use it as your primary line of defense. Even if they can't sneak a loyalist in under the terms, they'll undoubtedly find a way to break apart the bulwark by making them break tiny details. No bulwark, no court.<br /> <br /> Also, think about how such pledges sound: &quot;A sure-fire way to eliminate loyalists and keep out the Gentry and Huntsmen? Sounds too good to be true. It relies heavily on the Wyrd? <i>...Are you one of them?</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:02:49-08:00","id":825412,"title":"","content":"Shadow, too, is also getting my love, taking some more time to look over this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Bronze too, wow, lot of good comments in the mean time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:09:27-08:00","id":825415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825411#post825411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, think about how such pledges sound: &quot;A sure-fire way to eliminate loyalists and keep out the Gentry and Huntsmen? Sounds too good to be true. It relies heavily on the Wyrd? <i>...Are you one of them?</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is brilliant.<br /> <br /> But also, using Pledges to neutralise one of the Huntsmen's weapons is just... not clever. I dunno, I don't want to come off as insulting, but to me it feels like it's not the changeling being cunning and outwitting his opponent, he's just using something he has in a very straightforward manner to say &quot;There, I'm immune.&quot; I approve of the idea of using Pledges to help Changelings against the Huntsmen, but IMO they should be clever and interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825412#post825412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow, too, is also getting my love, taking some more time to look over this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Bronze too, wow, lot of good comments in the mean time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and Charlaquin converted me. Just holding the line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:13:04-08:00","id":825417,"title":"","content":"I keep forgetting that you had converted, I admit. It warms the cockles of my heart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:15:45-08:00","id":825419,"title":"","content":"One thing my dad figured out when he was young, during a portion of the Red Scare: &quot;It's always the spies who are first in line to take loyalty oaths.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:33:02-08:00","id":825424,"title":"","content":"Make a pledge to never deal with a huntsman.<br /> <br /> &lt;Huntsman, disguised as another person&gt; Oh hey would you pick up some milk for me? Here's the money and I'll let you keep the change for doing it.<br /> <br /> And then suddenly we have an unwitting oathbreaker *and* the changeling the Huntsman disguised themselves as is probably about to get strung up.<br /> <br /> Make a pledge to never make a deal with a huntsman to get a token of reprieve.<br /> <br /> &lt;Huntsman, again disguised as someone else&gt; Hey would you do seemingly innocuous thing that gets me closer to my quarry in some fashion you could never conceivably know? Okay cool. btdubs, here is a token of reprieve for all of your good service and/or here is a goblin fruit I totally didn't hollow out and put a token of reprieve in just to fuck with you.<br /> <br /> Same thing.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Using pledges to keep out the huntsmen puts you in an arms race against your ability to word things against the huntsmen's ability to exploit them. It's much like the war against computer viruses, except your antivirus can only update once per year/season/etc. and if it ever fails once the whole program collapses in an irreplaceable way. If you really think this is such a good idea, feel free to try and craft some fool proof pledges and I'll show you how a huntsman can have a field day with them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T08:47:37-08:00","id":825429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825417#post825417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep forgetting that you had converted, I admit. It warms the cockles of my heart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In all honestly, Changeling's my favourite gameline and I <i>desperately</i> wanted to get on board with the Huntsmen, since they're one of the core aspects of 2e. Reading the spoilers for the new Court system and the Approaches made me fall in love with Changeling all over again.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking of a way to be clever with Pledges with regards to Huntsmen. How about &quot;Should you ever accept a Token of Reprieve from a Huntsman, you must ask him an important question about himself.&quot; (If the Huntsman is reticent, then it's up to the changeling to convince him of the harmlessness of the question). I can imagine a Spring Courtier or some other socialite asking &quot;I know your kind doesn't like this realm, but what do you find the most tolerable, or even enjoyable? What do you like the most about being here?&quot; and then, later on, the Huntsman is caught by surprise in his hideout by the changeling's Motley and the Freehold's warriors. &quot;When you said you enjoyed spending time in the park, I went there. I spent all day there, absorbing the sights and the sounds. You know what I noticed? You can hear the water burbling in the fountain no matter where you are. And then I travelled through the city, looking for something like it. Yesterday, I found this lovely place. Right next to the art exhibit, with its manufactured waterfall.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:13:04-08:00","id":825435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825429#post825429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In all honestly, Changeling's my favourite gameline and I <i>desperately</i> wanted to get on board with the Huntsmen, since they're one of the core aspects of 2e. Reading the spoilers for the new Court system and the Approaches made me fall in love with Changeling all over again.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking of a way to be clever with Pledges with regards to Huntsmen. How about &amp;quot;Should you ever accept a Token of Reprieve from a Huntsman, you must ask him an important question about himself.&amp;quot; (If the Huntsman is reticent, then it's up to the changeling to convince him of the harmlessness of the question). I can imagine a Spring Courtier or some other socialite asking &amp;quot;I know your kind doesn't like this realm, but what do you find the most tolerable, or even enjoyable? What do you like the most about being here?&amp;quot; and then, later on, the Huntsman is caught by surprise in his hideout by the changeling's Motley and the Freehold's warriors. &amp;quot;When you said you enjoyed spending time in the park, I went there. I spent all day there, absorbing the sights and the sounds. You know what I noticed? You can hear the water burbling in the fountain no matter where you are. And then I travelled through the city, looking for something like it. Yesterday, I found this lovely place. Right next to the art exhibit, with its manufactured waterfall.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that is a smart way of dealing with Huntsmen. You can bargin with them, but you need to get something of benefit for the Freehold too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:23:46-08:00","id":825438,"title":"","content":"Why does a Huntsman that has a Changeling over that much of a barrel need to offer a token of reprieve at all? So one has your family hostage, or has you at sword point at the gates of Arcadia, or whatever. Those are compelling reasons to sell somebody out. But if the Huntsman doesn't already have an offer you can't refuse (again, whether or not a token is involved), making the offer involves revealing themselves, which risks the Changeling alerting the rest of the Freehold instead of accepting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:24:40-08:00","id":825439,"title":"","content":"Unless the Huntsmen lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:34:07-08:00","id":825445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825438#post825438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does a Huntsman that has a Changeling over that much of a barrel need to offer a token of reprieve at all? So one has your family hostage, or has you at sword point at the gates of Arcadia, or whatever. Those are compelling reasons to sell somebody out. But if the Huntsman doesn't already have an offer you can't refuse (again, whether or not a token is involved), making the offer involves revealing themselves, which risks the Changeling alerting the rest of the Freehold instead of accepting.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO the Token is there to make sure the Changeling does as he agreed to do. A cornered Changeling will agree to anything, just to get some space. Once you take your eyes off him, he might just bolt or subvert your schemes in some way. You have no way of ensuring he complies. Even a loving Changeling might just abandon his family to the clutches of a Huntsman <i>because he will never go back there</i>. Once he accepts the Token, however, the pact is sealed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825439#post825439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the Huntsmen lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is detectable by the Subterfuge skill, and still provides a point of information with regards to that Huntsman. Even if the Changeling doesn't reveal that she got the Token from a Huntsman, to avoid admitting she didn't get an honest answer but she still got a Token, she still knows at least one thing about him that she didn't know before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T10:04:48-08:00","id":825457,"title":"","content":"Even the Changelings who do fall into the temptation of the Token don't have to be motivated entirely by fear. You can have some who think that they can get the token and then subvert the effort in some way. His friend doesn't get dragged back to Arcadia, he gets a Token, and if he's clever enough, his friend doesn't even need to know he was betrayed.<br /> <br /> Thus hubris rationalizes. If he succeeds, he might end up being praised as a trickster genius. If he fails, he's an arrogant fool who gambled his friend's freedom and lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T10:43:12-08:00","id":825466,"title":"","content":"So, ignoring the incredibly painful victim blaming already mentioned earlier,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825388#post825388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously that's personal taste but I'm not too interested in the Freehold fighting itself, except as a problem to be fixed. I'm far more interested by the Freehold united against external threats; or the Courts united against an external foe which is the other Courts in the Freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about this is that... well... of course it's a problem to be fixed. The problem is that you're using magic to fix the problem, rather than using trust, community building, etc.<br /> <br /> To me, this says that the problem isn't that you might have <s>Sedition</s>Anti-Huntsmen Acts written into the Wyrd, but that the writing of such laws being possible and magically enforceable is, itself, the problem. What I hear from your arguments is that Pledges need to be less airtight. It bothers me when Arc says that Changelings are masters of legalese; that rubs me wrong. To quote Gaiman, the law is a blunt instrument, not a scalpel. The idea that there exists some perfect set of laws that can be applied to all relevant people in all relevant cases perfectly and absolutely is just... well, it smells naive at best.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with a freehold <i>trying</i> to do this. That's a story worth telling. But I'm not okay with it being successful. To me, that kills the ability of the game to connect with real life. Sure, there are other places where it connects fine and those continue to work as they did before, but me? I feel like I should go back over the Pledge rules and figure out how to do a homebrew where they aren't pure and utter fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T10:45:52-08:00","id":825469,"title":"","content":"I mean yeah I would think subversion is the order of the day. If I'm not in the position to fight it myself, either due to physical incapability or because it has some form of leverage, my immediate goal is stalling and getting word to those who can.<br /> <br /> And that's where the real power of pledges, at least as they worked in 1st edition, comes in. It's not that pledges can't be broken, it's that everyone involved knows it happened. A pledge not to aid a Huntsman needn't be backed by harsh sanctions (unless 2e removed minor ones, idk), but it's a great way to alert everyone that a Hunstmen has made inroads into the freehold and it's time to redouble the defenses and root the invader out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T10:47:21-08:00","id":825470,"title":"","content":"I've honestly never used Pledges beyond the classics (Motley Oath, the one towards the Freehold/Monarchs, very rarely the romance one), so I'm probably not the right person to comment about the nature of Pledges. I found them intellectually interesting, but just not my thing. In D&amp;D terms, I'm too Chaotic for such Lawful things. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:14:08-08:00","id":825484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825396#post825396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that no one wants to be the guy who gets screwed over without any chances just because a Huntsman saw them as a weak link or chose to use them as a weapon against their quarry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody wants to be the guy who gets screwed over by another Changeling because they made a deal/were blackmailed by the Huntsmen either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825396#post825396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, are you even listening to yourself? You're comparing any Changeling who becomes a target of the Huntsmen as a means to get to their real objective to <i>cancer</i>. This smacks dangerously close to victim blaming. Granted, it's fairly common to find victims who blame themselves, but that's a horrible thing to say about Changelings as a detached party.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took the term from Hunter's &quot;cancer cells&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Also, I'm not blaming them for being targeted by a Huntsman, I'm blaming them for agreeing to help the Huntsman. Under duress or not, that's still a legitimately evil thing to do. From my perspective it seems people here have more sympathy for the Changeling who sold out a fellow member of the freehold to the Huntsmen than for the Changeling who got sold out. That seems backwards to me)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825407#post825407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest of this-Look man, if you don't see how a bunch of paranoid, opportunistic, mercurial victims might rail against something that pins them in a corner without possible answers might object to a system that forcibly creates corners for the their abusers to slam them into with no hope of escape, I'm not sure I can help you.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an easy way to &quot;help me&quot;.<br /> <br /> Demonstrate that this law creates more oppotunities for Huntsmen to trap Changelings in a corner than it takes away. Because to me it's looking like a net decrease in the amount of Changelings being trapped in corners.<br /> <br /> You're constantly bringing up the oppotunities it creates for Huntsmen; but you're not doing cost-benefit analysis against the oppotunities it takes away from huntsmen; and until you do the only cost-benefit I have to go by is mine, and mine's looking like a net negative in the amount of oppotunities for Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825410#post825410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirits were not actually antagonists. They were trials. Their narrative function is more akin to an inanimate obstacle to overcome or a riddle to solve than to actual entities of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div> However you could say that about, I'd guess somewhere between 50% to 90% of for-lack-of-a-better-word antagonists in faerie tales. The Giant from Jack in the Beanstalk is another example of an antagonist who's closer to an inanimate obstacle.<br /> <br /> More of an obstacle really. At least the Boy Who Set Out to Learn Fear actually spoke to the spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825410#post825410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the exact same way as you. The thing is, I assume that, in small Freeholds, Huntsmen are extremely rare. You'd see one every few years, or even once per decade. But when the Huntsman finally comes, it should cause tremendous upheaval.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why though? Why is this an assumption?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, a successful Huntsman could do that. But unless the Storyteller gives the Huntsman plot armour (which IMO is just a bad idea in RPGs) what's to stop the players from coming up with a really good plan or getting really lucky and stopping the Huntsmen before it can do much damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-07-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:20:12-08:00","id":825486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825484#post825484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However you could say that about, I'd guess somewhere between 50% to 90% of for-lack-of-a-better-word antagonists in faerie tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why it's important to analyse stories carefully and discern what is the true role of each major part of it. Not every person that stands in the way of the protagonist is an antagonist. Sometimes, they're just something else in person form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825484#post825484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why though? Why is this an assumption?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of preparedness/readiness and sheer statistical probability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825484#post825484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, sure, a successful Huntsman could do that. But unless the Storyteller gives the Huntsman plot armour (which IMO is just a bad idea in RPGs) what's to stop the players from coming up with a really good plan or getting really lucky and stopping the Huntsmen before it can do much damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely nothing. That's most certainly a possible outcome. However, it should be done because the characters worked their asses off to outwit the Huntsman and stay one step ahead at all times. Not because they simply neutralised some of his weapons beforehand. IMO there's no narrative weight in using a Pledge in such a direct, straightforward manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:34:14-08:00","id":825492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825486#post825486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why it's important to analyse stories carefully and discern what is the true role of each major part of it. Not every person that stands in the way of the protagonist is an antagonist. Sometimes, they're just something else in person form.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not if your goal is to find antagonists you can use as a template and your definition makes it impossible to find anything.<br /> <br /> Can you think of any actual antagonists in faerie tales? Because I'm leaning towards saying the spirits count as honoury antagonists because they're the closest thing we've got.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you can have an obstical that's not really an obstical because the charachter was immune to it; I don't see why you can't have an antagonist that's not an antagonist because the charachter is already immune to their tricks. I'm sure there's some faerie tales starring the devil trying to tempt someone that go like that but I can't remember the name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825486#post825486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lack of preparedness/readiness and sheer statistical probability.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why do you assume a lack of readiness? What factors go into your probability calculations?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825486#post825486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not because they simply neutralised some of his weapons beforehand. IMO there's no narrative weight in using a Pledge in such a direct, straightforward manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the player characters are a lawyer, a berauocrat, a royal, and an oracle (I've seen all but the beaurocrat in my games) - it seems far more narratively fitting that they defeat the Huntsman through foresight and preperation rather than a fast paced game of wits.<br /> <br /> Not every charachter is suited for a fast paced game of wits, and players should be encouraged to play to their charachters strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-07-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:36:50-08:00","id":825495,"title":"","content":"Examples that come to mind:<br /> <br /> 1) A huntsman finds out things his target wants to buy. He takes one of those things and hides his Token of Reprieve in an added hidden compartment or in some place the changeling is unlikely to look. He disguises himself in some manner that either doesn't give away his tell, or makes it part of a disguise as a changeling. He offers a seemingly mundane bargain to his target for the item with the hidden token. If the changeling accepts the bargain, 1) he's made a deal with a huntsman. 2) If he doesn't know he has the token inside his purchase, he won't know he accepted it as part of a package deal, or to declare it to the freehold.<br /> <br /> 2) A huntsman disguises himself as a drunk and gets himself stuck somewhere on the changeling's itinerary. &quot;Hey! Buddy! Help me up and I'll buy you a drink!&quot; Bargaining with a Huntsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:51:28-08:00","id":825502,"title":"","content":"Those two could both be countered by adding the phrase &quot;knowingly&quot; to the pledge.<br /> <br /> Heck, there's no reason why the Freehold law the Changeling's swear to obey can't say something like. &quot;Any Changeling who makes a bargain with the Huntsmen must, within 24 hours of learning that they have done so, fully disclose the details of their deal to the appropriate Freehold authorities.<br /> <br /> Upon learning of such a deal the Freehold authorities will arrange a trial by a jury of the Changeling's peers to determine the extent of Changeling's misdeed, and any mitigating circumstances, and the honourableness of the Changelings motives and conduct. Any Changeling found guilty in this trial must abide by the sentence of the court.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know trial by juries aren't perfect. But it does seem like a massive improvement over a Changeling knowing that a Huntsman is in town and not warning anyone about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I said several pages back, I'm not actually trying to write a watertight pledge in this discussion. I'm more interested in the concept of anti-huntsman laws rather than if my phrasing is perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:51:59-08:00","id":825503,"title":"","content":"No pledgecrafter worth the name forgets to add &quot;knowingly&quot; to the wording on a pledge where betrayal or the like has disastrous consequences. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the sanction is a slap on the wrist, it's *beneficial* to trigger even on unwitting betrayals because you know the instant that petty curse hits that you've been duped, and bam, outed the Huntsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:58:32-08:00","id":825508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825492#post825492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not if your goal is to find antagonists you can use as a template and your definition makes it impossible to find anything.<br /> <br /> Can you think of any actual antagonists in faerie tales? Because I'm leaning towards saying the spirits count as honoury antagonists because they're the closest thing we've got.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every tale needs an antagonist. A tale about self-discovery, such as the one you linked, where the boy discovers fear and finds his place in the world, often lacks antagonists and instead pits the protagonists against obstacles, puzzles and challenges that teach him about himself.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A good example of an antagonist is the sorceress in Snow White. She has her own motivations, personality, backstory and exists in the narrative as more than a simple obstacle or challenge to overcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825492#post825492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, if you can have an obstical that's not really an obstical because the charachter was immune to it; I don't see why you can't have an antagonist that's not an antagonist because the charachter is already immune to their tricks. I'm sure there's some faerie tales starring the devil trying to tempt someone that go like that but I can't remember the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the story you want to tell, go for it. You are absolutely right that, by making changelings immune to Huntsmen, they are no longer proper antagonists.<br /> <br /> The thing is, I'd be shocked if you found a story about a protagonist resisting temptation by citing an Oath, unless that Oath has extremely deep personal meaning for them. Resisting temptation, narratively speaking, is supposed to demonstrate the character's virtue, strength of will and/or incorruptibility. It becomes incredibly anticlimactic if they refuse temptation because of unrelated reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825492#post825492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you assume a lack of readiness? What factors go into your probability calculations?</div> </div> </div> </div>A small Freehold means a smaller amount of mid-Wyrd changelings, which are the ones Huntsmen are sent against. A smaller amount of Huntsmen means a lack of practical experience with them, a lack of general Huntsman lore and a lack of tried and true means of defending against them or fighting them. You can still succeed, mind you, but you're not as prepared and ready to face them as a larger Freehold that deals with them much more often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825492#post825492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the player characters are a lawyer, a berauocrat, a royal, and an oracle (I've seen all but the beaurocrat in my games) - it seems far more narratively fitting that they defeat the Huntsman through foresight and preperation rather than a fast paced game of wits.<br /> <br /> Not every charachter is suited for a fast paced game of wits, and players should be encouraged to play to their charachters strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>All three characters can outwit Huntsmen without having to engage in a fast-paced game of wits. Outwitting is merely outsmarting the opponent in a particularly cunning way, something all three characters are well equipped to do. I would definitely see the Lawyer and the Bureaucrat using the power of Pledges to defeat a Huntsman, but as a personal trait, not as a wide societal thing. The Oracle would most definitely win through clever use of foresight, but IMO it'd be narratively stronger if the Huntsman, when he comes to find the Oracle to make the offer, finds instead a flower and a &quot;No, thank you&quot; note. I feel that's a lot more interesting than a Pledge-born refusal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-07-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:06:10-08:00","id":825511,"title":"","content":"The problem I see with &quot;knowingly&quot; is that it allows them to freely make deals so long as they keep the changelings they deal with ignorant of their intentions and/or nature. Also, an unscrupulous changeling can <i>suspect</i> but technically not <i>know</i>, and is thus protected if he doesn't ask. Worse, having that pledge in place may provide Changelings with the illusion of security, and thus their vigilance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:10:05-08:00","id":825513,"title":"","content":"Also, a Huntsman can simply pretend to be a changeling that is willing to part with a Token of Reprieve for a really important favour. Which won't trigger any anti-Huntsman Pledges so long as nobody knows he's actually a Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:41:00-08:00","id":825537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, there's no reason why the Freehold law the Changeling's swear to obey can't say something like. &quot;Any Changeling who makes a bargain with the Huntsmen must, within 24 hours of learning that they have done.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this for two reasons:<br /> <br /> It makes it transparent that there is a 24 hour gap loop-hole which would be terrifying and short circuit any illusions of security, and the resulting complacence caused by that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worse, having that pledge in place may provide Changelings with the illusion of security, and thus their vigilance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also by having an easy transparent loophole you tempt people in a rush to use it if they lack integrity, they just decide to &quot;fully disclose&quot; with multiple overnight packages with confessions that they send on their way out of town or with a long distance phone call, skype and email.. (the redundancy is reduce the risk of violating the pledge due to any specific delay in delivery. Oh aren't you so clever.) This gets the traitor out of the town and put on a blacklist which increases the safety of the group. You <u>want</u> to filter out those without integrity from your society, it makes society safer, and <b>controlled channels that allow for damage control </b>are better than closing your eyes and hoping damage never happens. Also knowing that they'll either have to face the music or skip town is powerful motivations to do the right thing in the first place.<br /> <br /> Also I would not add &quot;knowingly&quot; to this pledge, its better to have changelings paranoid about whom they are bargaining with than have security what they know or their intentions protect them from violating a pledge. Knowledge of the law has never been a prerequisite to being accountable for the law, and it would be silly to make it that way in the game.<br /> <br /> Also Public Service Announcements in said freehold<br /> <br /> &quot;If whomever you bargain with turns out to be a Huntmen, you've set yourself up violate the pledge to uphold the Law!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's your responsibility to know who you're really dealing with.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It is still possible for freehold citizens to betray you to Huntmen!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Stay Calm, Stay Alert, and Trust No One!&quot;<br /> <br /> (In the traditional seasonal court freehold I imagine it'd be the Autumn Court Monarch's job to make these announcements)<br /> <br /> I think it is extremely important to remember that changeling society is filled with extremely disillusion and disenchanted people who'd most likely care much more about real security that the perception of security. Here in America we are very caught up in &quot;feeling safe&quot; so we can going about our day to day lives ignoring the threats of the world that we do things like security theater to provide ourselves comfort. Changelings don't have soft cushy life experiences that let them pretend everything is okay, they've had to struggle with life-and-death mind-shattering horrors and thus have Clarity about how unsafe the world really is. The Arcadian abduction is a beautiful and dark metaphor for what needs to happen to shake people out of complacency in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-07-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:48:57-08:00","id":825543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825513#post825513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Huntsman can simply pretend to be a changeling that is willing to part with a Token of Reprieve for a really important favour. Which won't trigger any anti-Huntsman Pledges so long as nobody knows he's actually a Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though with the jury system if he's ever revealed as a Huntsman later you'll have to stand trial and explain why you didn't look closer or why you didn't get a Pledge that they weren't here to do wickedness. You could put in clauses that require the Changeling to do due dilligence and get a pledge from anyone offering a Token of Repreve.<br /> <br /> As I said, it's probably several pages of legaleese once it's written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825508#post825508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: A good example of an antagonist is the sorceress in Snow White. She has her own motivations, personality, backstory and exists in the narrative as more than a simple obstacle or challenge to overcome.</div> </div> </div> </div> You'll notice though that the interactions between Snow White and the Queen follow the exact same pattern as the interactions between the Boy and the spirits.<br /> <br /> There's no change in charachter that lets Snow White overcome the Queen when she couldn't at the start. The Queen and the Spirits both attack 3 times. Snow White fails 3 times, the boy Succeeds three times. But they follow the same pattern.<br /> <br /> The difference is that Snow White's Queen has her own agency. The fact that the Boy is immune to attack and Snow White isn't dosen't really matter. If you wanted to look at it differently, you could say that the Boy's power is No-Fear and Snow White's power is Always-Being-Rescued and that makes both immune to their antagonist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825508#post825508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the story you want to tell, go for it. You are absolutely right that, by making changelings immune to Huntsmen, they are no longer proper antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think forbidding Changelings from making deals with Huntsmen is sufficent to make them outright immune to them. Nor was it my intent to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825508#post825508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, I'd be shocked if you found a story about a protagonist resisting temptation by citing an Oath, unless that Oath has extremely deep personal meaning for them.</div> </div> </div> </div> From what I remember their only reason was that &quot;boys are supposed to go to school&quot; - the devil was trying to tempt a schoolboy.<br /> <br /> So actually, that is citing the law.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825508#post825508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Oracle would most definitely win through clever use of foresight, but IMO it'd be narratively stronger if the Huntsman, when he comes to find the Oracle to make the offer, finds instead a flower and a &quot;No, thank you&quot; note. I feel that's a lot more interesting than a Pledge-born refusal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming they're not the same thing.<br /> <br /> Who crafted the pledge but the lawyer? The motives he has for crafting the pledge are the same motives that would let him reject a huntsman in person. 2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:07:11-08:00","id":825548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825543#post825543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll notice though that the interactions between Snow White and the Queen follow the exact same pattern as the interactions between the Boy and the spirits.<br /> <br /> There's no change in charachter that lets Snow White overcome the Queen when she couldn't at the start. The Queen and the Spirits both attack 3 times. Snow White fails 3 times, the boy Succeeds three times. But they follow the same pattern.<br /> <br /> The difference is that Snow White's Queen has her own agency. The fact that the Boy is immune to attack and Snow White isn't dosen't really matter. If you wanted to look at it differently, you could say that the Boy's power is No-Fear and Snow White's power is Always-Being-Rescued and that makes both immune to their antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citing the obsession of faerie tales with the number three doesn't really prove anything. :P<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;always being rescued&quot; is not an immunity. The Queen actually <i>does</i> affect Snow White with her powers. Furthermore, she's a proper antagonist not only because it's her who begins and drives the story, rather than her being a speedbump in the road to Snow White's self-discovery, but because she displays actual agency as a character.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're going to be super reductionist, we could argue that most protagonists have the &quot;I will come out triumphant in the end&quot; superpower, which is quite an inane thing to point out about faerie tales. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825543#post825543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think forbidding Changelings from making deals with Huntsmen is sufficent to make them outright immune to them. Nor was it my intent to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It removes one of the major ways Huntsmen interact with Changeling society. I'd say you're removing a full third of a Huntsman's identity. When he cannot be a Tempter, all he has left is being a Hunter and a Shapeshifter. It removes one of the Huntsman's more subtle means to get to his prey and instead forces him to take more direct means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825543#post825543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember their only reason was that &quot;boys are supposed to go to school&quot; - the devil was trying to tempt a schoolboy.<br /> <br /> So actually, that is citing the law.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still undermining the point of a resistance to temptation, which is the demonstration of incorruptibility, virtue or strength of will, by attempting to coerce people into doing so. If you are <i>forced </i> or <i>coerced</i> into refusing temptation, there's no virtue in doing so. Furthermore, Pledges are not laws. They're agreements between parties. A law does not require an agreement to take into effect. Hell, ignorance of the law is not a justification to break it. Laws are purely one-sided, Pledges are not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825543#post825543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're assuming they're not the same thing.<br /> <br /> Who crafted the pledge but the lawyer? The motives he has for crafting the pledge are the same motives that would let him reject a huntsman in person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're grasping the difference between a character who has his own reasons for refusing a Huntsman and an anticlimactic, impersonal, societal obligation/coercion into doing so. One is about the character's moral strength. The other is about an attempt to force moral strength to exist where there is none.<br /> <br /> A character that would refuse the offer does not need a Pledge to do so. Trying to prevent the ones that would accept from doing so is just postponing the inevitable, and not even in an interesting way. The Huntsman is backed by the power of narrative. <i>You have to face the Huntsman</i>. Sure, running and hiding is a valid way of facing the Huntsman, and cleverly doing so should buy you some well-earnt peace, even if you know he'll eventually come back. However, a Pledge like that has no narrative weight. It's like using a cheat to skip a boss fight in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:09:14-08:00","id":825550,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you're asking for perfectionism in all dealings at all times. Everyone's guilty of fatigue or incompetence in some way or another, and common sense is an oxymoron. The idea of Arcadia scares me is because it demands a similar perfectionism. If I were a changeling, I'd suspect the freehold was being run by loyalists if they asked me to make a sufficiently complex pledge. I escaped Arcadia so that I wouldn't have to rules lawyer my way through life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:33:49-08:00","id":825564,"title":"","content":"So let's assume there's a Huntsman after your friend, and the Huntsman corners you because they know you have a clue to your friend. In return for your information, you get a token of reprieve.<br /> <br /> ...What stops you from trying to reach your friend first, and give them the token of reprieve that you earned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:37:11-08:00","id":825566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825564#post825564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's assume there's a Huntsman after your friend, and the Huntsman corners you because they know you have a clue to your friend. In return for your information, you get a token of reprieve.<br /> <br /> ...What stops you from trying to reach your friend first, and give them the token of reprieve that you earned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Huntsman, buuuut theoretically nothing. It could be a fun race to the finish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:38:22-08:00","id":825567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825564#post825564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's assume there's a Huntsman after your friend, and the Huntsman corners you because they know you have a clue to your friend. In return for your information, you get a token of reprieve.<br /> <br /> ...What stops you from trying to reach your friend first, and give them the token of reprieve that you earned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Already discussed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme\">here</a>, my friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In short: The Huntsman himself. Can you outsmart the Huntsman and get to your friend in time? In theory, sure. Not terribly likely to happen. And if it does, you can bet the next Huntsman will be prepared for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:43:52-08:00","id":825570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825566#post825566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the Huntsman, buuuut theoretically nothing. It could be a fun race to the finish.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what I'm kind of thinking. You don't necessarily need to &quot;defeat&quot; the Huntsman. You don't need to outsmart them.<br /> <br /> A simple showing of actual loyalty to a friend that involves a real sacrifice... And the story is over. The Huntsman, technically by their own rules, won. They've completed their hunt and they get to return to Arcadia. This really strikes the notes of fairy tales being a moral lesson, in a way. I don't think that's a bad thing at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:51:01-08:00","id":825574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825570#post825570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I'm kind of thinking. You don't necessarily need to &quot;defeat&quot; the Huntsman. You don't need to outsmart them.<br /> <br /> A simple showing of actual loyalty to a friend that involves a real sacrifice... And the story is over. The Huntsman, technically by their own rules, won. They've completed their hunt and they get to return to Arcadia. This really strikes the notes of fairy tales being a moral lesson, in a way. I don't think that's a bad thing at all...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually not as resonant as you think, because the person that demonstrated loyalty was the <i>friend</i>, while the Huntsman was after the other guy. You didn't defeat your own Huntsman by displaying virtue, you defeated someone else's Huntsman without that person having any real agency over it. Since the changeling wasn't involved in defeating his own Huntsman, I wouldn't consider the case closed and the story resolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:07:54-08:00","id":825581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825574#post825574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually not as resonant as you think, because the person that demonstrated loyalty was the <i>friend</i>, while the Huntsman was after the other guy. You didn't defeat your own Huntsman by displaying virtue, you defeated someone else's Huntsman without that person having any real agency over it. Since the changeling wasn't involved in defeating his own Huntsman, I wouldn't consider the case closed and the story resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if you don't actually add nuance and detail to a simple idea, I can see why you don't think it's resonant. After all, &quot;Girl kisses a frog, who turns into a prince&quot; doesn't say much at all for a story either.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, the Huntsman doesn't have to be after you to create interesting drama for a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:11:20-08:00","id":825584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825581#post825581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you don't actually add nuance and detail to a simple idea, I can see why you don't think it's resonant. After all, &quot;Girl kisses a frog, who turns into a prince&quot; doesn't say much at all for a story either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note how even in the nine-word summary of the story, the protagonist actually has agency, because they're performing actions that have an effect on their own story.<br /> <br /> Your friend defeating your enemy before you even became aware that the enemy existed at all, and having all the agency in the story, does not create narrative resonance with you, it creates narrative resonance with him.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it makes for a bad story, it just makes for an unsatisfying ending. I'd recommend using that as either the start or the midway point of the story itself, rather than the conclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:19:32-08:00","id":825588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825584#post825584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note how even in the nine-word summary of the story, the protagonist actually has agency, because they're performing actions that have an effect on their own story.<br /> <br /> Your friend defeating your enemy before you even became aware that the enemy existed at all, and having all the agency in the story, does not create narrative resonance with you, it creates narrative resonance with him.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it makes for a bad story, it just makes for an unsatisfying ending. I'd recommend using that as either the start or the midway point of the story itself, rather than the conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shadow, in the scenario I'm proposing, the protagonist is the person dealing with the Huntsman. That's the PC, not the person the Huntsman is actually after. Your perception of what I'm talking about is completely backwards, and you're not talking about what I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:23:30-08:00","id":825591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825588#post825588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow, in the scenario I'm proposing, the protagonist is the person dealing with the Huntsman. That's the PC, not the person the Huntsman is actually after. Your perception of what I'm talking about is completely backwards, and you're not talking about what I'm talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>But you didn't defeat your Huntsman</i>. You defeated someone else's. If the friend is the protagonist, his story is not over yet because he hasn't faced <i>his</i> Huntsman. If the protagonist is the hunted changeling, his story is not over because he didn't demonstrate any agency in defeating his Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:27:41-08:00","id":825594,"title":"","content":"In no case is using a token of reprieve defeating a Huntsman. It's right there in the name *reprieve*. It's temporary, they'll be back eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:28:10-08:00","id":825595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825591#post825591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>But you didn't defeat your Huntsman</i>. You defeated someone else's. If the friend is the protagonist, his story is not over yet because he hasn't faced <i>his</i> Huntsman. If the protagonist is the hunted changeling, his story is not over because he didn't demonstrate any agency in defeating his Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I'm giving up. Have a good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:29:27-08:00","id":825596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825594#post825594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In no case is using a token of reprieve defeating a Huntsman. It's right there in the name *reprieve*. It's temporary, they'll be back eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this. This is very important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825595#post825595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I'm giving up. Have a good day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... sorry? For whatever I did...? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:37:17-08:00","id":825604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...What stops you from trying to reach your friend first, and give them the token of reprieve that you earned?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this was suppose to be a rhetorical question, but it has an answer other than &quot;nothing&quot; which I believe is the implied answer.<br /> <br /> One actual answer to the question is:<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen's double-crossing you to prevent exactly what you mention. Maybe the double -cross is a trap he arranged to snare you only if you try to intervene, maybe he double-crosses you no matter what; the former is better for business, the later is a petty vengeance against the Keeper and a 'screw you' to all the other Huntsmen because it reduces the likelihood of changelings ever accepting the temptation of the Token of Reprieve. Even if the second one wasn't true it'd behoove changeling to fabricate false stories of it being true to discourage changeling betraying each other to Huntsmen. It is also important to remember that if a Huntsmen is successful they cease to exist and thus are consequence free from retaliation for screwing over the True Fae and their own kind.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Already discussed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme\">here</a>, my friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Super interesting thread, I recommend reading it.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In no case is using a token of reprieve defeating a Huntsman. It's right there in the name *reprieve*. It's temporary, they'll be back eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things on this one. First, this is a great point. Second that username is AMAZING mix of snarky internet meme and Tolkien reference that puts a smile on my face, thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm giving up. Have a good day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to thank you for your contributions to this conversation, they have been valuable and the catalyst towards articulating and sharpening our understanding of the Huntsman's role in the narrative of changeling society through debating different points of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-07-2016, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:42:12-08:00","id":825606,"title":"","content":"One more time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825596#post825596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also this. This is very important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as you might think. As the excerpt stated, creating a Huntsman to go after a target is a Big Deal, one that is a commitment by the True Fae responsible. The entire purpose of a Token of Reprieve, is that you can hand it to the Huntsman after you and by the laws of Arcadia, the Huntsman must accept the token. The Huntsman's hunt is now officially over, they get to go back to Arcadia and the True Fae has to accept the bringing back of the token as a successful hunt. That Huntsman's job is done and they are no longer a problem. The True Fae might be able to create a new Huntsman...<br /> <br /> But that's a story for another day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825596#post825596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... sorry? For whatever I did...? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're monofocusing on the only story that matters as being &quot;You vs Your Specific Huntsman&quot;. This is not what I'm talking about. I am recognizing that there is story potential in the interaction of a Huntsman who has other quarry than you. Every time I'm talking about this, you're there saying that the only story that matters is the story where you deal with your own Huntsman.<br /> <br /> Therefore, you're not actually addressing what I'm talking about at all. I'm talking about oranges, you're talking about apples. Apples are fine and dandy, there's nothing wrong with apples. But it's entirely pointless when I want some citrus, because apples don't give me citrus.<br /> <br /> Why does this matter? Because by having the Huntsman's target not specifically be you, but someone you're familiar with, you entirely change the dynamic of the interaction with the Huntsman. It becomes a story with more nuance, because the equation changes to being about what you're willing to do, where you're willing to compromise, because there IS room to compromise. When the Huntsman is specifically after you, the room for compromise shrinks drastically.<br /> <br /> If you want a story with more nuance and complication, having a story where the Huntsman is after someone else than you opens up a dramatic amount of room to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:48:38-08:00","id":825607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825606#post825606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not as you might think. As the excerpt stated, creating a Huntsman to go after a target is a Big Deal, one that is a commitment by the True Fae responsible. The entire purpose of a Token of Reprieve, is that you can hand it to the Huntsman after you and by the laws of Arcadia, the Huntsman must accept the token. The Huntsman's hunt is now officially over, they get to go back to Arcadia and the True Fae has to accept the bringing back of the token as a successful hunt. That Huntsman's job is done and they are no longer a problem. The True Fae might be able to create a new Huntsman...<br /> <br /> But that's a story for another day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. I just don't consider the story to be over simply because the Huntsman was given a Token of Reprieve. The root cause was not actually addressed. Sending the Huntsman back with a Token of Reprieve and sending the Huntsman back in pieces send two very different messages. The former is nowhere near a conclusion. The latter is not necessarily one, but it <i>could</i> be one, believably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825606#post825606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're monofocusing on the only story that matters as being &quot;You vs Your Specific Huntsman&quot;. This is not what I'm talking about. I am recognizing that there is story potential in the interaction of a Huntsman who has other quarry than you. Every time I'm talking about this, you're there saying that the only story that matters is the story where you deal with your own Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually addressing this specific part:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825570#post825570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the story is over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't consider your suggestion to be a satisfactory conclusion to either the hunted changeling's story or his friend's. It feels more like the conclusion of the First Act, rather than the end of the story itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825606#post825606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does this matter? Because by having the Huntsman's target not specifically be you, but someone you're familiar with, you entirely change the dynamic of the interaction with the Huntsman. It becomes a story with more nuance, because the equation changes to being about what you're willing to do, where you're willing to compromise, because there IS room to compromise. When the Huntsman is specifically after you, the room for compromise shrinks drastically.<br /> <br /> If you want a story with more nuance and complication, having a story where the Huntsman is after someone else than you opens up a dramatic amount of room to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with everything you say here. It makes an excellent <i>part of the </i><i>story</i>, not an <i>end of the story</i>.<br /> <br /> But then again, that might be just personal preference. Your Mileage Might Vary and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:58:18-08:00","id":825615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825607#post825607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I completely agree. I just don't consider the story to be over simply because the Huntsman was given a Token of Reprieve. The root cause was not actually addressed. Sending the Huntsman back with a Token of Reprieve and sending the Huntsman back in pieces send two very different messages. The former is nowhere near a conclusion. The latter is not necessarily one, but it <i>could</i> be one, believably.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm actually addressing this specific part:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't consider your suggestion to be a satisfactory conclusion to either the hunted changeling's story or his friend's. It feels more like the conclusion of the First Act, rather than the end of the story itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I completely agree with everything you say here. It makes an excellent <i>part of the </i><i>story</i>, not an <i>end of the story</i>.<br /> <br /> But then again, that might be just personal preference. Your Mileage Might Vary and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's personal preference. The Huntsman returning to Arcadia with a token of reprieve can be the conclusion of a story. Whether you like it or not, frankly doesn't matter to me. You're not playing in my game, you don't have to read my stories.<br /> <br /> So, have a good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T15:47:36-08:00","id":825627,"title":"","content":"All right, true enough, I suppose. I just don't see how defeating someone else's antagonist is a satisfying conclusion to a story, but okay. Game on and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:01:47-08:00","id":825633,"title":"","content":"The enemy of my friend is my enemy. The Huntsman doesn't have to be after you for it to be personal. Changeling is a game of Stories, sure, but there's as much power in bucking the narrative as conforming to it. You follow the tropes when they benefit you, when they don't you try to cheat and change genres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:04:33-08:00","id":825637,"title":"","content":"Totally, but it still has to make for an interesting story, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:14:19-08:00","id":825645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825548#post825548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Citing the obsession of faerie tales with the number three doesn't really prove anything. :P<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;always being rescued&quot; is not an immunity. The Queen actually <i>does</i> affect Snow White with her powers. Furthermore, she's a proper antagonist not only because it's her who begins and drives the story, rather than her being a speedbump in the road to Snow White's self-discovery, but because she displays actual agency as a character.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're going to be super reductionist, we could argue that most protagonists have the &quot;I will come out triumphant in the end&quot; superpower, which is quite an inane thing to point out about faerie tales. :P</div> </div> </div> </div> You missed the most important part. Neither the Boy nor Snow White grow in any way during the story. All the traits they use, they have from the start.<br /> <br /> The boy's relationship to his trials (I'm still not convinced they're not antagonists) is identical to snow white's relationship to her antagonist. Thus reinforcing the idea that in faerie tales it's acceptable for a charachter to start off immune to their antagonist's primary power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825548#post825548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, Pledges are not laws.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is something Arc addressed earlier. You can have a Pledge to obey the Freehold laws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825548#post825548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you're grasping the difference between a character who has his own reasons for refusing a Huntsman and an anticlimactic, impersonal, societal obligation/coercion into doing so. One is about the character's moral strength. The other is about an attempt to force moral strength to exist where there is none.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or maybe I think the story of a society that overcomes it's scars and phobias to unify in the face of enemies trying to sow disharmony is more intersting than the story of an individual who overcomes temptations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825548#post825548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a Pledge like that has no narrative weight. It's like using a cheat to skip a boss fight in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like taking immune to fear when you're up against a boss who uses nothing but fear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-07-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T17:23:47-08:00","id":825669,"title":"","content":"Even if it's a pledge to abide by freehold laws, the problem is that you're still relying on the computer/literal genie of the Wyrd as a primary defense. This encourages the enemy and unscrupulous citizens to look for loopholes or means of causing false positives to sow distrust of their rivals. Sane people, knowing that no law can be perfect and that no compact is without loopholes due to the way human language works, even if they want to abide by spirit of the law, are going to be looking for loopholes to defend against and be wary of potential accidental violations. This requires more mental resources be spent on interaction with people, as if things weren't already nerve-wracking. The more you tighten the laws, the greater the burden it puts on all individuals operating under those laws, and the more you increase the likelihood that someone could be ostracized for being an oathbreaker because they got on the wrong side of a technicality or ambiguous language. The more hoops people have to jump through because of complex laws, the harder it becomes to tell the difference between criminal intent from psychological fatigue and hyper-vigilance from being manipulated by another's &quot;reasonable&quot; demands for transparency. When I see the legalese arms race that's going to come out of such an approach to freehold law, I'd be worried that it was an Arcadian invasion trying and <i>failing</i> to masquerade as a freehold.<br /> <br /> This is why laws and enforcement alone cannot improve lives. We need intelligent, compassionate people who know when to exercise mercy, recognize extenuating circumstances, and view actions from a human perspective. That's something the Wyrd is not interested in doing. That's what makes beings who default to solving their problems with the Wyrd so terrifyingly alien to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just after I posted, I figured out a way to summarize my perception of how using the Wyrd to create ideal laws would go.<br /> <br /> Step 1: Solve the Halting Problem.<br /> Step 2: Use the solution to determine if ideal laws can be reached in a finite number of iterations.<br /> Step 3: If so, begin iterating.<br /> Step N: Profit?<br /> <br /> Step 1 is tricky enough in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","user":"BronzeDog","date":". 02-07-2016, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T17:51:54-08:00","id":825677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825627#post825627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, true enough, I suppose. I just don't see how defeating someone else's antagonist is a satisfying conclusion to a story, but okay. Game on and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The protagonist is the leading character of the story. The antagonist is the character who is in opposition of the protagonist. If the protagonist doesn't want the Huntsman dragging their friend back to Arcadia, then the Huntsman is the antagonist of the story.<br /> <br /> Huntsman's goal = Bring the protagonist's friend back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Progatonist's goal = Stop the Huntsman from bringing my friend back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Direct opposition to each other. Therefore, your assumption of a Huntsman only being the antagonist of the specific Changeling that they are after, should probably be reviewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:03:34-08:00","id":825679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825645#post825645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You missed the most important part. Neither the Boy nor Snow White grow in any way during the story. All the traits they use, they have from the start.<br /> <br /> The boy's relationship to his trials (I'm still not convinced they're not antagonists) is identical to snow white's relationship to her antagonist. Thus reinforcing the idea that in faerie tales it's acceptable for a charachter to start off immune to their antagonist's primary power.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they did grow. The boy learnt to shudder. He learnt what he was good for and found a place in the world. Snow White learnt valuable lessons from the dwarves and was able to demonstrate her kindness towards them, which gave her the karmic/metaphysical weight to earn her happy ending.<br /> <br /> Snow White did change. Her journey allowed her to grow as a person even if she still had the same capabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825645#post825645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something Arc addressed earlier. You can have a Pledge to obey the Freehold laws.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I think the story of a society that overcomes it's scars and phobias to unify in the face of enemies trying to sow disharmony is more intersting than the story of an individual who overcomes temptations.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they're not overcoming. That's the thing. There is no challenge. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825645#post825645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like taking immune to fear when you're up against a boss who uses nothing but fear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're trivializing the fight in a way that isn't narratively satisfying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825677#post825677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The protagonist is the leading character of the story. The antagonist is the character who is in opposition of the protagonist. If the protagonist doesn't want the Huntsman dragging their friend back to Arcadia, then the Huntsman is the antagonist of the story.<br /> <br /> Huntsman's goal = Bring the protagonist's friend back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Progatonist's goal = Stop the Huntsman from bringing my friend back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Direct opposition to each other. Therefore, your assumption of a Huntsman only being the antagonist of the specific Changeling that they are after, should probably be reviewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I have a great dislike for what you're proposing is that the Changeling friend is damselled for the protagonist. You're literally taking one changeling's chance to grow and overcome adversity and giving it to someone else. Unless they both do it for each other, you're basically co-opting another character's development for yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:03:42-08:00","id":825680,"title":"","content":"Again, the power of Pledges isn't in their ability to force people to obey, it's that those involved know when it has been broken. You don't put the punishment in the pledge, or rather you make the magical, Wyrd enacted sanction minor. Slip ups and false positives happen, those responsible get a warning to be more careful in the form of a minor stroke of bad luck or something. Far, far more importantly, everybody else, especially those with the power to do something about it, are alerted that there has been a violation. Then they can go and investigate and use their discretion on how to proceed.<br /> <br /> Basically, you don't rely on the Wyrd to mete out significant punishment, you DO use it to flag you when something needs investigation.<br /> <br /> My first Motley had exactly this concern, and we ended up having our Pledge punish betrayal with Vulnerability. Betray the Motley, and they would instantly know and you got no defense against attacks or contracts. But, this sanction was also completely meaningless if the other members looked at the situation and realized it was a setup, because nothing compelled them to attack if that was, y'know, stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:15:21-08:00","id":825685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825679#post825679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I have a great dislike for what you're proposing is that the Changeling friend is damselled for the protagonist. You're literally taking one changeling's chance to grow and overcome adversity and giving it to someone else. Unless they both do it for each other, you're basically co-opting another character's development for yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please explain to me how this matters if the Changeling's friend is an NPC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T19:18:32-08:00","id":825707,"title":"","content":"What I'm seeing from these discussions is that ideally a functional freehold is going to do everything it can to give its members the conviction and the means to report Huntsmen activity as early as possible. A Changeling who trusts his Freehold to come rescue him from a Huntsman, and who has a reliable means to alert them, is a Changeling who is far less likely to bargain for a token or be recaptured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T23:06:20-08:00","id":825793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825685#post825685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please explain to me how this matters if the Changeling's friend is an NPC?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Asshole changeling:</b> &quot;Ah, sorry. Can't help you with that huntsmen problem. Wouldn't want to weaken your plotline. I'm sure your death will be very poetic and moving.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T00:30:40-08:00","id":825817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825793#post825793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Asshole changeling:</b> &quot;Ah, sorry. Can't help you with that huntsmen problem. Wouldn't want to weaken your plotline. I'm sure your death will be very poetic and moving.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using that somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T00:43:52-08:00","id":825825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825707#post825707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm seeing from these discussions is that ideally a functional freehold is going to do everything it can to give its members the conviction and the means to report Huntsmen activity as early as possible. A Changeling who trusts his Freehold to come rescue him from a Huntsman, and who has a reliable means to alert them, is a Changeling who is far less likely to bargain for a token or be recaptured.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, if Changelings actually succeed at building a healthy, almost utopian, society, Huntsmen won't really have a way in, yes. Which is exactly right, in my opinion. If you manage to peg every Changeling in the freehold to high Clarity for an extended period, I'd say you win the game. (And sure, you could totes try to achieve that using a Societal Oath, too, or whatever it's called.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:20:06-08:00","id":825858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825685#post825685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please explain to me how this matters if the Changeling's friend is an NPC?</div> </div> </div> </div>Developing the characters that are close to the protagonist is actually good writing advice. Not to mention that in a realistic setting, that Changeling has a personality and while some people would appreciate being saved like that, others (particularly those who understand how stories work) wouldn't be happy with the lack of agency on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:44:19-08:00","id":825867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825858#post825858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">others (particularly those who understand how stories work) wouldn't be happy with the lack of agency on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine they'd have very low mental scores... since most people Don't want to be involved with a Shapechanging Determinator out to get them. I'd expect most would be grateful if you resolved the issue for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T03:19:56-08:00","id":825887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825858#post825858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Developing the characters that are close to the protagonist is actually good writing advice. Not to mention that in a realistic setting, that Changeling has a personality and while some people would appreciate being saved like that, others (particularly those who understand how stories work) wouldn't be happy with the lack of agency on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you don't consider the relationship between the protagonist and the protagonist's friend as developing as the story focuses on the protagonist's efforts to help save their friend from being hunted down by the Huntsman?<br /> <br /> For some reason, I think you're assuming that I'd have the protagonist's friend as being a princess locked up in a tower who can't do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T07:24:16-08:00","id":825976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825867#post825867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine they'd have very low mental scores... since most people Don't want to be involved with a Shapechanging Determinator out to get them. I'd expect most would be grateful if you resolved the issue for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are they going to get stronger if they don't confront their fears and learn to overcome them? How are they going to get their Keeper to stop coming after them, one way or another, if they can't defeat the Huntsman?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that I am not saying that the changeling <i>must </i>face them, ready or not. I'm criticising the friend removing that choice from them by defeating the Huntsman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825887#post825887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you don't consider the relationship between the protagonist and the protagonist's friend as developing as the story focuses on the protagonist's efforts to help save their friend from being hunted down by the Huntsman?<br /> <br /> For some reason, I think you're assuming that I'd have the protagonist's friend as being a princess locked up in a tower who can't do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't actually consider that to develop their relationship. Does it develop the protagonist? Sure, he's overcoming challenges and facing an antagonist. But the lack of agency on the friend's part means that there is no growth or development to be had there. It's a purely one-sided affair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:18:58-08:00","id":826080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825976#post825976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are they going to get stronger if they don't confront their fears and learn to overcome them? How are they going to get their Keeper to stop coming after them, one way or another, if they can't defeat the Huntsman?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that I am not saying that the changeling <i>must </i>face them, ready or not. I'm criticising the friend removing that choice from them by defeating the Huntsman.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't actually consider that to develop their relationship. Does it develop the protagonist? Sure, he's overcoming challenges and facing an antagonist. But the lack of agency on the friend's part means that there is no growth or development to be had there. It's a purely one-sided affair.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, having agency doesn't always mean choosing the right course of action or achieving your goals in the end. The character being saved might be trying a different method to defeat the huntsman, one that's doomed to failure. Maybe the friend is an arrogant Fairest with a martyr complex who would rather die or be dragged back to Arcadia than accept help; failing to defeat the Huntsman on their own and being saved at the last minute makes them realize that they can't do it all on their own. Maybe it's an Ogre who keeps trying to solve the problem with their fists; they need to be shown that a clever solution is the best way to deal with some problems before they get themselves killed. Or perhaps the friend is a Darkling who learns that their friend has agreed to help the Huntsman who is after them, confirming their worst fears of betrayal, only to learn that their friend really can be trusted when they find out how they plan to use the token. There's a ton of potential for developing the friend who's getting rescued. Being rescued isn't <i>always</i> being damsaled.<br /> <br /> And it's not the end of the story for that friend. Maybe there will be another Huntsman summoned for them (that they are now better prepared for, thanks to their friend buying them time). Or maybe the way their friend used the Huntsman's own token against them gives them an idea on how to turn a pledge on their Keeper later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:22:45-08:00","id":826084,"title":"","content":"I do not agree with the notion of removing the agency of an adult because they might make mistakes. Way too paternalistic for me. Everyone deserves the right to make mistakes. It's the price you pay for the freedom to make your own choices.<br /> <br /> Also, do I actually need to remind people that the literal purpose of Seemings is to link Agency with Clarity? Because agency is actually extremely important for changelings as a splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:30:41-08:00","id":826093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825396#post825396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that no one wants to be the guy who gets screwed over without any chances just because a Huntsman saw them as a weak link or chose to use them as a weapon against their quarry. It's ludicrous to expect Changelings as a whole to be okay with a pledge backed law that makes them a sacrifice by default the moment they are confronted with that choice. Huntsmen may not be common, but they're inevitable, and that way of doing things is closing off more opportunities to <i>stay and continue living</i> (and help others) than the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the law in the end protects the bulk of the Changelings. The huntsman will quickly learn that the Changelings cannot be coerced into betrayal at knife-point, so there's little point in this endeavour. Sure it sucks to be the outlier in this case, but, overall it protects the bulk of them because the Huntsman will not be able to more even an inch closer to their target through this method.<br /> <br /> Sure it may not be in the best interest of the Changeling who gets grabbed in the vain attempt, but it's not like you know you're the outlier when you sign up. You don't sign the pledge knowing that you're the one that will be getting dragged off, you're signing the pledge because you agree that it's better that a single changeling get dragged off than the entire freehold imploding from a single huntsman.<br /> <br /> By signing into the Freehold, you're agreeing to a pact that is &quot;The needs of the group trump the needs of the individual.&quot; If this isn't the case, then there's no reason to have a freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 02-08-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:41:39-08:00","id":826103,"title":"","content":"Strings, not walls.<br /> <br /> It doesn't take much to make an example of someone under this law, using the unlucky one as the beginning of a scare tactic that can(and will) shake the freehold all the way through-Societal Oaths are framework chains, not walls.<br /> <br /> But you know what? I had a realization. One that bothers me more.<br /> <br /> This system that's getting pushed is Death Note.<br /> <br /> Okay, not exactly, but it's the same sort of thought process of Death Note, or maybe Minority Report. It's utterly totalitarian. &quot;We're going to prevent people from doing wrong before it can happen.&quot; In doing so, it chains the fuck up out of everyone and condemns before they can even do anything.<br /> <br /> That might be fun for a setting, a game, but I wouldn't want that as a norm, and in the end,a significant portion of this game is going to be about people trying to over throw it. That's not what the PC's have to do, but in the end, overthrowing the freehold is a big part of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like those sort of things. Paris is a city that could do with being overthrown. But it's not the norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:41:42-08:00","id":826104,"title":"","content":"Couple questions:<br /> 1. Can a Huntsman give tokens to non-Changelings?<br /> 2. Can someone use a token on another's behalf, or does it have to be handed over directly by the target.<br /> <br /> Either of these might be a way to circumvent certain oath-based prohibitions. <br /> <br /> (One possible example: Huntsman bargains with Lets say a vampire that has dealings with Changelings. The vampire helps the Huntsman and waits for an ideal opportunity to use the token. A new Huntsman comes to town. Vampire offers the token to the target in exchange for a huge favor. Or the Vampire simply trades it to a Changeling for future use. That's just one of many possible ways this could provide a workaround. Imagine how valuable tokens would be to family members who are aware of their loved one's nature and the dangers they face.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:46:01-08:00","id":826107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826104#post826104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple questions:<br /> 1. Can a Huntsman give tokens to non-Changelings?<br /> 2. Can someone use a token on another's behalf, or does it have to be handed over directly by the target.<br /> <br /> Either of these might be a way to circumvent certain oath-based prohibitions.<br /> <br /> (One possible example: Huntsman bargains with Lets say a vampire that has dealings with Changelings. The vampire helps the Huntsman and waits for an ideal opportunity to use the token. A new Huntsman comes to town. Vampire offers the token to the target in exchange for a huge favor. Or the Vampire simply trades it to a Changeling for future use. That's just one of many possible ways this could provide a workaround. Imagine how valuable tokens would be to family members who are aware of their loved one's nature and the dangers they face.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt they'd need tokens for non-changelings, unless the happen to know they have a changeling friend that isn't the target. There might be some clause to give them some other reward instead. Maybe something like the Demon's Pacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:53:09-08:00","id":826117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826103#post826103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This system that's getting pushed is Death Note.<br /> <br /> Okay, not exactly, but it's the same sort of thought process of Death Note, or maybe Minority Report. It's utterly totalitarian. &quot;We're going to prevent people from doing wrong before it can happen.&quot; In doing so, it chains the fuck up out of everyone and condemns before they can even do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep feeling that the general idea is to &quot;gotcha&quot; the Huntsmen, to come up with some impervious plan that bypasses confrontation entirely. It feels more like OOC rules-lawyering than an actual attempt to justify the way things work IC.<br /> <br /> A Freehold that is so totalitarian <i>is not going to have Changelings</i>. I would rather take my chances on my own than live in a Freehold where I can get punished for insane reasons, where people can easily set me up if they don't like me, and where <i>it's not even a guarantee that it won't get sabotaged or infiltrated by Loyalists and Huntsmen anyway</i>. It's like taking the worst parts of Arcadia and trying to use them to defend yourself against Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Orwellian regimes don't make you feel safe. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T11:58:08-08:00","id":826123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are they going to get stronger if they don't confront their fears and learn to overcome them? How are they going to get their Keeper to stop coming after them, one way or another, if they can't defeat the Huntsman?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that I am not saying that the changeling <i>must </i>face them, ready or not. I'm criticising the friend removing that choice from them by defeating the Huntsman.<br /> <br /> I don't actually consider that to develop their relationship. Does it develop the protagonist? Sure, he's overcoming challenges and facing an antagonist. But the lack of agency on the friend's part means that there is no growth or development to be had there. It's a purely one-sided affair.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10056\" data-vbnamecard=\"10056\">ShadowKnight1224</a><br /> <br /> I am very fond of your posts and how you think. Your ability to understand the harmony resonating through a narrative, the nuanced interplay of tropes, and general polite rational discourse in these forums are quite admirable.<br /> <br /> I think it is important to remember that to those within the world we are playing have a wide array of perspectives and motivations; While changelings have been emotionally scarred and their brain put through a cheese-grater of the in-cosmos narrative-defined True Fae Arcadian Realms that being meta-to-the-point-of-mental-illness would be an uncommon reaction (though certainly not rare) to be clear what I mean by mental illness is a mental disorder as conceptualized as a clinically significant behavioral or psychological syndrome or pattern that occurs in an individual and that is associated with present distress (e.g., a painful symptom) or disability (i.e., impairment in one or more important areas of functioning).<br /> <br /> Common examples of important areas of functioning include, work life, social life, home life, and being able to hold and maintain important relationships. This is a broad definition but is used by the Psychiatric DSM 5. In less clinical terms it seems like any strangeness in thinking or behavior that negatively disrupts your life in a way that is meaningful can be classified as a mental illness. Even seeing that definition makes me cast a wary eye in a cursory audit of my thoughts, behavior, and life, but that makes me consider the poor plight of changelings. In a similar way to being a hypochondriac over-analyzes their physical bodies and sensations, I can see some changeling poring over every inch of their life story with the same type of sickness.<br /> <br /> When I read your post hinting from a semi-in-character perspective meta-awareness about overcoming story obstacles I am reminded of this <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=2724\" target=\"_blank\">Comic</a>.<br /> <br /> I cite a previous post of your to make this point more keenly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, changelings have different motivations. Not all of them want to go back home. Some of them want to create a home of their own, or just travel from place to place, or delve deep into the secret of their fae existence, or numb their memories with nightclubs and lovers, and so on. What motivates changelings is wildly different.</div> </div> </div> </div>People who aren't blinded, gagged, deafened, and completely tied down by petty and normal things tend to be <u><b><i>!CRAZY</i></b></u>! and even those that are so restrained are still crazy (Lower case and not bold/underlined/italicized. It is my hope this punctuation/formatting carries the tone and inflection of how I would say &quot;crazy&quot; differently to convey my meaning).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-08-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:00:48-08:00","id":826126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826084#post826084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not agree with the notion of removing the agency of an adult because they might make mistakes. Way too paternalistic for me. Everyone deserves the right to make mistakes. It's the price you pay for the freedom to make your own choices.<br /> <br /> Also, do I actually need to remind people that the literal purpose of Seemings is to link Agency with Clarity? Because agency is actually extremely important for changelings as a splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>But rescuing someone isn't necessarily removing that character's agency. Agency is just about being an active participant in the story and having a real effect on it. It doesn't mean you always do everything on your own or don't ever need help or that you are always going to be the one who solves all of your problems.<br /> <br /> I think it's far more paternalistic to not help someone when they're clearly going to get themselves hurt. It's the misguided parent who makes their child suffer because &quot;how will they learn if I'm always there to bail them out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:18:09-08:00","id":826136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826126#post826126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's far more paternalistic to not help someone when they're clearly going to get themselves hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally the exact opposite of what that word means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:27:51-08:00","id":826147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826117#post826117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep feeling that the general idea is to &quot;gotcha&quot; the Huntsmen, to come up with some impervious plan that bypasses confrontation entirely. It feels more like OOC rules-lawyering than an actual attempt to justify the way things work IC.<br /> <br /> A Freehold that is so totalitarian <i>is not going to have Changelings</i>. I would rather take my chances on my own than live in a Freehold where I can get punished for insane reasons, where people can easily set me up if they don't like me, and where <i>it's not even a guarantee that it won't get sabotaged or infiltrated by Loyalists and Huntsmen anyway</i>. It's like taking the worst parts of Arcadia and trying to use them to defend yourself against Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Orwellian regimes don't make you feel safe. Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Huntsmen are such a threat, don't you think that they'd warrant enforcing a rule that benefits the whole of the Freehold?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I find it kind of bothering that people think a law that's essentially &quot;Do not be complicit in human trafficking, even at gunpoint&quot; is totalitarian. Geez, how can you have a society at all if no one wants to follow laws that prevent crime.<br /> <br /> It's like saying that you don't want to take a vaccine because you might get autism, and you'd rather trust your unimmunized body to the whims of fate than subject yourself to &quot;the man and his plan.&quot; It undermines the whole concept of Herd Immunity. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:28:49-08:00","id":826149,"title":"","content":"I just had a funny thought:<br /> <br /> How many people here, in this forum thread, contemplate agency within our own real lives, and who feels a little alienated from most normal conversations when they bring it up?<br /> <br /> I will raise my hand first, since I brought up the topic.<br /> <br /> I think this is interesting because there is an in-game reflection of this meta-awareness and those with this similar bent are the ones most at risk for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826123#post826123\">'Memetic Hypochondria'</a>, to coin a phrase. Also if changelings with this type of disorder rise into power, what steps would they take to counter Huntsmen (the topic of this thread)?<br /> <br /> I think there are definitely evidence that this affliction exists in-cosmos, especially from the 1 edition Talecrafting rules and many things that seem to borrow heavily conceptually from those ideals in 2nd edition, like court approaches, freehold bulwarks and the freehold being aware their stories matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-08-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:35:46-08:00","id":826155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826147#post826147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like saying that you don't want to take a vaccine because you might get autism, and you'd rather trust your unimmunized body to the whims of fate than subject yourself to &quot;the man and his plan.&quot; It undermines the whole concept of Herd Immunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're comparing sanity-threatening blackmail to the flu and ignoring the fact that Herd Immunity doesn't work as a metaphor when most of the people you know are protected from neither Huntsmen nor more generalized treachery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:38:43-08:00","id":826157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826136#post826136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is literally the exact opposite of what that word means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not literally the exact opposite, no. The opposite would be allowing them complete freedom, regardless of what you think is their best interest. That's not the same as withholding help when it is clearly needed, which is what I was talking about. Though, I admit that what I was talking about isn't exactly paternalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:41:59-08:00","id":826161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826155#post826155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're comparing sanity-threatening blackmail to the flu and ignoring the fact that Herd Immunity doesn't work as a metaphor when most of the people you know are protected from neither Huntsmen nor more generalized treachery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's not a totally accurate metaphor. However, the point being that if you want the protections you must make certain agreements. Society only exist because everyone can sort of trust one another. Those that can't get at least basic trust like &quot;Don't traffic your fellows&quot; &quot;Don't murder your fellows&quot; etc. and have no punishments in place, then you're running the freehold on entirely good will. That simply won't work. Society requires some baseline for order, if you don't have that then the freehold is little better than an oversized motley.<br /> <br /> It does offer some protections though, because it will quickly become apparent that holding Changelings at gunpoint or trying to buy them off won't work without getting them outed to the entire freehold. So you are cutting off one way that the huntsman has to get to it's target. Is it full-proof by any means? No. But it's some kind of protection beyond those of the approaches. If the huntsman is able to drag off any changeling at a whim, I think you have much greater problems if your constituents are being dragged off en-masse. It builds a baseline for trust that you can at least trust that <b>your</b> freehold won't sell you out. Unaffiliated changelings and those of other freeholds are under no compulsion, presumably. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:48:55-08:00","id":826168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826093#post826093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the law in the end protects the bulk of the Changelings. The huntsman will quickly learn that the Changelings cannot be coerced into betrayal at knife-point, so there's little point in this endeavour. Sure it sucks to be the outlier in this case, but, overall it protects the bulk of them because the Huntsman will not be able to more even an inch closer to their target through this method.</div> </div> </div> </div>The confronted person gets screwed regardless, and the Huntsman is none the worse for it aside from their presence potentially being revealed. They won't learn that there's little point in it. They'll learn they can destabilize a freehold by repeatedly engineering circumstances where they can make Changelings take a Token of Reprieve. It will either let them remove several changelings from the equation before getting to their target or being caught, or make it more difficult for the Freehold to function until they're discovered. In both cases, they could take something from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826093#post826093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure it may not be in the best interest of the Changeling who gets grabbed in the vain attempt, but it's not like you know you're the outlier when you sign up. You don't sign the pledge knowing that you're the one that will be getting dragged off, you're signing the pledge because you agree that it's better that a single changeling get dragged off than the entire freehold imploding from a single huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you just know when you sign up that the moment you become a tangential victim to the Huntsmen you're finished, and even being dragged to Arcadia or dying won't stop them from potentially claiming a second and third person. If they're patient enough, they will use the terms of this law against the Freehold, and then it's going to implode anyways, to borrow your choice of words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826093#post826093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By signing into the Freehold, you're agreeing to a pact that is &quot;The needs of the group trump the needs of the individual.&quot; If this isn't the case, then there's no reason to have a freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Freeholds exist for Changelings to protect each other and the populace from the fae. This is supposed to include you if you're in danger, or there's no reason to have a freehold. Do you see the problem with this argument?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-08-2016, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:51:33-08:00","id":826171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826161#post826161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's not a totally accurate metaphor. However, the point being that if you want the protections you must make certain agreements. Society only exist because everyone can sort of trust one another. Those that can't get at least basic trust like &quot;Don't traffic your fellows&quot; &quot;Don't murder your fellows&quot; etc. and have no punishments in place, then you're running the freehold on entirely good will. That simply won't work. Society requires some baseline for order, if you don't have that then the freehold is little better than an oversized motley.</div> </div> </div> </div>When in practice the law becomes &quot;don't traffic your fellows, who are mostly relative strangers to you, even if your human connections, who are likely people you've known for a significant length of time, may in fact be directly related to you, and are the foundation upon which your Clarity is built, are threatened,&quot; you have fucked up a perfectly good society.* The entire reason changelings were able to escape Arcadia is because they were prepared to break the rules, but the very exceptional circumstances that entailed mean it's a terrible idea to try to build a functional society with laws that require them to cling together in an increasingly maddened insular clutch or obviate the point of such a law by becoming oathbreakers all and burning their Clarity down.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Look at it. It's got rampant paranoia.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:53:50-08:00","id":826173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826161#post826161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know it's not a totally accurate metaphor. However, the point being that if you want the protections you must make certain agreements. Society only exist because everyone can sort of trust one another. Those that can't get at least basic trust like &quot;Don't traffic your fellows&quot; &quot;Don't murder your fellows&quot; etc. and have no punishments in place, then you're running the freehold on entirely good will. That simply won't work. Society requires some baseline for order, if you don't have that then the freehold is little better than an oversized motley.<br /> <br /> It does offer some protections though, because it will quickly become apparent that holding Changelings at gunpoint or trying to buy them off won't work without getting them outed to the entire freehold. So you are cutting off one way that the huntsman has to get to it's target. Is it full-proof by any means? No. But it's some kind of protection beyond those of the approaches. If the huntsman is able to drag off any changeling at a whim, I think you have much greater problems if your constituents are being dragged off en-masse. <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>But it probably would still work (holding Changelings at knifepoint etc.).I think most (or at least many) Changelings, given the choice between death or breaking a pledge, will probably break the pledge and quickly skip town. And some will be willing to do it for less. So what this system really gets you isn't less people betraying their fellows to the Huntsman; it just gets you a Freehold that shrinks by a few self-interested Changelings each time a Huntsman comes to town. It doesn't guarantee that the remaining Changelings are actually loyal, they just haven't been tested. So the Huntsman doesn't really need to change tactics much, and there aren't likely to be any tokens of reprieve in circulation to get rid of them either. It's a loss for the Freehols to have those kind of pledges; they lose Changelings who have to skip town due to breaking the pledge, they probably still lose just as many Changelings to Huntsman, and they lose a distasteful but valuable method of getting rid of Huntsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 02-08-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:54:02-08:00","id":826174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826123#post826123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very fond of your posts and how you think. Your ability to understand the harmony resonating through a narrative, the nuanced interplay of tropes, and general polite rational discourse in these forums are quite admirable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I appreciate your clever posts as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826123#post826123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is important to remember that to those within the world we are playing have a wide array of perspectives and motivations</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have been a bit overzealous in defending the agency of changelings. It's a topic that's very dear for me.<br /> <br /> I will however, defend my &quot;meta&quot; speak when it comes to changelings.<br /> <br /> Remember that time someone called you out on something you did, and you knew they were right even if you protested otherwise? That deep-seated feeling that you know someone else is right even though your emotions might be angry or in denial, is the way I imagine changelings feel about stories. They just <i>know</i> that they can't run away from Huntsmen and the True Fae forever, just like they <i>know</i> that when their best friend tells them &quot;you always fall for guys that are bad for you!&quot;, their best friend is right.<br /> <br /> Call it the Wyrd, call it Arcadia and the True Fae being made of stories and changelings being part of that, call it narrative intution. Whatever it is, I think changelings know full well when an evasive manoeuvre is a daring, climactic escape and when it's an attempt to avoid facing something difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826123#post826123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who aren't blinded, gagged, deafened, and completely tied down by petty and normal things tend to be <u><b><i>!CRAZY</i></b></u>! and even those that are so restrained are still crazy (Lower case and not bold/underlined/italicized. It is my hope this punctuation/formatting carries the tone and inflection of how I would say &quot;crazy&quot; differently to convey my meaning).</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of being cynical to the point of deflating an otherwise witty argument, sanity is simply whatever the majority agrees is acceptable behaviour, just like &quot;normalcy.&quot; :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826126#post826126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But rescuing someone isn't necessarily removing that character's agency. Agency is just about being an active participant in the story and having a real effect on it. It doesn't mean you always do everything on your own or don't ever need help or that you are always going to be the one who solves all of your problems.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://dictionary.reference.com/browse/agency?s=t\" target=\"_blank\">Agency</a>:<br /> 9. the state of being in action or of exerting power; operation: the agency of Providence.<br /> 10. a means of exerting power or influence; instrumentality: nominated by the agency of friends.<br /> <br /> By removing the chance for the character to exert power or influence, or be in action, you are removing their agency. The character doesn't get to do anything about the Huntsman. They get to exert no power or influence, or take any action (except take the Token given by their friend and then hand it over to the Huntsman).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826126#post826126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's far more paternalistic to not help someone when they're clearly going to get themselves hurt. It's the misguided parent who makes their child suffer because &quot;how will they learn if I'm always there to bail them out.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Every relationship has its own balance point between not helping enough and helping too much. Learning when to accept help and when not to offer help is an important part of being an adult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826149#post826149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people here, in this forum thread, contemplate agency within our own real lives, and who feels a little alienated from most normal conversations when they bring it up?</div> </div> </div> </div>For personal reasons, I deliberately try to have as much agency in my life as I can. It's one of the reasons Changeling resonates with me.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826147#post826147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Huntsmen are such a threat, don't you think that they'd warrant enforcing a rule that benefits the whole of the Freehold?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I find it kind of bothering that people think a law that's essentially &quot;Do not be complicit in human trafficking, even at gunpoint&quot; is totalitarian. Geez, how can you have a society at all if no one wants to follow laws that prevent crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't think changeling society should have laws. I know, controversial opinion. Swearing fealty to a monarch should be a loose affiliation at best.<br /> <br /> I do not see a Freehold as a proper society, but as a support group of sorts. Pledges are the sort of thing changelings should use carefully. Too many strings attached and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-08-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T12:59:11-08:00","id":826181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826168#post826168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The confronted person gets screwed either way, and the Huntsman is none the worse for it aside from their presence potentially being revealed. They won't learn that there's little point in it. They'll learn they can destabilize a freehold by repeatedly engineering circumstances where they can make Changelings take a Token of Reprieve. It will either let them remove several changelings from the equation until getting to their target or being caught, or make it more difficult for the Freehold to function until they're discovered. Either way, they could take something from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if you're losing that many changelings that quickly to a single actor then you have other problems. Because then it outlines that your freehold is so vulnerable that your approaches and the like are basically irreverent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826168#post826168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you just know when you sign up that the moment you become a tangential victim to the Huntsmen you're finished, and even being dragged to Arcadia or dying won't stop them from potentially claiming a second and third person. If they're patient enough, they will use the terms of this law against the Freehold, and then it's going to implode anyways, to borrow your choice of words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so then don't join a freehold. There, easy. If you don't want to play by the rules of the freehold, then you don't belong in the freehold. If the Huntsman is claiming that many people, again you have other much deeper problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826168#post826168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freeholds exist for Changelings to protect each other and the populace from the fae. This is supposed to include you if you're in danger, or there's no reason to have a freehold. Do you see the problem with this argument?</div> </div> </div> </div>The freehold protects you by making it incredibly difficult for Huntsmen to get to you. If you can't trust your neighbor not to sell you out at the drop of the hat then the freehold is doing you no good. Because not only is your name out in the open, but there's a greater risk for betrayal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826171#post826171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When in practice the law becomes &quot;don't traffic your fellows, who are mostly relative strangers to you, even if your human connections, who are likely people you've known for a significant length of time, may in fact be directly related to you, and are the foundation upon which your Clarity is built, are threatened,&quot; you have fucked up a perfectly good society.* The entire reason changelings were able to escape Arcadia is because they were prepared to break the rules, but the very exceptional circumstances that entailed mean it's a terrible idea to try to build a functional society with laws that require them to cling together in an increasingly maddened insular clutch or obviate the point of such a law by becoming oathbreakers all and burning their Clarity down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, then don't join the freehold. If you cannot play by society's rules then you don't belong in the society. Just hide away and make yourself an unknown, therefore no one knows you and cannot really betray you.<br /> <br /> If you can't agree to even basic terms like &quot;Don't fuck over your fellows&quot; then why are you even here, really? You just want to piggyback on everyone else, but be entirely free to backstab them at the earliest opportunity? I can't imagine a freehold working on principles like that. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:02:10-08:00","id":826186,"title":"","content":"You can't fight distrust with distrust. You have to fight it with discretion and trust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:08:07-08:00","id":826191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826186#post826186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't fight distrust with distrust. You have to fight it with discretion and trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the whole point of the pledges to ensure that you can trust your neighbor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:09:06-08:00","id":826193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826181#post826181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, then don't join the freehold. If you cannot play by society's rules then you don't belong in the society. Just hide away and make yourself an unknown, therefore no one knows you and cannot really betray you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if the only options you can conceive of are &quot;Destroy your sanity in this isolating story-cult&quot; or &quot;Isolate yourself in the very fashion that endangers your loved ones (and thereby your sanity) and makes it easier to be dragged back to hell&quot; then you've utterly failed to understand the point of an alliance with a narrative backing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:09:48-08:00","id":826194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826191#post826191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't the whole point of the pledges to ensure that you can trust your neighbor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust them more, maybe. But even with pledges, you can't have full trust. Anything fully binding is restrictive, and everything has loopholes. Pledges are a safety net, not an edifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:12:55-08:00","id":826195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826193#post826193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, if the only options you can conceive of are &quot;Destroy your sanity in this isolating story-cult&quot; or &quot;Isolate yourself in the very fashion that endangers your loved ones (and thereby your sanity) and makes it easier to be dragged back to hell&quot; then you've utterly failed to understand the point of an alliance with a narrative backing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the point of a freehold that can't trust one another? If there's no insurance that the person next to you isn't selling you out to the huntsman right now, then why are you even with them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826194#post826194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trust them more, maybe. But even with pledges, you can't have full trust. Anything fully binding is restrictive, and everything has loopholes. Pledges are a safety net, not an edifice.</div> </div> </div> </div>So because it's not a perfect solution, why bother with it at all?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:13:33-08:00","id":826197,"title":"","content":"I think there's a saying that applies here.<br /> <br /> Something about sacrificing freedom for security.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:15:57-08:00","id":826198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826195#post826195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So because it's not a perfect solution, why bother with it at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. It may still be worth trying, and it will probably help. But it won't no-sell the Huntsmen, even on that one front. And it means that a pledge of this nature will not be a part of every freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:15:59-08:00","id":826199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826197#post826197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a saying that applies here.<br /> <br /> Something about sacrificing freedom for security.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of that quote, I thought of it when writing the posts. However, should there be no laws at all, because it might sacrifice some freedom, like the freedom to murder and maim your neighbor because he beat you in poker?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826198#post826198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, no. It may still be worth trying, and it will probably help. But it won't no-sell the Huntsmen, even on that one front. And it means that a pledge of this nature will not be a part of every freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, it doesn't have to be a perfect solution. You could make a game out of how a hole in the law risks the freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:16:38-08:00","id":826201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826191#post826191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't the whole point of the pledges to ensure that you can trust your neighbor?</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>should </i>be. Well, technically.<br /> <br /> Think of Pledges, instead, as a <i>manifestation</i> of trust...or distrust. After all, the terms are made by the people, not inherently by the Wyrd, and the words you use are an expression of your feelings about a person or a society. The Pledge coalesces from that trust/distrust. The Pledge just reinforces the feelings and ideas that are already present.<br /> <br /> In this way, Pledges bind people. It's a question wrapping your hands together with ribbon...or stabbing each other, refusing to let go of the knives, and calling that binding 'safe'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:19:05-08:00","id":826203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826174#post826174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 9. the state of being in action or of exerting power; operation: the agency of Providence.<br /> 10. a means of exerting power or influence; instrumentality: nominated by the agency of friends.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But you're not removing their ability to exert power or effect the story. You could rescue them after their actions/exertions of power have failed (agency doesn't guarantee success), at which point you're just altering the consequences of their failure. And they could be (and probably are) fighting the Huntsman the whole time you're trying to get to them with the token - just evading and/or holding off a Huntsman is exerting power and demonstrating agency. Unless they're just sitting there like a lump waiting to be saved, they have other ways to exercise agency.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826174#post826174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By removing the chance for the character to exert power or influence, or be in action, you are removing their agency. The character doesn't get to do anything about the Huntsman. They get to exert no power or influence, or take any action (except take the Token given by their friend and then hand it over to the Huntsman).</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides, you're not doing anything to limit what they can do. You just gave them another option. As you have just pointed out, they have to hand the token over to the Huntsman. They can say &quot;I don't need this&quot; and throw it down or break it or whatever and fight the Huntsman to the death (which would be a pretty cool scene.) Or they can accept that the Huntsman is too much for them to defeat now (and they'll level up to defeat the next one on their terms), or that their pride isn't worth the lives the Huntsman might take if it escapes to keep hunting them, and hand over the token. That decision is still an act of agency.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:21:19-08:00","id":826206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826195#post826195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the point of a freehold that can't trust one another? If there's no insurance that the person next to you isn't selling you out to the huntsman right now, then why are you even with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the odds of that being the case for <i>everybody in the freehold</i> are sufficiently low that, even if there's no love lost between any given two of you, you can come to an agreement flexible enough that the consequences of your loss are unpleasant enough that they'd be better off just skipping town themselves to avoid the Huntsman that doesn't have their scent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So because it's not a perfect solution, why bother with it at all? </div> </div> </div>Are you actually outright invoking the Perfect Solution Fallacy <i>as a serious argument for draconian freehold laws</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:22:37-08:00","id":826209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826199#post826199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware of that quote, I thought of it when writing the posts. However, should there be no laws at all, because it might sacrifice some freedom, like the freedom to murder and maim your neighbor because he beat you in poker?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't run Freeholds as &quot;mortal society, but with changelings!&quot;. Changelings don't <i>need</i> Freeholds. They're ridiculously convenient, yes, absolutely. But they're not so necessary that a changeling would be willing to chain himself to a quasiArcadian system.<br /> <br /> So yes, my Freeholds don't have laws. Swearing fealty to the Freehold/Monarchs basically means that you acknowledge that if you do them wrong, there will be consequences coming your way.<br /> <br /> The idea that only laws prevent changelings from murdering each other for trivial reasons is rather sociopathic. It implies the absence of both empathy and morality. That said, changelings do wrong each other rarely, and such things get dealt with privately and swiftly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:22:54-08:00","id":826210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826206#post826206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the odds of that being the case for <i>everybody in the freehold</i> are sufficiently low that, even if there's no love lost between any given two of you, you can come to an agreement flexible enough that the consequences of your loss are unpleasant enough that they'd be better off just skipping town themselves to avoid the Huntsman that doesn't have their scent.<br /> <br /> Are you actually outright invoking the Perfect Solution Fallacy <i>as a serious argument for draconian freehold laws</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Don't aid the Gentry&quot; is draconian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:26:39-08:00","id":826215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826203#post826203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But you're not removing their ability to exert power or effect the story. You could rescue them after their actions/exertions of power have failed (agency doesn't guarantee success), at which point you're just altering the consequences of their failure.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The situation proposed involved absolutely no actions on the saved changeling's part. Yes, all those things are possible. They are not, however, the situation I was discussing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826203#post826203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they could be (and probably are) fighting the Huntsman the whole time you're trying to get to them with the token - just evading and/or holding off a Huntsman is exerting power and demonstrating agency. Unless they're just sitting there like a lump waiting to be saved, they have other ways to exercise agency.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> If the Huntsman is offering you a Token of Reprieve or chasing you before you can reach your friend, then he is not simultaneously being evaded/held off by your friend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826203#post826203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, you're not doing anything to limit what they can do. You just gave them another option. As you have just pointed out, they have to hand the token over to the Huntsman. They can say &quot;I don't need this&quot; and throw it down or break it or whatever and fight the Huntsman to the death (which would be a pretty cool scene.) Or they can accept that the Huntsman is too much for them to defeat now (and they'll level up to defeat the next one on their terms), or that their pride isn't worth the lives the Huntsman might take if it escapes to keep hunting them, and hand over the token. That decision is still an act of agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all cool things, but not the situation that was being discussed.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826210#post826210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Don't aid the Gentry&quot; is draconian?</div> </div> </div> </div>As pointed several times in this thread, you'd have to resort to draconian measures in order to actually enforce such an open-ended and tricky law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-08-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:26:50-08:00","id":826216,"title":"","content":"Actually, yes. For the reason Satchel says below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:26:51-08:00","id":826217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826210#post826210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Don't aid the Gentry&quot; is draconian?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Don't aid the Gentry&quot; is hopelessly vague and the means by which a pledge is enforced is markedly <i>not vague</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:27:48-08:00","id":826218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826217#post826217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Don't aid the Gentry&quot; is hopelessly vague and the means by which a pledge is enforced is markedly <i>not vague</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just the basic idea, without any legalese. Is the basic premise of the legalese flawed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:29:40-08:00","id":826220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826218#post826218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just the basic idea, without any legalese. Is the basic premise of the legalese flawed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the steps to which you'd have to resort in order to enforce it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:32:48-08:00","id":826225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826218#post826218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just the basic idea, without any legalese. Is the basic premise of the legalese flawed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic premise of the legalese is <i>the reason freeholds are established</i>, which is not itself subject to <i>wordplay</i>, which the fae as a whole are typically well-practiced in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:37:38-08:00","id":826229,"title":"","content":"I would assume that some Freeholds could have Pledges to not aid Huntsmen, with varying degrees of granularity/stringency/draconian measures. Given the reasons outlined by a lot of folks, the pledges would work on some of the Huntsmen some of the time, but wouldn't prevent an approach, and wouldn't be ubiquitous among freeholds. Some would help, but that system would be just as subject to corruption as any other.<br /> <br /> Tangent: This current direction of discussion now has me thinking of a Freehold with a Law Court (or Court of Law): courtiers are legal experts, their theme is Control, their ritual involves some kind of mystical obfuscating bureaucratic processes, and their Approaches force Huntsmen to find loopholes in pledges like the ones being discussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:46:37-08:00","id":826236,"title":"","content":"Remember when I suggested that Freeholds use Pledges as a net?<br /> <br /> A little thing on that. A good Freehold has Societal Oaths and encourages Pledges that manipulate anyone who swears on them to help one another rather than kick anyone out. Instead of keeping Loyalists out, a good Freehold <i>binds the Loyalist to everyone else</i>, snaring them and obliging them to help whenever the Gentry and their Huntsmen come in.<br /> <br /> Pledges of that sort have the added benefit of encouraging a society where people watch out for each other and help each other, building a sense of communal trust and service, as opposed to breathing down their necks saying &quot;Go ahead, betray us, we dare you.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the problem with the 'wall' pledges, it just reinforces a sense of distrust, a distrust every changeling has upon returning. It tells them that the city doesn't trust individuals to do the right thing, so why should they trust them. And it also tells them they don't care about the little guys, particularly the newly returned, because the system encourages a system of exploitation of the newly returned for the Huntsmen. All of this encourages and creates the distance that tragically makes it happen, because the alternative is living in a pressure cooker of distrust.<br /> <br /> Freeholds exist to bring everyone together, to get the innately paranoid newly returned to start trusting their neighbors and the state, to get them working for one another's benefit. You can't do that with 'wall' Societal Oaths, you need 'ribbon' Oaths. Personal Oaths can become more wall-like, because it's a small enough and close enough circle of people that such trust is usually warranted, hell, it becomes loyalty at that point. But the point is that a freehold needs to make a community that actively will want to circle the wagons when the Huntsmen come, a place where people are actually likely to watch each others backs. And you can't do that if you have laws from on high telling you, the freeholder, that everyone around you is going to stab you in the back.<br /> <br /> I have gone a long way to explain changelings nature as paranoid and opportunistic people. What a freehold should do is subject these lesser instincts to everyone's better angels. Thus, <i>I will never go back</i> can actually transform into the Long Way Home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:51:29-08:00","id":826238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825564#post825564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's assume there's a Huntsman after your friend, and the Huntsman corners you because they know you have a clue to your friend. In return for your information, you get a token of reprieve.<br /> <br /> ...What stops you from trying to reach your friend first, and give them the token of reprieve that you earned?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the initial scenario from the thread. It seems vague enough to me to allow for any of that. Paradim even mentioned that it was a basic idea and would have nuance added to it if actually implemented and that the friend would not be a princess locked in a tower. Note that in the scenario you are trying to reach your friend before the Huntsman. It's a race. The Huntsman is by default pursuing your friend (so they could be evading, at least, if not fighting them) and you are trying to reach them first.<br /> <br /> Regardless, when I started commenting on the topic, I was specifically responding to this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825976#post825976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are they going to get stronger if they don't confront their fears and learn to overcome them? How are they going to get their Keeper to stop coming after them, one way or another, if they can't defeat the Huntsman?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that I am not saying that the changeling <i>must </i>face them, ready or not. I'm criticising the friend removing that choice from them by defeating the Huntsman.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't actually consider that to develop their relationship. Does it develop the protagonist? Sure, he's overcoming challenges and facing an antagonist. But the lack of agency on the friend's part means that there is no growth or development to be had there. It's a purely one-sided affair.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that defeating your friend's antagonist doesn't necessarily rob your friend of agency. That taking any opportunity to help your friend by circumventing a major threat isn't the same thing as damseling. And that both characters have a plethora of opportunities to develop and exercise agency in the scenario.<br /> <br /> You had also said that defeating someone else's Huntsman made for an unsatisfying story, which I disagree with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:53:49-08:00","id":826243,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://www.trbimg.com/img-56b00191/turbine/la-ed-0202-vaccination-rates-20160201-001/750/750x422\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I still strongly feel like this is what's going on here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:56:30-08:00","id":826246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826238#post826238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that defeating your friend's antagonist doesn't necessarily rob your friend of agency. That taking any opportunity to help your friend by circumventing a major threat isn't the same thing as damseling. And that both characters have a plethora of opportunities to develop and exercise agency in the scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>The post you quoted wasn't the one I was talking about. I'm going to have good faith here and assume you missed it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825570#post825570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I'm kind of thinking. You don't necessarily need to &quot;defeat&quot; the Huntsman. You don't need to outsmart them.<br /> <br /> A simple showing of actual loyalty to a friend that involves a real sacrifice... And the story is over. The Huntsman, technically by their own rules, won. They've completed their hunt and they get to return to Arcadia. This really strikes the notes of fairy tales being a moral lesson, in a way. I don't think that's a bad thing at all...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the post I was referring to. You will see that it brooks no room for agency on the other changeling's part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826238#post826238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You had also said that defeating someone else's Huntsman made for an unsatisfying story, which I disagree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you can find a way to make it interesting for the person doing the defeating. Not so much for the other character.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826243#post826243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still strongly feel like this is what's going on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>As scientist in the field of medicine, I find this comparison personally offensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:58:43-08:00","id":826249,"title":"","content":"The better metaphor is America's mixed attitude towards immigrants now, particularly the Syrian refugees. Some people can only see terrorists, some people can only see the lost.<br /> <br /> And then some can see how the response of society determines who will be what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:59:20-08:00","id":826251,"title":"","content":"I always had some issues with the Pledge system from 1e. I'm hoping we get to see the 2e version soon.<br /> <br /> One of the things I always disliked about Pledges was the ability to use legalese. It just themed off theme to me. Faerie tale bargains are typically simple affairs and the trickiness is about clever language and words with double meanings, not clauses and small print - that stuff seems more suited to Demons to me. I wish there was a way to limit the linguistic complexity of Pledges without instating an arbitrary word count cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:03:44-08:00","id":826254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826249#post826249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The better metaphor is America's mixed attitude towards immigrants now, particularly the Syrian refugees. Some people can only see terrorists, some people can only see the lost.<br /> <br /> And then some can see how the response of society determines who will be what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so why is an attitude of &quot;If you want our protection and social benefits, you must abide by our morals&quot; utterly unacceptable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:08:59-08:00","id":826256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826254#post826254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so why is an attitude of &quot;If you want our protection and social benefits, you must abide by our morals&quot; utterly unacceptable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it makes too many assumptions.<br /> <br /> It assumes that Freeholds have an organised set of morals to abide by.<br /> <br /> It assumes that the Freehold gives more to the changeling than the changeling gives to the Freehold, so that the changeling is somehow &quot;indebted&quot; to the Freehold.<br /> <br /> It assumes that it's a Freehold's job to enforce morality.<br /> <br /> It assumes that changelings need morality enforced upon them.<br /> <br /> It assumes that obedience is the proper &quot;payment&quot; to the Freehold for its services.<br /> <br /> It assumes that the Freehold knows what's best for changelings as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:12:39-08:00","id":826261,"title":"","content":"Because that's not a <i>free</i>hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:04:35-08:00","id":826316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826261#post826261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's not a <i>free</i>hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, accept everyone without a filter, even those with radically different concepts of morality? Seems like a recipe for disaster. If they can't agree to even basic principles or tenets of the freehold, then why are they there? If your reason is that a freehold isn't free if it expects the Changelings that are apart of it to agree to a code of conduct, then I would say that it's not really any form of governance or authority because there is no baseline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:11:49-08:00","id":826325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826316#post826316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your reason is that a freehold isn't free if it expects the Changelings that are apart of it to agree to a code of conduct</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Throw yourself under the bus if a Huntsman shows up&quot; is not a fucking code of conduct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:17:30-08:00","id":826328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826325#post826325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Throw yourself under the bus if a Huntsman shows up&quot; is not a fucking code of conduct.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I want to have my cake and eat it too. If a huntsman shows up I want the protections and resources the freehold offers, but I also reserve the right to sell out my peers for a get out of jail free card.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what I understand out of this whole conversation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:25:22-08:00","id":826331,"title":"","content":"I'm confused now. Are we still talking about Changeling or are we talking about America?<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, let's try another way of saying this.<br /> <br /> I prefer positive guidelines to negative ones. The Long Way Home is better than <i>I will never go back</i>. The latter might have the power, but it's destructive, it's raw fire. The former turns it into a steam engine. But positive statements and power statements, they do the same things as negative ones but draw more in.<br /> <br /> For example, instead of &quot;Don't help the Gentry&quot;, I prefer &quot;Help each other out&quot;. That not only says &quot;Don't help the Gentry&quot; but it also establishes helping each other, binding them together. People are stronger than words and magic and fate, and freeholds need to take advantage of that. They can't do that with a system that encourages everyone to look at teach other as a traitor, like they're already doing. Freeholds need to build trust, and that means that their laws and Societal Oaths need to encourage that.<br /> <br /> The added benefit: If we have a system that says &quot;Don't help the Gentry&quot;, Loyalists can't get in. If we have a system that says &quot;Help each other out&quot;, we have a system that let's them in...and might just give them the space to change into something else. Like, you know. Not a Loyalist.<br /> <br /> If you want to have a wall that keeps out enemies, if you want to make a bubble that you're pretty much safe in....why not become a True Fae? No one can touch you in your Arcadian coffin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:27:05-08:00","id":826333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826328#post826328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to have my cake and eat it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the purpose of cake, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a huntsman shows up I want the protections and resources the freehold offers, but I also reserve the right to sell out my peers for a get out of jail free card. </div> </div> </div>&quot;If a Huntsman shows up I want the option to con him out of an escape clause instead of becoming another statistic for the freehold numerologist because if he's here and offering to not take me away then he's not over there actually taking the other guy away and there's a chance I can alert the rest of this big support group I'm in that I saw a Huntsman heading for the trod leading to the Baron's Hollow.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what I understand out of this whole conversation. </div> </div> </div>Fuckall, in other words, which is rapidly becoming business as usual. Black-and-white thinking is going to screw up your comprehension of a lot of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:39:39-08:00","id":826337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826331#post826331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to have a wall that keeps out enemies, if you want to make a bubble that you're pretty much safe in....why not become a True Fae? No one can touch you in your Arcadian coffin.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except other True Fae.<br /> <br /> No one is ever 100% safe in the Chronicles Of Darkness. And that's OK, because without even the possibility of danger, you are no longer playing a horror game. Without at least the chance of conflicting interests, you're not even playing a game.<br /> <br /> Besides, anyone who believes there is such a thing as a perfect law is about as far away from reality as the Gentry themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:42:12-08:00","id":826340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826337#post826337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except other True Fae.<br /> <br /> No one is ever 100% safe in the Chronicles Of Darkness. And that's OK, because without even the possibility of danger, you are no longer playing a horror game.<br /> <br /> Besides, anyone who believes there is such a thing as a perfect law is about as far away from reality as the Gentry themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, the Strangers 'play' with one another. Yes, there's a life and death risk there, but at that point is literally is just part of the game, and even then it's somewhat muted. Remember that the odds work in the weaker Strangers favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-08-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:48:10-08:00","id":826342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so why is an attitude of &quot;If you want our protection and social benefits, you must abide by our morals&quot; utterly unacceptable? </div> </div> </div>It's not and if anyone in the freehold has any sense of justice and morality they'll concede that basic morality needs to be imposed.<br /> <br /> Is it okay to kidnap and cannibalize helpless mortals and fellow freehold members?<br /> <br /> Is it alright for changelings to sell changelings in the goblin market?<br /> <br /> Is it alright to do the vilest violations imaginable to those who have no defense?<br /> <br /> These are actions some mentally disturbed people be who've been severely damaged be drawn to due to re-enacting trauma now in the abuser role, and even though they once were victims they should and must be held accountable or you become monsters complicit in their predatory schemes through your knowing inaction.<br /> <br /> Enforcing norms, mores, and etiquette are basic functions of any and all social groups, cultures and subcultures. This is more universally True than Newtonian laws because it is possible to have a consistent fictional universe without those, but even in fictional universes social groups enforcing norms, mores, and etiquette because it is easier to conceptualize a universe without conservation of energy than one with social groups that is actually without standards of thought and behavior. (Do not be confused by certain groups claiming to be rule free, those groups merely lacking self-awareness or are deceivers of themselves and/or others)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-08-2016, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:48:12-08:00","id":826343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=825976#post825976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are they going to get stronger if they don't confront their fears and learn to overcome them? How are they going to get their Keeper to stop coming after them, one way or another, if they can't defeat the Huntsman?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note that I am not saying that the changeling <i>must </i>face them, ready or not. I'm criticising the friend removing that choice from them by defeating the Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you complain to the police if they stopped an assassin from killing you? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T15:53:56-08:00","id":826347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826343#post826343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you complain to the police if they stopped an assassin from killing you? </div> </div> </div> </div>If the assassin was some random person, no. But if it's an assassin with a personal connection to me that will not stop until I'm dead, then yes. I would be quite displeased with the police for preventing me from putting a permanent end to things. I know better than to expect the assassin to give up or remain imprisoned for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:00:52-08:00","id":826355,"title":"","content":"You do realize you have to actually use the Token of Reprieve? Someone giving you one in no way prevents you from attempting to kill the Huntsman if you think you're prepared to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:04:43-08:00","id":826359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826355#post826355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize you have to actually use the Token of Reprieve? Someone giving you one in no way prevents you from attempting to kill the Huntsman if you think you're prepared to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was not the situation originally proposed. The situation proposed specifically stated that the Huntsman would not be defeated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:09:50-08:00","id":826364,"title":"","content":"Okay,stop. Need to get back on proper track.<br /> <br /> There's a balance, here, between two things being chatted about. On the one hand, Changelings are inherently paranoid, distrustful, and opportunistic....and on the other hand, a freehold needs to operate on bringing people together, building trust, and giving people a safe space to become free in. And somewhere between these two, we have &quot;Make it a law not to accept a token of reprieve from the Huntsmen&quot;, essentially, and as an extension of that, &quot;Don't help the Gentry.&quot;<br /> <br /> Truth be told, everything exists in the middle. On the negative hand, changelings, even high up in the freehold, don't want to stop the sweet, sweet revenue of certainty that comes from a Token of Reprieve and therefore keep open the possibility of betrayal just so the income...comes in. On the positive hand, changelings, even high up in the freehold, want people to not be alienated, thrown under a bus, or feel like they're being scrutinized too much.<br /> <br /> Truth of the matter is that all these reasons and more apply. Yes, your rulers want people to be safe, but if people aren't going to be safe, they might as well try and get some benefit out of it. Yes, your rulers want people to stick together, but they also don't want bad guys to come on in. We're asking questions people have been asking since the dawn of time. Which is why we have a question of &quot;Would you complain to the police if they stopped an assassin from killing you?&quot;, which ties into larger questions of justice, mercy, security, safety, etc.<br /> <br /> Of course we have very divergent ideas of how to handle the problems of outsiders and criminal behaviors and lots and lots of questions about psychology. And in particular, it asks the questions any trauma victim asks. It's a tough ass question, and we're not going to get far with it.<br /> <br /> I feel like Changeling the Lost <i>does</i> take a definitive stance by the way it frames and discusses True Fae, particularly in light of the Becoming Nightmare mechanic(Which, admittedly, is optional and therefore not as significant a matter of discussion in this as I'm suggesting it does), and I think that's something that can go double when you look at what trauma victims have to get over and how they work to get over it. I think it's worth talking about.<br /> <br /> But I'll be honest. I think we've all gotten really super deep into this discussion and we're tangled up and heated and such. And I think, being a little more objective about it, it's not a subject we can really be right on.<br /> <br /> So, I'ma gonna propose a cease fire for now. Let's all leave the thread alone for, like, a day or two, come back to it later. Because we have crossed into heavy shit, and I think it'll help to move away for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:17:01-08:00","id":826371,"title":"","content":"Hmm... why is there no delete post button....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":".  Cease fire appeared while I was posting. 02-08-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:19:26-08:00","id":826372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it's an assassin with a personal connection to me that will not stop until I'm dead, then yes. I would be quite displeased with the police</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one grievance I wouldn't publicly seek redress from the government for. Worst case scenario is you're taken seriously and thus have drawn the attention of supernaturally savvy police whom are also probably monster hunters, best case scenario they mock you in disbelief, in between those two they disbelieve you and lock you up for being a clear danger to yourself and other with delusions of being hunted unstoppable shape-shifting reincarnating bounty hunter whose only after you specifically because a godlike being which is like a parody of a nursery rhyme captured you for its personal play toy and through your own personal sacrifices were able to break free. aka You're barking mad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-08-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:32:24-08:00","id":826378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826316#post826316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, accept everyone without a filter, even those with radically different concepts of morality? Seems like a recipe for disaster. If they can't agree to even basic principles or tenets of the freehold, then why are they there? If your reason is that a freehold isn't free if it expects the Changelings that are apart of it to agree to a code of conduct, then I would say that it's not really any form of governance or authority because there is no baseline.</div> </div> </div> </div>You scare me, Reshy. It's not the core principle of mutual protection that's being questioned, it's that you're trying to use the methodology of the Gentry to accomplish it and don't realize how Changelings who've spent a chunk of their life being continually screwed by the Wyrd will react. The Wyrd is a soulless computer with the occasional viciousness of a jerk genie. The Wyrd has no sense of temperance, and will punish innocent mistakes and technicalities with the same severity as outright, intentional betrayal. The way you talk about the power of this collection of Wyrd-enforced laws and just seem to assume that it's common sense to put everyone on trial if the Wyrd marks them as an Oathbreaker and that the innocent have nothing to fear is what scares me. It's dangerously naive about the difference between theory and practice in law. It's dangerously naive about the psychology of witch hunts, scapegoating, and the seduction of easy answers. It's dangerously naive about how supposedly impartial and beneficial systems can be manipulated by those with radical politics and criminal intent.<br /> <br /> There are probably parts of Arcadia that would look nice, safe, and even heavenly in theory, but they still wind up being horrible in practice because the rules don't care about the intentions of someone who trips over a technicality. The same is true of human police states, and tyrants often use that pretty theory as their selling point to the naive. Human laws in free and just societies have purpose and can be bent if extenuating circumstances subvert those purposes. Errors can be forgiven and violators can be given warnings and explanations of their mistakes. Knowing that is why we don't all have to become lawyers. The Wyrd does not care about any of that. The Wyrd is more easily the ally of scoundrels and con artists than it is for compassionate, merciful people. The Gentry's weakness is that they don't understand the human social mindset. The more standardization and transparency you have of the Wyrd, the easier it is for the Gentry to adapt because the Wyrd is how they understand what they can get away with. Relying on a unified, Wyrd-enforced law is like trying to protect a computer network by posting the source code to its operating system on the company website, where the hackers and crackers can read it.<br /> <br /> Having human individuality and the freedom to keep secrets and prioritize friends over strangers means the Gentry will probe and fail more often. If a Motley mate breaks his vow, his close friends are going to hear him out and judge whether or not he had a good reason for the result because they are more familiar with his circumstances. False flags aren't automatically escalated and are thus less likely to reinforce the fear that enemy intends to manipulate. The freehold court isn't going to know everything about his circumstances, and with an enemy as dangerous and hated as the Gentry, far too many Changelings are going to assume the worst about a relative stranger by default and look for any excuse to confirm their biases. Having changelings of many different backgrounds, moral and ethical theories create a heterogeneous network of motleys and overlapping social circles means that they can distinguish signal from noise using human intuition better than a brittle, overly transparent society that jumps at every ping on the radar. The more you rely on any one detection system, the easier it is for the enemy to deceive and thus manipulate you.<br /> <br /> Using the Wyrd to foster unity makes you look like a pseudo-benevolent Faerie trying to form a human society despite not understanding that it's not the laws themselves that foster trust among the community. There are unwritten social rules that are brought up before we subject someone to the harsh eye of the law that the Wyrd skips entirely. Being too quick to assume that anyone who breaks those laws is doing so maliciously makes you look like one of those angelic members of the Gentry who go on about how they love everyone and then show no mercy anyone who's the tiniest bit disobedient. The problem with so many utopias is that they're built with angels or Faeries in mind, not humans or changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:03:49-08:00","id":826402,"title":"","content":"You do not have to make a Pledge where the Wyrd smites the offender. <br /> <br /> Okay? That's not a requirement, at least until 2e officially says otherwise. <br /> <br /> When you make a Pledge, you decide what Sanctions to include. Those can be quite minor, particularly the Pishogues. You know what those do? They cast a Contract on the oathbreaker. You can pick something super minor like Hearth 1. A -2 to your next instant action is like, a 5 dollar fine. A ten minute jail sentence. Hell, it's theoretically possible to break a Pishogue Pledge and get a potent BUFF in the form of Elements 5 or something. You don't want to go the buff route in case of malicious conspirators, but the point is nobody's caught between death by Huntsmen or death by Pledge. <br /> <br /> And there is an *incredibly* good reason to have a pledge against working with Huntsman. If it breaks, you know there is a Huntsman, and you know that the person who just broke the oath is likely in incredible danger and needs help. Even if they don't have a phone, even if they're unconscious, the message gets out, instantly.<br /> <br /> Flip the assumptions on their head for a moment. Nobody wants to work with a Huntsman, doing so probably means they're at the point of a blade or the metaphorical equivalent. That person needs help, ASAP. Now, they have a chance to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:15:06-08:00","id":826408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826402#post826402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay? That's not a requirement, at least until 2e officially says otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're drawing from the 1e mechanics I invite you to look closely at what breaking a pledge does to your Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:27:39-08:00","id":826413,"title":"","content":"See with free Clarity gain under the correct circumstances Clarity loss by itself is not a facet of universal justice or even a good measuring stick for morality. It is just a reflection of being to personally deal with mental and emotional trauma, often through indulging a wounded psyche in socially unacceptable ways.<br /> <br /> So even if breaking pledges cause mental distress to changelings and thus cause Clarity breaks, that is easily and quickly overshadowed by the potential to max out and refresh a point of Clarity every chapter.<br /> <br /> I am going to have to side on not trying to make laws which make it impossible to betray each other but rather working to make channels for such behavior that leaves the society safer after the passing storm. The worst thing you can do is make a false sense of safety. It is far more safe for everyone to be constantly vigilant and on high alert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:32:14-08:00","id":826414,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'll take a Clarity 4 breaking point for a guaranteed method of alerting my Monarch that there's a Huntsman in my face, right now. That's a drawback, sure, but not one I find nearly enough to dissuade me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:34:37-08:00","id":826415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826413#post826413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So even if breaking pledges cause mental distress to changelings and thus cause Clarity breaks, that is easily and quickly overshadowed by the potential to max out and refresh a point of Clarity every chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once per story. I'm not appealing to morality so much as &quot;it's a terrible idea to expect your constituents to need to risk their sanity by making oaths that you expect them to break under conditions that all but guarantee even non-malicious individuals will be subject to threats and blackmail that will at best cause further damage to their perception of reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826414#post826414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I'll take a Clarity 4 breaking point for a guaranteed method of alerting my Monarch that there's a Huntsman in my face, right now. That's a drawback, sure, but not one I find nearly enough to dissuade me</div> </div> </div> </div>Your view of the mechanics is blatantly against the spirit of their use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:45:41-08:00","id":826420,"title":"","content":"It's Changeling, using the letter of the law to violate the spirit is par for the course. Huntsmen are going to come, and Changelings in the freehold are going to be subject to threats and blackmail with or without pledges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:51:29-08:00","id":826422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826420#post826420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Changeling, using the letter of the law to violate the spirit is par for the course.</div> </div> </div> </div>In-universe, yes, which has no bearing on this twee &quot;break the pledge to get a buff&quot; reading that isn't remotely supported by the way the game presents their use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huntsmen are going to come, and Changelings in the freehold are going to be subject to threats and blackmail with or without pledges. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and <i>not having those pledges means getting approached by a Huntsman is not a no-win situation.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T18:03:31-08:00","id":826431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826422#post826422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-universe, yes, which has no bearing on this twee &quot;break the pledge to get a buff&quot; reading that isn't remotely supported by the way the game presents their use.<br /> <br /> Yes, and <i>not having those pledges means getting approached by a Huntsman is not a no-win situation.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>No win for whom, and at what level of accountability? Should people be able to &quot;win&quot; at the severe cost to the sanity/life of others with no cost or accountability themselves? What is the definition winning that you are using? Final question of the post: How do you know the above with the certainty that you state it as fact?<br /> <br /> (I would say not being betrayed by a potential traitor is a &quot;win&quot; for the changeling being hunted by the Huntsmen, not exactly a &quot;no win&quot; by not allowing people to openly betray each other. Obviously someone gets some benefit out of the rules. I'd dare say painfully dying with integrity is better off than being a dirty traitor and having to be something so loathsome for the rest of your life, because you only die once and not every single day.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-08-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T18:08:23-08:00","id":826432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826414#post826414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I'll take a Clarity 4 breaking point for a guaranteed method of alerting my Monarch that there's a Huntsman in my face, right now. That's a drawback, sure, but not one I find nearly enough to dissuade me</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that neither the Pledge rules nor the Clarity rules have actually been spoiled, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T18:13:03-08:00","id":826436,"title":"","content":"I hazard that he thinks that nothing in there will make the sacrifice any less right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T18:21:22-08:00","id":826441,"title":"","content":"My bad, didn't mean to make the conversation too heated. I'll back off, since I'm one of the main opposers to the pledge thing and I think it falls under &quot;feel free to run things at your table however you want.&quot; Hope no feelings were hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T18:31:55-08:00","id":826445,"title":"","content":"1e is canon until/unless updated by 2e. I've stressed multiple times that 2e may change how it works. Seeing as I don't have access to the 2e rules, all I can do is work with the existing rules.<br /> <br /> So yeah, maybe that plan will be nixed because the rules change. That has not happened yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:11:39-08:00","id":826501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826445#post826445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e is canon until/unless updated by 2e. I've stressed multiple times that 2e may change how it works. Seeing as I don't have access to the 2e rules, all I can do is work with the existing rules.<br /> <br /> So yeah, maybe that plan will be nixed because the rules change. That has not happened yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>At present we're evenly split between Integrity stats that work like Integrity and Integrity stats that work like Humanity. If Clarity works like Integrity then the plan is fucked.<br /> <br /> The plan is <i>already</i> fucked if you're assuming that in 1e participants in a pledge innately know when it's been broken, I think the multiple examples in Rites of Spring to the contrary and the multiple subtypes of pledge in the corebook that specify who automatically knows when a pledge is broken (none of which are a basic vow with a minor sanction) are sufficient evidence against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:48:13-08:00","id":826515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826246#post826246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the post I was referring to. You will see that it brooks no room for agency on the other changeling's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't missed it, but I was under the impression that your arguments were directed at the scenario in general (the one I quoted), rather than that particular statement. My apologies for misconstruing your argument. I'm also clearly reading the statement you've quoted differently than you are; I thought Paradim was referring strictly to the method of resolution for the scenario (which wouldn't preclude plenty of other interesting development and uses of agency beforehand in the story), whereas you seem to be reading it as being the sum total of the story being told in the scenario (if I'm understanding you properly). I have no idea which way Paradim intended it.<br /> <br /> Either way, if you agree that a character <i>could</i> be rescued without necessarily being robbed of agency and that a character <i>could</i> possibly undergo some meaningful development in the process of being saved by their friend, then I suppose we're on the same page. At the very least the same chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826246#post826246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure you can find a way to make it interesting for the person doing the defeating. Not so much for the other character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still going to have to disagree with you on this one, though. Terminator 2 is still a pretty interesting and exciting story for John Connor. Leon the Professional is still a great story from Matilda's point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:10:31-08:00","id":826524,"title":"","content":"Setting idea / relevant thought exercise:<br /> <br /> Two Freeholds, relatively close together, in a large metro area. One Freehold has strict, oath-enforced rules about Tokens of Reprieve. The second Freehold has no such rules, and offers sanctuary to Changelings fleeing the first Freehold for forswearing the pledges forbidding taking or posessing tokens. How would politics and society differ between the Freeholds as a result of these differences? Would the Huntsman treat the Freeholds differently? Play them against each other? Would they end up at war?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:15:57-08:00","id":826567,"title":"","content":"I just posted Clarity in a new thread. FYI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https:/