is what I've said, despite my attempts to clarify that no, I've said nothing at all about that. Frankly, it's really frustrating.<br /> <br /> To state as clearly as possible, your tangent on &quot;agency&quot; has no relevance to what I've talked about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:30:14-08:00","id":826628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826515#post826515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hadn't missed it, but I was under the impression that your arguments were directed at the scenario in general (the one I quoted), rather than that particular statement. My apologies for misconstruing your argument. I'm also clearly reading the statement you've quoted differently than you are; I thought Paradim was referring strictly to the method of resolution for the scenario (which wouldn't preclude plenty of other interesting development and uses of agency beforehand in the story), whereas you seem to be reading it as being the sum total of the story being told in the scenario (if I'm understanding you properly). I have no idea which way Paradim intended it.<br /> <br /> Either way, if you agree that a character <i>could</i> be rescued without necessarily being robbed of agency and that a character <i>could</i> possibly undergo some meaningful development in the process of being saved by their friend, then I suppose we're on the same page. At the very least the same chapter.<br /> <br /> Still going to have to disagree with you on this one, though. Terminator 2 is still a pretty interesting and exciting story for John Connor. Leon the Professional is still a great story from Matilda's point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can just be asked what I meant, and yes, it's just an identification of a method of resolution. Simply that, and nothing more.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Leon the Professional is a great story, and I think especially from Matilda's point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:34:35-08:00","id":826777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826628#post826628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can just be asked what I meant, and yes, it's just an identification of a method of resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for not asking directly. Thought you might have abandoned ship and didn't want to drag you back into the argument. I'm not big on forums; still pretty fuzzy on etiquette.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:28:29-08:00","id":826799,"title":"","content":"It's an intrinsic part of the pishogue sanction, regardless of vow type or level. If it includes a Pishogue, the person who cast it will know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:11:45-08:00","id":827225,"title":"","content":"I reaffirm, there is literally no way to word a pledge even to do something as simple as &quot;Don't Help the Gentry&quot; that doesn't give the Gentry a whole new set of tools to work with to dismantle the freehold. I am willing to put my best foot forward here and demonstrate this if someone wishes to put forth a hypothetical oath to prove me wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:21:46-08:00","id":827232,"title":"","content":"First problem I can think of is that the Pledge doesn't care if you do it knowingly or not, so you could unintentionally aid the Gentry, break the Pledge, and get hunted down as an oathbreaker","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:00:22-08:00","id":827455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=826333#post826333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuckall, in other words, which is rapidly becoming business as usual.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">That's not an acceptable way to address another forum member Satchel. Avoid the editorializing and don't do it again. Thanks.\u200b</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T17:50:25-08:00","id":827887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting idea / relevant thought exercise:<br /> <br /> Two Freeholds, relatively close together, in a large metro area. One Freehold has strict, oath-enforced rules about Tokens of Reprieve. The second Freehold has no such rules, and offers sanctuary to Changelings fleeing the first Freehold for forswearing the pledges forbidding taking or posessing tokens. How would politics and society differ between the Freeholds as a result of these differences? Would the Huntsman treat the Freeholds differently? Play them against each other? Would they end up at war?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the exact premise for how I'll be running the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=804036#post804036\">Portland Privateer Freehold of Shanghai Stumptown</a> which will be grossly oppressing and victimizing the surrounding Lost populations for Tokens of Reprieve, while building a retinue of Fetch slaves which they get from their Privateering of mortals (the source of the inflated lost population in the area). This of course to go with the Human Trafficking motif I have in my Chronicle.<br /> <br /> The difference in how the Freehold is run compared to its neighbors is radically different and the Huntsmen would have trouble passing through their Hedge without hearing how cooperative Portland Lost are for claiming bounties on outsiders, and how &quot;wealthy&quot; they are with Tokens of Reprieve. Does that cause some impetuous Huntsmen seek a quick score to get a moment of rest from existing? Possible but unlikely, it'd ruin their chances to get eager help for the more permanent solution of catching their quarry and taking it back to Arcadia, especially if the Huntsmen can short circuit the Token of Reprieve their target may have by having their target captured by Lost who steal all the possessions of their victim, so they have no token of Reprieve to present the Huntsmen.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-10-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T19:16:15-08:00","id":827927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=827887#post827887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is the exact premise for how I'll be running the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=804036#post804036\">Portland Privateer Freehold of Shanghai Stumptown</a> which will be grossly oppressing and victimizing the surrounding Lost populations for Tokens of Reprieve, while building a retinue of Fetch slaves which they get from their Privateering of mortals (the source of the inflated lost population in the area). This of course to go with the Human Trafficking motif I have in my Chronicle.<br /> <br /> The difference in how the Freehold is run compared to its neighbors is radically different and the Huntsmen would have trouble passing through their Hedge without hearing how cooperative Portland Lost are for claiming bounties on outsiders, and how &quot;wealthy&quot; they are with Tokens of Reprieve. Does that cause some impetuous Huntsmen seek a quick score to get a moment of rest from existing? Possible but unlikely, it'd ruin their chances to get eager help for the more permanent solution of catching their quarry and taking it back to Arcadia, especially if the Huntsmen can short circuit the Token of Reprieve their target may have by having their target captured by Lost who steal all the possessions of their victim, so they have no token of Reprieve to present the Huntsmen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was just talking about a Freehold that took a more<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> laissez-faire and pragmatic approach versus one that was more strict and idealistic. A whole Freehold full of Privateers is a very different, much more extreme, case. I feel like they'd almost certainly end up at war with any neighboring Freeholds.<br /> <br /> Edit: Cool Freehold concept, by the way. Would make for a very unusual game of CtL. Lots of story potential.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 02-10-2016, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}